window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_TRANSMIGRATED_INTO_A_SISTER_FORTUNE_ON_THE_FARM_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Meeting Li Tianchong at the Shop","paragraphs":["After a moment of contemplation, Song Jinzhao said, \"The selling part is your responsibility. I just need to make a profit. However, I suggest adding another one hundred and fifty wen. Otherwise, once we sell at this price, word will get out, and we'll never be able to charge higher in the future.\"","Jiang Zhutao stared at the price Song Jinzhao had calculated on the paper. He also felt the buyer was pushing too hard; otherwise, he wouldn't have come to discuss it with Song Jinzhao.","\"Alright, I'll talk to him again when I get back.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"You could try contacting other southern merchants to actively promote it. Whether it succeeds or not, it'll give him a sense of urgency.\"","Jiang Zhutao nodded. \"You're right. I'll have someone look into it as soon as I return.\"","On the bustling main street, an agent was showing Song Jinzhao some shops.","\"Huaqing Road and Ziwu Road have the highest prices. There aren't many shops that meet your requirements, Miss Song, and there are already two pharmacies in the area. My suggestion is to consider the east side.\"","\"It's not only cheaper but also more crowded. The people there just don't have much money; they're mostly poor. But small profits can add up to a worthwhile sum.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head in refusal. \"If the surrounding residents have weak purchasing power, no one will buy my food.\"","A cup at Sweet Snow Pavilion sold for forty wen, and one with ice for fifty wen. Song Jinzhao planned to lower her price by ten wen from that. Previously, at the entrance of Anyang Academy, this price had sold quite well.","If the area around the shop was full of poor people, not only could they not afford it, but even those with a bit of money wouldn't want to buy things in a poor neighborhood.","They would look down on it, feeling even setting foot there was beneath their status.","Rounding the street corner, Song Jinzhao pointed to Jianye Street and asked, \"This street looks quite good. I don't see any pharmacies or clinics around. Are there any shops for sale here?\"","The agent rubbed his temple with a troubled expression, looking conflicted. \"The shops on this street are for rent only, not for sale.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"With dozens of shops on the street, has no one ever tried to negotiate a purchase?\"","The agent spread his hands. \"People have wanted to buy in the past. We've negotiated over a dozen times but never succeeded. All the shops on this street belong to the Li family. Scholar Li has never relented.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow in surprise. \"Scholar Li? Is his son named Li Zien? The one whose daughter married a prince?\"","The agent nodded vigorously. \"That's right, that Li family. They aren't short of money. No amount of silver would work.\"","Song Jinzhao gazed at the stream of people on Jianye Street. Owning the entire street, this Second Prince's money bag was indeed well-filled.","\"Miss Song?\" Li Tianchong had just stepped out of a shop when he spotted a man and a woman standing below the steps, pointing at the storefront.","He recognized both of them. One was an agent from the brokerage, and the other was Song Jinzhao—he had seen her before, though she hadn't seen him.","\"Who are you?\" Song Jinzhao was sure she didn't know him, yet his face looked somewhat familiar, resembling someone.","Seeing Li Tianchong approach, the agent immediately cupped his hands in a respectful greeting. \"Scholar Li.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes widened slightly. It was Li Zien's father.","Looking closely, their features were practically carved from the same mold.","It was just that every time she saw Li Zien, he was putting on an act, while his father appeared much more steady and composed.","Li Tianchong cupped his hands towards Song Jinzhao, speaking in a gentle manner. \"I am Li Tianchong, Li Zien's biological father. Speaking of which, our families have done quite a bit of business, but this is the first time we've met face to face.\"","\"Miss Song, are you looking to rent or buy a shop?\"","The agent hadn't expected them to know each other, and they seemed on good terms.","Remembering how Li Zien had recently set his sights on her regarding marriage, Song Jinzhao felt no goodwill towards Li Tianchong.","\"To recognize me at a glance without ever having met me before, Scholar Li must be particularly unwilling to see me in the prefectural city.\"","The agent looked at Song Jinzhao in surprise. He had thought they were on good terms a moment ago, but now it sounded like there was bad blood?","Li Tianchong had already learned from his son's personal servant about what happened a few days prior.","He had said all along that Song Jinzhao would absolutely not take a liking to his son.","But the boy, arrogant and refusing to believe it, had charged forward headstrong. Not only did he fail to win her over, but he also offended her, leading to her unfavorable attitude towards him as well.","\"Miss Song, what are you saying? My son is young and has been sheltered by me since childhood. If there's anywhere he has acted inappropriately, I ask for your understanding. I will certainly discipline him more strictly in the future.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at the humble expression on his face, not having expected this attitude from him.","The agent frowned. The young master of the Li family seemed several years older than Song Jinzhao. To call him young and immature in front of her felt somewhat odd.","Seeing Song Jinzhao remain silent, Li Tianchong thought of her earlier actions and guessed part of her intention.","\"There happens to be a shop on Jianye Street for sale. If you're interested, Miss Song, I can take you to see it right now.\"","The agent's eyes widened. A shop on Jianye Street for sale?","Could it be that besides having a scholar brother, this young lady had other significant connections? Otherwise, why would Scholar Li treat her with such deference?","A faint smile curled at the corner of Song Jinzhao's mouth, but the amusement in her eyes only skimmed the surface, not reaching their depths.","\"No, thank you. This street doesn't meet my requirements for purchasing a shop. Farewell.\"","Watching Song Jinzhao turn and leave decisively, the agent was momentarily stunned. He nodded to Li Tianchong before hurriedly catching up.","\"Miss Song, Scholar Li himself said he would sell the shop. Why did you refuse?\"","The Li family were relatives of the imperial family. Countless people wanted to befriend them; those without substantial family backgrounds couldn't even get through the door.","How come with Song Jinzhao, when they were practically offering it to her, she still pushed it away?","Song Jinzhao walked straight ahead without pausing her steps.","\"The location isn't suitable, the owner isn't suitable, and having only one available is even less suitable. Let's look for others.\"","Li Tianchong was more scheming and profound than his son. Song Jinzhao didn't believe he had no ulterior motive.","Rather than constantly guarding against being ensnared, it was best to simply avoid their traps altogether.","Jianye Street's location was good, but there were plenty of places to choose from in Anyang Prefecture. It wasn't as if she had to buy there. Why get unnecessarily entangled with the Li family?","The agent observed her resolute expression and became even more determined to find out Song Jinzhao's background as soon as he returned.","He needed to avoid unknowingly slighting an important guest out of ignorance.","The next day, while continuing to show Song Jinzhao shops, the agent stole several careful glances at her.","She looked slender and petite, yet she apparently knew martial arts.","She had reportedly fought her way in and out of Northern Spy dens and mountain bandit lairs multiple times. Truly, appearances could be deceiving; this young lady was not to be trifled with.","To have received an imperial decree of reward from the Emperor, and for her brother to be not just an ordinary scholar but the top candidate in the exams... no wonder Scholar Li's attitude towards her was unusual."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: Wanting to Apprentice Under Ye Liangyu, Slave Market","paragraphs":["It took Song Jinzhao seven days to finalize the deal for two adjacent shops.","Both shops were not very large. Besides the storefronts, each had a storeroom in the back. The advantage was that they were fully equipped, requiring no renovation, and were only a fifteen-minute walk from the house Song Jinzhao currently rented.","The two shops cost a total of six hundred taels of silver. The slightly smaller one, Song Jinzhao decided, would be used for a food and beverage shop, while the larger one would house a pharmacy and medical clinic.","The medicinal herbs gathered from the mountains weren't comprehensive, so she purchased some additional ones from local medicinal merchants.","Elsewhere, upon hearing the news, Li Tianchong looked at Li Zi'en with surprise. \"Opening a medical clinic? Does Song Jinzhao know medicine?\"","Li Zi'en nodded hesitantly. \"She probably does. But a woman running a clinic... I'm afraid not many people would seek her out for treatment.\"","Li Tianchong's fingers tapped rhythmically on the scalding hot teacup. \"On the day of the opening, pick out a couple of decorative pieces that attract wealth and protect the household to send over. Be polite about it. And completely dismiss any thoughts of taking her as a concubine from your mind. Don't think about it anymore.\"","Li Zi'en pursed his lips and gritted his teeth. You don't need to tell me; I wouldn't dare marry her anyway. I have no desire to be beaten up all day long.","Inside Anyang Academy, Yan Baoyi bumped into Song Qiming's shoulder with a smug expression as he walked past him.","Song Gaoli frowned deeply, leaning close to Song Qiming to whisper, \"If this continues, even the outer division classmates will start avoiding you when they see you. We need to think of a solution.\"","Less than three days into the term, Yan Baoyi's dislike and targeting of Song Qiming were known to everyone in the outer division. With Instructor Ding backing him, many students, to avoid offending Yan Baoyi, had already begun steering clear of Song Qiming.","Song Qiming exhaled a breath of pent-up frustration from his chest. \"Those who fawn on others for favor aren't worth associating with in the first place. At least the instructors treat me fairly.\"","Song Gaoli anxiously dragged his chair over to sit down. \"The outer division instructors treat everyone equally, yes. But what about when we move to the inner division? Instructor Ding teaches the inner division.\"","\"I think you need to find a master teacher whose status surpasses Instructor Ding's to formally study under. Then they wouldn't dare bully you.\"","With Song Qiming's status as the top candidate in the entrance exams, it wasn't impossible for him to become a disciple of a renowned teacher.","Song Qiming lowered his gaze, hesitating. \"I want to become Master Ye's disciple, but he hasn't agreed yet.\"","Song Gaoli's eyes widened like copper bells. \"Master Ye is still instructing you?\"","Due to Scholar Zheng's request, Ye Liangyu had exceptionally guided them for three months. After passing the exams, when they visited him, his attitude remained limited to that brief tutorship, never hinting at any intention to take on disciples.","Song Qiming said quietly, \"My elder sister is treating Master Ye's leg. Because of that connection, he takes extra care of me. I want to try.\"","A Second-Class Presented Scholar surely possessed more talent than the instructors at Anyang Academy. Moreover, he had once been an official. The ways of governance weren't something ordinary people could access.","At that moment, Song Gaoli just felt like sighing inwardly. Comparing people to others is truly disheartening.","Not only was he more gifted in studies, but he also had an elder sister who could help with everything.","People always said he was lucky, but Song Qiming's luck was clearly even better.","\"I heard from a dormmate that several academy instructors have visited Master Ye, but were all turned away. If you can become his disciple, then even if Yan Baoyi tries any more underhanded tricks once we're in the inner division, out of consideration for Master Ye, they wouldn't dare do anything to you.\"","Before entering the academy, Song Gaoli only knew Ye Liangyu was a Presented Scholar and a former official. After entering, he learned the man had been a high-ranking third-grade official in the capital, one who could see and speak with the emperor daily.","If he could learn even half of what Master Ye knew, the provincial exams in two years wouldn't be a worry.","Song Qiming thought of the care Ye Liangyu had shown him recently. It already far exceeded the usual relationship between teacher and student. So why did he not answer when he brought up becoming his disciple?","Ye Residence.","Ye Liangyu's hands gripped the wooden frame, veins bulging on his forehead, sweat dripping from his chin onto the blue brick floor.","Yunhe, standing beside him with hands outstretched ready to support him at any moment, advised with concern, \"Master, rest for a while. You can practice more later.\"","Ye Liangyu turned his head, wiping the sweat from his chin onto his shoulder. \"No. The time isn't up yet.\"","Before, when the imperial physicians said it was incurable, he had no choice but to endure and wait for death. Now that there was hope, he was willing to try, no matter the cost.","Finally completing the morning's weighted training plan, Ye Liangyu collapsed into the wheelchair placed under the eaves, his entire body looking as if he had just emerged from water.","Yunhe handed over a damp towel.","After wiping the sweat from his body, Ye Liangyu instructed, \"Go fetch Song Qiming's schoolwork from the table.\"","Yunhe swiftly turned and went inside to get the assignments.","\"Master, what you're doing now is almost the same as a master teacher would. Why are you still unwilling to agree to take Song Qiming as your disciple?\"","He clearly cared about the boy's studies, summoning him daily to ask questions and assigning separate work. He also genuinely appreciated Song Qiming.","Ye Liangyu placed the essay in his hand on his lap. \"This child's path has been too fast and too smooth. I want to temper his character, to see how long he can persist.\"","\"Also, I don't want him to think I'm willing to take him as a disciple only because his sister is treating my leg.\"","Yunhe's lips moved slightly. He hesitated, then spoke again. \"But wasn't there a reason related to Miss Song when you considered taking him as a disciple?\"","Ye Liangyu looked up at the sky. \"Initially, yes, but it was only to look out for him a bit more.\"","\"Later, it was truly because I saw promise in Song Qiming. The recovery period is long and arduous. Taking on a disciple to nurture might be good, at least it would keep my mind from stagnating.\"","Yunhe pressed his lips together and fell silent. He very much wanted to ask his master if, once his legs were healed, he would return to that place that devoured people without spitting out the bones.","But after a moment's thought, he felt asking was pointless. The answer was obvious, hardly requiring any guesswork.","Slave Market. The slave broker holding a pole with a flag for buying and selling servants looked at the young woman approaching, accompanied by a child and an older person, with surprise in his eyes.","What is someone so young doing here?","Song Jinzhao glanced at the flag and stepped forward to ask, \"Are you Broker Zhao? I was referred here by the Jinyun Agency.\"","The broker raised an eyebrow, lowering his arms which were crossed over his chest. \"Miss, are you looking to buy or sell servants?\"","The Slave Market and agencies often had business dealings. Typically, when a newly relocated wealthy family bought a house and then wanted to purchase servants, the agency would refer them to a familiar broker, taking a small commission afterward.","Song Jinzhao said, \"I want to buy two servants, one man and one woman, adults who can work.\"","With the shops about to open, between hiring workers and buying bonded servants, Song Jinzhao chose to buy servants. Having their life indentures in hand gave her more peace of mind.","The broker gathered up his flag pole and gestured ahead. \"This way, Miss.\"","Inside a simple building facing the street, the courtyard was filled with people of various ages sitting or squatting.","They were sallow and thin, their expressions timid, bodies curled together. Apart from their clothes being relatively neat, they were almost indistinguishable from beggars.","As the broker led Song Jinzhao inside, the servants waiting to be sold looked up to steal glances at her, trying to discern if the newcomer looked kind, if she had money, if she could support them.","The broker summoned the able-bodied male and female servants of prime working age to stand in a row before Song Jinzhao.","\"Take your time and have a good look, miss. These are all skilled workers, ready to be useful the moment you buy them.\"","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept over the faces of the eight people. \"Stretch out your hands, palms up.\"","The eight of them presented their open palms before Song Jinzhao.","The woman had broad knuckles and very short-trimmed nails, with scars from frostbite on the back of her hands. Though without hair ornaments, her hair was neatly coiled. She had likely done rough work in a wealthy household.","The man's skin was chapped and extremely rough, his fingernails caked with dirt—clearly a farmer who had toiled in the fields for years.","There were also two with relatively fair skin and no calluses on their hands, probably maidservants who did delicate work.","Song Jinzhao looked at the slave broker. \"Show me their deeds of sale.\"","The broker immediately pulled a stack of deeds from his bosom, extracting the top eight and handing them to Song Jinzhao.","\"These people have clean backgrounds, absolutely no issues with their origins.\"","After reading the deeds, Song Jinzhao pointed to one man and one woman. \"How much for these two?\"","The man had been sold twice before, had done hard labor and knew how to drive a carriage. The woman was a rough servant from a merchant family, and most importantly, she was somewhat literate and knew basic accounting.","The broker glanced at the two Song Jinzhao had chosen. \"The man, ten taels. The woman, twenty.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. \"A female servant of her age typically costs around ten taels of silver. You're asking for twenty?\"","That was enough to buy two.","The broker's wrinkles bunched up as he bared his yellowed front teeth.","\"Though her age is a bit off, she can do embroidery and is somewhat literate. Selling at this price is already a loss for me.\"","\"Qian Sanya, new goods have arrived!\" A rough shout came from the front door.","The broker craned his neck to look, quickly waved for his underling to receive them, then turned back to haggle with Song Jinzhao.","\"Skilled slaves in the market are all expensive. Since you picked her out at a glance, you must have seen her value. If you think it's too dear, you can look at the others. These are all only ten taels each.\"","Qian Sanya could tell Song Jinzhao had a discerning eye. Having seen the good ones, she surely wouldn't settle for the inferior.","He opted for a strategic retreat to push the deal.","The underling who had just stepped out ran back in a few steps, looking troubled. \"Third Master, two of the goods aren't right.\"","Qian Sanya raised an eyebrow and said to Song Jinzhao, \"Please wait a moment, miss. I'll be right back.\"","He instructed his underling to attend to Song Jinzhao and hurried outside.","Qian Sanya saw the two people lying in the cage, his eyes widening larger than a bull's.","\"What are you dragging two half-dead invalids here for? I won't take them.\"","The slaver, seeing it was Qian Sanya who came out, improved his attitude considerably.","\"They're already here, and there's nowhere to return them. Just take them, sell them cheap.\"","Qian Sanya raised an eyebrow. \"How cheap? Just the medicine will cost me several taels of silver.\"","The slaver leaned in and whispered, \"The woman, two taels. The man sold himself voluntarily, didn't ask for a single coin, just begged for a chance to live.\"","He bent down, pinched the man's chin, and turned his face. \"Look at these features. Clean him up, let his wounds heal, and send him to the alleyways—guaranteed to fetch a good price.\"","Qian Sanya studied the face carefully for a long moment before asking, \"What's their background?\"","The slaver produced two deeds. \"The woman's a peasant. She was abducted by bandits and lost her virtue. Her husband died, so her in-laws sold her off.\"","\"The man's a beggar. When I found him, he'd been beaten half to death. He sold himself voluntarily to survive. He passed out because I forced three bowls of medicine down him.\"","Seeing the official seals and fingerprints were clear on the deeds, Qian Sanya grimaced. \"Fine, carry them in. I'll find a physician to look at them.\"","Song Jinzhao had been chatting with the man and woman she had her eye on. They spoke directly without flattery, were honest but not dull. Compared to the others, these two seemed the most agreeable.","Song Shixue, standing beside her, noticed the newcomers and looked closely.","She quickly covered Song Anhao's eyes and nudged Song Jinzhao's arm with her own. \"Elder Sister.\"","It was that little beggar with blue eyes.","Song Jinzhao looked up, but her gaze fell on another familiar face.","It was the woman who had been violated by Duanshan Lang at Half-Moon Cliff. Wasn't she handed over to the authorities to be taken back home?","Why was she here, covered in wounds, and sold?","The slaver carried the two to a corner under the eaves, set them down, took the money Qian Sanya handed over, and left.","Qian Sanya walked up to Song Jinzhao and ordered his underling, \"Go find a physician from the alley, the cheapest one. Don't let these two die.\"","\"Have you decided, miss? Still want these two?\"","Song Jinzhao pointed at the unconscious woman in the corner. \"How did she come to be sold?\"","Qian Sanya glanced at Song Jinzhao, surprised she'd ask about a half-dead slave.","\"Sold off by her in-laws. Her husband was killed by bandits trying to save her. She lost her virtue, her in-laws hated her for causing their son's death, and with her own family all dead and no one to back her, she ended up sold.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned. \"Who beat her? Those injuries?\"","Qian Sanya: \"The slaver said when she was sold, they dragged her out of a pigsty. If it weren't for the fact that disfigurement hurts the price, that trouble-attracting face would have been ruined long ago.\"","Song Jinzhao's brows knitted tighter.","Seeing her expression change, Qian Sanya sensed something and asked curiously, \"Do you know her, miss?\"","Song Jinzhao looked expressionlessly at the broker, her tone icy. \"There was a government bounty. I took the notice. I was the one who led the constables up the mountain to wipe out the bandit den that abducted her.\"","Qian Sanya was stunned. Meeting Song Jinzhao's cold, deep gaze made him feel a bit unnerved.","\"Does the miss wish to buy her?\"","Song Jinzhao walked to the corner, crouched down, and checked the woman's pulse. She had fainted from hunger, who knew how many days she hadn't eaten.","There were ligature marks on her neck, and external injuries on her arms from beatings with sticks. Judging by the wounds, one spot had been struck at least a dozen times. They hadn't been treated; beneath the purplish-red skin was congealed blood.","Remembering the woman's frenzied and resolute expression when she stabbed Duanshan Lang dozens of times, Song Jinzhao stood up and said, \"I'll buy those two. Give this one to me.\"","Qian Sanya's mouth opened and closed. \"I bought her for two taels. You should at least give me something, miss. Don't let me take a loss.\"","Song Jinzhao gestured with her chin towards the woman. \"Treating these injuries of hers will cost at least a tael of silver. She's killed someone. Aren't you afraid of trouble if you sell her?\"","The color drained from Qian Sanya's face as if struck by lightning. \"Killed someone?\" The slaver hadn't mentioned that.","No one dared buy a slave who had killed someone. If word got out, his reputation would be ruined!","Song Jinzhao: \"If you don't believe me, send someone to inquire in Haoyue City. The constables at the county yamen all know. Over fifty slashes. The bandit leader who violated her was hacked into a pulp of flesh by her, impossible to gather even by hand, leaving only a head with eyes wide open in death.\"","His throat moved. \"How does the miss know this?\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lip in a seemingly joking, scornful smile. \"I was standing right there at the time. I was the one who handed her the knife.\"","A chill ran down Qian Sanya's back, feeling as if his whole body was suspended over a bottomless cliff.","This girl looked only in her teens. How could she speak of killing not only without fear, but seemingly with relish?"]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: Meet Again, You Saved My Life","paragraphs":["The male beggar who had been lying unconscious in the corner slowly opened his eyes, his pale blue irises glinting under the sunlight.","When he saw Song Shixue, his unfocused gaze paused for a moment.","\"Eyeballs, pretty, Anhao wants.\"","Seeing the colorful, luminous object, Song Anhao's round little eyes shone with delight. His chubby little hands opened, reaching out to touch the man's blue eye.","Song Shixue swiftly grabbed his hand and pulled his arm back.","\"Don't touch. You can't have that.\" It wouldn't be pretty if dug out.","It was only then that Qian Sanya noticed that the freebie he'd taken in, originally for his face, actually had heterochromia, and one eye was blind at that.","A blind man wouldn't fetch a high price in the dark alleys. He'd have to spend money treating his injuries too. What a waste of effort.","A murderer capable of chopping someone into mincemeat, and a blind man with blue eyes. Thinking of the slave trader who had taken the money and left, Qian Sanya cursed the man ten thousand times in his heart.","\"Young lady, two taels of silver. Take both of them.\"","Song Jinzhao frowned and glanced at the man. Blue eyes—either a genetic mutation or foreign blood. \"Let me see their deeds of sale.\"","Qian Sanya was desperate to get rid of the two sickly burdens immediately.","\"The deed is issued by the authorities. It doesn't matter if you drag him back and he dies. He's just a servant who signed a life-and-death contract anyway.\"","Song Jinzhao grabbed the man's arm, checking him over thoroughly. Her brows knitted tightly, a flicker of surprise passing through her eyes.","She had thought he was at least in his twenties, but judging by his pulse, he hadn't even passed sixteen.","Song Jinzhao's voice turned cold. \"How old are you?\"","\"Fourteen.\" The hoarse voice sounded as if his throat was tearing with every word.","Qian Sanya's eyes widened in surprise as he looked the boy up and down.","Only fourteen? Anyone would think he was twenty-four.","Song Jinzhao pried open his mouth. His tonsils were so inflamed they were almost rotten.","His throat seemed to have been irritated by something, the entire area in a state of ulceration.","\"What can you do?\"","The boy struggled to raise his eyelids; his lips moved. \"I've learned a little and can read. I can cook. I can endure beatings. My life is hard. If you buy me, this life will be yours. I'll be your ox and your horse; I'll do anything.\"","Knowing the young man was literate, Qian Sanya's expression immediately brightened with excitement.","\"You can read too! That can't be thrown in for free. That's worth two taels by itself.\"","\"Young lady, I see your younger brother and sister seem quite taken with him. How about this: four taels of silver, and you take both.\"","Song Jinzhao scoffed. \"Limbs all broken, throat rotten down to a shred of skin, and blind in one eye. After spending over ten taels to treat him, he'll still end up crippled. Do you take me for a fool?\"","Qian Sanya paused, then quickly reached out to feel the young man's limbs. They swung limply and unnaturally. They really were broken.","No wonder he was selling himself without asking for money. He was just a cripple.","He'd either starve to death, be beaten to death, or kill himself.","The servant who had been sent out returned with a physician.","Qian Sanya pointed at the young man and said to the physician, \"Check him first. How much would it cost to treat him?\"","After a thorough examination, the physician said, \"All four limbs broken, throat damaged, heart and lungs injured. This person is covered in wounds from head to toe. The treatment is very difficult. Consultation and medicine combined would cost at least twenty taels of silver. In the end, he'll be left permanently disabled, and his throat probably won't work like a normal person's. He'll be very hoarse, practically mute.\"","The youth, his hair a tangled bird's nest, heard the physician's words, and the light in his eyes instantly grew even dimmer.","Song Shixue tugged on Song Jinzhao's finger. The meaning in her eyes was clear to Song Jinzhao without even looking.","Meeting him once, then twice... it really was inescapable.","Thinking that the boy was only fourteen, an age that would still be in middle school in the modern era, Song Jinzhao took a deep breath and quietly waited for the slave trader's reaction.","Hearing that treatment would cost twenty taels and still leave a blind and mute cripple, Qian Sanya's idea of making money off him vanished once more.","He waved his hand in annoyance. \"No treatment. I didn't spend a single coin on him. I won't lose out even if he dies.\"","He then turned back to Song Jinzhao with a full smile: \"The original price still stands. Two taels of silver, take them both.\"","Song Jinzhao pointed to the man and woman she had initially picked: \"Thirty taels is too expensive for my liking. Adding these two would be just right. Otherwise, I'll go to the next shop.\"","\"I only came to you on the recommendation of the Golden Luck Agency. If we can't make a deal, I'll come back after I've finished looking around.\"","Qian Sanya quickly stopped her, his face pained as he cried poverty. \"Thirty-two taels of silver. I'm really not making any profit at all.\"","Song Jinzhao pushed his hand aside. \"Thirty taels exactly. Not a coin more, not a coin less. I'll come to you next time I need to buy people.\"","Thinking of a murderer who could dismember people and a blind, mute cripple, Qian Sanya closed his eyes, gritted his teeth, and said, \"Fine. Thirty it is.\"","When that slave trader comes next time, I'll definitely get those two taels back.","With the slave trader's guarantee, they swiftly went to the magistrate's office to complete the official red-seal contracts. Holding the deeds of sale and documents for all four people, Song Jinzhao took them back.","A storeroom for miscellaneous items was cleaned out. Though small, it was fine for two servants.","As for the two men, Song Jinzhao directly arranged for them to stay in the woodshed.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"I haven't asked your names yet.\"","The man and woman knelt down. \"This humble one is Fushun.\"","\"This humble one is Chunxing. If the young lady dislikes the names, you may bestow new ones.\"","Changing names with each new master was a habit they were long accustomed to.","The young man lowered his gaze. \"I have no name.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. \"Keep your original names. I can't be bothered to think of new ones. As for you...\"","\"Shixue, you were the one who wanted to save him. You give him a name. And you treat these injuries of his.\"","Song Shixue's hand, holding the medicine chest, tightened slightly. \"Leave it to me. Is A-Jie not going to intervene?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in silent confirmation. \"Have more confidence in yourself. This is your first patient.\""]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: Zhang Xialian Awakens at Midnight","paragraphs":["After downing a bowl of thin rice porridge, Zhang Xialian woke up in the middle of the night. Outside the window, it was pitch black, and she couldn't see a thing.","Her body felt clean yet slightly sticky, as if something had been smeared on it.","Had she reached the underworld?","Even in death, her body didn't ache as much as it used to.","Her hand groped to the side, and the sensation of warmth made every muscle in Zhang Xialian's body tense up.","Instinctively, she kicked out.","\"Ah!\" In her sleep, Chunxing first felt a sharp pain in her thigh, followed by a strong sense of weightlessness, then her chest and arms throbbed from the impact.","Hearing a woman's voice, Zhang Xialian looked down at the floor beside the bed in surprise. \"Who are you?\"","There was no moon tonight, and the room was so dark it was impossible to see anything.","Chunxing climbed up from the floor, fumbled to find the fire striker on the table, and lit the candle.","\"You're finally awake.\"","Seeing the woman's face clearly, Zhang Xialian looked utterly bewildered. She glanced around at the unfamiliar surroundings, which didn't look like the place where human traffickers locked up their slaves.","\"Who are you? Where is this?\"","Chunxing stared at the wounds on her neck, recalling the scars she had seen while changing Zhang Xialian's clothes. There wasn't a single patch of good skin on her body; it was as if she had been beaten to death.","\"My name is Chunxing. While you were unconscious, the trafficker sold you to the young mistress. We're in the master's house now.\"","Zhang Xialian lifted her collar and sniffed; it was the scent of medicine.","\"My injuries...?\"","Chunxing: \"The master applied the medicine for you. She seemed to know you.\"","Hearing that the person who bought her knew her, Zhang Xialian's expression changed.","She hugged her knees and shrank into the corner. \"What's the name of the person who bought me? Who is she?\"","Seeing her so frightened, Chunxing quickly tried to reassure her. \"Don't be afraid. The young mistress is very kind. Besides you, she also bought a cripple who was nearly dead.\"","\"Having only been here half a day, I only know the master's family name is Song. The young mistress in charge seems to be only in her teens. There are also two young masters and a young lady in the household, all quite young. It's a simple family, should be easy to serve.\"","Hearing that her buyer's surname was Song and that she was a teenage girl, a flicker of uncertainty appeared in Zhang Xialian's eyes. She ventured tentatively, \"Is her name Song Jinzhao?\"","Chunxing shook her head. \"I'm not too sure about that. Having only been here half a day, we haven't spoken much. She only said she'd assign work tomorrow.\"","\"But she said you had killed someone, and it was she who handed you the knife. It scared the trafficker out of his wits, and he sold you to the master for nothing, as a throw-in.\"","Zhang Xialian's head thudded heavily against the wall. Her pupils contracted sharply, and she seemed dazed for a moment.","Scenes from the bandit den at Half-Moon Cliff replayed in her mind one by one, especially the image of Song Jinzhao handing her the knife, which remained vivid to this day.","Seeing her state, Chunxing waved a hand in front of her face. \"Go to sleep, it's very late.\"","Zhang Xialian leaned against the wall, her eyes open all night. Chunxing woke up several times and was startled each time.","After daybreak, Chunxing got up briskly, dressed, and washed up.","Seeing her get up, Zhang Xialian immediately tried to rise as well.","Chunxing said, \"Your injuries aren't healed yet, I can manage.\"","Zhang Xialian shook her head, enduring the pain all over her body, and together they fetched water. Both stood outside Song Jinzhao's room holding wooden basins.","She desperately wanted to confirm whether the person who bought her was indeed her savior, that peerlessly skilled heroine.","On the other side, the early-rising Fushun was already cleaning the stables.","Even though the masters hadn't assigned tasks yet, as servants, they needed to have initiative. Otherwise, they'd be seen as lazy and might be sold off again.","Song Anhao was the first to wake, opening his eyes and crying out that he was hungry and wanted food.","Song Shixue opened the door to see the two newly bought servants standing outside holding basins.","Unaccustomed to having servants, she seemed a bit awkward. She stepped aside and said, \"Put the basins on the stand.\"","Zhang Xialian stared at Song Jinzhao, who was sitting in front of the bronze mirror combing her hair, as if rooted to the spot, the wooden basin still held in her hands, not put down.","Chunxing nudged her with a hand, her eyes signaling, What are you doing?","Zhang Xialian snapped back to reality and hurriedly put the basin down. It was indeed her.","Song Jinzhao stood up, a slight curve at the corner of her mouth as she met Zhang Xialian's gaze. \"Awake?\"","Zhang Xialian was stunned for a long moment, then suddenly knelt, kowtowing. \"Thank you, young mistress, for saving my life twice.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up the towel drying on the wooden rack and dipped it in the water. \"That day on the mountain, you were quite decisive and ruthless.\"","\"What happened? Couldn't bring yourself to do it when facing the in-laws who beat and sold you?\"","Zhang Xialian lowered her head, her gaze fixed absently on the ground.","\"My husband died saving me. I also have a twelve-year-old son. When the bandits captured me and took me up the mountain, he protected me and was pushed down the slope, hitting his head and injuring his mind. I couldn't fight back.\"","The tip of Song Jinzhao's eyebrow twitched slightly. \"Weren't you afraid they would treat your son poorly?\"","A trace of self-mockery tinged Zhang Xialian's curved lips. \"He's the only male heir for three generations, their only grandson to carry on the family line.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Do you still want to go back?\"","Zhang Xialian shook her head without hesitation. \"Everyone in the village knows I was defiled. They all curse and blame me, thinking I should have killed myself immediately for losing my purity. I don't want to go back. That place has no room for me anymore.\"","When the bandits violated her, she wished she could die immediately. After the failed assassination attempt, she had also thought her worthless life might as well end.","Until Song Jinzhao appeared.","The young girl's valor was like a deity descending to save her from endless darkness, the very image she had desperately longed for in her desire for revenge.","After Song Jinzhao subdued Duan Shanlang, she let her wield the blade against her enemy.","The scene of madness, everything she saw stained with blood, Zhang Xialian remembered it all clearly even now. After waking, she felt killing someone was nothing more than that.","The knot in her heart had been dug out and crushed by her own hands. She no longer wanted to die, even dreaming that one day she could become someone like Song Jinzhao.","Afraid of nothing, with no one daring to bully her, and those who did would have to die.","Song Jinzhao's voice softened. \"Can you bear to leave your son?\"","Zhang Xialian's eyes grew slightly moist. \"My disappearance is what's best for him.\"","\"In that case, stay. From now on, obey my commands, take me as your master. All that belongs to the past has nothing more to do with you. I give you the name Qingshuang. Throw away the old Zhang Xialian completely.\"","Under Song Jinzhao's intensely oppressive gaze, she felt like a trapped beast locked in a cage in her eyes.","And Zhang Xialian willingly submitted.","Her forehead knocked heavily against the ground. She raised her right hand and swore, her eyes like tempered mountain fire from a fierce purgatory, blazing and resolute.","\"Thank you, young mistress, for bestowing the name. Qingshuang vows to serve you unto death, willing to be your ox or horse, and will never betray you.\"","In the main hall, Song Qiming was sitting on a stool eating breakfast, his eyes occasionally darting towards Chunxing and Fushun.","He had once promised that after he became an official, he would hire servants to take care of his elder sister and younger siblings. Now, before he had even passed the provincial exams, his elder sister had already bought servants.","She was always running ahead, forever out of reach.","Song Jinzhao had hired workers to break through the courtyard wall behind the two shops, digging out a small, deep underground cellar for storing ice.","In the woodshed, Song Shixue pursed her lips, her brow furrowed in concentration. Her movements were extremely careful as she meticulously scraped away every bit of rotten flesh.","\"I thought of several names last night. Which do you prefer, Lanxi or Yuebai?\"","The youth lowered his gaze, his eyes resting on Song Shixue's fair fingers as she held the medicine bowl.","\"Lanxi is quite nice.\"","Song Shixue curled the corner of her mouth. \"I think it's a good name too. It suits your blue eyes particularly well.\"","The hand Lanxi had clenched on the bed board tightened instantly, his eyelids trembling slightly as if trying to hide his pale blue irises.","After scraping away the rotten flesh, Song Shixue stared at the wound that resembled a blade cut. Recalling the scene she had witnessed outside the city wall that day, she couldn't help but ask, \"Were the knife wounds on your body also inflicted by those beggars?\"","Lanxi's throat bobbed as he shook his head in reply. \"No. I was cut by bandits I encountered while fleeing.\"","Song Shixue applied the ointment to the wound and covered it with gauze.","\"Your wounds weren't treated and bandaged in time. Once the new flesh grows, the scars will definitely not fade.\"","Lanxi's expression remained calm. \"It's fine if they don't fade. Thank you for your trouble, Second Miss.\"","A spark of excitement unique to someone practicing medicine alone flickered in Song Shixue's eyes. \"You are my first patient. I will definitely cure you, though it might take a bit longer.\"","\"If it were my elder sister, it would be much faster. But she's extremely busy, with many tasks to do every day. I need to heal you quickly so you can help her with the work.\""]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: New Delicacies, Dean Mu","paragraphs":["In the sweltering kitchen, Song Jinzhao was teaching Chunxing and Qingshuang how to make cold skin noodles, cold noodles, and various tea drinks and milk teas.","By the well in the courtyard, Fushun sat on a small stool washing various pig offal. He scrubbed them back and forth with plant ash three times, changing the water over a dozen basins before the intestines were washed thoroughly white.","Just selling cold skin noodles, cold noodles, and drinks wasn't enough. Song Jinzhao also planned to add braised goods to the menu.","The aroma of the braise drifted next door. Ye Liangyu, who was doing weighted training in his courtyard, stopped his movements, looked up, and gazed in the direction the fragrance was coming from.","Yunhe walked to the wall and sniffed. \"Master, it's coming from the Song household. Starting dinner preparations at the beginning of the Shen hour, isn't that a bit too early?\"","Ye Liangyu took a deep breath of the enticing aroma, his mouth beginning to water.","He withdrew his gaze and said, \"Miss Song's food stall is opening in a few days. She's probably testing recipes.\"","Yunhe helped Ye Liangyu sit down in his wheelchair. \"Not just a food stall, it seems she's also planning to open a medical clinic.\"","Ye Liangyu stared at his own straight legs. \"If Song Jinzhao can cure an illness even the imperial physicians couldn't, her opening a clinic is a good thing for the common people.\"","A woman who is well-read, highly skilled in martial arts, knows how to make money, and possesses exceptional medical skill—such women are rare in this world.","It's just a pity she's a woman; otherwise, a mere place like Anyang Prefecture wouldn't be able to contain her talents.","The drifting braising aroma caused the three households living nearby to come out one after another to look. Upon realizing it was from the Song family, they all scratched their heads in agitation.","What dish were they making that smelled so incredibly good, teasing everyone's appetites?","After simmering over a low flame for half a shichen, the fire was stopped to let the food soak and absorb the flavors, ready to be eaten by evening.","Chunxing and Fushun sat in the courtyard, swallowing their saliva.","Both had occasionally eaten dishes rewarded by their masters while working for other families before, but none were as fragrant as this.","Even pig offal could be turned into something exquisite. No wonder the master's family, despite their farming background, could become prosperous so quickly.","Once the eldest young master passes the provincial examination and then the metropolitan examination, the Song family's status will be completely transformed.","After school, Song Qiming went to the neighbor's house as usual for tutoring. Song Jinzhao stopped him and handed him a food box.","\"New snacks made this afternoon. Take them over for Teacher Ye to try.\"","Seeing Song Qiming enter carrying a food box, Ye Liangyu, sitting in his wheelchair, had already guessed seventy to eighty percent of the reason.","\"Teacher, these are new dishes my elder sister made. Thinking you might like them, she cut some for you to try.\"","Ye Liangyu signaled Yunhe to take it, a smile curling at the corner of his mouth. \"The aroma has been drifting all afternoon; finally I get to know what it is.\"","Yunhe opened the food box. Inside was a plate of braised meat and a plate of braised pig offal.","Seeing something that looked like intestines, Ye Liangyu's brow furrowed slightly.","Yunhe also saw the pig offal and was about to remove the other plate when Ye Liangyu stopped him.","\"Go get a pair of chopsticks.\"","Pig offal had never been fit for the tables of wealthy families—too strong a smell, disgusting no matter how prepared.","Pig large intestine was something one never even laid eyes on; it was the place that held waste, eating it was akin to eating waste itself.","Yet when the lid was lifted, Ye Liangyu detected only the rich aroma of braising, with no trace of foul or fishy smell.","The food was a glossy red, neatly sliced and sprinkled with crushed peanuts and cilantro flakes—Ye Liangyu's favorite. He couldn't resist wanting to taste it.","Song Qiming put down his book and placed the compiled booklet of questions on Ye Liangyu's desk.","Then he knelt by the low table himself, pondering over the previous day's homework that had been returned with comments. This was almost his daily routine.","Ye Liangyu first picked up a piece of braised meat. The grain of the meat was distinct, the fat parts crystal clear like amber, the lean parts coated in a beautiful sauce color, giving an immediate impression of exceptional deliciousness.","Rich flavor filled his mouth upon the first bite. His pupils contracted slightly as he chewed. The fatty parts were tender but not mushy, the lean parts fragrant and not dry. An extreme freshness instantly captured his taste buds.","After eating three pieces in a row, he moved his chopsticks towards the pig offal, starting with the large intestine.","He sniffed it first, detecting only the perfect balance of spicy aroma, neither too strong nor too faint, just right.","Chewing it, the first sensation was springiness. After biting through the outer skin, the inside was soft and glutinous. Rich, non-greasy fat exploded on the tip of his tongue, the fragrance filling his entire mouth.","This was a delicacy Ye Liangyu had never tasted before—not smelly, exceptionally delicious, even better than the meat.","Seeing him take several more bites, nearly finishing the large intestine, Yunhe's eyes flashed with surprise.","Ye Liangyu said regretfully, \"What a pity I can't drink alcohol. These would make perfect accompaniments for wine.\"","Song Qiming glanced up, then lowered his head again to concentrate on his thoughts.","The teacher praised it so highly; he should have taken a couple of bites himself before coming.","Another servant boy walked in from outside, cupped his hands, and said, \"Master, Dean Mu of Anyang Academy is outside requesting an audience.\"","Ye Liangyu placed his chopsticks on the dish, used his hands to move his wheelchair out from behind the desk, and said, \"Invite him in.\"","Then he instructed Song Qiming, \"Don't make a sound. Wait until I call you before you come out.\"","Hidden behind the screen, Song Qiming looked up in confusion, only able to vaguely glimpse the situation outside through a crack.","Hadn't the Dean gone traveling to Jiangnan and not returned yet? Why would he come to see the teacher?","Mu Hongyue walked in, swinging the hem of his trousers, a wine pot in his right hand and side dishes in his left.","His gaze swept over Ye Liangyu's legs, pausing for half a second before shifting away.","\"Retiring to your hometown without telling me in advance. If the teachers at the academy hadn't written to inform me, I wouldn't have known you were back,\" Mu Hongyue said with a deliberately light smile.","Ye Liangyu stared at the wine pot in his hand. \"Who in this world is as carefree as you, Dean Mu? Running off to Jiangnan for half a year without returning, quite the dashing life.\"","Seeing him in good spirits, Mu Hongyue secretly breathed a sigh of relief in his chest.","He had feared that after becoming disabled, Ye Liangyu would be crushed. It seemed the situation was much better than he had imagined.","He raised his hands before Ye Liangyu's eyes, lifting the right, then the left.","\"This is 'Dongting Spring Hue' I specially brought back from Jiangnan, and soy sauce beef from Chaoyang Tower. Have Yunhe prepare a couple more dishes, let's have a few drinks.\"","Ye Liangyu's shoulders drooped regretfully. \"I'm abstaining from alcohol now. Staying for a meal is fine, but drinking is out of the question.\"","Mu Hongyue was taken aback for a moment, then handed the wine and side dishes to Yunhe.","\"Store these here. We'll drink them whenever you feel like it. Now that you're back, what are your plans? You can't just stay at home all the time.\"","\"Since you're not an official anymore anyway, the academy is short of teachers with real talent and learning. Could you help me teach the Upper Hall?\"","Behind the screen, Song Qiming's attention was completely captured by the conversation outside.","Teacher Ye and Dean Mu seemed to be on very good terms. Was he going to become a teacher at the academy?","Seeing Ye Liangyu remain silent, Mu Hongyue continued, \"In the entire academy, aside from me, there's no one with your level of erudition. If you could come help me, cultivating a few top-three scholars in the next imperial examination would be effortless.\"","Ye Liangyu couldn't help but laugh. \"Aren't you daydreaming? There are only three in the top tier: Zhuangyuan, Bangyan, Tanhua.\"","\"Anyang Prefecture hasn't produced a top-tier scholar in nearly a hundred years. Even you and I were only second tier.\"","I was seventh in the second tier; you were seventh from the bottom in the second tier. My scholarship is much better than yours; don't go embellishing yourself.","Seeing the smile spread across Ye Liangyu's face, Mu Hongyue happily curved the corners of his own mouth upward.","\"Having traveled extensively across the land these years, who is more learned is not yet certain. If you have the ability, pick a few students from the Upper House, and let's compare their exam results.\"","Ye Liangyu leaned back, joking, \"You're just trying to find a roundabout way to prod me into bringing you students. You're the dean, I'm just a tutor. Thinking of making me work for you? Not a chance.\"","Mu Hongyue: \"So you're just going to idle at home like this? Such a waste, with all that talent in your belly having no outlet.\"","Ye Liangyu turned his head to look at the screen, \"I've recently taken on a new disciple. Let me introduce him to you.\"","\"Qiming, come out and meet your dean.\"","Mu Hongyue's expression became neutral. His attention had been entirely on his friend earlier, so he hadn't noticed anyone behind the screen.","\"Where did you find this disciple? Hiding him away, not wanting me to see? You only call him out now after I've been here for ages.\"","Ye Liangyu stroked his beard, \"Afraid you'd snatch him, didn't want you to see.\"","Upon suddenly hearing Ye Liangyu declare him as his newly accepted disciple, Song Qiming felt both elated and nervous.","He stepped out from behind the screen and bowed with clasped hands towards Mu Hongyue, \"Student Song Qiming pays his respects to Dean Mu.\"","Mu Hongyue's shrewd eyes swept over him up and down. After a few moments, he shifted his gaze back to Ye Liangyu.","\"You certainly don't stand on ceremony, taking advantage of my absence to snatch away this year's top candidate.\"","Ye Liangyu picked up his teacup and took a sip, washing away most of the five-spice flavor in his mouth.","\"You didn't even return for the academy's opening. Presumably, you've seen too many top candidates to care anymore.\"","\"I have a discerning eye. He's a student of your academy regardless, so how can it be called snatching?\"","Mu Hongyue glanced sideways at Song Qiming, \"When did you become his disciple?\"","Song Qiming stole a glance at Ye Liangyu and, receiving an affirmative look, replied in a steady voice, \"It was before the academy entrance examination.\"","Ye Liangyu curled the corner of his mouth in a smile, saying nothing.","Mu Hongyue took a deep breath, his gaze towards Song Qiming now holding a hint of a smile.","This was good too. Having something to do and a goal to strive for meant he wouldn't have to worry about his friend sitting around all day, letting his mind run wild, brooding over his crippled legs.","\"Study well under your teacher. He was seventh in the second tier of the imperial examinations back in his day. You must not fall short of him.\"","Song Qiming nodded firmly, \"This student will spare no effort, striving to live up to the expectations of my teacher and the dean.\"","After scrutinizing the essay written by Song Qiming for a long while, Mu Hongyue said to Ye Liangyu with a smile, \"You've taught him well. He can advance to the Inner House during the end-of-month assessment.\"","Ye Liangyu said proudly, \"I wouldn't have taken him on without some talent.\"","\"The hour is about right. Qiming, you may return home for today. Come again tomorrow.\"","It was nearly mealtime. He intended to keep Mu Hongyue for a small gathering, and Song Qiming's presence would be inconvenient.","Song Qiming bowed in farewell to the two men. The moment he stepped outside, his face broke into a wide grin, and he hurried home with quick steps.","\"Elder Sister, Master Ye has accepted me as his disciple. He is my teacher now.\"","Chunxing and Qingshuang, who were just setting dishes on the table, stopped and turned their heads to look at him in unison, calling out, \"Young Master.\"","Song Qiming self-consciously touched his nose, his steps slowing down and becoming more composed. He gave them a slight nod of acknowledgment.","He had almost forgotten. There were now four more servants in the house, not just Elder Sister and the others.","Song Jinzhao looked at the slightly awkward Song Qiming.","First, he wasn't used to being served, and second, this house was indeed starting to seem a bit small.","Even though the four of them were currently staying in the storeroom and woodshed, and Lanxi was still bedridden.","But with seven people present in the same space at once, a sense of crowding immediately emerged.","\"Master Ye hadn't agreed before, right? Why did he suddenly relent?\" It couldn't possibly be because of those two plates of braised delicacies.","Song Qiming walked up to Song Jinzhao, his mouth stretched in a grin.","\"Our academy's Dean Mu and Master Ye are close friends. Dean Mu returned from Jiangnan and wanted to invite Master Ye to teach at the academy. They even argued over whose students would perform better in exams. Then Master Ye told Dean Mu that I was his newly accepted disciple, saying he had a discerning eye and praised my talent.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows. \"In that case, you should prepare a formal letter requesting to become an apprentice. Tomorrow morning, go next door to present tea to your teacher and take part in the apprenticeship ceremony.\"","Ye Liangyu being close friends with the dean of Anyang Academy made recognizing him as a teacher truly worthwhile.","Next door, Ye Liangyu and Mu Hongyue sat facing each other.","Mu Hongyue gestured with his eyes towards the soy sauce beef on the table, \"Really no wine?\"","From the moment he entered until now, nearly an hour had passed. He could tell that his friend's relaxed happiness wasn't feigned.","If that was the case, why had he even lost interest in drinking wine?","Ye Liangyu instructed Yunhe, \"Go fetch my crutches.\"","He placed both hands on the armrests of his wheelchair and stood up unsteadily. Taking the crutches, he endured the pain and took two steps beside the dining table.","Yunhe followed closely beside him, hands outstretched, ready to support him at any moment.","Mu Hongyue watched with wide eyes as Ye Liangyu's legs, supported on the ground, slid forward. He could see force was being applied.","\"Didn't they say the imperial physician from the palace diagnosed that you would never stand again?\"","\"Has it healed now?\"","Ye Liangyu handed the crutches back to Yunhe, leaning on his arm to sit back down with a bitter smile, \"Still far from it. It will take at least a year to walk like a normal person. No alcohol, can't drink for this period.\"","Mu Hongyue asked in surprise, \"Which miraculous physician treated you? You even overturned the diagnosis of the palace's imperial physician!\"","No wonder he seemed like nothing was wrong—it turned out he could be cured.","Ye Liangyu tilted his head toward the next-door room. \"It's Song Qiming's elder sister, Miss Song, who lives next door.\"","Mu Hongyue was utterly stunned this time. He had heard that Song Qiming's sister was Song Jinzhao, the inventor of the waterwheel. Did she also know medicine?","\"I wondered why you, who had never taken a disciple before, suddenly accepted one. So that's the reason.\"","Ye Liangyu shook his head gently, \"Not only because Song Jinzhao can cure my legs, but also because Qiming truly has talent and is diligent.\"","\"Since my legs won't recover in a short time anyway, I might as well take on a disciple to pass the time. Otherwise, I'd really be idle to death staying home all day, just as you said.\"","Mu Hongyue looked toward the neighboring room and said, \"Now I truly wish to meet this Miss Song.\"","Ye Liangyu picked up his chopsticks to eat the meat, \"You'll meet her sooner or later. When her medical clinic opens one day, you can go see her for treatment.\"","Mu Hongyue put on a stern face and used her chopsticks to block the beef. \"I'm healthy and strong — I don't need a doctor. You always know how to needle me. Don't eat the soy‐sauce beef I bought. Chaoyang Lou hardly ever makes it this good.\"","Ye Liangyu pushed the plate containing the braised meat over, \"Try this. It's even better than Chaoyang Lou's soy sauce beef.\"","Mu Hongyue frowned, \"Why is there so little?\"","Ye Liangyu: \"If you hadn't suddenly come over, even this little bit wouldn't be left.\"","With one bite of the braised meat, Mu Hongyue's eyes lit up.","He eagerly picked up another piece. The more he ate, the better it tasted, and the plate was empty in no time."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: Formal Apprenticeship Ceremony and New Store Opening","paragraphs":["Seeing another dish on the table, Mu Hongyue immediately reached his chopsticks over.","Ye Liangyu swiftly blocked him, \"This is pig offal. You don't mind?\"","Mu Hongyue picked up the last piece of braised pork large intestine. \"I saw you enjoying it quite thoroughly.\"","The expression on his face upon tasting it was subtle; he had never tried it before. The soft, glutinous texture in his mouth left him craving more, but when he went to pick up another piece, there was none left in the dish.","\"Where did you buy this? Has a new shop opened in Anyang Prefecture?\"","A young servant approached carrying a plate of braised chicken wings and pig's ears.","Ye Liangyu looked up, \"Did Qiming send these over?\"","The servant's lips curled into a smile, \"Yes. Young Master Song said there's more, and he's gone to fetch it.\"","As soon as the words were spoken, Song Qiming walked over carrying two plates of braised chicken feet and a cold salad.","Setting the plates on the table, he said with a smile to Ye Liangyu, \"My elder sister knew you were inviting Dean Mu to stay for dinner, Teacher, and specifically asked me to bring a few dishes over. She said they'll be available in the shop in a few days and wanted you and the Dean to try them first.\"","After speaking, he smiled at Mu Hongyue.","Ye Liangyu shot his friend a smug glance, his mouth watering rapidly as he stared at the dishes on the table.","\"Your sister is very thoughtful. This braised food is exceptionally delicious. When the shop opens in a few days, I'll definitely have Yunhe buy plenty.\"","Song Qiming had already tasted the braised dishes and had to admit they were truly stunning; once you started eating, you couldn't stop.","\"I'm glad you like it, Teacher. If you ever wish to eat it in the future, just let your student know, and I'll set some aside for you first.\"","Watching Song Qiming's retreating figure, Mu Hongyue tightened his grip on his chopsticks. \"You really hit the jackpot with this disciple—a student, a divine physician, and a cook all in one. Why does such good fortune never fall on my head?\"","Ye Liangyu picked up a chicken wing; its tenderness was just right.","\"In any case, Miss Song's shop will open in a couple of days. If you want to eat it, you can go buy it yourself.\"","Mu Hongyue said to Yunhe, \"Go fetch the 'Dongting Spring Hue' wine for me. Such dishes demand wine.\"","Yunhe looked towards his own master.","Ye Liangyu glared, \"I said you can't drink.\"","Mu Hongyue raised an eyebrow, \"You can watch me drink. I'll save one flask for you.\"","Ye Liangyu helplessly pursed his lips and shook his head. Seeing this, Yunhe went to fetch the wine flask and cups.","That evening, Song Jinzhao sat on the bed counting money.","The house they currently lived in was rented. To buy a two-courtyard house nearby would cost roughly three to four hundred taels of silver.","A two-courtyard house would be just enough to live in. If they needed to buy servants later and wanted to live more spaciously, they would need at least a three-courtyard house.","She still had a thousand taels on hand. The money was sufficient, but if she bought a house, there wouldn't be much working capital left.","Thinking of the housing prices in Anyang Prefecture, Song Jinzhao pondered for a moment and decided to first get the shop running and earn some silver.","With servants at home, Song Jinzhao no longer had to lift a finger for the three daily meals or household chores.","Chunxing and Qingshuang could take care of Song Anhao, freeing up Song Shixue's time.","Early the next morning, Song Qiming first delivered the formal apprenticeship letter to the neighbor next door. The apprenticeship ceremony was scheduled for the academy's rest day three days later.","At the hour of Si, sandalwood incense burned on the altar table in the main hall.","Song Qiming, dressed in a white scholar's robe, knelt respectfully before Ye Liangyu. Holding a teacup with both hands raised above his eyebrows, his tone was firm and powerful: \"Teacher, please accept this tea.\"","Ye Liangyu sat upright in his chair, lightly tapping the table with his fingertips.","Gazing at Song Qiming's refined features, he couldn't help but recall the scene of his own apprenticeship many years ago.","Nearing fifty, he could now understand the feelings his own teacher must have had when accepting him as a disciple.","Ye Liangyu said, \"I observe that your nature is sincere, steadfast, and resolute. You show considerable talent for scholarly pursuits, and you are diligent, tireless, and unashamed to ask questions.\"","\"Today, I drink this cup of apprenticeship tea and accept you as my disciple. Remember these three sentences from your teacher.\"","\"A gentleman devotes himself to the fundamentals. Once the fundamentals are established, the proper way will manifest.\"","\"On the path of study and imperial examinations, you must achieve broad learning, thorough inquiry, careful reflection, clear discrimination, and earnest practice.\"","\"If one day you pass the highest examinations and enter court as an official, you must be someone who 'cultivates personal virtue in solitude and benefits all under heaven when achieving success'.\"","Song Qiming's eyes lowered slightly as he raised the teacup high. \"This student will respectfully remember Teacher's instructions.\"","The slightly scalding tea rolled down his throat, warming his heart. Ye Liangyu's heart settled, his chest feeling as if burdened with a certain shackle, heavy and weighty.","Sitting on a chair, Song Jinzhao watched with eyes full of gratification. The apprenticeship ceremony of ancient scholars truly gave one the illusion that a teacher for a day is a father for life.","Once a master is acknowledged, it's for a lifetime; once a disciple is accepted, they must be supported. No matter how far they grow in the future, the shadow of the teacher remains. This feeling touched her heart.","Thinking that Song Qiming might one day hold a high official position, some other ideas arose in Song Jinzhao's mind.","Perhaps cultivating a few hidden guards for fun wouldn't be a bad idea either.","The two shops opened together. Just looking at the storefronts, one could tell the owner was the same.","Song Family Delicacies. Song Family Medical Clinic.","Red silk ribbons fluttered at the entrance. Chunxing, Qingshuang, and Fushun stood at the door in uniform, welcoming customers.","Under the eaves stood a promotional sign announcing the new store opening with a storewide 30% discount.","The exterior walls of the shops were covered with product illustrations hand-drawn and colored by Song Jinzhao. The vibrant colors combined together made it clear at a glance what was being sold.","Cold skin noodles, cold noodles, braised delicacies, and drinks each had their own designated areas and service windows inside the shop, arranged in a square formation.","Three rows of tables and chairs were placed in the middle, just like a food court in a tourist area.","Seeing the iced drinks that were a full ten copper coins cheaper than those at Sweet Snow Pavilion, some people were already pulling out money, wanting to know which shop's tasted better.","Chunxing guarded the tasting table, beckoning the curious commoners one by one and handing them bamboo skewers.","Song Shixue looked at the bustling delicacies shop and then at the deserted medical clinic, suggesting, \"Elder Sister, should we go over and help?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head, \"The three of them are enough. Cold skin and cold noodles are no longer novelties in Anyang Prefecture. At most, there will be more people buying the braised food.\"","When Li Zien arrived with his servant, he saw one shop packed with people.","Some were even standing, creating a noisy, bustling crowd, while the other shop had no customers.","The stark contrast between left and right was such that if not for the shared 'Song' character on both signs, passersby would likely shake their heads and make some disparaging remarks.","The servant pointed at the illustrations on the wall, \"Young Master, each of their items is ten copper coins cheaper than ours.\"","Li Zien's fan swished noisily in his hand.","\"Song Jinzhao just loves playing the game of small profits but quick turnover. In Xining City, a cup of iced dark plum and rock sugar tea only cost twenty copper coins. Now it's doubled, which is already quite a lot.\"","Noticing the colorful, richly varied illustrations of braised delicacies on the wall, Li Zien stepped towards the Song Family Delicacies shop.","Who would have thought that after entering, the window selling braised food would have the most people, so crowded he couldn't even squeeze in.","The servant was jostled from front and back like a pancake, the decorative item he had prepared as a gift almost getting crushed. He should have left it in the carriage.","His voice strained from his throat, \"Young Master, why don't you sit down first? I'll queue here.\"","Li Zien looked towards the area with tables and chairs; there wasn't a single seat available.","\"I'll wait for you in the carriage. Buy a bit of everything. I want to taste just what this braised food flavor is all about.\"","Even when Sweet Snow Pavilion opened, business wasn't this good.","Li Zien waited a full half-hour in the carriage before his servant came running over with several oil-paper packages. The silk knot wrapping the decorative item in his arms had been completely loosened by the crowding.","\"Young Master, I got everything. Try it quickly.\"","The servant eagerly unwrapped the oil-paper package, the aroma at his nose growing richer, his throat involuntarily bobbing.","Without chopsticks, Li Zien could only use a bamboo skewer meant for sampling to pick at the food.","The moment it entered his mouth, his expression changed.","After tasting every variety, Li Zien put down the skewer, his gaze distant as he gritted his teeth and pursed his lips.","\"How does Song Jinzhao have so many new recipes in her head, and every single one is this delicious?\"","The servant discreetly wiped the sweat from his temple and retied the silk cloth to wrap the package again.","\"Young Master, perhaps we should deliver the gifts first?\"","Even though he hadn't tasted the food, the shop's packed scene, the enticing scent in the air, and his young master's dejected, listless appearance told him the man had suffered another blow.","Li Zien straightened his open outer garment, picked up the skewer, and continued eating as he spoke. \"First, go buy me a cup of iced dark plum and rock sugar tea. We'll go after I finish eating.\"","The servant placed the ornaments flat in the carriage and turned to squeeze back into the shop.","Fortunately, the line for drinks wasn't as long as the one for the braised delicacies; this time he only waited a quarter of an hour before making the purchase.","Once satiated and refreshed, using the plum tea to rinse his mouth, Li Zien, accompanied by his servant and carrying two wealth-attracting ornaments, headed towards the clinic.","Song Shixue, who had been coaxing her younger brother, immediately stood up and greeted the customers warmly upon their entry. Recognizing Li Zien, her smile faded.","\"Are you two here to see the doctor or to fetch medicine?\"","Li Zien snapped his folding fan shut and turned his face towards Song Jinzhao, who was sitting on a chair to the side. \"Neither. I'm looking for your sister.\"","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes at him. Li Tianchong hadn't disciplined his son after last time? Why was he here again?","\"What business does Young Master Li have?\"","The servant behind him promptly stepped forward, placed the ornaments on the table, untied the silk knots, and then retreated behind Li Zien.","One was a white jade Pixiu, the other a bronze three-legged money toad—both ornaments suitable for display in a shop, symbolizing the attraction of wealth and treasure.","\"My father learned of Miss Song's shop opening and specifically sent me to deliver gifts, wishing Miss Song prosperous business and a steady flow of wealth.\"","\"My previous inquiry about Miss Song's marital prospects was purely out of curiosity. If I spoke out of turn, I ask for Miss Song's generous forgiveness.\"","Song Jinzhao didn't even intend to have Song Shixue pour a cup of tea. She crossed her legs and spoke leisurely.","\"Young Master Li, as a man, discussing a woman's marriage prospects without cause is quite frivolous. You must remember not to do such things in the future. Otherwise, if you encounter someone with a short temper, it wouldn't be worth getting a sack thrown over your head and a beating halfway down the road.\"","Li Zien averted his gaze, his eyes blinking rapidly and unfocused a couple of times before he changed the subject.","\"Miss Song's braised delicacies are delicious. I wonder if you're interested in opening branch stores. If capital is insufficient, you could form a partnership with my Li family.\"","Song Jinzhao puffed her cheek. Sharp eyes, targeting it on the very first day of opening.","\"The new shop has just opened; I have no such intentions for the time being. If I do later, I presume my funds will be sufficient by then.\"","Not only did Li Zien not leave, he even took a seat on the chair opposite Song Jinzhao.","He said in a low voice, \"I presume Miss Song is not yet aware that the current Second Prince, His Highness Prince Ying, is my brother-in-law.\"","\"As long as we partner, in the future, when your younger brother enters officialdom, with Prince Ying backing him from behind, he is sure to rise rapidly and soar to great heights.\"","Song Jinzhao couldn't help rolling her eyes towards the ceiling. The first stroke of the character isn't even written, yet he's already drawing a grand pie.","He probably says this to every scholar who tops the prefectural exam, doesn't he!","If that were really the case, wouldn't word get out and jeopardize this Prince Ying's very position as a prince?","The Emperor of Dongzhao didn't seem old enough yet to tolerate his princes openly forming factions and engaging in cronyism.","\"My brother-in-law is still far from even passing the provincial exam, let alone daring to hope for Prince Ying's favor. Young Master Li would be better off seeking someone else.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao remain unmoved by such a great temptation, Li Zien felt, on one hand, that she was short-sighted and foolish; on the other hand, he felt she was too arrogant, not even placing the imperial relatives in her eyes.","A chestful of stifled anger pressed down. At that moment, he very much wanted to throw his fan and leave, but remembering his father's words, he could only swallow it down hard.","\"Since Miss Song is unwilling, I won't insist. The Li family's door is always open for you. Should you encounter difficulties in the future, you may seek assistance at any time.\"","Song Jinzhao uncrossed her legs and stood up to see the guest out. \"You are too kind, Young Master Li. The troubles a minor figure like me might encounter can be resolved by the local magistrate's office. There's no need to trouble a royal relative like yourself.\"","Li Zien left finally with his heart clogged with resentment.","To think that Song Jinzhao was once merely a peasant girl carrying wild game to their door to sell. Now she actually dared to disregard him so completely.","Ever since his younger sister married into the royal family, even the Prefect of Anyang had to show him some respect, yet Song Jinzhao simply refused to give him face.","Returning home, Li Zien reported the matter to his father.","Li Tianchong put down his cup. \"I told you this girl is different from ordinary women. Neither threats nor flattery are likely to move her.\"","Li Zien said dejectedly, \"Then what do we do now?\" Since they wanted to win over Song Qiming, they couldn't just do nothing.","Li Tianchong pondered. \"At the Flower-Pinning Banquet, Song Qiming offended Yan Baoyi. This man is narrow-minded and intensely jealous. He is also Ding Weiyue's disciple; he probably won't let Song Qiming off easily.\"","\"Tomorrow I will visit Master Yang. When Song Qiming is targeted by Ding Weiyue, Master Yang can then appear and take him as a disciple. Song Qiming will naturally become one of our people.\"","Li Zien's mind whirred for a long moment before he waved, signaling the servants to leave.","He sat beside Li Tianchong and whispered stealthily, \"Father, winning over scholars and waiting for them to become officials would take at least several years. Why don't we just send silver directly to the capital? There are plenty of ready-made sixth or seventh-rank capital officials.\"","Li Tianchong slapped Li Zien on the head, breathing heavily, his eyeballs nearly bulging out of their sockets.","\"Sending silver to the capital is called bribery. Nurturing scholars in the academy is called patronage. They are completely different matters.\"","\"Sending silver to Prince Ying's residence is for the merit of supporting the future dragon. Cultivating our own people is for the future. Directly bribing capital officials—if Prince Ying found out and mistakenly thought we had divided loyalties, not only would your sister's life in the residence become difficult, but His Highness would also cease to trust us.\"","Li Zien was stunned by the blow, the spray of spittle dampening his face.","\"Just talk, Father, why get so angry? It was just a flash of inspiration, I didn't actually do it.\"","Li Tianchong, exasperated at his son's failure to meet expectations, shooed him out. \"By the time you act, it will be too late. You'd better focus on managing the family business properly and not worry about other matters.\"","If he had known earlier, he should have had his wife bear a few more legitimate sons. Now it was too late to have more.","The servant, watching Li Zien being driven out, pretended to see nothing, tilting his head to gaze at a forty-five-degree angle towards the sky."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Your Student Is Being Targeted, A Special Patient","paragraphs":["Yang Yanfeng was reviewing the coursework of the inner college students when they came looking for him.","\"Have me take Song Qiming as a disciple?\" He asked Li Tianchong with a somewhat surprised expression.","Li Tianchong nodded. \"Exactly. I want to win him over, but his elder sister is a bit of a tough nut to crack. We can only start with Song Qiming himself.\"","Yang Yanfeng frowned. \"Song Qiming just entered the academy. The next provincial examination is in two years; he might not pass.\"","Li Tianchong: \"I looked into Song Qiming's background before choosing him. He only started studying at age ten, yet he topped the county-level exam in less than two years. Proper nurturing will surely make him a great talent.\"","With a troubled look, Yang Yanfeng stood up and paced. \"But he's at odds with Yan Baoyi. Taking him as a disciple would not only offend the Yan family but also displease Master Ding.\"","Li Tianchong said solemnly, \"That's precisely why it's easier to win him over. Offering help in times of need is more effective than adding flowers to brocade.\"","\"Brother Yang, when have we ever made a losing deal? Just trust me on this once.\"","Worry lines etched deeply between Yang Yanfeng's brows. Remembering how Li Tianchong's scheming had successfully married his own daughter to the Second Prince, his heart wavered slightly.","\"Tomorrow, I'll ask the outer college instructors to assess Song Qiming's scholarly aptitude. If he truly is a genius as you say, I'll take him as my disciple.\"","The fine wrinkles at the corners of Li Tianchong's eyes almost reached his hairline as he smiled. \"Make sure to offer help only when he's truly desperate and in dire straits. That's when it will be most effective.\"","Yang Yanfeng nodded in agreement. \"I understand your meaning, Brother Li. I will act according to the circumstances.\"","For the first three days after opening, the food shop's business got better each day. Nearly half the households in Anyang Prefecture knew a shop selling braised dishes and tea drinks had opened on Wuyi Street.","The braised dishes made each day sold out before afternoon. They had to make another batch in the afternoon to meet the demand from evening customers.","Mu Hongyue arrived with a small jug of wine to find Ye Liangyu. Seeing the table before him laden with dozens of different braised dishes, a pang of envy stirred in his heart.","\"You told me to visit your shop, but my servant couldn't buy braised pork intestines for three days straight. Turns out they're all here with you.\"","Ye Liangyu signaled to Yunhe to bring another set of bowls and chopsticks. \"That's because the Song Family Food Shop's business is too good. You all go too late.\"","Mu Hongyue chuckled lightly and sat down. \"I heard your student's situation at the academy isn't too good. Are you really not considering becoming a lecturer in the upper college?\"","Ye Liangyu's hand, holding his chopsticks over a piece of meat, paused. He looked up and asked gravely, \"What's wrong with Qiming? He seems fine when he comes by every day.\"","Mu Hongyue tilted his chin up slightly. \"The student who came second in this academy exam is very resentful of him, the top scorer. Student jealousy and rivalry — you know how it is.\"","Ye Liangyu pressed, \"Is the other party well-connected?\"","Mu Hongyue shook his head, extending his little finger to indicate a tiny amount. \"The Yan family are merchants, without much power. If Yan Baoyi has any illusion of superiority, it's just that his family has a bit of money and he found Ding Weiyue to be his teacher. In terms of talent and comprehension, he really can't compare to Song Qiming.\"","The Yan family had placed high hopes on Yan Baoyi since childhood, sending him to the best private tutors in Anyang Prefecture. Even so, he still didn't outscore Song Qiming.","\"Ding Weiyue is an instructor in the inner college. Once Song Qiming passes the monthly exam and enters the inner college, he'll be under Master Ding's jurisdiction.\"","Ye Liangyu frowned. \"Can't you, as the academy head, do something about it?\"","Mu Hongyue rested his elbows on the table, leaning forward. \"As long as they don't act blatantly, I, as the head, can't say much.\"","\"Yan Baoyi is already inciting the outer college students to isolate Song Qiming. He still has Song Gaoli with him for now, but once he reaches the inner college, he'll truly become a lone soul.\"","Seeing Ye Liangyu's expression grow increasingly grim, a faint, almost imperceptible curve lifted the corner of Mu Hongyue's mouth. He picked up his wine cup and drained it in one go.","Having just one student wasn't enough. If such a heaven-sent talent was left unused, wouldn't he be failing as the academy head?","The food shop was bustling with customers, but for the three days since the clinic opened, not a single patient had come through the door.","Song Shixue measured out medicines one by one according to prescriptions patients had gotten elsewhere, sending them off with a smile that held a trace of bitterness.","\"Sister, there are clearly no other clinics around, and plenty of people, so why does no one come to us for treatment!\"","Song Jinzhao, sitting in a chair, was organizing the medical knowledge points she had learned during her schooling in her mind. \"The clinic just opened; it's normal for patients not to trust us yet. Take it slow, don't rush. In the end, it's medical skill that matters.\"","At the newly opened clinic, when patients heard the resident physician was a sixteen-year-old girl, they turned and left without a moment's hesitation.","Thankfully, they had started out by hunting. If they had truly relied on medical practice from the beginning, they'd be drinking the northwest wind.","Song Shixue placed the abacus in front of Song Anhao for him to play with, then walked over and sat down opposite Song Jinzhao.","\"Sister, Lanxi's blinded eye was caused postnatally. I can heal the external injuries and the broken arm and leg bones with some extra time. It's just the eye; I don't know how to proceed.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"You've been treating Lanxi's injuries for several days now. Have you figured out what kind of person he is?\"","Song Shixue propped her chin on her hand, looking up at a forty-five-degree angle as she recalled.","\"He's not afraid of pain. He didn't make a sound when I set his bones.\"","\"A bit cold, often lost in thought. It always feels like he's hiding some sadness in his heart that he can't tell anyone.\"","\"And I've noticed, he doesn't seem to like his own eyes very much. Even though his pale blue pupils are as beautiful as the sky, he often lowers his head, unwilling to let people see them.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. \"You think blue eyes are pretty?\"","Song Shixue nodded without hesitation, touching her own eyes with her hand.","\"Not only do I like them, even Anhao often tries to grab at them. Especially when sunlight shines on his eyes, they sparkle like gemstones.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the medical notes written on the table; the ink was half-dry.","\"Lanxi's eye lost sight due to blood stagnation blocking the channels after a head impact, leading to monocular blindness. It could have been cured originally, but he delayed treatment for months without medicine. To cure it now requires internal herbal prescriptions and external acupuncture therapy.\"","Song Shixue shrank back, her tone carrying a hint of defeat. \"My needle technique isn't at the level where I can work on the brain yet. Could you treat Lanxi's eye, Sister?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"There's a first time for everything. First, you formulate the prescription to dispel the blood stagnation. I'll supervise when it's time for the acupuncture.\"","Song Shixue's heart settled immediately. She stood up and went to the counter to start pondering the prescription.","A woman dressed in a light blue short-sleeved, narrow-cut shirt walked in hesitantly from outside. Meeting Song Shixue's gaze, her shoulders drew back slightly.","Seeing someone enter, Song Shixue's eyes lit up and she immediately greeted, \"Are you here for a consultation or to fill a prescription, miss?\"","The woman stole a glance towards the consultation desk. Seeing the person sitting there was indeed a young woman, she cautiously approached the counter and asked in a low voice, \"Your resident physician is a female doctor?\"","Hearing this, Song Jinzhao stopped writing and turned to look at the woman.","Song Shixue nodded in response. \"Yes, both my sister and I are female physicians. Is the young lady here for a consultation?\"","Qiu Ye glanced behind her to ensure no one was paying attention before approaching Song Jinzhao. \"It's not me, it's my friend. She couldn't come today. Is the physician available every day?\"","Song Jinzhao gestured for her to sit and picked up the patient record book beside her. \"I am here for consultations after the hour of Si and before the hour of Wu in the morning, and after the hour of Wei and before the hour of You in the afternoon.\"","\"What seems to be troubling your friend?\"","Qiu Ye lowered her voice to a whisper only the two of them could hear. \"Her monthly courses are irregular. They used to come once a month, but five months ago they started coming every month and a half. Last month, they didn't come at all.\"","She quickly added, \"My friend is unmarried, she is... a maiden.\"","Song Jinzhao's hand paused for a moment. \"How old is your friend?\"","Qiu Ye: \"Sixteen.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed further, \"Are there any other symptoms?\"","\"For instance, has she been feeling anxious lately, sleeping less, often waking startled in the middle of the night?\"","\"Has there been any noticeable change in her figure? How is her hair loss?\"","Qiu Ye's breath hitched, her fingertips trembling.","\"She has indeed been losing more hair than usual. When her courses were regular, she would sleep for four ke a day, but now she wakes after just two. She doesn't feel tired during the day. Her figure seems a bit fuller, but her appetite hasn't changed; she doesn't eat more than before.\"","She didn't look like someone who couldn't afford treatment. How could she have delayed for so long?","\"Has she not seen any other physicians in the past six months?\"","Qiu Ye shook her head. \"Matters concerning the monthly courses are not something to be known by outsiders.\"","Song Jinzhao set down her brush. \"The patient needs to come in person. I need to examine her and check her pulse to determine the cause.\"","Qiu Ye nodded. \"Tomorrow during the hour of Si. Please do not receive other patients then. I will bring my friend.\"","Song Jinzhao noticed the faint calluses on her fingertips and nodded, gesturing behind her. \"There is a separate examination room inside. You may bring your friend directly.\"","Qiu Ye craned her neck to look inside. Seeing the room offered reasonable privacy, she felt slightly reassured.","After leaving the clinic, Qiu Ye went to a pastry shop, bought a box of sweets, and returned to the Guo residence as if nothing was amiss.","The young lady, who had been waiting anxiously all morning, immediately pulled her personal maid into the inner chamber as soon as she returned.","\"Well? Is she a female physician? Did you find out her background?\"","Qiu Ye set down the pastries and spoke softly, \"Rest assured, miss, she is a female physician. There's also a younger apprentice in the clinic; the two look like sisters.\"","\"I've made inquiries. The Song family who opened the clinic moved to Anyang just a few months ago because their younger brother was taking the academy entrance examination. After he enrolled in the Anyang Academy, the whole family relocated from their hometown. They have no relatives here in Anyang Prefecture.\"","\"Most importantly, the clinic has only been open for a few days and doesn't have many patients. The Madam would never notice such a place.\"","Guo Yiyao bit her lip, troubled. \"It's just that we don't know how skilled this female physician is, or if she can cure my illness quickly.\"","Qiu Ye quickly comforted her, \"Don't worry, miss. When I told the physician about your condition, she seemed to already have an idea. We'll go see her tomorrow.\"","\"There are still three months until the wedding. There's definitely enough time.\"","The next day at the hour of Si, two women wearing long veiled hats entered the Song Family Clinic.","Qiu Ye lifted her veil and nodded to Song Jinzhao. Only after entering the inner room did they remove their hats.","Judging by their attire, they didn't look like friends, but more like mistress and maid.","Song Jinzhao gestured. \"Please sit and extend your hand.\"","Qiu Ye moved a stool and wiped it with a handkerchief before Guo Yiyao sat down.","Song Jinzhao noted this but didn't ask, placing her fingers on the woman's pulse.","\"Did you used to have abdominal pain two days before your courses? And has that pain stopped since they became irregular?\"","Guo Yiyao seemed struck by a chord. The corners of her mouth lifted briefly before her eyes fell again.","\"Yes. If it weren't for the fear of infertility, I'd almost prefer not to treat it.\"","\"Please stick out your tongue.\"","Song Jinzhao leaned closer to examine Guo Yiyao's face and neck.","Under her makeup, faint red spots were visible. The acne on her neck and the back of her neck was more pronounced, and her neck had a slight darkening.","\"Did these acne breakouts only start appearing in the last six months? Would it be possible for me to see your back and chest?\"","Guo Yiyao looked at her maid. Qiu Ye immediately went outside to stand guard.","Song Jinzhao glanced at her chest and back after she loosened her collar.","Guo Yiyao: \"There are some on my chest and back, but fewer. On my back, one or two keep appearing, healing and then popping up elsewhere. My appetite is normal. Apart from the irregular courses, everything else seems fine.\"","Song Jinzhao parted her hair to examine her scalp, finding slight scabbing at the back.","\"Do you have a particular fondness for sweet foods in your daily diet?\"","Guo Yiyao pursed her lips and nodded, gesturing slightly. \"Not that much, just two plates of pastries a day.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"How has your mood been lately?\"","Guo Yiyao lowered her eyes, twisting her handkerchief tightly. \"Not very good. I lack energy, have no interest in anything, feel a bit anxious and irritable.\"","Irregular menstruation, metabolic issues, signs of high androgen levels... it was basically diagnosable as polycystic ovary syndrome.","\"It's not a serious problem. I'll prescribe some medicine for you. Take it on time, avoid raw, cold, and cooling foods during this period, and don't eat sweets.\"","\"Engage in moderate exercise every morning. Keep your spirits up, don't suppress your feelings. The more you hold it in, the more depressed you'll become.\"","Guo Yiyao pressed, \"Physician, roughly how long until I'm cured? When will my courses return to normal? Will it affect my fertility?\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together, trying to accept that a sixteen-year-old girl marrying and bearing children was normal in this era.","\"Your friend said you are unmarried. Are you in a hurry to have children?\"","Guo Yiyao stiffened slightly, avoiding Song Jinzhao's gaze. \"I am to be married in a few months.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"Your condition requires careful regulation. If you take the medicine on time for two to three months, the menstrual irregularities and acne should show significant improvement. After that, pay attention to your diet to prevent a relapse.\"","\"You may engage in marital relations once your courses have been regular for six months, but it's best not to conceive before then.\"","At the mention of \"marital relations,\" Guo Yiyao's face flushed slightly.","She replied in a low voice, \"I understand. Please keep today's matter confidential. Could you also prescribe a separate formula for loss of appetite and stomach discomfort? If anyone comes asking, please say that's why I came for a consultation.\"","Seeing her cautious demeanor and considering the potential intrigues within a wealthy household's inner quarters, Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement. \"A physician keeps their patients' conditions confidential. You may rest assured.\""]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Food Incompatibility: Entering the Inner Chamber","paragraphs":["At the entrance of the Guo residence, as they returned, Guo Yiyao and Qiu Ye had already removed their veiled hats. The medicine packages in their hands were concealed by the hats, so no one could tell they were hiding anything.","The moment her right foot stepped into the courtyard, a maid waiting at the door of her room hurried forward, her face etched with worry. \"Miss, the matron from the Madam's courtyard came by a quarter of an hour ago. She knew you were out and said you must go to the main courtyard immediately upon your return.\"","Guo Yiyao's heart leapt into her throat, her breath catching for a moment. She returned to her room first to straighten her dress and adjust her makeup before heading to the main courtyard with Qiu Ye.","The woman sitting on the daybed had slightly upturned phoenix eyes, a gentle smile playing on her lips.","Guo Yiyao curtsied, greeting respectfully, \"Mother.\"","A flicker of displeasure crossed Liu Fufeng's face. \"You went out today?\"","Guo Yiyao lowered her chin, adopting a meek and submissive demeanor. \"Yes. I heard a new delicacy shop opened on Wuyi Street, famous for its delicious braised dishes. I thought to buy some for Father and Mother to try first. But the shop was so crowded there was barely room to stand, so I had no choice but to return.\"","The warmth in Liu Fufeng's eyes gradually chilled. \"The wedding is in three months. You should stay home during this time to properly prepare. Leave such trivial matters to the servants in the future.\"","Guo Yiyao clenched her fist inside her sleeve, but on the surface, she nodded obediently in agreement.","After she left, the matron beside Liu Fufeng showed a look of disdain. \"The eldest young miss is deep and cunning, always finding new ways to curry favor with the Master. Just some common street food, yet she goes to buy it herself? She's clearly planning to present it to the Master to claim credit.\"","Liu Fufeng's face was cold. \"She has always been calculating. Otherwise, why would the Master remain so firm about the Meng family marriage?\"","The matron lowered her voice. \"If Madam cannot persuade the Master, perhaps we can approach this marriage from the Meng family's side.\"","\"The Meng family has had only one male heir for three generations, they treat the continuation of the family line as paramount. If the eldest young miss were to be... infertile, the Old Madam Meng would certainly not agree to the marriage. Then, Madam could rightfully replace the candidate with the second young miss.\"","Liu Fufeng's eyebrows, sharp as swords, furrowed. After a moment's thought, she raised her head and motioned for the matron to come closer.","\"Quietly find a physician. Figure out an undetectable way to tamper with Guo Yiyao's food. Be quick.\"","The matron bowed and retreated. \"This old servant will see to it at once.\"","Song Qiming left the academy and went to the Ye residence.","Since formally taking Song Qiming as his disciple, Ye Liangyu had added another desk to his study.","\"The academy's monthly exam is in three days. How is your preparation?\"","Song Qiming's voice was firm and resolute. \"Do not worry, Teacher. This student will surely advance to the Inner Lodge this time.\"","Ye Liangyu studied Song Qiming and asked, \"Have you encountered any trouble at the academy recently?\"","Thinking of his Outer Lodge classmates who kept their distance, and of Yan Baoyi's repeated provocations, Song Qiming's gaze fell to the desk. He clenched his jaw tightly, then immediately released it.","\"My classmates are somewhat aloof, but the Outer Lodge instructors treat everyone equally and have not given me a hard time. I can handle minor troubles myself.\"","Recalling what his friend had said, Ye Liangyu fell into thoughtful silence for a long moment, looking at Song Qiming as if reaching a decision.","Yang Yanfeng obtained Song Qiming's daily assignments from an Outer Lodge instructor. After reviewing them, he confirmed the young man indeed had the talent of a top scholar.","The Outer Lodge curriculum was relatively simple. Wanting to gauge Song Qiming's true depth, Yang Yanfeng devised a rather difficult essay question on policy and had the Outer Lodge instructor assign it to all students.","After the essays were submitted, Yang Yanfeng read Song Qiming's piece three times. A weak, helpless smile lifted the corner of his mouth as he shook his head with a bitter laugh.","Li Tianchong's eye was as sharp as ever. Among so many students, he had truly managed to pick out a genius.","During the midday meal, Guo Yiyao stared at the crab on the table with suspicion. \"Why is the main courtyard suddenly willing to send crab to me this year?\"","Qiu Ye said with a smile, \"Perhaps it's because the young miss is soon to marry into the Meng family. Considering the Meng family's status and the Master's face, Madam might be trying to show goodwill.\"","\"However, crab is cooling in nature. It would be best if the young miss did not eat it.\"","Physician Song had explicitly warned against consuming raw, cold, or cooling foods. Since returning from the clinic, Guo Yiyao had been especially careful about her diet, not even touching pastries anymore.","\"It would be a waste not to eat what's been sent. I'll reward you with half. Have the rest distributed among the others.\"","\"Thank you, miss.\"","Qiu Ye moved the crab to the side, planning to clear it away after Guo Yiyao finished her meal.","In the afternoon, the kitchen sent a plate of persimmons to Guo Yiyao's desk, along with many fattening sweets.","In the middle of the night, Qiu Ye made several urgent trips to the outhouse in her sleep, seriously suspecting she had eaten too much crab during the day.","The next day at noon, frowning at the returned iced dessert, Guo Yiyao felt uneasy.","She took out the list of foods to avoid, written for her by Song Jinzhao, which included raw, cold, and cooling items. Staring at the dishes on the table, her brow furrowed deeply.","She set down her chopsticks and whispered to Qiu Ye, \"Go quietly to the kitchen and find out who ordered these dishes and pastries to be sent over the last two days. Don't let anyone see you.\"","Qiu Ye first raised an eyebrow, then thought of yesterday's crab and her own multiple bouts of diarrhea during the night.","Her heart sank with a thud, a sense of foreboding washing over her.","Her expression turning serious, she bowed. \"This maid will go and inquire at once.\"","By the afternoon, Qiu Ye hurried back into the room. \"Miss, it was Nanny Lu from the Madam's side who gave the orders. She said the weather is hot, and since the young miss has a sweet tooth, chilled drinks and pastries must not be lacking. Even the fruit must be iced before being sent.\"","The needle she was using to embroider her wedding dress pricked her finger, but Guo Yiyao seemed not to feel the pain.","Master and maid stood frozen in place, one sitting, one standing, for a very long time, until Guo Yiyao used a handkerchief to wipe the blood from her finger.","\"Let's play along. Make them think I ate it.\"","Qiu Ye's eyes reddened. She lowered her head, holding back her emotions. \"Yes.\"","For three consecutive days, Nanny Lu came before Liu Fufeng as if to claim credit. \"Madam, everything is proceeding smoothly with the eldest young miss. The physician said it will take effect in two months.\"","Liu Fufeng nodded with satisfaction, her mind already picturing Guo Yiyao's face, filled with despair, upon hearing the physician's diagnosis once it was done.","At the end of the month, during the academy examinations, Yan Baoyi stared at the rankings posted on the board, his face livid. His fists, hanging at his sides, began to tremble involuntarily, his back teeth clenched so tightly they seemed about to shatter.","Once again, Song Qiming had pressed him down into second place. It was utterly infuriating.","The Outer Lodge classmates gathered around saw his expression and quickly lowered their heads to leave.","When the city gate catches fire, the fish in the moat suffer. They had no desire to be those fish.","Song Gaoli placed a disappointed hand on Song Qiming's shoulder. \"I was so close to entering the Inner Lodge.\"","Out of a hundred students taking the exam, only the top ten could advance. Song Gaoli had placed fifteenth.","Song Qiming patted his back in return. \"Don't worry. There's an exam every month. Keep working hard, and you'll surely make the top ten next month.\"","Song Gali nodded vigorously. \"I will definitely come to the Inner Lodge to find you next month.\"","Yan Baoyi's eyes were fixed like death on Song Qiming and Song Gaoli talking not far away, as if he wanted to devour them.","Song Gaoli felt a chill run down his spine. He turned and met a pair of eyes fiercer than any ghost's.","Turning back, he grabbed Song Qiming's arm forcefully and said, \"Yan Baoyi failed to surpass you in the exam again. Looking at his expression, he seems like he wants to drink your blood and eat your flesh. Once we're in the inner school, with Master Ding backing him, he'll definitely target you even more.\"","Song Qiming's expression remained calm, showing no trace of fear. \"We'll cross that bridge when we come to it. It depends on what they plan to do. I'll counter their moves one by one and won't retreat a single step.\"","On the first day of entering the inner school, Master Ding placed Song Qiming at the very last row near the back door.","During the lesson, out of the ten students who had advanced to the inner school, only Song Qiming was never called upon to answer a question. Master Ding didn't even glance his way once.","The students in the room keenly sensed that Master Ding seemed to hold some dislike for Song Qiming.","This year's top scholar in the county examination, and first place in the inner school entrance exam—shouldn't such a student be a teacher's favorite?","Why did it feel like he was being treated as if he didn't exist?","Su Luobai, sitting in the middle, let his gaze shift between Song Qiming and Master Ding.","Song Qiming had been at the academy for less than a month. Had something unpleasant happened in between?","After class, Su Luobai walked over and sat down beside Song Qiming's desk.","Seeing it was him, Song Qiming's eyes curved, his face showing indescribable trust. \"Brother Luobai.\"","Su Luobai smiled and praised, \"I knew you could do it. You've become my classmate so quickly.\"","\"It went fairly smoothly. The academy is just as you described, Brother Luobai—there are too many talented classmates. If I don't work hard, it would be terrible if I got left behind.\"","Su Luobai lowered his voice slightly and asked, \"Do you have some grievance with Master Ding? His attitude towards you seems a bit off.\"","The smile instantly vanished from Song Qiming's face.","\"I have no grievance with him. Today was even our first meeting. However, Master Ding's disciple, Yan Baoyi, was the second-place candidate in this year's academy examination. He dislikes me. Back in the outer school, apart from Gao Li, almost no one dared to befriend me.\"","Su Luobai recalled the student Master Ding Weiyue had praised twice earlier. He turned to look and happened to meet Yan Baoyi's gaze, which was filled with needle-like contempt.","\"What place did he get in this inner school advancement exam?\"","Song Qiming tilted his head. \"Second place. I got first.\"","Su Luobai swallowed hard, murmuring to himself, \"No wonder.\"","Being constantly overshadowed by someone—a narrow-minded person would surely hold a grudge.","\"He's already become Master Ding's disciple, yet you still surpassed him. That's quite impressive.\"","Song Qiming gestured for Su Luobai to lean his ear closer and whispered, \"Master Ye has taken me as his disciple.\"","Su Luobai's eyes widened in disbelief, staring fixedly at Song Qiming's face. He opened his mouth with difficulty to confirm, \"The formal kind? With the bowing ceremony and offering tea?\"","Song Qiming nodded emphatically. \"It happened just a few days ago. But even before the formal ceremony, my teacher had always looked after me.\"","Su Luobai's eyes went vacant, his thoughts in disarray.","This was a living example of the latecomer surpassing the old-timers, truly the student surpassing the master.","\"How did you win over Master Ye? He doesn't even give face to the other teachers at the academy.\"","Song Qiming raised his right hand, bending his fingers down one by one.","\"Personal connections, plus talent, plus hard work, plus perseverance. Not a single one can be missing.\"","Su Luobai felt thoroughly crushed.","All that worry for nothing. If others knew Song Qiming was Ye Liangyu's disciple, who would dare bully him?","Not rushing over to call him 'big brother' would already count as being restrained.","When Yang Yanfeng entered the lecture hall, he didn't see Song Qiming at first glance. It was only after stepping onto the platform that he noticed Song Qiming sitting at the very back, while Yan Baoyi was in the best seat in the third row.","They couldn't even wait past the first day.","Everyone in the hall noticed that Master Ding never called on Song Qiming once, while Master Yang, on the contrary, praised Song Qiming highly.","The other eight students who had advanced from the outer school sat in their seats, looking down, their eyes shifting. The situation seemed a bit off; they didn't know how things would unfold next.","Would Song Qiming break through successfully, or would he end up like in the outer school—solitary, a lone figure, becoming invisible?","Watching Master Yang praise Song Qiming, Yan Baoyi's brows furrowed tightly, his eyes filled with displeasure. He needed to ask his teacher to have a word with Master Yang.","The unlit backyard could only be illuminated by the moon hanging in the sky.","Qingshuang lay on the ground, her whole body soaked with sweat as if she had just climbed out of water.","Song Jinzhao sat on a chair nearby, legs crossed, her voice emerging from her throat. \"Can't even last an hour?\"","Qingshuang pushed herself up slowly with her hands. Sweat flowed into her eyes, causing a sharp sting and burning sensation in her eyelids.","\"I can hold on. Please continue, Miss.\"","In the woodshed, Fushun, exhausted from a busy day, was already fast asleep, his snores echoing in the room, loud enough to keep others awake.","Lanxi lay by the window, his gaze fixed intently on the two practicing martial arts in the courtyard, his eyes full of envy.","He looked down at his own leg bound in splints and his arm suspended in a sling, took a deep breath, and fell back onto the bed.","His eyes were closed, but his ears remained pricked, listening intently.","Inside the clinic, Song Jinzhao reviewed the account books from the past few days. The food shop's business had now stabilized, with daily profits around twenty taels of silver.","They braised twice a day. The batch made in the morning would sell out before lunch. The batch braised at noon would be cleared out before 5 PM in the afternoon.","It was a bit insufficient to meet demand. They needed to negotiate with suppliers for more raw materials and increase their stock.","With the business stable, they could start considering looking for a house.","\"Doctor! Doctor!\" Urgent shouts came from outside the shop. Song Shixue, who had been reading a medical book handwritten by Song Jinzhao, suddenly looked up.","Seeing a burly man rushing in carrying another man whose head was wrapped in cloth, she quickly put down the book and called out, \"Elder Sister, a patient is here.\"","She hurried out from behind the counter and had the burly man place the injured man on a wheelchair.","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to reach out to unwrap the cloth, the burly man stopped her with a puzzled look. \"Are there any other physicians here?\"","Song Shixue's hands, holding a tray, froze instantly.","Song Jinzhao straightened up, staring directly at the burly man. \"We only have female physicians here. Will you accept treatment or not?\"","The burly man's eyes shifted between Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue's faces. They could run a clinic, so they must know how to treat illnesses.","\"Yes, treat him, Doctor. My brother fell from a cart and hit a stone lion by the roadside. He lost consciousness on the spot. The wound kept bleeding profusely, and it hasn't stopped yet.\"","He had already rushed to three other clinics, but the resident physicians weren't there. If he had to find another one, he was truly afraid the man would die on the way.","Song Jinzhao unwrapped the cloth binding the man's head. There was significant blood loss.","While pressing a gauze pad against the man's bleeding wound, she asked, \"When did the impact happen? Did he regain consciousness at any point?\"","The burly man replied, \"Half an hour ago. He woke up once in between, kept crying out in pain, and then lost consciousness again not long after.\""]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: A Succession of Patients Seeking Consultations at Midnight","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao pried open the man's eyelids to check his pupils, then decisively inserted a silver needle into his philtrum acupoint.","The moment the man woke, he felt a sharp pain on his head. He was about to struggle when Song Jinzhao pressed down on his arm.","\"Don't move. How does your head feel now? Still dizzy?\"","Seeing that the person questioning him was a young woman, the man's mind went blank for a second. He answered in a daze, \"A bit dizzy... feels heavy.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her index finger and held it before his eyes. \"Follow this with your gaze. Can you see it clearly?\"","The man: \"Yes.\"","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes and said to Song Shixue, \"Clean the wound for me.\"","She stood up and walked to the shelf to prepare the tools needed for suturing.","Just as Song Shixue finished applying the anesthetic, a woman carrying a little girl on her back rushed in through the door.","The two of them turned to look. When there were no patients, none came; but as soon as one arrived, two came at once.","\"Shixue, go take a look.\"","Song Shixue capped the medicine bottle, placed it on the tray, stood up, and went to meet the woman.","Song Jinzhao, focusing on the wound, said to the man, \"Don't move. This will be over quickly.\"","Under the stunned and fearful gaze of the burly man who had brought the patient, the needle and thread began to weave back and forth through the man's wound.","The man in the wheelchair was so terrified he didn't dare move a muscle; his entire body went stiff.","The wound was numbed with anesthetic, so the pain wasn't intense, but he could clearly feel the friction of the needle piercing and the thread dragging through his skin.","In the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, Song Jinzhao finished suturing the wound. She applied antibacterial ointment and bandaged it with gauze.","\"After you return home, don't let the wound get wet. Once the anesthetic wears off, the injured area will hurt.\"","\"From what I can see now, the brain likely wasn't injured. The dizziness is probably due to a concussion. I'll prescribe two doses of medicine for you first. Come back in seven days to have the stitches removed.\"","\"Avoid alcohol, pungent and spicy foods, and foods that cause inflammation. Rest well at home, and absolutely no strenuous exercise or heavy labor.\"","The burly man and the injured man stared fixedly at Song Jinzhao, who was now sitting on a stool writing out the prescription and instructions. The whole experience felt surreal to them.","Sewing up a wound with a needle... they had never seen a physician treat someone like this before. Yet the wound had indeed stopped bleeding, and it didn't hurt much.","\"Doctor, how much in total?\"","In his earlier panic, he had forgotten to ask about the fee. With such a novel method, it probably wouldn't be cheap, would it?","\"Consultation fee, treatment fee, and medicine cost, one tael of silver in total.\"","The burly man grimaced in heartache. This was almost as expensive as Huiming Hall, the best medical clinic in Anyang Prefecture.","But the treatment was already done, so he could only bear the pain and take out the silver.","Song Jinzhao asked the two men to sit on the chairs and wait for her for a moment.","She walked into the inner room and knocked on the door. \"Shixue, how is it going?\"","Inside the room, Song Shixue was using a towel wrapped around ice to cool the little girl under her armpits.","Hearing Song Jinzhao's call, she handed the towel to the woman. \"Don't apply it continuously. Apply for a while, pause, then apply again.\"","The woman nodded.","Song Shixue opened the door to let Song Jinzhao in.","\"She's had a fever for three days without seeking treatment. Symptoms include coughing, throat inflammation, severe cold, and a very high forehead temperature. We're currently using towels and ice to bring her temperature down.\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to examine the little girl, confirming that Song Shixue's diagnosis was correct. \"You write the prescription.\"","Song Shixue nodded and went out.","Song Jinzhao then walked to the medicine cabinet to prepare the medicine for the man with the head injury.","After Song Shixue wrote the prescription, she handed it to Song Jinzhao for review.","After reading it, Song Jinzhao tapped her finger on the paper. \"Increase forsythia and burdock fruit by one qian each. After three days of taking this, change the prescription.\"","Song Shixue thought for a moment and then understood.","She had considered the patient's young age and reduced the dosage accordingly.","But she had overlooked that a chronic condition dragged into an acute one requires swift and decisive action. A stronger formula is needed first to curb the illness, and then it can be switched to a gentler one once the condition stabilizes.","After seeing off the two patients and their families, it wasn't long before two more patients arrived—one with a stomachache and another with a cold.","After diagnosing, treating, and sending them off with their medicine, Song Shixue stood at the clinic entrance, peering left and right. She muttered, \"Why are there suddenly so many patients today? Could there be more?\"","Since opening, they had only treated that one young lady in the first few days.","Why did several come all of a sudden today? And they didn't turn and leave upon learning the physicians were women.","Song Jinzhao thought of the man with the cracked skull, who had bumped into a stone lion in the city.","Why did it take half an hour for him to get here? With such a long journey, there should have been other clinics nearby.","The commoners who came for treatment in the afternoon gave Song Jinzhao the answer.","\"Most of the physicians in the city have been invited to the Meng and Liao residences for consultations. Only a few apprentices are left minding the clinics. Even Huiming Hall only has Physician Zhao left to see patients, and he's too busy—you have to wait forever.\"","Song Jinzhao asked to confirm, \"Auntie, by Meng and Liao residences, do you mean the residences of the Prefect and the Vice Prefect?\"","The ailing woman nodded, a hint of envy in her eyes. \"Yes. Besides officials, who else could be so extravagant as to invite so many physicians at once? Just the consultation fees are more than we common folk can afford.\"","She continued, shaking her head with a sigh, \"Who knows what illness it is. It's been several hours already, and none of those physicians have returned.\"","Before closing for the day, Song Shixue organized the patient records. Her tone was somewhat dejected as she spoke.","\"Elder Sister, why do you think they didn't invite you for a house call?\"","All those physicians in Anyang Prefecture were invited, yet their Song Family Clinic was overlooked. Did they look down on their medical skills?","Song Jinzhao immediately understood Song Shixue's thoughts. \"We're new here and have no reputation. It's normal they didn't invite us.\"","\"Think of it this way: it's a good thing they didn't invite us. Otherwise, what would we have done with all the patients today?\"","Song Shixue blinked, thinking her elder sister had a point.","The food shop next door had already closed early to go prepare dinner.","As soon as Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue returned home, Song Anhao immediately rushed over, hugged their legs, and began swaying from side to side, cooing.","\"Eldest Sister, Second Sister, why did you come back so late? I missed you so much.\"","The clinic had been too busy today, so Song Jinzhao had asked Chun Xing to bring the child home earlier. They had even returned for lunch, so it had only been a little over two hours since they'd seen him.","With this level of clinginess, one would think she and Shixue hadn't been home for days and nights.","She bent down to pick up Song Anhao, letting him sit on her arm. \"What did you do at home this afternoon? Did you take a nap?\"","Song Anhao wrapped his arms around Song Jinzhao's neck, pressing his chubby cheek against hers.","\"I played clapping games with Lan Xi, and I slept for a long time~\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow and looked at Song Shixue. \"His hand is better?\"","Song Shixue put down her things. \"I'll go check.\" Playing clapping games with his arm in a sling... hopefully the bone hasn't shifted.","When she saw Lan Xi, Song Shixue noticed a fresh scratch on his face. \"What happened to your face?\"","Lan Xi lowered his head. \"I accidentally bumped into the firewood. Got scratched a little.\"","Song Shixue looked at the temporary wooden bed set up in the firewood shed. The space was indeed a bit cramped.","But since he wasn't supposed to get out of bed, how did he bump into the firewood?","Thinking he must have been restless, Song Shixue checked his arm while admonishing him, \"You still can't move around recklessly. Stay put and rest properly to recover from your injury.\"","\"Once you're healed, you can wander around as much as you like. There's no need to rush it now.\"","In the dead of night, while everyone was deep in sleep, the courtyard gate suddenly began to rattle under frantic pounding, the doorframe shaking as if it might shatter inward and crash to the ground the next second.","Fushun opened his eyes and sat up in bed. \"Who's knocking at this hour?\"","The knocking continued. Fushun threw off the thin quilt, opened the door, and walked out.","Lanxi twisted her waist to crawl to the window and peer outside.","\"Who is it?\"","\"I am a servant from the Meng residence, here to request Physician Song to come to the manor for a consultation.\"","Upon hearing this, Fushun drew back the door bolt and opened the gate. \"A house call at this hour? Our eldest young lady is already asleep. Which Meng family?\"","The servant holding a lantern replied, \"The Meng family of the Anyang Prefect. Our elderly mistress is critically ill. We urgently request Physician Song to come with me immediately.\"","Hearing it was the Prefect of Anyang's family, Fushun quickly nodded in agreement. \"Wait a moment, I'll go call our eldest young lady right away.\"","Song Jinzhao opened her bedroom door with a furrowed brow. \"Bring the horse out.\" She had woken at the first sound of knocking.","The storeroom door opened, and Chunxing and Qingshuang walked out.","Song Jinzhao instructed the two, \"Keep an eye on the young master. The second young lady and I are going out.\"","Fushun had already led the horse to the entrance. She wrapped an arm around Song Shixue's waist and flew onto the horse's back in one fluid motion.","The lantern-carrying servant boy wanted to run after them.","Song Jinzhao said, \"No need to follow. I must go to the clinic first to fetch my medicine chest. I will arrive shortly.\"","The sound of hooves was exceptionally clear in the silent night, clip-clopping, creating a sense of urgent tension.","When they arrived at the Meng manor, they realized the servant who came for the doctor had understated the situation.","It turned out the Meng and Liao families had summoned over half of Anyang's physicians, and now it seemed nearly every physician in the entire prefecture was gathered at the Meng residence.","At a glance, the courtyard was filled with bearded physicians well past fifty.","Standing in the yard, each speaking their piece, the chatter was more clamorous than a chicken coop.","As the two sisters entered, many gazes fell upon them.","They had been dismissive of the news that a new clinic in Anyang had a female physician in charge, and one only in her teens.","They hadn't expected the Meng family to summon her in the middle of the night. It seemed they were desperate, willing to try anyone.","Meng Hechuan looked at the five newly summoned physicians, his gaze resting on Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue among them, and gave a slight nod of acknowledgment.","Song Jinzhao responded with a light dip of her chin.","\"My mother began suffering from severe abdominal pain this morning and it has not ceased. I ask all physicians present to prescribe a treatment. If you can cure my mother, my Meng family will surely offer generous thanks.\"","The five newcomers were arranged to enter Elderly Madam Meng's room for examination one by one.","Song Jinzhao was the last to enter. Elderly Madam Meng lay curled up on the bed, her face pale, her hair streaked with white soaked through with sweat.","After taking the pulse, Song Jinzhao had the elderly madam lie flat and began checking the painful area with her hands.","\"Does it hurt here?\"","The elderly madam weakly shook her head.","\"What about here?\"","The elderly madam bit her lip and nodded.","\"The pain has been constant since this morning. Was there any moment when it suddenly lessened, only for the pain to intensify again?\"","The patient closed her eyes, then opened them, looking at Song Jinzhao with a feeble gaze as she shook her head. \"No, it never let up.\"","Song Jinzhao reached out to touch her forehead.","There was a low fever, likely not exceeding 38 degrees Celsius.","Pain in the lower right abdomen, with a fixed tender point. Pressure intensified the pain.","Song Jinzhao looked up and asked the maid, \"Since the abdominal pain began, has the elderly madam experienced any nausea or vomiting?\"","The maid nodded. \"She has vomited twice since this morning, bringing up all her breakfast. She hasn't touched lunch or dinner since.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"Has this happened before?\"","The maid blinked, thinking. \"There was an episode over a year ago, but Physician Liu from Huiming Hall cured it. This time, the same medicine was prescribed, but it had no effect.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and stepped away from the bedside. \"Bring me the prescription to see.\"","It was likely a recurrence of appendicitis, not yet perforated.","Low fever, no abdominal distension, onset only this morning, no sign of abscess formation.","Someone immediately went out and brought back the prescription, along with the dregs of the decoction that had been half-consumed.","After reading the prescription, Song Jinzhao stood still, her gaze fixed on Elderly Madam Meng's pained expression on the bed.","Seeing her remain silent, the woman standing beside Meng Hechuan couldn't help but ask, \"Physician Song, do you have a treatment?\"","Song Jinzhao looked up. This person was likely the wife of Prefect Meng.","\"It's a recurrence of appendicitis. Judging by the current symptoms, it appears to be acute.\"","Seeing the blank looks on the faces of those present, Song Jinzhao pointed to the right abdomen. \"It's an inflammation caused by a blockage or infection in a small organ attached to the end of the intestine.\"","Meng Hechuan frowned, pressing urgently, \"How is it treated? Please, Miss Song, prescribe a remedy immediately to save my mother's life.\"","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept over the Meng family. \"The patient already suffered from appendicitis over a year ago. This is a recurrence. Ordinary decoctions may not be very effective. The best course is to completely eradicate the affected area.\"","Madam Meng, noticing her hesitant expression, immediately added, \"As long as Physician Song can cure my mother-in-law's illness, the cost is no object.\"","Meng Xiaozhe, standing to the side, nodded in agreement.","The three of them stared intently at Song Jinzhao, as if she were their last lifeline.","Song Jinzhao gave a slight shake of her head. \"It's not a matter of silver. To completely cure this illness, the best method is to surgically remove the appendix. Please consider it.\"","The room fell silent instantly, leaving only the faint moans of the delirious Elderly Madam Meng on the bed.","Meng Xiaozhe, standing by his father, was slightly stunned and asked hesitantly, \"When Physician Song says 'remove the appendix,' do you mean cutting open my grandmother's abdomen and cutting out the diseased part?\"","No one in the room initially believed that was what Song Jinzhao meant, but upon reflection, it seemed she did.","Song Jinzhao nodded with a serious expression, using her fingers to indicate a length of about ten centimeters. Her words were clear and firm.","\"Not 'cutting open the abdomen.' It's only making an incision about this long on the right side of the abdomen, removing the appendix, and then suturing the wound with catgut.\"","Madam Meng was the first to cry out, \"That's impossible! How could anyone survive having their belly cut open? I've never heard of such a treatment. The person would likely die the moment the knife goes in!\"","Meng Xiaozhe stared at Song Jinzhao in disbelief. \"Our bodies, hair, and skin are received from our parents; we dare not injure them in the slightest. Otherwise, how could one have a whole corpse after a hundred years? Can't it be treated without cutting out the appendix?\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together. She had known they would think this way.","The patients she had sutured before were all poor, and since there were already existing wounds and no organs needed removal, neither the patients nor their families had objected.","But the Meng family had power and influence, coupled with old-fashioned beliefs, so naturally they wouldn't easily consent to her performing surgery."]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: Disbelieved and My Article Dismissed as Worthless","paragraphs":["\"This is a recurrence of appendicitis. Ordinary decoctions have very limited effect. This is only the first day. If it is not removed promptly, the condition will become increasingly severe.\"","\"The adhesion of the appendix will worsen. By the time surgery is performed then, not only will bleeding be more likely, but the risk of post-operative infection will also greatly increase.\"","Meng Hechuan looked at his mother lying on the bed, her face devoid of color. A day and night of torment had left her utterly haggard.","\"Ask Physician Liu and Physician Gu to come in. For the others who have no solution, give them silver and send them home.\"","The servant, upon receiving the order, immediately left the room to call for the men in the courtyard.","Liu Xuanqing of Huiming Hall and Gu Zhongheng of the Gu Family Clinic were the most skilled physicians in the entire Anyang Prefecture. A year ago, it was Liu Xuanqing who had cured Old Madam Meng's appendicitis.","The physicians in the courtyard, who had been discussing the patient's condition among themselves and were puzzled by Song Jinzhao's prolonged absence, were surprised when the Meng family offered them silver to leave.","Seeing Liu Xuanqing and Gu Zhongheng being led inside by a Meng family servant, the others felt this was only right and proper.","When the two physicians, both over sixty, heard Song Jinzhao's proposed treatment method, Gu Zhongheng immediately voiced his doubts without hesitation.","\"Using a knife to cut open the belly! Young lady, where did you learn your medicine? In all my years of practice, I have never encountered such an outlandish treatment method.\"","\"The person lying on that bed is not livestock. You are toying with a human life!\"","Song Jinzhao's expression darkened, and she frowned, meeting his gaze directly. \"As a physician, I would never toy with a patient's life.\"","\"The world is vast. Just because Physician Gu hasn't seen it doesn't mean it doesn't exist. You are also welcome to present your own treatment plan.\"","Gu Zhongheng was left speechless by Song Jinzhao's retort. He had already prescribed medicine, but it had shown no effect whatsoever; otherwise, the Meng family wouldn't have kept summoning physicians for consultation.","Liu Xuanqing, who hadn't objected immediately, looked at Song Jinzhao and asked, \"If you cut open the lower abdomen with a knife and it bleeds incessantly, what then? Sew it back up?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"The appendix hasn't perforated or formed an abscess yet, so the adhesion shouldn't be too severe. If we are careful, the bleeding won't be excessive. Moreover, I can use silver needles to temporarily stanch the bleeding.\"","Liu Xuanqing asked, \"Will removing the inflamed appendix not affect future digestion and diet?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"The impact won't be significant. If we don't remove it now, and the condition worsens further, she will even lose her life.\"","Liu Xuanqing felt a flush of heat on his neck, his mind reeling from this sudden influx of new knowledge. It was a lot to process.","He pointed to his own right abdomen. \"After cutting out the appendix and sewing it up with thread, the threads on the skin can be removed later. But what about the threads you use to sew the intestine? Do you wait for the intestine to heal, then cut open the abdomen again to remove the threads from the intestine, and sew it up once more?\"","The three members of the Meng family listening in the room shuddered at the thought.","One cut after another... this wasn't a piece of pork. It was utterly chilling.","Song Jinzhao explained, \"For suturing the cecum, we would use catgut that can be absorbed by the body on its own. There's no need to reopen the wound to remove stitches.\"","Seeing the two go back and forth, Gu Zhongheng tugged at Liu Xuanqing's sleeve and questioned him, \"You're not actually considering listening to her nonsense, are you? She's only in her teens. How many patients has she treated!\"","Liu Xuanqing countered in a low voice, \"You and I have practiced medicine for many years. It's not like we haven't encountered cases like Old Madam Meng's current situation.\"","\"This is the second time. The decoction has had no effect at all. Do you have any other methods?\"","Typically, if this dragged on for another two days, the condition would deteriorate, and the patient would die.","Gu Zhongheng gritted his teeth and pointed at Song Jinzhao. \"Do you think her method is effective? What difference is there between this and murder!\"","Song Shixue, standing to the side with her medicine chest, saw Gu Zhongheng pointing at Song Jinzhao and accusing her of murder with a fierce expression, and immediately spoke up in rebuttal.","\"My elder sister's medical skills have never failed. Just because you can't do it doesn't mean my elder sister can't.\"","Seeing such a young girl speak so boldly, Gu Zhongheng felt as if the sky were falling. He could already imagine the chaos these two sisters would stir up in Anyang Prefecture's medical circles in the future.","\"I was practicing medicine before you two young ladies were even born.\"","\"You accuse me of speaking wildly? I say it is you who are spouting nonsense, risking Old Madam Meng's life just to curry favor with the Prefect.\"","Seeing Gu Zhongheng, old enough to be their grandfather, pointing and shouting at the two young girls, Liu Xuanqing quickly intervened.","\"We are discussing medical techniques. Let's just discuss medical techniques. You are old enough to be their grandfather. How can you speak to juniors like that?\"","Gu Zhongheng's face turned ashen. He turned his head away, took a few deep breaths, and then seemed to make an important decision.","He bowed respectfully to Meng Hechuan and said, \"Your Honor, my master lives at the Cold Mountain Temple outside the city. We could invite the venerable master down to examine Old Madam Meng. Perhaps there is still a glimmer of hope.\"","Madam Meng's eyes lit up. \"Hasn't Physician Mu already stopped seeing patients? Can you really persuade him to come down, Physician Gu?\"","Gu Zhongheng straightened his chest, full of confidence. \"If I go to beg my master, he should agree to come down the mountain.\"","Meng Hechuan then said to Song Jinzhao, \"Miss Song, cutting open the body is far too dangerous. My mother is advanced in years. It would be better to choose a safer treatment method.\"","Song Jinzhao wasn't angry either, just nodded calmly and lightly.","\"In that case, I shall take my leave.\"","Meng Hechuan gave a slight nod and a smile, signaling with his eyes for the steward to see her out.","Liu Xuanqing still wanted to ask about the surgical removal of the appendix and immediately moved to leave with Song Jinzhao.","But Meng Hechuan stopped him. \"Physician Liu, Physician Gu is about to go to Cold Mountain Temple. I must ask you to remain in the residence, in case my mother's condition worsens and she cannot hold on until Physician Mu arrives.\"","Liu Xuanqing watched Song Jinzhao's retreating back and reluctantly agreed. He would have to visit her another day.","Meng Hechuan said to Gu Zhongheng, \"Physician Gu, I will have someone escort you to Cold Mountain Temple immediately. Please, you must persuade your master to come down the mountain.\"","\"As long as it can cure Old Madam Meng's illness, this humble one will naturally do his utmost.\"","Gu Zhongheng glanced at Liu Xuanqing, a hint of smugness in his eyes.","On the way back, Song Shixue sat on her horse, leaning her head back to comfort Song Jinzhao.","\"Elder Sister, you are the best physician in the whole world. It's their loss not letting you treat her. Sooner or later, your name will be known far and wide.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled gently and reached out to pinch Song Shixue's cheek.","\"Elder Sister isn't upset. There are so many patients in the world; it's impossible for every single one to seek us out for treatment.\"","Sometimes a physician treating a patient also depends on fate. If the predestined connection isn't there, it's just not meant to be. There's no need to force it.","In modern times, there were plenty of patients trying to get appointments with specialists or pull strings to have experts operate on them.","As long as the other party had better medical skills, in Song Jinzhao's view, this was perfectly normal.","But could Physician Mu, the master Gu Zhongheng mentioned, really cure Old Madam Meng?","Lanxi, who had been keeping alert and hadn't fully fallen asleep, heard the sound of hoofbeats outside and immediately nudged Fushun's thigh with her foot.","\"Wake up! The Eldest Miss and Second Miss are back.\"","Fushun groggily opened his eyes, his gaze still unfocused, but his mouth opened first. \"They're back?\"","Lanxi nodded. \"The hoofbeats just stopped. They'll probably knock on the door any moment.\"","The next instant, knocking sounded. Fushun grabbed his clothes and scrambled out of the woodshed to open the gate.","Song Qiming heard the noise and came out of his room, opening the door. \"Elder Sister, did you cure the Meng family's illness?\"","Chunxing and Qingshuang walked out from another room, their gazes also filled with curiosity.","Being called out for a consultation so late at night must mean it was an emergency.","Song Jinzhao threw the reins to Fushun, while Chunxing stepped forward to take the medicine chest from Song Shixue's shoulder.","\"The condition was somewhat complex. The Meng residence wants to find other physicians to treat Old Madam Meng. They paid the consultation fee and sent us back.\"","Upon hearing this, Song Qiming yawned sleepily, his eyes watering.","\"There are less than three watches until dawn. Elder Sister, you should go to sleep quickly, or you'll be tired at the clinic tomorrow.\"","When morning came, Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue went to the clinic as usual, and Song Qiming left for the academy.","Staring at the essay handed back, covered in harsh criticism, the air around Song Qiming grew heavier. The humility between his brows vanished without a trace, replaced by a coldness in his pupils that carried an imposing severity.","Ding Weiyue walked to the lectern, his gaze settling on Song Qiming, and said in a deep voice, \"I have read all the essays submitted yesterday. Many were well-written, but there were also those that missed the point, were shallow in thought, or impractical.\"","\"Those with more than three corrections on their essays must rewrite and submit a new one to me today. If it fails again, the punishment will be to copy 'Lu Xiangong's Memorials' one hundred times.\"","\"Especially you, Song Qiming. Your essay had the most problems. I truly wonder how you managed to achieve the top scholar rank and first place in the monthly exam.\"","Yan Baoyi, sitting in the third row, curled his lips smugly.","Song Qiming, seated on his stool, let out a soft, derisive snort. He picked up his essay, stood, and faced everyone with a smile. \"Master Ding took the trouble to criticize my essay from beginning to end, leaving not a single gap. That must have been quite laborious.\"","\"I hadn't realized my essay was so poor. Perhaps, Master Ding, you could go ask the examiners who graded the academy entrance exams, or the outer college masters who graded the monthly exams. I, too, would like to know how I managed to earn the top scholar rank and first place.\"","The room fell utterly silent, even the sound of breathing seemed pronounced.","Ding Weiyue's eyebrows shot up, his face dark and fearsome. He hadn't expected Song Qiming to have the audacity to publicly mock him.","\"Even the best can slip up. No matter how talented you are, if you grow arrogant and stop striving, you will regress. In future classes, listen attentively, consult your fellow students more, and be unashamed to ask questions. Only then can you improve and not waste the innate scholarly talent you were born with.\"","Song Qiming's lips curved into a smile.","In just two sentences, the criticism had escalated to his character and attitude, sarcastically implying his achievements were solely due to innate talent, with no effort at all.","Master Ding and his disciple were truly cut from the same cloth, birds of a feather.","\"Rest assured, Master, after class I will take your corrected essay and consult every fellow student and teacher in the academy one by one, seeking their guidance, so I can submit a satisfactory essay.\"","\"After all, I certainly don't want to be punished with copying 'Lu Xiangong's Memorials' one hundred times. Finishing that would probably cripple my hand.\"","Having said this, Song Qiming sat back down with a smile and opened his book, as if nothing had happened.","Su Luobai, sitting on his stool, clenched his teeth, covering his mouth with his hand to stifle his laughter.","One shouldn't provoke the tiger. With an elder sister as formidable as Song Jinzhao, one is influenced by their company. How could Song Qiming possibly swallow insults and bear humiliation?","Zhao Jinmin, full of admiration, lay his head on the desk and turned to stare at Song Qiming sitting behind him.","So tough. His personality was nothing like his gentle appearance.","For the entire class, no one dared to speak, fearful of becoming the venting target for the scowling Master Ding.","After class, in front of Ding Weiyue, Song Qiming picked up his heavily annotated essay, walked to the front row, and with a smile, bowed to consult each student one by one.","After consulting everyone inside, he even went outside to the outer college to ask others.","On the way, whenever he encountered other masters, he respectfully presented his essay, saying he didn't fully understand some of the annotations and didn't know how to rewrite it, seeking their guidance.","The students and masters who read the essay were momentarily at a loss for words.","The students felt Song Qiming's essay was better than theirs. If this was considered rubbish, then what they wrote must be worse than rubbish.","The other masters believed Song Qiming's essay used small details to illustrate larger themes, brilliant throughout.","If revised according to Ding Weiyue's annotations, it would become like an old woman's foot-binding cloth—long, tedious, and foul-smelling.","It would be left an empty shell, and one made of paper at that, scattering with the first breeze, full of nonsense.","Was this the extent of Master Ding's ability?","Had his scholarship declined, or was he deliberately trying to stupefy his students? Could someone like this still serve as an inner college lecturer?","In the Wenjing Hall, Ding Weiyue sensed the other masters secretly glancing at him. He felt as if sitting on pins and needles, his chest about to explode with pent-up fury he couldn't release.","Song Qiming was indeed wildly arrogant about his talent, daring to oppose him like this just because he had some ability.","If he didn't drive him out, how could he remain at the academy in the future?","The day's events also led to Yan Baoyi being discussed around the academy. After dismissal, he immediately went to the Ding residence to find Master Ding.","\"Teacher, Song Qiming comes from a lowly background and has no sense of propriety. Today, he was clearly deliberately making things difficult for you.\"","Ding Weiyue gripped his wine cup tightly, as if to crush it.","\"Of course I know Song Qiming did it on purpose. I have already devised a plan to deal with him. This time, I will definitely expel him from the academy, leaving him no chance to recover.\"","Yan Baoyi's eyebrows shot up, and he eagerly pressed, \"What plan?\"","Ding Weiyue: \"The inner college holds monthly assessments. The ten lowest-ranked students are demoted back to the outer college. If Song Qiming is caught plagiarizing or cheating during this assessment, violating academy rules, he will be expelled and barred for life.\"","\"Teacher, how do you plan to do it?\" Given Song Qiming's scholarly ability, the chance of him plagiarizing or cheating was low. It would have to be orchestrated.","Ding Weiyue set down the empty cup, looking into Yan Baoyi's eyes. \"I will tell you when the plan is set. You just need to cooperate.\"","Yan Baoyi, thinking of how he had been suppressed by Song Qiming time and again, nodded heavily. \"As long as we can drive Song Qiming out of the academy, I will do anything.\"","If Song Qiming wasn't removed, he would never have his day in the sun.","Yang Yanfeng arrived at the Li residence and with a smile recounted the day's events to Li Tianchong.","\"So now they are thoroughly enemies. Initially, Ding Weiyue was making trouble for Song Qiming on behalf of his disciple. After today, it's personal; he himself wants to deal with Song Qiming.\"","\"I intend to accept Song Qiming as my disciple soon. We can't delay this any longer.\"","Seeing Yang Yanfeng's attitude change so quickly, Li Tianchong's eyes crinkled at the corners. \"What did I tell you? Song Qiming is a talent.\"","\"However, it's best to wait a little longer. When Ding Weiyue targets Song Qiming next time, you step in. The effect will be even better.\"","Yang Yanfeng shook his head, his expression serious. \"Talents are hard to come by. After today's incident, every master in the academy will have seen that essay Song Qiming wrote. If I don't act quickly, I'm afraid others will get there first.\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: Go to Back Him Up: The Bond Between Master and Disciple","paragraphs":["Mu Hongyue sat on the stool, holding a wine cup and laughing heartily.","\"You have no idea what Qiming did at the academy today. Ding Weiyue's face was dark all day, like a rat scurrying across the street. He left before classes were even dismissed.\"","Ye Liangyu gazed at Mu Hongyue with deep, somber eyes.","He didn't find it funny; he only felt a pang of heartache.","It was precisely because the boy had lost his parents early, with no one to rely on and no one to stand up for him, that he had to resort to such methods to fight back.","While getting revenge might feel satisfying in the moment, he would undoubtedly become the subject of gossip and whispered criticism from everyone at the academy behind his back. Who knew how much idle talk there would be.","\"I promise you, I will start teaching at the academy next month. I'll begin with the Inner Hall, and move to the Upper Hall once Qiming passes the exam to enter it.\"","The smile faded from Mu Hongyue's face.","\"With your talent and status, if you teach in the Inner Hall, I won't be able to justify it to the Upper Hall students.\"","The best teacher should teach the best students.","Otherwise, people would think he, as the headmaster, was being unfair, favoring the Inner Hall.","Ye Liangyu took away the plate of braised pork intestines, preventing Mu Hongyue from eating more. \"I don't care if you can justify it or not. If it weren't to ensure Qiming isn't bullied, I wouldn't be going to teach at Anyang Academy at all.\"","Mu Hongyue said, \"Your concern is clouding your judgment. From Song Qiming's actions today, it's clear he's not someone easily bullied.\"","\"Whether you teach in the Inner Hall or the Upper Hall, once people know Song Qiming is your disciple, they won't dare bully him again.\"","Although he knew Mu Hongyue spoke the truth, Ye Liangyu insisted on his original plan.","\"In the capital, I was constantly constrained, wary of this prince and fearful of that one. Now that I've retired and returned to Anyang Prefecture, I'll do as I please.\"","\"If you don't agree, I'll simply wait until Qiming enters the Upper Hall before I go. Tomorrow, I'll send invitations to every instructor at your academy, summon them all here, and have a firm word with them.\"","Hearing this, Mu Hongyue knew he was serious and quickly said, \"Alright, alright, the Inner Hall it is. Anyway, the annual exams are in just three months. Time will pass quickly.\"","His friend had lived a lifetime without wife or children, a solitary man.","At this age, he had only taken Song Qiming as his disciple, protecting him as if he were his own son.","Song Qiming had just entered when he saw Mu Hongyue and Ye Liangyu sitting face-to-face, one drinking tea, the other wine.","It wasn't even dinner time yet, were they eating so early?","He approached and bowed respectfully to them. \"Master, Headmaster Mu.\"","Mu Hongyue turned his head and teased, \"Qiming, whenever I send someone to your family's shop to buy braised pork intestines, they come back empty-handed four out of five times. If it weren't for your master having some here, getting a taste would be difficult.\"","Song Qiming replied, \"My elder sister has been considering expanding the supply recently. It should improve in a while.\"","As master and disciple were heading to the study, Mu Hongyue didn't stay long and left.","In the study, fragrant with sandalwood incense, Ye Liangyu spoke. \"Next month, I will begin teaching at Anyang Academy. I'll start with the Inner Hall and move to the Upper Hall once you advance there.\"","Ink dripped from his brush tip onto the rice paper. Song Qiming looked up. \"Master, you already know?\"","Ye Liangyu said, \"Your headmaster comes by every other day with gossip. How could I not know?\"","\"He had asked me before to become an instructor at Anyang Academy. Considering my limited mobility, I never agreed. Now, I think teaching might be quite nice.\"","Song Qiming had originally planned to wait until he got home that evening to write the deliberately terrible essay Ding Weiyue had demanded, just to hand something in and muddle through. It wouldn't be a big deal to just go through the motions.","But hearing Ye Liangyu's words now, his heart suddenly tightened with a bittersweet ache, feeling somewhat wronged.","He hadn't done anything wrong. Just because he studied hard and outperformed others, he became a target for bullying. The more he thought about it, the more infuriating it was.","He wished he could be like his elder sister dealing with the thugs who bullied her—beat them up and throw them in the river to drown, only then would his anger be vented.","But he couldn't do that. He could only endure and find fault with the other party.","\"Master, your scholarship surpasses even Headmaster Mu's. Wouldn't it be a loss to just be an ordinary instructor? How about becoming deputy headmaster? With your learning and status, you are absolutely qualified.\"","Ye Liangyu looked at Song Qiming, his gaze as gentle as willow branches stirred by a spring breeze—three parts delight, three parts appreciation, four parts fondness.","\"After my leg fully recovers, I might leave Anyang Prefecture. I won't stay at the academy for very long.\"","Song Qiming's pupils froze for a moment before flickering slightly. He asked with concern, \"Master, are you returning to the capital?\"","Ye Liangyu moved his hand from his knee, his gaze falling on his legs. \"Yes.\"","\"There are some matters I cannot accept. I want to go and seek an answer.\"","He reached out as if to pat Song Qiming's head, but withdrew his hand midway.","\"But there's still plenty of time. Your elder sister says it will take at least another year for me to recover completely, perhaps even a year or two longer. By that time, you'll be taking the provincial examinations.\"","Song Qiming tightened his grip on the brush and vowed, \"Master, I will pass.\"","Ye Liangyu lowered his gaze fondly, then raised it again, placing his complete trust in Song Qiming.","\"Of course you will. How could a disciple of Ye Liangyu possibly fail to become a provincial graduate?\""]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: Mu Songnian Descends the Mountain and Pays Another Visit","paragraphs":["By nightfall, Liu Xuanqing was administering medicine to Old Madam Meng for the thirteenth time that day.","She would vomit after drinking it, and the little that was absorbed had minimal effect. The pain in her abdomen was worsening. If they waited any longer, he truly feared she wouldn't last until Gu Zhongheng brought the venerable Physician Mu.","After having the apprentice tidy up the medicine chest and return to the guest room to rest, Liu Xuanqing couldn't help but recall Song Jinzhao's suggestion of performing surgery.","In his decades of practice, he had encountered the same illness seven times. The patients either suffered for dozens of days before dying, or, after being cured, relapsed within a year or so.","The lucky ones, if cured again, might last another year or two, or even several years. The unlucky ones would end up like Old Madam Meng, unable to survive the first relapse, ultimately meeting the same fatal end.","For this illness, he had never achieved a permanent cure.","Yet Song Jinzhao had proposed a method that promised complete eradication. Even though he had never heard of such a thing, upon careful consideration, he couldn't help but feel inclined to believe it, to want to try it.","If it truly succeeded, a new treatment method would emerge in medical history. To witness it in his lifetime would make his career worthwhile.","It was a pity the Meng family hadn't agreed in the end.","Given the patient's current critical state, he could only hope that Physician Mu could indeed cure her, so these two days of suffering wouldn't be in vain.","Gu Zhongheng returned with the physician on the afternoon of the second day after his departure. By then, three full days had passed since Old Madam Meng's attack.","In just three days, the once pampered Old Madam Meng seemed to have withered away by dozens of pounds, lying in bed with only the faintest breath entering her body.","Meng Hechuan personally came out of the room to greet them. \"Physician Mu, I entrust my mother's health to your care.\"","Gu Zhongheng, standing behind his master, couldn't suppress the triumphant glee in his eyes.","Mu Songnian, over ninety years old, had long since gone gray. He nodded slowly at Meng Hechuan. \"Prefect Meng, this old man must first examine Old Madam Meng's condition to determine the appropriate treatment.\"","Meng Hechuan gestured. \"Please, Physician Mu, this way.\"","After checking her pulse and examining her, and reviewing the prescriptions Liu Xuanqing had written both a year ago and in the past two days, Mu Songnian spoke. \"The patient is over sixty. Her digestion was already poor due to age, and this is a relapse—an acute attack. With three days having passed, the situation is extremely grave.\"","\"This old man will prescribe a formula immediately. If she can survive tonight, there is still hope for recovery. However, the likelihood of relapse is very high. The intervals will grow shorter, and each recurrence will be more severe and more difficult to treat than the last.\"","Meng Hechuan gasped, struggling to accept this. \"Physician Mu, please help my mother through this crisis first. If it recurs, we will treat it again.\"","Mu Songnian dictated the prescription, and Gu Zhongheng wrote it down beside him.","Nearly half an hour later, Old Madam Meng was forced to drink a bowl of medicine. She vomited half of it up, and another bowl was forced down.","Having traveled day and night, the elderly Mu Songnian was exhausted.","The Meng family prepared a guest room. After the medicine was administered, Mu Songnian went to rest, leaving Gu Zhongheng and Liu Xuanqing to watch over Old Madam Meng.","\"My master's medical skills are superb. This time will surely be successful,\" Gu Zhongheng said.","Liu Xuanqing's eyes were filled with worry. \"Physician Mu said the next relapse will only be more severe. Without a permanent cure, it's ultimately not a long-term solution.\"","Gu Zhongheng gave a light shrug and smile. \"Too many people die of illness every day in this world. Many diseases simply cannot be cured. If Old Madam Meng can pass this hurdle, she will already be luckier than most. There's no use in you thinking so much.\"","Liu Xuanqing said hesitantly, \"It's just... I feel Doctor Song's method sounds reasonable. Perhaps we could try it.\"","Gu Zhongheng glared at him. \"I think you're getting old, your eyes are failing, and your mind is becoming muddled.\"","\"Cutting out a piece of intestine from the belly? Such an outrageous idea she came up with, and you say it sounds reasonable? I think you're becoming obsessed with finding a cure.\"","In the latter half of the night, Old Madam Meng, who had been unconscious, suddenly clutched her stomach and began writhing on the bed.","The maid keeping watch by the bed immediately pulled back the bed curtains and called out, \"Doctor Liu! Doctor Gu! My mistress's stomach hurts terribly!\"","Startled awake, Liu Xuanqing and Gu Zhongheng rushed over.","\"Where does it hurt? What kind of pain is it?\"","\"A gripping, twisting pain... here, all over this area. I'm dying from the pain!\"","Gu Zhongheng turned and ran out. \"I'll fetch my master!\"","Not long after, Gu Zhongheng helped Mu Songnian into the room.","The three members of the Meng family, alerted by the commotion, hurried over and stood anxiously by the bed, hearts filled with dread.","Mu Songnian's expression grew increasingly grave. After a long moment, he supported himself on the bed frame, stood up, and shook his head heavily at Meng Hechuan. \"I regret that I am powerless. It is too late.\"","Meng Hechuan, in his forties, trembled slightly.","Madam Meng refused to give up. \"Physician Mu, please think of another way.\"","Meng Xiaozhe supported his mother, his own face pale.","The elderly Mu Songnian bowed slightly with clasped hands to the three of them. \"She has at most two days left. Sir, you should begin preparing for the funeral arrangements.\"","Gu Zhongheng stood rigidly in place, unmoving. If he had known it was hopeless, he should have kept his head down and not gotten involved in the first place.","Seeing the Meng family plunged into grief, Liu Xuanqing timidly spoke up. \"Should we... try Doctor Song's method?\"","Since she was going to die anyway, trying something was better than simply waiting for death.","Meng Hechuan and the others stared blankly at Liu Xuanqing, momentarily unsure how to decide.","Mu Songnian looked at Liu Xuanqing and asked curiously, \"What method? Which Doctor Song?\"","Liu Xuanqing stepped closer. \"A newly arrived female physician in Anyang Prefecture. Three days ago, she came to the Meng residence for a consultation. She said this illness is caused by blockage and infection in an organ called the appendix at the end of the intestine.\"","\"She proposed making an incision on the right side of the abdomen, removing the appendix, and then suturing the wound. That would completely cure it, with no future relapses.\"","Mu Songnian stood quietly, his brow slightly furrowed.","After a long while, he asked, \"Has this female physician used such a treatment method before?\"","Liu Xuanqing shook his head. \"I don't know. But she seemed quite confident.\"","He looked at Meng Hechuan. \"I think since there's no other way to save her, it's better to give it a try. There might be hope. It's better than doing nothing.\"","Mu Songnian asked, \"How old is this female physician now?\"","Gu Zhongheng's tone was flat, suppressing his inner turmoil. \"She looks to be only in her teens.\"","Meng Hechuan interjected, \"Song Jinzhao is sixteen this year.\"","\"So young?\" Mu Songnian found it hard to believe. At sixteen, most medical practitioners were still apprentices, far from being able to treat patients independently.","In the latter half of the night, Fushun was sleeping soundly when a violent banging on the door, like an earthquake, startled him so badly he fell right out of bed.","\"Again?!\"","He scrambled up from the floor to open the door. \"Who is it?\"","\"From the Meng residence. We're here to fetch Doctor Song for a consultation.\"","Fushun opened and closed his mouth, utterly exasperated.","Why did it always have to be the middle of the night? Couldn't they let people sleep?","He opened the door and said wearily, \"Wait here. I'll go call my young mistress.\"","Song Qiming emerged from his room, frowning. \"Didn't they say they'd find someone else to treat her? Why are they here in the middle of the night again?\"","Song Jinzhao opened her door, her expression grave. \"Most likely, the treatment failed.\"","This time, they returned to the clinic to gather all necessary equipment before heading to the Meng residence.","Approaching the hour of Yin, the rear courtyard of the Meng residence was brightly lit.","As Song Jinzhao entered, both Meng Hechuan and Liu Xuanqing stepped forward to meet her.","\"Miss Song, I beg you, save my mother. I am willing to undergo the procedure you mentioned, the one where you cut open the belly and remove part of the intestine.\"","\"Doctor Song, Old Madam Meng's condition seems to have worsened. Please take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept over the elderly man standing with Gu Zhongheng. He looked frail with age, at least ninety years old. Was this his master?","She stepped forward to examine and question the patient. There was severe, persistent pain throughout the abdomen, and a vague mass could be felt upon palpation. This indicated perforation, and an abscess had already formed.","\"It has perforated and formed an abscess. Even if we successfully remove the appendix now, the risk of subsequent infection will be extremely high.\"","She would do her utmost to sterilize and disinfect, but this was, after all, ancient times, not a modern operating room.","Meng Hechuan stepped forward, his eyes filled with a mix of despair and entreaty. \"Are you saying it cannot be removed now?\"","Song Jinzhao met his gaze. \"It must be removed. Removing it offers a sliver of hope. Not removing it means certain death.\"","\"The decision rests with you, sir. Shall we proceed?\"","Meng Hechuan lowered his head. \"Remove it. Whether we operate or not, she will die. What harm is there in trying?\"","If only he had known that Old Master Mu couldn't save his mother, he would have agreed to the surgery three days ago. At least the success rate would have been higher then.","Song Jinzhao: \"Alright. The surgery will begin immediately. Shixue, tell them what needs to be prepared. Uninvolved personnel, please wait outside.\"","Liu Xuanqing said urgently, \"Doctor Song, might I be permitted to stay and observe? I truly wish to understand how this is treated, how the removal is done.\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. \"You may only stand to the side. Speak little, observe much. Do not interfere with the surgery.\"","Liu Xuanqing nodded vigorously, his sixty-year-old head bobbing up and down as fast as a pecking chicken.","Mu Songnian spoke up, \"Doctor Song, might this old man also stay to observe? As a fellow physician, I am exceedingly curious about this 'surgery' you speak of.\"","Song Jinzhao: \"You may. But your disciple cannot. I truly fear that the moment I open the patient's right abdomen, he will start shouting that I'm committing murder.\"","Gu Zhongheng opened his mouth, his throat feeling clogged. With no other choice, he said to Mu Songnian, \"Master, I will wait outside.\"","He was determined to see for himself whether Song Jinzhao could actually save Old Madam Meng.","He would bide his time for now. It wouldn't be too late to mock her once the outcome was clear."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: Appendectomy","paragraphs":["The surgery began, leaving only Song Jinzhao, Song Shixue, Liu Xuanqing, and Mu Songnian in the room.","After drinking the medicinal decoction, Old Lady Meng fell into a deep coma.","Song Jinzhao, holding a specially crafted No. 10 scalpel, made a ten-centimeter incision below the patient's right abdomen.","\"The appendix is inflamed. The greater omentum and appendix have adhered, forming an inflammatory mass. Give me the No. 15 scalpel.\"","Song Shixue immediately passed the No. 15 scalpel over.","Liu Xuanqing and Mu Songnian, wearing masks, stared at the tray holding surgical tools of various sizes and shapes, astonished and somewhat unable to gather their thoughts.","Every move Song Jinzhao made was an assault on their years of medical knowledge, shattering their minds to pieces, held together only by a thin layer of skin to keep them from falling apart.","Time passed minute by minute. The Meng family waiting outside the room was already anxiously pacing in circles.","Madam Meng clenched her handkerchief, her heart in turmoil. \"We still don't know what's happening inside. There's not a single sound.\"","Meng Hechuan sat on a chair with his head bowed, his eyes fixed unwaveringly on the door, not uttering a word.","Song Shixue used gauze to wipe the sweat beading on Song Jinzhao's forehead.","The adhesions were severe; separating them required extraordinary effort, all while trying to minimize the surgery time. Song Jinzhao's entire focus was now on her hands.","Although it was only her hands and mind at work, her whole body was tense, the inner layer of her clothes already half-soaked with sweat.","In modern times, appendicitis is a minor surgery, but here, the difficulty was amplified at least tenfold, and it could be fatal at any moment.","\"Clamp.\"","Her voice showed not a trace of fluctuation; Song Jinzhao was the picture of absolute calm at this moment.","She severed the mesenteric vessels and swiftly ligated them to stop the bleeding.","\"Catgut suture.\"","They watched as Song Jinzhao deftly used a needle holder to perform a double ligation at the base of the appendix, then cut it off and placed it on the tray.","Mu Songnian, over ninety years old, had poor eyesight. He rubbed them a few times before clearly seeing Song Jinzhao's actions.","Liu Xuanqing stared at the small, intestine-like object on the tray. Was this the inflamed appendix?","After burying the stump into the cecum, suctioning out the pus from the abdominal cavity, and rinsing it once with medicinal solution, she finally began suturing the peritoneum, muscle, subcutaneous tissue, and skin.","Song Jinzhao: \"Don't suture the wound completely here. Leave an opening at the end and insert mulberry bark paper for drainage.\"","Song Shixue asked curiously, \"If an abscess hadn't formed from perforation before the surgery, would drainage not be necessary?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded: \"Correct. Adding this step increases the risk of wound infection. So, once appendicitis recurs after treatment, the best method is excision, the sooner the better.\"","Seeing the wound suturing completed, Liu Xuanqing cautiously checked Old Lady Meng's pulse. Only after confirming the pulse was stable did he suppress the excitement in his heart and let out a sigh of relief.","The door opened, and the Meng family rushed forward in a crowd, urgently asking, \"How did it go? Was the surgery successful?\"","Liu Xuanqing stepped aside. \"Better let Physician Song explain to you, sir.\"","Song Jinzhao walked out holding the tray. \"The appendix has been removed. The next three days are the most critical. As long as there's no infection, it can be considered a success.\"","Madam Meng saw the contents of the tray clearly, covered her mouth and nose with a handkerchief, and retreated several steps.","Meng Xiaozhe stared at the pinkish-red object on the tray, his neck retracting, somewhat frightened.","\"Physician Song, what is this?\"","Song Jinzhao offered the tray towards him. \"Your grandmother's appendix. Didn't you say she wanted to be buried whole after death? Burn this, and when the time comes a hundred years from now, place it in the coffin with her. That way, all her organs will be complete.\"","Meng Xiaozhe's mouth twitched. His eyes darted between Song Jinzhao and the tray several times before he finally, with trembling hands, took the tray. His gaze was conflicted, as if he had grievances he couldn't voice.","\"My previous remarks were improper. Thank you, Physician Song, for considering my grandmother's wishes.\"","Song Jinzhao relaxed her expression and glanced at Meng Hechuan. \"The old lady will likely wake in about half an hour. She must abstain from food and water for three hours. She can get out of bed and walk moderately to prevent internal adhesions from prolonged immobility.\"","Meng Hechuan quickly spoke up: \"We have guest rooms in the residence. To guard against any unforeseen complications while my mother recuperates, could Miss Song possibly stay temporarily?\"","Considering she would need to change the drainage mulberry bark paper frequently over the next few days, Song Jinzhao glanced at Song Shixue and then nodded in agreement.","Gu Zhongheng stepped forward to help Mu Songnian out of the room. \"Master, did Song Jinzhao really cure Old Lady Meng?\"","Having stood for so long, a wave of fatigue washed over Mu Songnian as he relaxed.","He shook his head. \"It depends on her recovery over the next few days. But at least for now, the patient is still alive and well after having her appendix cut out.\"","Gu Zhongheng's arm stiffened. He clenched his lips, a pang of panic in his chest.","Meng Hechuan had someone escort Song Shixue home first, while Song Jinzhao returned to the guest room to rest.","Three quarters of an hour later, Old Lady Meng woke up.","The ordeal of the past few days, combined with the surgery, made her feel as if she had crawled back from hell—her head throbbing, her entire body weak and feeble.","Three hours later, two maids helped Old Lady Meng out of bed.","After just two steps, she shook her head uncomfortably at Song Jinzhao. \"It hurts. Can I not walk? Lying down doesn't hurt as much.\"","Song Jinzhao firmly refused: \"No. Walk back and forth in the room once. Lying down can cause internal adhesions in the abdomen. That can be fatal.\"","Hearing it could be fatal, Old Lady Meng had no choice but to continue taking slow, plodding steps.","Once she had finally managed the number of steps Song Jinzhao required, she immediately had the maids help her back to bed to lie down.","\"Physician Song, when will I recover?\"","The hole in her belly wasn't fully sewn up yet; the mulberry bark paper plugged the opening. She always felt an unsettling emptiness inside, as if her internal organs were exposed, which gave her the creeps.","Song Jinzhao leaned over to check the drainage from the pus. The color and viscosity appeared normal.","\"As long as you can get through the next three days, the stitches can be removed after seven days. You'll be able to walk normally after half a month, and be completely recovered in a month.\"","Old Lady Meng grabbed the back of Song Jinzhao's hand. \"Are you sure it won't recur again?\"","She truly didn't want to endure such pain a third time.","Song Jinzhao offered a faint, reassuring smile. \"I'm sure. How can it recur when the appendix is gone?\"","She changed the mulberry bark paper twice daily. By the second day, the amount of pus discharge had significantly decreased.","On the fourth day, Song Jinzhao applied anesthetic to the affected area. \"Bear with it, don't tense up. Just two stitches.\"","Old Lady Meng turned her head away and shut her eyes tightly, not daring to look. Who would have thought the day would come when her own flesh could be sewn like fabric.","After finishing the sutures, Song Jinzhao packed her things and took her leave from Meng Hechuan. \"Old Lady Meng has safely passed the critical period. I will return when it's time to remove the stitches.\"","Meng Hechuan bowed gratefully towards Song Jinzhao. \"Miss Song's medical skills are extraordinary. I apologize for my previous lack of trust and ask for your understanding.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled lightly, unconcerned. \"Lord Meng, please don't dwell on it. Most people would choose to see an older physician. There's no need to apologize.\"","Madam Meng approached Song Jinzhao holding a wooden box, which she opened. \"This is the consultation fee and payment for the medicine. We've troubled you these past few days, Physician Song. Please, you must accept it.\""]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: Five Hundred Taels as Reward, A Sixty-Year-Old Apprentice","paragraphs":["A flicker of surprise passed through Song Jinzhao's eyes. Inside the box was a five-hundred-tael silver note.","She took the box and said, \"The precautions I've noted down have already been given to the maid serving the old madam. I will return in four days.\"","Meng Xiaozhe saw Song Jinzhao to the gate.","The horse she had ridden from home that night was being held by a Meng family servant waiting below the steps. Its coat was glossy and sleek, and it even looked a bit sturdier.","Arriving home, Song Shixue, hearing the commotion, turned and saw Song Jinzhao. She dashed out of the house, leaving Song Anhao behind.","\"Elder Sister, you're back.\"","During these past few days staying at the Meng residence, Song Jinzhao would return home to check during the day, but not spending the nights at home left Song Shixue feeling an empty, unsettled unease.","Song Jinzhao tied the reins to a post and led Song Shixue inside. \"I came back once the wound stopped festering.\"","As they walked, Song Shixue looked up, talking to Song Jinzhao.","\"The patient who had stitches in his head a few days ago is healing very well. He came to the clinic yesterday afternoon, and I already removed the stitches for him.\"","Yesterday was the seventh day, the last day. Song Shixue had opened the door, having calculated the time.","Song Jinzhao covered her mouth with her hand, yawning. Home truly gave a sense of belonging. No matter how nice the room was at someone else's house, she just couldn't sleep well.","\"We'll open the clinic tomorrow. I need to sleep first.\"","Song Shixue nodded. Having cared for the patient tirelessly through the night, Elder Sister must be exhausted now.","Song Anhao, holding onto the doorframe with his right hand, threw himself at Song Jinzhao.","After wrapping his arms around her neck, his soft, tender little lips planted a kiss on her cheek. \"Eldest Sister, Eldest Sister, Anhao missed you.\"","\"I don't think you missed me at all. You've even gained weight.\"","Song Jinzhao couldn't help but gently pinch his chubby little cheek. She wondered who he'd learned to act so coquettishly from; his words were incredibly sweet.","Constantly missing you, loving you, the clinging and hugging seemed almost innate.","Song Anhao rested his head on Song Jinzhao's shoulder and wriggled. \"Not fat. Pretty.\"","After bathing, she collapsed onto the bed. When she woke up, it was already dark outside.","Qingshuang, who was practicing martial arts in the courtyard, saw Song Jinzhao come out and immediately stopped, stepping forward to ask, \"Young Miss, would you like something to eat?\"","Song Jinzhao looked up at the golden full moon hanging in the sky. \"Wontons. Something light.\"","After eating, Song Jinzhao sat in the courtyard enjoying the cool breeze. Qingshuang glanced towards the woodshed and whispered to Song Jinzhao, \"These past few days, while practicing, I often noticed Lanxi watching by the window. He seems very interested.\"","Song Jinzhao looked towards the woodshed window; it was closed now.","Fourteen was just the right age. He should learn more easily than Qingshuang did.","The next day when the clinic opened, the first to arrive weren't patients, but an excited Liu Xuanqing, and Gu Zhongheng helping Mu Songnian over.","Liu Xuanqing rushed up to Song Jinzhao, his hands trembling.","\"Physician Song, I heard Old Madam Meng's condition has greatly improved. The wound didn't become infected? Her life is saved?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in confirmation. \"Yes. In a few more days, the stitches can be removed.\"","Before Mu Songnian could speak, Liu Xuanqing suddenly knelt before Song Jinzhao. \"Physician Song, I wish to become your disciple and study medicine. I beg you to accept me as your student.\"","A woman who had just stepped over the threshold froze in place, rubbing her eyes, wondering if she had misheard or misseen.","Physician Liu from Huiming Hall wants to become Physician Song's disciple?","A young girl in her teens.","His age could be her grandfather.","Seeing the woman enter, Song Shixue left the awkward scene to go attend to her.","She had come a few days before; she was the mother of the little girl who had caught a cold with a high fever.","The woman rested her hand on the counter and said slowly, \"The medicine prescribed before is finished. My daughter still has a slight cough. I'd like to get two more doses.\"","\"How does she cough? Is it a throat discomfort, coughing a couple of times then stopping, or continuous coughing? At night or during the day?\"","The woman replied, \"Just a couple of coughs then stops. Her nose is still a bit stuffy.\"","Song Shixue said, \"It's not a big issue. I'll write a new prescription for recuperation. Three days of this should clear it up.\"","The woman nodded, her eyes constantly darting to the side.","Song Jinzhao remained silent. Liu Xuanqing was still kneeling on the ground, not having risen.","Gu Zhongheng stood gaping, mouth agape. Having lived over sixty years, he had never seen anything so absurd, and it was happening to Liu Xuanqing.","Song Jinzhao watched Liu Xuanqing's lips part and close. \"Becoming a disciple is unnecessary. If you wish to study medicine, you can take a few medical texts I've written back to read.\"","Liu Xuanqing's gaze was firm, firmly locking onto Song Jinzhao.","\"A teacher transmits the way, imparts knowledge, and resolves doubts. Although I am a bit older, my health is good. I can still live for decades. It's not too late to learn now. I beg Miss Song to accept me as your disciple.\"","Merely reading medical texts couldn't compare to the efficiency of hands-on teaching. Moreover, some medical techniques couldn't be learned from books alone.","Like yesterday's appendectomy surgery. Even if it were written in a book, without guidance, he would never learn it.","Mu Songnian pushed away Gu Zhongheng's supporting hand and walked up to Song Jinzhao. \"To be frank, this old man has also come today to become a disciple.\"","The medicine package in the woman's hand fell to the ground. Everyone turned to look. She hurriedly picked up the package from the floor and fled without looking back.","That man looked at least ninety if not a hundred. Not just a grandfather, more like a great-grandfather.","With one foot practically in the grave, how could he still want to become the disciple of a teenage girl? Were they mad, out of their minds?","Faced with a ninety-year-old's request to become a disciple, Song Jinzhao shook her head even more swiftly.","\"Old Master Mu, you should forget it. Performing surgery requires good eyesight. Your physical condition is no longer quite up to it.\"","Forget the lack of magnifying lenses; even with them, no hospital had a ninety-year-old surgeon as the lead operating physician. Their stamina simply couldn't keep up. At most, they could stand by and offer guidance.","Seeing Song Jinzhao refuse so quickly, Mu Songnian felt immensely disappointed.","Born at the wrong time, ironically decades too old.","He turned to stare at Gu Zhongheng, who got goosebumps under the gaze.","Gu Zhongheng realized his master's intention and quickly shook his head. \"Master, perhaps we should just take a few medical texts back to study? Becoming a disciple... I think we should forget it.\"","Mu Songnian's eyelids drooped, giving him a clear look of disdain.","Not seizing such a good opportunity! How could the disciple he taught be so foolish, lacking even half of Liu Xuanqing's cleverness and wit.","In the end, Song Jinzhao still refused Liu Xuanqing's request to become her disciple.","First, she had no time to take on another disciple.","Second, Liu Xuanqing's age was truly rather advanced, even a few years older than her own father, Song Laodie.","As he left, Liu Xuanqing's gaze lingered on Song Shixue for a moment.","She was Song Jinzhao's younger sister and also her disciple. She must receive very dedicated teaching normally.","Since he couldn't become the master's disciple, then becoming the master's master's disciple would achieve the same effect.","He was absolutely determined to learn this medicine. Otherwise, it would be the greatest regret of his life. Liu Xuanqing was utterly convinced of this."]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: Rising to Fame, Yang Yanfeng Proposes to Become a Disciple","paragraphs":["The Meng family had summoned physicians from across the entire Anyang Prefecture for a consultation. Now, word spread that Old Madame Meng's illness had been cured. All the physicians who had taken their fees and left believed it was Liu Xuanqing and Lao Gu who had accomplished the cure.","Liu Xuanqing stood beneath the signboard of Huiming Hall and shook his head. \"Old Madame Meng's illness was not cured by me or Lao Gu. It was Physician Song from the Song Family Clinic, that talented female doctor.\"","The visitor stared at Liu Xuanqing with dumbfounded eyes, his body rooted to the spot like a wooden stake.","\"Physician Liu, you must be joking, surely?\"","A female doctor had cured an illness that had stumped all the physicians in Anyang Prefecture, and she was only in her teens!","Liu Xuanqing patted his colleague's shoulder solemnly. \"The waves of the Yangtze River push the waves ahead; the younger generation is formidable. We old relics can no longer afford to look down on others.\"","Anyang Academy.","Song Gaoli ran to the inner dormitory to find Song Qiming and pulled him into a pavilion.","\"I heard Sister A'zhao cured Old Madame Meng's illness. Is it true?\"","He had been startled to hear this news in his dormitory room and thought it was false.","If all the physicians in Anyang Prefecture couldn't cure it, and only Song Qiming's sister could save her, how exceptionally skilled must her medical art be?","Most importantly, saving Old Madame Meng meant essentially connecting with the Prefect himself.","The corners of Song Qiming's mouth stretched almost to his ears as he nodded happily and emphatically. \"That's right, it was my elder sister.\"","Song Gaoli plopped down on a stone stool, pursed his lips tightly, his mouth twitching, his eyes and heart filled with both admiration and envy.","\"Sister Jinzhao is just too amazing. If she were a man, she'd be a thousand, no, ten thousand times more capable than you.\"","Song Qiming smiled even wider, showing his teeth.","\"If my elder sister were a man, in martial prowess she could sweep across battlefields, in literary pursuits she could top the imperial examinations, in medicine she would surely be a royal physician in the palace, and even in commerce, she would undoubtedly amass great wealth.\"","Song Gaoli suppressed a laugh; the corner of his mouth twitched and his throat felt slightly choked.","This was a full-blown sister-con. Praise her once, and he'd praise her to the heavens.","Forget the rest, but topping the imperial examinations? That statement was truly a bit grandiose.","He himself wouldn't even dare think such a thing.","Under the eaves not far away, Ding Weiyue held a book, his gaze deep and fixed on Song Qiming. Yan Baoyi stood beside him, his fists clenched so tight they seemed about to shatter.","\"Forget about what I asked you to do yesterday. The Song family has connected with Prefect Meng. If anything happens to Song Qiming, it's hard to guarantee his sister wouldn't plead her case before the Prefect.\"","Yan Baoyi gnashed his teeth, asking unwillingly, \"So we just let him off?\"","Ding Weiyue turned away with a livid face and walked forward. \"Who let him have a capable sister? Even if Song Qiming truly committed plagiarism or fraud, Prefect Meng, for his sister's sake, would likely intervene to protect him.\"","\"Forcing him out of the academy would only incur Prefect Meng's displeasure with us. If it were discovered, it would be you and I who suffer the consequences.\"","Yan Baoyi's features contorted, the hatred in his eyes nearly overflowing.","Song Qiming had outshone him at the Hairpin Flower Banquet with that imperial-bestowed fabric, and now, because his sister cured the Prefect's mother, he gained another powerful backer.","A woman, instead of staying home washing clothes and cooking, parades herself in public all day, scheming and maneuvering. She really is a nuisance.","Song Jinzhao, currently busy without a moment to spare, was unaware that someone had already begun to resent her.","After news spread of her curing Old Madame Meng, the clinic's business instantly boomed.","The benches at the entrance were filled with commoners waiting to see the doctor, a quick glance estimating over a dozen people.","There were even healthy onlookers standing at the door, stealing glances at Song Jinzhao, wanting to see what the talented female doctor, whose skill surpassed all physicians in Anyang Prefecture, actually looked like.","After a busy day, Chunxing returned home in the evening and was cooking in the kitchen. Under the eaves, Song Anhao was lying on Lan Xi's stomach, playing with his hair with his little hands.","Watching the chubby little hand trail from the boy's temple to the corner of his eye, then grab the clothes on his chest.","Lan Xi frowned, pulling his neck back to avoid it, but a white scratch appeared on his face, not serious, only surface-level.","Song Shixue's eyelashes fluttered rapidly twice. She walked over, picked up Song Anhao, and held his hand. His nails, uncut for a while, were a bit long.","Staring at the scratch on the boy's face, she had a suspicion but didn't voice it directly.","\"Elder sister said she will start treating your eyes in a couple of days.\"","Lan Xi's breath hitched, his mind going completely blank in an instant.","He lifted his gaze to look at Song Shixue. \"My eyes... can be cured?\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"Elder sister says it's possible. Such beautiful eyes, it would be a pity if they couldn't see.\"","\"Touch, touch, touch.\" When Song Anhao heard a sensitive word, he leaned forward, his hand reaching towards Lan Xi's eyes.","Song Shixue reached out and pulled him back. \"Touch what, touch? Such long nails, let your second sister trim them for you.\"","Watching Song Shixue's retreating figure as she carried the child away, Lan Xi tried to lift his bandaged, sling-bound arm to touch his blind eye.","Whether in the past or now, everyone had always disliked and despised his eyes, finding them insulting—an anomaly. Only the Song family was different.","Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming treated him as an ordinary person, thinking blue eyes were no big deal.","Both Song Shixue and Song Anhao actually liked his eyes. One would always glance at them a few extra times with an appreciative look whenever she saw them; the other expressed his fondness unabashedly through touch.","So what if his face got scratched? It was just a bit of broken skin. Compared to those who wanted to kill him, this was a trivial matter, too small to be smaller.","Every time those pure, innocent big eyes came close and stared at him, Lan Xi always felt a sense of peace.","As if everything from the past no longer had anything to do with him. He was no longer He Mingjue, but Lan Xi, simply Lan Xi.","Song Qiming stopped suddenly after classes were dismissed, utterly bewildered as he stared at Yang Yanfeng, who had expressed a desire to take him as a disciple.","Since entering the inner dormitory, Tutor Yang's attitude towards him had been quite good. He never expected him to want to take him as a disciple.","Seeing Song Qiming silent, Yang Yanfeng thought he was too surprised to react.","So he continued, \"I admire your talent greatly, and your performance since entering the inner dormitory has been outstanding.\"","Originally, I hadn't planned to take you as a disciple. But later I discovered that Tutor Ding was trying to make things difficult for you because of Yan Baoyi. After some thought, the only way is for me to accept you as my disciple. Then, out of respect for me, he won't continue to pick on you, and the other students won't avoid you anymore either.","Song Qiming bowed with his hands clasped. \"Thank you for your recognition, Tutor. However, this student already has a master and cannot become a disciple of another.\"","Now it was Yang Yanfeng's turn to be stunned.","He raised his voice in disbelief, \"You've already become an apprentice? Which tutor at the academy is it?\"","His own speed was already quite fast. Who could have beaten him to it?","Song Qiming smiled and introduced his teacher. \"My teacher is not currently teaching at the academy. You likely know him, Tutor. It is Master Ye, who resides at the Ye Residence.\"","Yang Yanfeng blinked, his mind buzzing, feeling as if it had been kneaded over three times.","\"You mean Ye Liangyu, Master Ye? The former Vice Censor-in-Chief, Lord Ye? The one living at the Ye Residence near the academy?\"","Yang Yanfeng's voice grew louder with each question, the man utterly unable to calm down.","Song Qiming nodded calmly. \"That's correct. Even before the academy entrance examination, I was already receiving instruction from Master Ye at the Ye residence. After entering the academy, I have been going there daily. It has been over half a month since I formally became his disciple.\""]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: Song Qiming Already Had a Master Long Ago, Removing the Stitches","paragraphs":["Yang Yanfeng looked up at the sky, down at the earth, and felt utterly hollow inside.","He never would have thought that Song Qiming would become Ye Liangyu's disciple. That Ye Liangyu.","A former third-rank Deputy Censor-in-Chief of the court. Even though he had retired to his hometown, his network of connections within the imperial court was something ordinary people could only dream of.","All the academy tutors, himself among them, had been turned away at his door, yet Song Qiming had already become his guanmen disciple (a \"closing-door\" disciple, i.e., the last disciple).","When Yang Yanfeng went to the Li residence that evening, his legs felt weak. If Ye Liangyu found out he had tried to poach his disciple, he couldn't imagine how much he would be ridiculed.","When he saw Li Tianchong, Yang's tense face was a picture of misery.","He said listlessly, \"Brother Li, I knew you had a good eye, but I never realized just how good.\"","\"Why couldn't you have investigated properly before sending me to recruit him? You've made me take a terrible tumble!\"","Li Tianchong stopped in his tracks, bewildered. \"What's wrong? Was Song Qiming unwilling to become your disciple?\"","Yang Yanfeng plopped down into a chair, picked up a teacup, took a large gulp, and set it down heavily.","\"Unwilling? That's putting it mildly. Do you know he's already apprenticed himself to someone else?\"","Li Tianchong's eyes widened. \"Who?\"","Yang Yanfeng heaved a heavy sigh, his tone firm and forceful. \"Ye Liangyu. The very same Ye Liangyu who just retired from the position of Deputy Censor-in-Chief.\"","Seeing Li Tianchong was stunned, Yang softened his attitude and said, \"Your vision is truly sharp, but it's far too late. Song Qiming had already connected with Ye Liangyu before the academy examination.\"","\"Ranked thirty-sixth in the prefectural exam, then achieving first place in the academy exam—such rapid progress is all due to Ye Liangyu's guidance behind the scenes.\"","\"With a backer like that, your hopes of winning Song Qiming over are probably impossible now.\"","Li Tianchong's breath hitched, his chest vibrating with the force of it.","Ye Liangyu was impervious to both soft and hard tactics, loyal only to the Emperor.","If he had been willing to take sides, he would never have ended up in his current situation.","With Song Qiming as his disciple, that piece on the board was effectively useless, impossible to salvage.","Li Tianchong looked up and asked, \"Who else knows about the relationship between Song Qiming and Ye Liangyu?\"","Yang Yanfeng shook his head. \"Probably very few. Otherwise, Ding Weiyue wouldn't dare target him so blatantly.\"","\"However, from what I gathered from Song Qiming's words today, it seems Ye Liangyu is planning to come teach at the academy.\"","Li Tianchong wearily pressed his fingers against his temples. After a long moment of thought, he spoke, \"Trouble you, Brother Yang, to keep an eye out at the academy for a few scholars who are talented yet come from impoverished families. Having lost Song Qiming, I must cultivate a few others.\"","Yang Yanfeng also felt somewhat dejected. Such a gifted disciple had slipped right through his fingers. It seems it just wasn't meant to be.","\"Students from poor families are a dime a dozen, but their talent and innate ability certainly won't match Song Qiming's.\"","Li Tianchong closed his eyes with a sigh. \"Pick the tallest among the short. My Li family lacks not for money. Cast a wider net, and we're bound to find a good one eventually.\"","For now, this was the only way he could console himself.","On the day Song Jinzhao went to remove Old Madam Meng's stitches, Liu Xuanqing noticed the clinic was empty except for Song Shixue. His eyes darted around twice before he strode right in and started helping.","Song Shixue stared blankly at Liu Xuanqing, who had begun diagnosing patients. Once she regained her senses, she walked over and asked, \"Doctor Liu, what are you doing?\"","Liu Xuanqing was enthusiastic, his face beaming with a smile. \"Second Miss Song, business at Huiming Hall hasn't been great these past few days. I see you're a bit shorthanded here. How about I become your apprentice? I could stay here from now on to see patients, what do you say?\"","Song Shixue's mouth fell slightly open. Was her hearing faulty, or had Doctor Liu misspoken?","\"Are you seeing patients or not? We've been waiting for quite a while!\" An elderly woman with bent legs grew impatient and shouted at the two of them.","Liu Xuanqing instantly turned his head. \"Yes, yes, seeing them! One at a time, we'll start right now.\"","Song Shixue watched him act as naturally as if he were in his own home. He was clearly older than her grandfather, yet he seemed less sensible than Lanxi.","A patient who recognized Liu Xuanqing craned his neck, looking him up and down curiously. \"Isn't this Doctor Liu from Huiming Hall? What's he doing here?\"","Old Madam Meng's personal maidservant led Song Jinzhao towards the inner courtyard.","\"These past few days, the old madam's mood has been getting better and better, and her appetite has returned. However, we've strictly followed your instructions, giving her only light, easily digestible liquids, and controlled the portions so she doesn't overeat.\"","\"But today, since you're coming to remove the stitches, she's been nervous since she woke up this morning, constantly asking if it will hurt.\"","When Song Jinzhao entered the room, Madam Meng was sitting on the couch with Old Madam Meng, chatting.","Seeing them enter, Old Madam Meng stiffened, her expression becoming somewhat unnatural.","Madam Meng promptly rose to greet Song Jinzhao. After exchanging a few pleasantries, she went out and closed the door.","The maidservant lifted Old Madam Meng's loose outer garment, revealing the wound on her right abdomen, still covered with gauze.","Seeing Song Jinzhao about to remove the gauze and begin, Old Madam Meng couldn't help but call out to stop her.","\"Doctor Song, shouldn't you apply some anesthetic? Pulling the thread out from inside the flesh must be very painful.\"","Even as she spoke, Song Jinzhao deftly removed the gauze. No infection, redness, swelling, or discharge. Ready for suture removal.","\"It's not very painful. Grit your teeth, close your eyes, and by the time you open them, it'll be out.\"","Old Madam Meng, with the resolve of one facing death, grabbed her maid's hand and closed her eyes.","A stinging sensation, like a mosquito bite, followed by a slight tugging feeling as the thread was pulled, immediately made her whole body tense, her feet trembling involuntarily.","In the blink of an eye, Song Jinzhao had finished removing the sutures. She applied a thin layer of ointment to the wound and covered it with fresh gauze.","\"For the next half month, be careful with the wound when coughing or sneezing. Avoid straining your right abdomen. After half a month, you should be mostly fine.\"","Old Madam Meng grasped Song Jinzhao's hand. \"Doctor Song, this scar looks like a centipede. I know your medical skills are excellent. Is there any ointment that can remove scars?\"","Song Jinzhao: \"No. The surgical incision reached the dermal layer. Any ointment will find it very difficult to remove it.\"","A sixty-year-old's skin is already slack, with decreased cell regeneration capacity. Its self-repair function is much poorer than a younger person's, so the scar will only be more pronounced, likely remaining much as it looks now, freshly healed.","However, it was better not to tell her this, lest it spoil her mood. After all, even a sixty-year-old woman cares about her appearance.","Returning to the clinic, Song Jinzhao found Liu Xuanqing sitting in her own chair, seeing patients. For a moment, she thought she had walked into the wrong clinic.","\"Shixue, what's going on?\"","\"Why is Doctor Liu here?\""]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: Master, Grandmaster","paragraphs":["Song Shixue hurriedly handed the medicine packet to the waiting patient, her expression dazed, her thoughts a bit jumbled.","\"He said he wants to apprentice himself to me.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head to stare at Liu Xuanqing, who was examining a patient with a serious face.","How interesting. A man of his age, yet so persistent. To study medicine, he really has no bottom line at all.","On the surface, Liu Xuanqing was concentrating intently on taking the patient's pulse, but in reality, his mind had already wandered far away.","He didn't dare look up at Song Jinzhao, afraid of being rejected and driven out. So he pretended he hadn't seen or heard anything.","He focused on demonstrating how hardworking he was, how correct his attitude was, doing his utmost to please Song Jinzhao.","Given how earnest he was being, surely she would take him on.","Song Jinzhao watched Liu Xuanqing's consultation process for the entire afternoon. She had to admit, having practiced traditional medicine for so many years, the man did have some real skill. No wonder Huiming Hall was the best medical clinic in Anyang Prefecture.","As the patients dwindled, Liu Xuanqing's mood grew increasingly anxious.","The surroundings quieted down, the thumping of his own heartbeat loud in his ears, as if it might leap out of his chest at any moment.","Song Jinzhao's eyes held an intimidating, authoritative air, her voice calm. \"If Physician Liu practices here, what about Huiming Hall?\"","Liu Xuanqing shuddered, instantly standing up, his eyes filled with seriousness and anticipation.","\"Doctor Zhao and my two sons are at Huiming Hall. It won't matter much if I'm not there.\"","\"If Miss Song minds, I can close Huiming Hall and have them all come over.\"","Song Shixue's pupils dilated. All of them coming to become apprentices?","Their place was small; they couldn't possibly fit that many people.","Qingshuang and Fushun, having finished cleaning up next door and noticing Song Jinzhao and the others hadn't come out for a long time, had just reached the doorway when they heard Liu Xuanqing talk about closing Huiming Hall.","Song Jinzhao sat on the chair with her legs crossed, her hands resting casually on the armrests.","\"Shixue, are you willing to take Physician Liu as your disciple?\"","Meeting Liu Xuanqing's fervent gaze, Song Shixue looked up, thinking.","Since their reputation had spread, many patients had come to the clinic these past two days. She and her sister had been so busy they couldn't stop. Having a free laborer didn't seem like a bad idea.","And he wouldn't need training; he could be put to work right away. When they went home for the New Year, someone would still be there to mind the clinic.","After pondering for a moment, Song Shixue straightened her posture, putting on an air of maturity as she walked up to Liu Xuanqing.","\"I can take you as my disciple and let you practice at our family's clinic, but there will be no wages. As an apprentice, you'll have to work for me for several years for free.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together tightly, a smile touching her eyes as she lowered her gaze.","Liu Xuanqing agreed immediately without a second thought, showing no hesitation at all.","He nodded joyfully at Song Shixue. \"Since ancient times, when a physician takes on a disciple, it requires decades of close, personal instruction. Not to mention a few years of free labor, even ten or twenty years would be perfectly reasonable.\"","Song Shixue was somewhat flustered by his eager attitude.","Ten or twenty years? By then he'd be seventy or eighty years old!","She looked at Song Jinzhao, wanting to know what to do next.","A few years of free labor was a good deal, but really ten or twenty?","Song Jinzhao uncrossed her legs, folding her arms across her chest. \"Since Physician Liu is sincere in wishing to apprentice himself, then you may stay.\"","\"You are my younger sister's first disciple. Remember to call me Grandmaster from now on.\"","Liu Xuanqing grinned, the wrinkles on his face all gathering together.","Excited, he immediately knelt and kowtowed to Song Shixue and Song Jinzhao right there on the spot. \"Your disciple, Liu Xuanqing, pays his respects to Master and Grandmaster.\"","Qingshuang and Fushun, standing at the door, exchanged a look. The world really was changing.","A man of his age, with one foot already in the grave—was it necessary to strive so hard?","Liu Xuanqing returned to Huiming Hall beaming, his entire demeanor changed, looking at least five years younger at a glance.","Seeing him like this, Doctor Zhao felt half his heart die.","\"Did Song Jinzhao agree to take you as her disciple?\"","Liu Xuanqing shook his head. \"She didn't agree, but her disciple did. I am now Song Jinzhao's grand-disciple.\"","Standing in front of the medicine cabinet, Liu Renyi and Liu Renzong were as motionless as mummies, only their rising and falling chests indicating they were still breathing.","Doctor Zhao slapped his own forehead, feeling as if the sky had darkened and the earth was spinning.","\"You have money and fame now. Why must you force this issue and go through all this trouble?\"","\"You're sixty years old. Song Jinzhao's younger sister hasn't even had her coming-of-age ceremony yet. A twelve-year-old girl as your master, a sixteen-year-old as your grandmaster—how will people laugh at you when word gets out?\"","Liu Xuanqing said solemnly, \"That's because you haven't seen with your own eyes how Song Jinzhao performs surgery. As a physician, when there's an illness others can cure but you cannot, how can I possibly be content with that?\"","\"Mu Song, past ninety every year, still goes down the mountain to save people. I'm only sixty. It's not too late at all.\"","Suppressing his anger, Doctor Zhao retorted, \"What will happen to Huiming Hall if you leave?\"","Liu Xuanqing looked into his eyes, his gaze full of trust. \"With you and Renyi and Renzong here, I am at ease. Starting tomorrow, your share of the consultation fees will increase by thirty percent. I'll have to trouble you to take more care of Huiming Hall from now on.\"","Facing his old friend's tone, which sounded as if he were entrusting him with an orphan, Doctor Zhao closed his eyes, feeling only helplessness.","\"It's not about the money. I just think at your age, it's really unnecessary. You finally taught Renyi and Renzong all you know; you should be enjoying your life now.\"","Liu Xuanqing frowned, but his eyes were bright.","\"The path of medicine is endless in learning. Now that such a splendid opportunity has appeared, if I don't move forward, I will regret it for the rest of my life and die with my eyes open.\"","Seeing his resolute, almost martyr-like determination, Doctor Zhao could no longer voice any opposition.","Calm and restrained for a lifetime, to have this one moment of madness in old age—let him be.","Liu Renyi raised his hand and spoke. \"Father, after you learn Physician Song's skills, can you teach me?\"","Liu Xuanqing held his breath. \"After your father's position is secure, I will seek the permission of the master's lineage to teach you.\"","Doctor Zhao rolled his eyes skyward. \"By then, your two sons will have to call Song Jinzhao, who is over twenty years their junior, their Great-Grandmaster...\"","Liu Renyi and Liu Renzong shut their mouths tightly, their eyes darting around.","It was a little embarrassing. But with their father taking the lead, they, as sons, probably wouldn't feel too awkward.","After all, their master was their own father. As for who their grandmaster and great-grandmaster were, if no one brought it up, who would ask? At most, someone might ask who their master was.","The next morning, Liu Xuanqing arrived with celery, lotus seeds, red beans, dates, longans, and dried meat to perform the formal three kneelings and nine prostrations of the apprenticeship ceremony.","The common people who came to seek treatment were stunned.","It was like a drop of water splashing into hot oil, instantly causing a sizzling commotion everywhere.","Physician Liu of Huiming Hall was now the disciple of the younger female physician at the Song Family Clinic. Not the disciple of the female physician who cured Old Madam Meng, but the disciple of that female physician's own disciple.","A sixty-year-old physician apprenticing himself to a twelve-year-old girl.","Had Physician Liu gone mad?","When Gu Zhongheng heard the news, a thunderclap seemed to explode in his mind, and the medicinal pillow in his hand fell to the ground.","Song Jinzhao wouldn't take him, so he apprenticed himself to Song Shixue instead. Why was this man so stubborn? So her medical skills were a bit better—was it really necessary?","There are so many patients in the world; how could you possibly save them all!"]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: Song Gaoli Passes the Inner College Entrance Exam, Yan Baoyi Breaks Down","paragraphs":["After Liu Xuanqing visited the Song Family Clinic for a consultation, both Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue felt considerably more at ease.","Through their interactions over many days, Liu Xuanqing discovered that Song Jinzhao was not only incredibly skilled at suturing, but also possessed unique insights and treatment methods for other illnesses.","\"Master, was our Grand-Master's medical skill even greater than our Master's?\" he whispered, leaning close to Song Shixue.","Song Shixue, feeling awkward about having a disciple over forty years her junior, shook her head and replied, \"I never met Elder Sister's master. She said he had already passed away.\"","Liu Xuanqing sighed, his curiosity piqued, and pressed on, \"I wonder what our Grand-Master's name was, and what venerable age he attained when he passed?\"","Song Shixue shook her head again. \"I don't know. He was probably quite old. He was an itinerant doctor, and I don't know his name.\"","\"Elder Sister was taken as his disciple not long before his death. He said he didn't want his lifetime of medical knowledge to have no successor.\"","Liu Xuanqing's mind conjured the image of an ethereal, white-haired elder. To train a disciple to such excellence in such a short time, he must have been a truly extraordinary person.","The agent from Jinyun Property Agency held a ledger and followed beside Song Jinzhao, his mouth running non-stop since they left the house.","\"In the entire Anyang Prefecture, there are three hundred and sixty-two three-courtyard residences. Our agency has registered all one hundred and seventy-three that are currently for sale. Among those, twenty-six are located near the Anyang Academy, most belonging to scholars.\"","\"Either they passed the provincial exams and moved away, or they failed repeatedly and eventually gave up, returning to their hometowns.\"","\"The layout of these houses is very well-considered, the courtyard feng shui is specially arranged, and servants clean them daily. You could move in immediately upon purchase.\"","In just two months, this young lady's status had climbed another rung.","Not only was her food shop thriving, but the reputation of her clinic had already surpassed that of Huiming Hall.","Few outsiders could establish such a firm foothold in Anyang Prefecture in such a short time, let alone when the head of the household was a sixteen-year-old girl.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Let's start by viewing the ones near the Anyang Academy. Given how much business I've brought your agency, you'd better lower the commission for me.\"","The agent smiled and fawned, \"Naturally, of course. We would have offered a lower rate even if you hadn't mentioned it.\"","\"With Song's Delicacies doing such brisk business, you'll probably be buying another shop before long. Please don't forget to come to me when that time comes.\"","The Anyang Academy's monthly exam for the Outer College arrived, and the monthly elimination assessment for the Inner College officially began.","Yan Baoyi glanced back at Song Qiming sitting in the last row, suppressed the anger in his heart, and focused on answering the questions.","This time, he absolutely had to outscore him.","Yang Yanfeng, who was proctoring the exam with Ding Weiyue, sat on the podium, his gaze resting on Song Qiming as he sized him up.","New students entering the Inner College, no matter how well they performed, typically only ranked in the middle to lower tiers initially. Some, unable to keep up, would even be sent back to the Outer College.","Song Qiming had been personally tutored by Ye Liangyu. It was uncertain what kind of result he would achieve in this monthly exam.","The academy's exam results were posted the next day. In front of the bulletin board, Song Gaoli excitedly threw an arm around Song Qiming's shoulders, his voice low with excitement. \"Ninth place! I can enter the Inner College!\"","Song Qiming's face broke into a brilliant smile. He tilted his chin towards the ranking list next to the Outer College monthly results. \"Seventh place. I've successfully stayed in the Inner College too.\"","\"Elder Sister bought a new residence. The academy has a break the day after tomorrow for moving. Come over for a meal.\"","Song Gaoli tilted his head. \"I think you're just calling me over to help with the move.\"","Song Qiming said, \"We have servants at home; it won't take long. If you don't want to come for the Manchu-Han Imperial Feast, that's fine.\"","\"I'm coming, I'm coming! How could I not go?\"","Song Gaoli grabbed Song Qiming's arm, spreading his own arms to demonstrate. \"Eating three meals a day in the academy dining hall, hardly any oil, average taste—I've gotten skinny from hunger.\"","Yan Baoyi stared fixedly at the two departing figures, all smiles, then turned to look at the rankings for who knows which time.","Nineteenth place. Twelve people stood between them; he wasn't even in the same row as Song Qiming anymore.","How could this be? He was just a farm boy with no private tutor. How could he possibly score so well just by attending academy classes?","He broke into the top ten, leaving me so far behind!","In a distant pavilion, Ji Youming, holding a white piece during a game of Go, set it down, raised his head, and smiled faintly. \"Seventh place right after entering. Don't you feel any pressure? There are only three spots for advancement to the Upper College each year.\"","His handsome, willow-leaf eyebrows arched upwards. Hu Fengye placed a black piece, blocking Ji Youming's path.","\"It's not just me who should worry, you're in the same boat. Competition breeds motivation. Our rivals are far more numerous than just those within the academy walls.\"","\"The provincial exams held every three years gather all the xiucai from the entire Longbei Province. The metropolitan exams every three years assemble juren from all corners of the Eastern Zhao Kingdom—the rivalry between north and south. Having one more Song Qiming in the mix only makes it better.\"","Ji Youming placed a piece to extricate himself. \"You're quite open-minded. Yan Baoyi certainly isn't thinking so broadly.\"","Hu Fengye shook his head with a cold laugh, his expression full of disdain. \"A self-important fool. He and Song Qiming are not cut from the same cloth.\"","Since entering the Inner College, everyone had witnessed the targeting of Song Qiming by Ding Weiyue and Yan Baoyi.","Despite all their overt and covert schemes, they had still been left far behind, unable to even catch his dust.","On moving day, both the food shop and the clinic only opened for the morning.","The new residence Song Jinzhao bought was slightly farther from the Anyang Academy than their previously rented courtyard, adding about a quarter of an hour to the walk.","But its advantage lay in its ample space, especially the small garden it included. Looking out from the rooms, one no longer saw walls but the lush, verdant scenery of the garden.","Song Gaoli arrived with gifts to help move things. Ye Liangyu sent his own servants over to assist as well.","Chunxing and Qingshuang were busy in the kitchen. Before the sun had set, a table laden with a sumptuous feast of meat and vegetable dishes was already laid out.","Song Gaoli stared at Song Qiming, who was chatting animatedly with Ye Liangyu. A formally acknowledged master-disciple relationship really was different. One could almost mistake them for father and son.","It's just that Mr. Ye's head of white hair made the age difference seem a bit off.","Father and son seemed a stretch, but grandfather and grandson felt slightly off too.","Ye Liangyu noticed Song Gaoli's gaze and glanced his way. \"I heard from Qiming that you tested into the Inner College?\"","Song Gaoli hurriedly nodded, scratching his head with an embarrassed smile. \"Ninth in the monthly exam. I almost had to wait another month. I'll be troubling you again from now on, sir.\"","From their earlier conversation, Song Gaoli had already learned that Ye Liangyu would begin teaching at the academy the next day, and it happened to be the Inner College class.","Ye Liangyu picked up his teacup, took a sip, and smiled kindly.","\"Ninth place isn't scraping by; tenth place is the borderline. Your current standing is the fruit of your hard work day and night.\"","During their brief three-month master-disciple relationship, Song Gaoli had been the least academically gifted of the three.","Perhaps from living alone in the dormitory, Ye Liangyu saw evident growth in him.","This change wasn't as pronounced in his observations of Song Qiming.","But from the moment he entered the house until now, whether facing Song Jinzhao or Ye Liangyu, Song Gaoli's attitude remained consistently humble and respectful, his personality having grown much more tactful."]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: Ye Liangyu Enters the Academy, Song Qiming Is His Disciple","paragraphs":["The next day, it was Mu Hongyue himself who went to pick up Ye Liangyu and bring him into the academy.","Yunhe pushed the wheelchair, and the passing students' gazes kept shifting between Mu Hongyue and Ye Liangyu.","Who was the man sitting in the wheelchair? Why was the academy head walking beside him?","Upon hearing the news, Yang Yanfeng was the first to rush out of the Wenjing Hall. He was finally here.","With Ye Liangyu's talent and learning, he would surely teach the Upper Division. But Song Qiming was in the Inner Division. Where would he go?","Ding Weiyue walked to the doorway, his gaze first hardening slightly as he noticed the wheelchair Ye Liangyu was sitting in. The moment he lowered his head, a trace of contempt flashed in his eyes, vanishing without a trace when he looked up again.","After entering the Wenjing Hall, Mu Hongyue announced before all the instructors, \"I presume everyone knows Master Ye. Our academy had to repeatedly urge and invite him before he agreed to come as an instructor. For now, he will teach the Inner Division.\"","All the teachers' eyes widened in shock.","Teaching the Inner Division? Shouldn't it be the Upper Division?","Which of those present could match this man's scholarly achievements or official rank? Teaching the Inner Division seemed like a demotion. Would Ye Liangyu accept it?","Yet when they looked at Ye Liangyu, they found he showed no dissatisfaction whatsoever; on the contrary, he was smiling.","This was utterly bizarre.","Ding Weiyue clenched his fist, his eyes darkening.","Among all the teachers in the Inner Division, his own talent and status were the highest. If Ye Liangyu came, he would undoubtedly overshadow him.","What should he do?","When Yunhe pushed Ye Liangyu onto the lecture platform, the students of the Inner Division were stunned.","Ji Youming and Hu Fengye, sitting in the front row, exchanged a glance. With him here, whether one went to the Upper Division or not seemed less important.","Song Gaoli and Su Luobai turned their heads and winked at Song Qiming.","Your master is here to back you up. No one would dare bully you now.","Noticing Song Qiming sitting in the last row, an unnoticed spot, Ye Liangyu was already displeased.","He directly had Yunhe push him down from the platform and stopped in the aisle to begin his lecture.","This forced the students in the front rows to keep turning their heads.","Throughout the lesson, Song Qiming received frequent attention from Ye Liangyu. Even the slowest in the room sensed something unusual.","Teacher Ye seemed to favor Song Qiming greatly.","When Song Qiming stood up to answer questions, Teacher Ye's expression remained smiling, in stark contrast to his more neutral demeanor towards others.","After class, Ye Liangyu openly called out to Song Qiming, \"Qiming, come out with your teacher for a moment.\"","The already quiet lecture hall fell so silent that even the sound of breathing vanished.","Someone's book fell to the floor with a 'thud,' the sound striking everyone's hearts and leaving their bodies numb.","After the morning lecture ended, Ding Weiyue came over. His gaze swept coldly over Song Qiming's face as he announced loudly, \"Seating will be rearranged according to the rankings of this month's exam, starting from first place. Choose wherever you want to sit.\"","Watching Ding Weiyue leave with a flick of his sleeve, the displeasure radiating from him was palpable to anyone.","After everyone had chosen their seats, Song Qiming sat in the middle of the third row, while Yan Baoyi moved to a desk by the wall in the fourth row.","Su Luobai leaned to the right, lowering his voice to whisper, \"It must have been Teacher Ye who demanded Master Ding change the seating. He was unhappy the moment he entered and saw you in the last row.\"","After classes ended at noon, Ji Youming pulled Hu Fengye out for a meal.","\"Who would have thought Song Qiming is Ye Liangyu's disciple? No wonder his progress has been so miraculous. With a master like that, Song Qiming entering the Upper Division is a certainty.\"","The corner of Hu Fengye's mouth lifted in a faint smile. \"If not for Song Qiming being in the Inner Division, Ye Liangyu probably wouldn't have come to teach there either.\"","Ji Youming shook his head helplessly. \"At the start of the term, all the academy's teachers who visited his home were turned away. Now he's willing to lower his status. Besides Song Qiming, I can't think of any other reason.\"","He held up three fingers. \"Three spots. Wang Rui sits high above like a cloud. You, me, and Song Qiming are competing for two. Who will get them?\"","Hu Fengye stabbed his chopsticks through a roast chicken. \"We'll each rely on our own abilities. But I know one thing: once Song Qiming passes into the Upper Division, Ye Liangyu will definitely follow.\"","In the Upper Division lecture hall, the mere ten students instantly erupted upon hearing that the former Vice Censor-in-Chief, a Second-Ranked Palace Graduate placed seventh overall, had gone to teach in the Inner Division.","\"Why didn't the Headmaster assign Elder Ye to the Upper Division? Are we less outstanding than the Inner Division students?\"","The annual academy exam only allowed three students to advance from the Inner to the Upper Division. Their teaching resources had always been the best. Now that Ye Liangyu had gone to the Inner Division, these proud talents began to feel unsettled.","The lecture hall door was pushed open from outside as Wang Xu walked in. \"It's because Elder Ye's disciple is in the Inner Division. That's why he went to teach there.\"","Everyone was puzzled. \"Who? Elder Ye has a disciple?\"","Wang Xu had just learned the news from his younger brother Wang Rui. Setting down his book, he said gravely, \"It's Song Qiming, this year's top candidate in the academy entrance exam. He just entered the Inner Division a month ago.\"","He Feixuan, the top student of the Upper Division, asked, \"What rank did he get in this month's Inner Division exam?\"","Wang Xu shook his head dejectedly, understanding He Feixuan's implication. \"Seventh.\"","The expressions of the Upper Division students darkened like a cloud covering the sun. Only seventh.","Only three students from the Inner Division could enter the Upper Division each year. Song Qiming wasn't even close.","If he couldn't pass the exam, would Elder Ye have to teach in the Inner Division for his entire life?","In just one morning, Song Qiming, at the center of the storm, received friendly treatment from his Inner Division classmates. Even former Outer Division classmates came to discuss essays with him.","Most of these people had previously wanted to stay far away from him, not even exchanging a nod when they met, let alone speaking.","Su Luobai threw an arm around Song Qiming's neck. \"Just give them a few perfunctory replies; you don't need to worry about saving their face. No one in the academy dares to offend you now.\"","Song Qiming turned a page in his book. \"I don't plan to engage with them. The most important thing now is the year-end exam. I can't let my teacher stay in the Inner Division with me forever.\"","Su Luobai shook his head with a sigh. \"Only three spots. Wang Rui, Ji Youming, Hu Fengye—they consistently dominate the top three in every exam. Trying to snatch a spot from them is extremely difficult.\"","Song Qiming looked up, his expression serious and determined, his right fist pressed on the paper. \"No matter how difficult, I must fight for it. Studying day and night, enduring hardship—I've never been afraid of that.\"","Su Luobai pressed his lips together, meeting Song Qiming's eyes. Already ranked seventh and still pushing this hard?","What were ordinary people like them supposed to do? Chase after him by not sleeping all day and night?","That evening, Yan Baoyi slammed a fist onto the desk in Ding Weiyue's home. \"Teacher, what should we do now? Just let Song Qiming overshadow me like this?\"","Seeing him lose control of his emotions in this furious state irritated Ding Weiyue immensely.","\"Right now, it's not just Song Qiming overshadowing you. There are a full eighteen people above you. From now on, don't just fixate on Song Qiming. Pour all your effort into studying. Don't dwell on anything else.\"","No matter how much the Yan family paid, it wasn't worth opposing Ye Liangyu. He couldn't afford to offend him either."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: Buying a Villa to Build a Farm","paragraphs":["Outside the city, on a dilapidated estate, muddy earth and crumbling courtyard walls were everywhere. If not for the three tiled-roof houses standing in the middle, anyone would think the place was deserted and uninhabited. How could this possibly be an estate for sale?","The agent stepped into a patch of mire, and foul-smelling muddy water splashed all over his clothes.","He looked at Song Jinzhao with a troubled expression, fearing she might turn and walk away immediately.","\"Though the estate is rundown, its advantage is its size. The farmland in front plus the small hill slope at the back totals two hundred mu. You can grow anything you want.\"","Fushun pushed open the main door, revealing a room full of cobwebs, with daylight even leaking through the roof.","He looked speechlessly at Song Jinzhao. Young mistress, are you really going to buy this estate?","By all appearances, it was an unwanted piece of junk, abandoned for who knows how many years.","Song Jinzhao planned to buy an estate outside the city to build a farm for raising poultry.","The butcher shops in the city could no longer supply enough goods. If she wanted to open a branch store, unless she shipped supplies from other cities, she would face a shortage of raw materials.","Seeing the state of the interior, the agent regretted not having sent someone to clean it up beforehand. Mainly, he hadn't expected Song Jinzhao to be interested.","If the deal fell through now, wouldn't his effort (and potential commission) be wasted?","\"The place is dilapidated, but when it was built, they used genuine, solid materials. Once cleaned and repaired, it will stand firm against any storm.\"","After inspecting the houses, Song Jinzhao took a stroll around the small hillside.","The slope wasn't large; one could walk its entirety in half a shichen.","\"The soil on the slope is exactly the same as the farmland in front—extremely poor drainage. With no river nearby, rice can't be grown here. What did the previous owner of this estate do with it?\"","The agent stealthily wiped sweat from his brow with his elbow. \"I heard it was rented out to tenant farmers. Later, a drought led to poor harvests, so no one rented it. It's been empty for several years.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head and stared at him. \"I suspect there were no harvests at all. They probably couldn't even afford the government grain tax.\"","The agent coughed awkwardly twice. \"Actually, they could have harvested some millet, but they stubbornly planted rice instead. Naturally, there was no yield.\"","Song Jinzhao confirmed, \"The deed states two hundred mu?\"","The agent nodded rapidly, afraid any delay might ruin the deal.","\"Exactly two hundred mu. The annual grain tax is levied as dry land. The main point is it's cheap—only one tael of silver per mu.\"","This estate was mortgaged to the agency by a merchant at the end of the year before last. They originally intended to sell it, but who knew they couldn't find a single buyer?","Stuck with it for two years, just on grain taxes for last year and this year, the agency had lost five taels of silver, not to mention the original two hundred taels the estate was mortgaged for.","Now selling it for two hundred taels, the Jinyun Agency was actually taking a loss.","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"Too expensive. I think it's only worth one hundred taels.\"","The agent's face stiffened like a brick, his heart filled with bitterness.","\"Miss Song, you must be joking. One hundred taels would mean our agency loses half.\"","Song Jinzhao rubbed the toe of her shoe on the ground. Sandy loam soil was best for planting sweet potatoes and potatoes, but unfortunately, they weren't available here.","\"Leaving it empty means losing even more. I offer one hundred taels. At least you can recoup a loss of one hundred taels.\"","The agent shook his head vehemently. \"Really can't do it. One hundred taels is far too little. At most, we can lower it by ten taels.\"","The agency had never done business at a loss; this was the first time.","If that merchant back then hadn't been left with only this estate, they wouldn't have agreed to take it as debt payment.","Song Jinzhao pointed at the house and courtyard walls, which were practically ruins. \"It's already in this state. I'd have to spend over ten taels just to tear it down and rebuild.\"","The agent waved his right hand dismissively. \"No need to tear it down. Only the courtyard walls need rebuilding with a fence. The house just needs a good cleaning and minor repairs to be livable.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"How about your agency repairs the house first, then I'll pay one hundred and fifty taels.\"","The agent pursed his lips, thinking hard for a long while, before finally speaking with difficulty, trying to close the deal.","\"No repairs on the house. One hundred and fifty taels as is. The original price of this estate was two hundred taels. Our agency is already selling at a loss.\"","Song Jinzhao walked another half-circle along the ridge. The two sides remained deadlocked for a long time, and the agent refused to lower the price further.","\"This estate belongs to your agency. Does that mean the commission fee is waived?\"","The agent's soles were already aching from walking. He clenched his jaw and said firmly, \"Naturally.\"","Early the next morning, after completing the transfer at the magistrate's office, Song Jinzhao went to the slave market again.","Qian Sanya saw her and greeted her with an enthusiastic smile. \"Back to buy servants, miss? A new batch arrived just yesterday. Several have skills, and one is even literate. You're sure to like them.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"The requirements aren't as high this time. Preferably refugees sold into servitude, the cheaper the better.\"","Upon hearing this, Qian Sanya led Song Jinzhao to sit in the courtyard and called a group of people over.","\"These are all five taels each. Pick as you please, miss.\"","Song Jinzhao took their deeds of sale and looked them over. They were all displaced farmers, some even from the same village.","She selected eighteen male slaves and two female slaves, all between thirty and forty years old.","First, clean up the estate, then immediately start building the chicken coop, duck pen, and pigsty.","The two female slaves were left at the shop for Chunxing and Qingshuang to train, while Fushun went to oversee the estate.","Lan Xi sat cross-legged on the bed, slightly tense. Song Jinzhao stood beside him, watching.","\"Relax, don't be nervous. Just like going to sleep, don't think of anything. Shixue, proceed.\"","Song Shixue took a deep breath, picked up a silver needle, and inserted it into Lan Xi's Baihui point, Fengchi point, Hegu point, Taichong point...","A drilling pain in his head made Lan Xi frown tightly. The longer it went on, the more sweat beaded on his forehead and neck.","His limbs had mostly recovered, and he would be able to walk normally before long.","Fushun couldn't manage the estate alone, and he wasn't very literate. Song Jinzhao planned to cure Lan Xi's eyes as soon as possible so he could go help at the estate.","Although the boy was young, he was mature for his age. With Fushun there, she could worry less about the farm herself.","Every four days, silver needles were used to clear the meridians in his head, combined with decoctions to invigorate blood circulation and dispel stasis. If all went well, results would be seen within a month.","At the Guo residence, Guo Yiyao looked at the table full of various mutually incompatible dishes. Her expression had shifted from initial shock and grievance to now numbness and hatred.","\"The wedding is in one month. Liu Fufeng is growing increasingly impatient.\"","Qiu Ye's hand holding the chopsticks trembled. \"Raw ginkgo nuts paired with river clams... how did they even come up with that?\"","\"Young mistress, I've recorded all these days' menus and snacks on paper. The evidence is solid. Should we tell the master?\"","Guo Yiyao shook her head, saying solemnly, \"If we expose this ourselves, for the sake of the family's reputation, Father will certainly protect Liu Fufeng, not letting her bear the stigma of harming her stepdaughter.\"","\"Since they set this trap, they must be the ones to fall into it.\"","Qiu Ye gritted her teeth and clenched her fists. If the mistress were still here, how could she let the young mistress suffer such injustice?","For nearly ten years, she had endured humiliation to preserve the peace. Finally enduring until marriage, and now they want to ruin her wedding.","Childbearing is a matter of great importance for a woman. How can they be so venomous, determined to ruin her entire life?"]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: Invited to the Meng Family's Birthday Banquet","paragraphs":["Nanny Lu entered the room holding two paper packets, a look of triumph on her face.","\"Madam, it's done.\"","\"These are the medicinal dregs found in the Eldest Young Lady's rear courtyard. Qiu Ye was sneaking around burying them in the soil. If our people hadn't been meticulous, they would never have been discovered.\"","Upon opening the packets, a pungent odor wafted out. Liu Fufeng wrinkled her nose in distaste, covering it with a handkerchief as she leaned back.","\"Have they been shown to a physician? What ailment are these dregs meant to treat?\"","Nanny Lu pointed to the dregs on the right. \"On the surface, they were brewing this one for stomach troubles and poor appetite. But the dregs Qiu Ye secretly buried are actually from a formula for regulating menstruation and treating infertility. They're trying to pull the wool over everyone's eyes.\"","Liu Fufeng let out a cold laugh. \"She certainly has her ways, managing to procure medicine even without leaving the house.\"","She pointed at the dregs on the left and pressed, \"How effective is this prescription? Can it cure Guo Yiyao's condition?\"","Nanny Lu shook her head, eager to claim credit, her plump cheeks squeezing together into several unpleasantly deep folds.","\"Rest assured, Madam. After two months of consuming those specially prepared meals, the Young Lady's condition cannot be cured so easily.\"","\"She cannot leave the estate. Whether it's because the physician Qiu Ye found is incompetent, or because she couldn't describe her symptoms clearly, the prescription is flawed. It's missing two key herbs, and the dosages are incorrect. The treatment effect is minimal at best; it simply won't cure her.\"","Liu Fufeng leaned back against the soft pillows on her daybed, a wave of satisfaction washing over her. \"Afraid the Meng family will find out, she dares not let word of such an illness spread.\"","\"In a few days, it will be Old Madam Meng's birthday. Since she has recently recovered from her illness, the Meng family plans a grand celebration. If, on such an occasion, Guo Yiyao were to appear as if suffering a miscarriage... even if a physician later diagnosed it as a misunderstanding, her condition of being unfit for pregnancy would be impossible to conceal.\"","\"The Meng family would surely disdain her and demand to break off the engagement. That's when I will propose a substitution. Both the Master and the Meng family will agree.\"","Inside the Song Family Clinic, Song Jinzhao was checking the account books.","Once the farm connected to the hills behind the villa estate was built, they would buy a first batch of piglets.","Before the weather turned cold, they should also incubate another batch of breeding eggs, aiming for them to hatch before November. By the following spring, the chickens and ducks would be ready for market.","The 120 mu of vacant land in front of the estate could be used to plant peanuts come spring. If the peanuts didn't sell, they could be pressed for oil. The peanut oil market here was completely untapped; she would be the first to seize the opportunity.","As for the idle time during winter, she pondered setting up a vegetable greenhouse. It might yield a considerable profit.","\"Miss Song.\"","Both Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue looked up.","\"Miss Bihe.\" It was Old Madam Meng's personal maidservant.","Bihe walked up to Song Jinzhao with a smile and respectfully presented a golden-edged birthday invitation with both hands.","\"In three days, it will be my mistress's sixty-fifth birthday. She specifically asked me to deliver this invitation to you, Miss. You must bring your family to join the festivities.\"","Song Jinzhao took the invitation and opened it.","Bihe made polite conversation. \"That day coincides with a break at Anyang Academy. Several of the teaching masters will be attending. You could bring Young Master Song and the Second Young Lady Song along to the banquet.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly and closed the invitation. \"Thank you for making the trip, Miss Bihe. If nothing comes up, I will certainly bring my younger brother and sister to offer our congratulations to the Old Madam.\"","Bihe gave a slight nod, bid farewell, and turned to leave.","Liu Xuanqing handed a wrapped package of medicine to a patient, then turned to remind Song Jinzhao.","\"Every year for Old Madam Meng's birthday banquet, Lord Meng invites all the dignitaries and nobles of Anyang Prefecture. If you wish to make connections, this is an excellent opportunity.\"","The golden invitation gleamed on the table. After returning home, Song Jinzhao mentioned the matter to Song Qiming.","\"The Meng residence also sent an invitation to my teacher. He said he would take me along.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow in slight surprise.","Ye Liangyu still couldn't walk without his crutches. He went to the academy in a wheelchair pushed by a servant and rarely went out otherwise.","Considering the number of guests at the birthday banquet, it was surprising he had agreed.","\"In that case, stay with Master Ye then. I expect the men's and women's seating will be in separate areas.\"","Song Anhao tugged on Song Jinzhao's clothes, looking up at her to plead. \"Anhao wants to go too.\"","Song Jinzhao picked him up and sat him on her lap, putting on a stern face. \"There will be many people at the banquet, and your elder sister won't be able to watch you closely. You stay home and be good.\"","Song Anhao buried his head in Song Jinzhao's neck, wriggling his body like an itchy caterpillar. \"Anhao wants to go. Anhao will go. Eldest Sister, take me.\"","It really would be inconvenient to bring a two-year-old to such an event.","Song Shixue pointed at Lanxi, who was sweeping the courtyard. \"Second Sister will have Lanxi stay home and play ball with you.\"","Song Anhao stopped wriggling. His two faint, misty eyebrows, delicate as distant mountains, furrowed together adorably.","He tilted his head, resting it on Song Jinzhao's shoulder. \"Alright then. But remember to bring back tasty treats. I want date paste rolls.\""]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: The Disturbance at the Gate of the Meng Family Mansion","paragraphs":["In the courtyard, Lan Xi, who was holding a broom and sweeping dried leaves into a dustpan, suddenly felt a wave of dizziness before his eyes. His right hand instinctively reached out to steady himself against a tree trunk.","Blinking rapidly, his vision was filled with a gray haze, as if a bright light was shining directly into his eyeballs.","\"What's wrong with you?\" Noticing his unnatural sway and near fall, Song Shixue ran over to ask with concern.","Lan Xi steadied himself, his right hand moving to cover his eyes, which had lost their sight once again. Surprise was quickly followed by fear.","\"Just now, this eye seemed to see for a moment, but now it's gone again.\"","Hearing this, Song Shixue moved to stand in front of Lan Xi, looking up to examine his eyes.","\"Can you see my hand? Does your eye feel anything?\"","Lan Xi shook his head. \"I can't see, but it feels like there's a breeze on my eye, cool.\"","Song Shixue took the broom and dustpan from his hands and placed them beside him, then grasped his elbow to guide him back to his room.","\"It's normal for your eyes to have reactions during the treatment. It means the time for your sight to return is coming soon.\"","\"The light is harsh. Don't stay outside too long. Next time you go out, cover your eyes so you won't be suddenly stimulated like this.\"","The spot on his elbow where she held him through his clothes felt scalding hot. He allowed himself to be led into the room and seated like a soulless shell.","Staring at her retreating figure, his pale blue pupils seemed somewhat vacant.","Song Shixue reported Lan Xi's condition to Song Jinzhao.","Reduce the dosage of the prescription. Change the meridian-clearing treatment from once every four days to once every seven days.","Song Shixue nodded in understanding. \"I see. I'll change the prescription tomorrow.\"","Qiu Ye entered Guo Yiyao's boudoir with a grim expression, carrying a tray, her voice low and dejected. \"Miss, this is the dress Madam just had Nanny Lu deliver. She said it was specially tailored for you for Old Madame Meng's birthday banquet.\"","Staring at the plain white dress Qiu Ye unfolded, were it not for the few embroidered pink peach blossoms, one might have mistaken it for mourning attire at first glance.","\"Aunt Meng gifted me a light purple gauze dress with scattered blossoms for the spring flower-viewing banquet this year. I'll wear that one on the day of the birthday banquet.\"","Qiu Ye bit her lip and lifted the white dress disdainfully. \"What about this one?\"","A cool, detached light shone in Guo Yiyao's eyes, devoid of any warmth, appearing both aloof and indifferent.","\"The dress got stained with ink and became unwearable, so naturally I had to change. The other dress was a gift from Aunt Meng, making it all the more appropriate.\"","On the day of the banquet, seeing Guo Yiyao not wearing the plain white dress, Liu Fufeng frowned with displeasure.","\"Today is the last time you'll meet the Meng family before marrying into their household, and on such a formal occasion as a birthday banquet. Why are you wearing this outfit? It looks too somber.\"","\"What about the dress I had Nanny Lu send over? That's the new autumn style from Brocade Cloud Workshop. Do you dislike your mother's taste, is that why you don't want to wear it?\"","Guo Yiyao's father, Guo Qishi, narrowed his eyes at her, displeasure rising in his gaze.","Guo Yiyao curtsied, her brows and eyes filled with self-reproach. \"The dress Mother chose is naturally excellent. Unfortunately, I accidentally knocked over an inkstone while fetching Buddhist scriptures, and ink splattered all over the dress. I had no choice but to change.\"","\"This dress was a gift from Aunt Meng when she invited me to the flower-viewing banquet this year. I thought wearing this would show closer affinity, so I chose it. It was my fault for not considering the color might be too subdued.\"","Hearing that the dress was a gift from Madame Meng, the displeasure on Guo Qishi's face instantly vanished, replaced by satisfaction.","\"You'll be marrying into the Meng residence soon. It's good to dress somewhat conservatively.\"","\"Why aren't Zhi'er and Shu'er out yet? Don't dawdle and delay us.\"","\"Father, there will be so many people at the banquet today. I have to dress properly.\"","The moment she saw Guo Yishu, Guo Yiyao's politely smiling pupils contracted slightly.","A jade-green misty gauze dress, its colors as dazzlingly bright as rosy clouds—this was the genuine new-season treasure from Brocade Cloud Workshop.","Guo Qishi raised his eyebrows, nodding in satisfied admiration. \"Your mother's taste is still the best. This dress looks very beautiful on Shu'er.\"","Guo Yishu shot a covert glare at Guo Yiyao, her dark gaze fixing on the light purple gauze dress Guo Yiyao wore, her lips pursed in jealousy.","Even if Guo Yiyao's dress couldn't compare to her own, it was a gift from Madame Meng, which made its significance different.","Wearing it on purpose to show off was just to curry favor with the Meng family.","Song Jinzhao went to the banquet first with Song Shixue, while Song Qiming would arrive later with Ye Liangyu.","As their carriage neared the entrance of the Meng residence, it stopped. Fushun turned his head to explain to those inside, \"Young Miss, the road ahead is blocked by too many carriages and sedan chairs.\"","Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain to look ahead. A dark mass of vehicles left no room to even step down. Who knew how long they would have to wait for their turn.","\"The Meng residence is just ahead. We'll get off here. Take the carriage to the shop entrance and come back to fetch us in an hour.\"","Guo Yishu irritably pulled open the carriage window, her voice sharp. \"How much longer do we have to wait? Can't they let us through first?\"","The coachman found it hard to voice his difficulties. Even if someone was willing to yield, there was simply no space ahead to move into. They could only wait.","\"Who is that? Among the guests invited by the Meng residence, there are those who can't even afford a carriage or sedan chair? Their clothes look splendid, though. Who are they putting on a front for?\"","Guo Yishu looked disdainfully at Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue, who were walking past their carriage, displeased at being overtaken.","With keen hearing, Song Jinzhao halted her steps. She turned towards the source of the voice, her gaze settling on Guo Yishu, who had stuck her head out of the window.","Guo Yishu's fingers slid across her exquisitely embroidered collar as she shot Song Jinzhao a haughty, scornful look.","\"What are you looking at? You don't even have a carriage and dare to get ahead of me? Don't you know the distinction between superior and inferior, noble and base? You have no manners at all.\"","She knew all the dignitaries and nobles in Anyang Prefecture. These two were on foot and not accompanied by a matriarch. They were probably from some newly arrived minor family, rushing to flatter Prefect Meng by taking advantage of Old Madame Meng's birthday banquet.","Song Jinzhao's calm, placid eyes lightly fixed on Guo Yishu's face.","\"Whether I have manners or not, I don't know. What I do know is that the main street is not a latrine. If you need to relieve yourself, go home and do it. Spraying it everywhere—you may have no shame, but I still find it disgusting.\"","Inside the carriage, Guo Yiyao, hearing these shocking words, couldn't help but shift and crane her neck, wanting to see who was arguing with Guo Yishu.","Seeing the familiar face, she blinked in astonishment. It was Doctor Song.","Seeing Guo Yiyao appear in the carriage, Song Jinzhao's eyebrows raised slightly, curious about this family's identity.","Hearing that Song Jinzhao actually dared to insult her, Guo Yishu, who had never suffered any grievance, immediately wanted to get down from the carriage to teach Song Jinzhao a lesson.","Liu Fufeng pressed down on her hand with a dark expression. \"Don't start a dispute at the Meng residence's doorstep.\" They could settle the score later by finding them after returning home.","Catching a glimpse of Guo Yiyao's composed face from the corner of her eye, Guo Yishu felt as if the other was mocking her.","She angrily threw a threat at Song Jinzhao, \"You just wait. I won't let this matter rest today.\"","In the entire Anyang Prefecture, aside from the Prefect, her father, the Assistant Prefect, held the highest authority. It would be easy to teach two people a lesson later; even if they were beaten half to death, no one would dare utter a word.","Song Jinzhao curled her lip. Such lawless arrogance likely meant they came from an official family. She wondered what rank they held, and if it was high enough for her to kill.","Guo Yishu clenched her fists and closed the carriage window. After the birthday banquet concluded, she would definitely make that woman pay.","This matter wouldn't be settled until she was forced to kneel and kowtow one hundred and eighty-eight times.","After entering the Meng residence, a maid smilingly led Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue into the inner courtyard.","Seeing unfamiliar faces, and two young ladies unattended by any matron, many began inquiring about Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue's identities.","\"Whose daughters are these? Why haven't we seen them before?\"","Old Lady Meng spotted Song Jinzhao from afar and hurriedly waved for Bihe to bring her over.","She turned to Old Lady Liao and said, \"The Doctor Song I mentioned has arrived. If you don't believe me, you can ask her yourself. The needle went in and out of my belly just like sewing clothes.\"","When Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue entered the flower hall, all the ladies seated inside turned their gazes towards the two.","So this was the highly skilled Doctor Song. She looked far too young, perhaps not even of age yet.","Song Jinzhao placed her hands folded before her abdomen and gave a slight curtsy. \"Congratulations on your birthday, Madam. May your golden daylilies ever flourish, and your motherly bamboo enjoy enduring spring.\"","Old Lady Meng chuckled happily and bid Song Jinzhao to rise. \"There's no need for such formality, Miss Song. You are my lifesaver. Please, come sit here.\"","Song Jinzhao handed the brocade box in her hand to Bihe and calmly took a seat.","Old Lady Liao, sitting beside Old Lady Meng, looked at Song Jinzhao and said, \"I've long heard that Anyang Prefecture's new female physician is not only highly skilled but also very young. Seeing you today, I wonder, Miss Song, if you have come of age?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded calmly. \"I came of age last year.\"","After nearly a quarter-hour of introductions and small talk, Song Jinzhao had a fairly good understanding of the identities of the dozen or so ladies in the flower hall.","They were all the elderly matriarchs and ruling mistresses from official families in Anyang Prefecture.","Old Lady Liao was the mother of the Vice Prefect of Anyang Prefecture, the very Liao family that, like the Mengs some time ago, had summoned every physician in the prefecture for a consultation.","She was Old Lady Meng's close friend since their maiden days, and their relationship was intimate."]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: Miscarried Twelve Times: A Plot Within a Plot","paragraphs":["Guo Yishu walked into the flower hall and saw Song Jinzhao sitting on the stool, her expression changing slightly.","Why was she sitting in that seat?","Madam Meng saw Guo Yiyao enter and a gentle smile appeared on her face. \"Why are you so late today? Mother and I have been talking about you for a while now.\"","Guo Yiyao curtsied. \"The stream of distinguished guests coming to offer birthday congratulations today was endless, causing some delay on the road. I apologize for my tardiness, Old Madam Meng.\"","Old Madam Meng glanced at Madam Meng and reached out, gesturing for Guo Yiyao to come over and take her hand.","\"Grandmother is already overjoyed that you could come. But you look quite thinner; was it the hot weather recently affecting your appetite?\"","Standing nearby, Guo Yishu clenched her back teeth tightly to suppress the jealousy in her heart and keep it from showing.","After Liu Fufeng sat down, she inquired of the lady beside her, \"Who is that young lady in the light green dress?\"","The lady promptly replied, \"That's Song Jinzhao. She's the one who cured Old Madam Meng's illness.\"","Guo Yishu, sitting nearby, heard this and breathed a sigh of relief, murmuring quietly, \"So she's just a physician.\"","Liu Fufeng, her hand under the low table, pressed it onto the back of Guo Yishu's hand and shot her a sharp look.","Guo Yishu looked puzzled, not understanding why her mother had suddenly scolded her.","She wasn't wrong; she was just a physician.","Liu Fufeng let out a heavy sigh, feeling some regret.","Song Jinzhao might just be a physician, but her younger brother is a disciple of Ye Liangyu. It's best not to offend such people if possible. She should have stopped her daughter earlier.","Liao Xiwen, sitting next to Old Madam Liao, stole several glances at Song Jinzhao. When their eyes met, she smiled sheepishly and suggested, \"The chrysanthemums in the courtyard are in full bloom. Would you like to go out and admire them together, Miss Song?\"","Song Shixue secretly tried to get Song Jinzhao's attention under the table with her hand.","Having been sitting there eating and listening to people she didn't know talk, she was starting to feel restless.","\"I'd be delighted not to refuse. I noticed the beautiful chrysanthemums when I came in and was just wishing for someone to enjoy them with.\"","Song Jinzhao quietly left with Song Shixue and Liao Xiwen. Only after stepping out of the flower hall did the air feel fresh again.","The three of them stood before a pot of chrysanthemums. Liao Xiwen grabbed Song Jinzhao's sleeve, the smile fading from her face.","She gazed into Song Jinzhao's eyes and asked, \"Is your medical skill truly that excellent?\"","As if sensing her plea, Song Jinzhao countered with a question, \"Does Miss Liao have some matter you need help with?\"","Liao Xiwen released her grip. The rouge on her lips was slightly smudged from her biting them. \"I would like to invite you to the Liao residence to examine my mother.\"","Hadn't the Liao residence invited so many physicians recently without curing Madam Liao's illness?","It had been over a month already.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"May I ask what ailment your esteemed mother suffers from?\"","Liao Xiwen's gaze fell on the chrysanthemum's stamen. Her voice was soft and distant, as if it would scatter with a breeze.","\"A month ago, my mother had a miscarriage. The physician said she can never bear children again. Since then, she's become deeply melancholic, and recently she hasn't even been able to get out of bed.\"","Song Jinzhao's expression turned serious. \"How old is your esteemed mother, and how many months along was the pregnancy when she miscarried?\"","The mere thought of the circumstances of the miscarriage filled Liao Xiwen's heart with bitterness.","\"My mother is thirty-two this year. The child was lost at six months. The physician said it was a fully formed male infant.\"","Song Jinzhao instinctively pressed further, \"How many children has your esteemed mother given birth to in total?\"","Thirty-two was considered quite old for childbearing in ancient times. Liao Xiwen looked to be only in her teens, so she must have been pregnant more than once in between.","Liao Xiwen wrung her hands together. \"My mother only has me, one daughter. But she has been pregnant several times before, and each ended in miscarriage.\"","\"Several times?\"","\"Since I can remember, twelve times in total.\"","Song Shixue, who had been admiring the flowers nearby, immediately froze, straightening her back to look at Liao Xiwen.","Twelve times. That was far too many.","Song Jinzhao's brows knitted tightly together. \"Were they natural miscarriages or accidents? How many months along was she each time?\"","Twelve miscarriages would cause immense damage to a woman's body.","She needed to determine if the miscarriages were due to innate factors, acquired circumstances, or... human intervention?","Liao Xiwen glanced around, then took small, quick steps closer to Song Jinzhao, leaning in to whisper by her arm.","\"Some were miscarriages for no apparent reason, some were accidents. Most didn't go beyond three months. This last pregnancy lasted the longest. We all thought it would come to term, but then she suddenly started bleeding, and the child couldn't be saved.\"","\"The physicians said the physical damage from the miscarriage can be treated with tonics, but the distress in her heart is hard to cure. That's why I wanted you to see my mother. If she could still bear children, her heartache would naturally be resolved.\"","Song Jinzhao swallowed hard, uncomfortably averting her gaze and shaking her head.","\"So many physicians have said it's impossible. I can only take a look first. As for whether she can bear children again, I cannot make any promises.\"","Trying to have a child after twelve miscarriages was practically playing with one's own life.","At the entrance of the Meng residence, the steward, upon seeing Ye Liangyu being helped down from the carriage, immediately sent a servant inside to announce his arrival.","Meng Hechuan, seeing Ye Liangyu enter leaning on a cane, felt a flicker of shock in his eyes.","Wasn't it said his legs were crippled and he could never stand or walk again? How could he now be using a cane?","He stepped forward and cupped his hands in salute. \"Master Ye honors us by gracing my mother's birthday banquet. Our humble Meng residence is truly illuminated.\"","Ye Liangyu raised a hand to stop Meng Hechuan's gesture. \"This old man no longer holds an official post. There's no need for such formality, Lord Meng.\"","After being invited to the seat of honor, the gazes of everyone in the main hall focused on the two men sitting at the head of the room.","Li Tianchong's eyes swept over Song Qiming sitting below Ye Liangyu. \"Ye Liangyu's legs must be related to Song Jinzhao. This makes his connection to the Song family even closer.\"","Li Zien lowered her head and whispered her guess, \"If his legs are completely healed, might he be reinstated to his official post and return to the capital?\"","Li Tianchong held his breath, concentrating. Given the Emperor's trust in Ye Liangyu, a single word from him would make reinstatement a simple matter.","This news needed to be relayed to the Second Prince as soon as possible.","A fearless, outspoken Censor-in-Chief deeply trusted by the Emperor was like a club—anyone who ran into him would have a hard time.","After exchanging a few pleasantries, Meng Hechuan glanced at Song Qiming and said to Ye Liangyu, \"When this official went to Song Village to deliver the imperial decree, I saw Qiming and thought even then this child would achieve great things in the future. I never imagined he would become your disciple, Master Ye. It seems you hold him in high regard?\"","When talking about Song Qiming, the affection in Ye Liangyu's eyes and the pride in his tone were evident to anyone—his satisfaction with this disciple was clear.","\"This old man has only taken Qiming as my disciple in this lifetime, so naturally I have high hopes for him. The boy has talent and works hard. I am truly fond of him.\"","Yan Baoyi, sitting on a stool in the distance, kept his face lowered. Hearing the crowd's flattery of the master and disciple, his eyes turned bloodshot.","He couldn't surpass him in exams, but at least his family background was better.","Now, with Ye Liangyu backing him, even his status had been overtaken.","Why did all the good fortune in the world fall on Song Qiming? A lowly farm boy from a humble background—what right did he have?","When the banquet began at noon, a huge red character for 'Longevity' hung in the central hall. The Meng family had invited the most famous opera troupe in Anyang Prefecture to perform. The stage was set up across from the pond.","It provided a clear view and displayed their refined taste.","A thin gauze curtain separated the men's seating area from the women's. Voices could be heard, but faces were unclear.","Song Shixue strained her eyes, trying to locate where Song Qiming was sitting, but after looking for a long time, she couldn't find him.","Song Jinzhao pointed to the table at the very front and said, \"Master Ye is sitting next to Lord Meng. Your brother is at the table right behind him, back-to-back.\"","Song Shixue leaned forward, but the gauze curtain in between only allowed her to see a vague silhouette.","\"Forget it, I'll see Brother soon anyway. If I'd known the banquet would be this boring, I wouldn't have come. I'd have been better off reading a few more pages of medical texts at home.\"","Song Jinzhao reached out and gently patted the young girl's head. \"It's good to get out and about. At least this time you've seen all the officials and merchants of Anyang Prefecture, big and small.\"","The birthday banquet was halfway through, and the opera on stage had already changed three times.","Liu Fufeng exchanged a glance with Nanny Lu, who then silently turned and left the main hall.","Song Shixue pressed her legs together and whispered, covering her mouth, \"Elder Sister, I need to use the privy.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and led Shixue away from their seats. Once outside the main hall entrance, she stopped a maid and asked, \"Excuse me, where is the privy?\"","The maid respectfully curtsied and led the way. \"This way, please, honored guests.\"","While Shixue was inside, Song Jinzhao and the maid waited not far from the privy.","After a while, with no sign of her coming out, Jinzhao called out from the doorway.","Song Shixue's voice came out, strained and muffled. \"Elder Sister, I have a bit of diarrhea. Please wait a little longer for me.\"","\"No rush, take your time. I'll be right outside.\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to the maid. \"You may go back. I'll take my sister back myself once she's done.\"","The maid glanced at the privy. Considering it wasn't far from the main hall and there was much to attend to at the banquet, she curtsied in reply. \"Then this servant will take her leave. The main hall is just through the rockery ahead. Please don't lose your way, miss.\"","Song Jinzhao waved her hand. \"It's just a few steps, I won't get lost. You may go.\"","Not long after, Song Shixue emerged from the privy, her legs numb. \"Elder Sister, I'm done.\"","\"How did you get diarrhea all of a sudden? Did you kick off your blankets and catch a chill last night?\"","Song Shixue's eyes darted about, looking pitiful. \"I had a bowl of frozen cheese last night. Probably chilled my stomach.\"","Song Jinzhao scowled. \"Frozen cheese in the middle of the night? Don't you remember what's happening in a few days? Be careful of stomach cramps.\"","Shixue said, \"I remember. But it's still days away. I won't eat it again.\"","As they turned around the rockery, the scene that met their eyes made Song Jinzhao swiftly cover Shixue's mouth and pull her into the rocks.","It was Nanny Lu from Liu Fufeng's side. The other woman looked like a servant of the Meng household. They were putting something into a bowl.","Song Shixue kept her mouth tightly shut, her eyes signaling Jinzhao to let go. Her voice was smaller than a mosquito's hum. \"Elder Sister, what are they doing?\"","Song Jinzhao observed the situation outside through a small hole in the rockery. She saw the two women stir the contents of the bowl with a spoon after adding the substance, then leave one after the other.","\"I don't know, but it's certainly nothing good.\" She just didn't know who the target of this scheme was.","When the two returned to the banquet, they happened to see that same maid serving at the table where Liu Fufeng and others were seated. The soup bowls were already in many people's hands, being drunk.","Song Shixue stared at the identical soup bowl on their own table, goosebumps rising all over. She felt sure it contained poison too.","Song Jinzhao's gaze swept over that table. Recalling Guo Yiyao's visit to the clinic, a suspicion formed in her mind.","Guo Yiyao was Meng Xiaozhe's fiancée. They were to be married in a month. If something happened to her now, who would benefit the most?","Liu Fufeng was the stepmother, and that nanny was her person. Catching sight of Guo Yishu, dressed flamboyantly and sitting beside Liu Fufeng, a cold smile curled at the corner of Song Jinzhao's mouth.","Coveting her future brother-in-law—that was exactly the kind of thing Guo Yishu would do. That mother and daughter pair were cut from the same cloth.","Since the soup had already been drunk, they would just have to see what happened next. Not getting involved would be a disservice to Guo Yishu's arrogant behavior outside the mansion earlier.","After the time it takes to drink a few cups of tea, noticing Guo Yiyao's maid helping her to her feet, Song Jinzhao whispered to Song Shixue, \"Stay seated and don't move. I'll be right back.\"","Song Shixue nodded seriously, guessing her sister was going to deal with the drugging incident.","Song Jinzhao followed Guo Yiyao out of the main hall. She saw her being led by the maid who had administered the drug into a room.","Was this a scheme involving aphrodisiacs and being caught in bed?","Song Jinzhao poked a small hole in the window paper with her finger. The mistress and maid inside were changing clothes. No man was in sight.","Seeing Guo Yiyao pull a hairpin from her head and forcefully draw a cut on her arm, then smear the blood onto the discarded skirt, Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in surprise, a flash of delight in her eyes.","This development was unexpected. A scheme within a scheme?","After changing clothes, Qiu Ye opened the door. The maid waiting outside stepped forward, picked up the garments, and said respectfully with a smile, \"This servant will take these to the laundry immediately. Once they are washed and starched, we will send someone to deliver them to your residence.\"","Guo Yiyao gave a slight nod. \"I ate a bit too much earlier and feel unwell. I'll rest here for a moment. You may go.\"","The maid hurried off with the clothes.","Watching Guo Yiyao pick up a vase, smash it on the ground, and use a shard to press against the cut on her arm made by the hairpin, Song Jinzhao's eyes curved into a smile as she turned and left.","The mantis stalks the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind. A good show was about to unfold.","A maid from the Meng household ran up to Liu Fufeng with a face full of anxiety. \"Madam Liu, please come quickly! Miss Guo... she's bleeding heavily down below.\"","Liu Fufeng frowned and murmured, \"Two months without it, and it had to come now.\"","Her voice was neither too loud nor too soft, just enough for everyone at the table to hear.","Song Shixue, who had been sitting on her stool attentively observing the surroundings, turned to look.","Bleeding? The one who was drugged was that young lady who came to the clinic!","She was about to stand up when a pair of slender hands pressed down on her shoulders. Looking up, she called out happily, \"Elder Sister!\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head with a slight smile, leaning close to whisper in her ear, \"Don't worry. It's nothing serious.\"","They saw the maid, after delivering her message, skillfully avoid Madam Meng and instead whisper a few words into Old Madam Meng's ear.","Seeing the women of the Guo and Meng families leaving one after another, many of the guests began to feel restless.","As Liu Fufeng saw Old Madam Meng following them out, her expression grew somewhat unnatural. She forced a smile and said, \"Yao'er has been discourteous. It's unfortunate her monthly courses have come today. Please forgive her, Old Madam.\"","Seeing her behave as if she were covering something up, Old Madam Meng's gaze turned sharp. \"But I heard Yiyao hasn't had her courses for two months?\"","Madam Meng, standing beside them, looked anxiously between Liu Fufeng and Old Madam Meng's faces, hoping nothing was amiss."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: No Menstrual Period and No Miscarriage","paragraphs":["Seeing Liu Fufeng's face full of guilt, the sensitive nerves in the minds of the women who had followed to join the commotion began to twitch.","Suddenly, someone in the crowd said, \"Could it be that Miss Guo has had a miscarriage?\"","This sentence was like a bomb, shocking everyone, whether they had considered the possibility or not.","Guo Yiyao and Meng Xiaozhe were still a month away from their wedding, so how could she possibly be pregnant? Was it an illicit affair or a pregnancy before marriage?","Madam Meng said sternly, \"It's just irregular menstruation. Yiyao has been preparing for her wedding at the Guo residence all this time and hasn't even stepped out the door. How could she possibly be pregnant?\"","Seeing Madam Meng still speaking up for Guo Yiyao, a dark glint flashed in Liu Fufeng's eyes.","Even now, she still protects that wretch Guo Yiyao like this. Once Shu'er marries into the Meng household, won't she be bullied to death? She must find a way to get rid of her.","Liu Fufeng righteously and loudly declared, \"A daughter of the Guo family would absolutely never do anything to disgrace our family's reputation. If you all don't believe me, you can follow me to see for yourselves.\"","Song Jinzhao watched Liu Fufeng's performance with a smile. Those who didn't know better would really think she had such faith in Guo Yiyao.","A male guest, holding a wine cup and wanting to personally offer birthday wishes to Old Madam Meng, noticed her absence and looked questioningly at the maid standing behind the chair.","The maid lowered her head and bowed, saying, \"The Old Madam has gone to freshen up. Esteemed guest, you may come again a little later.\"","The man's gaze swept over the women's seating area, and he frowned in confusion.","Several tables were empty of people. Had they all gone to freshen up?","The door to the guest room was forcefully pushed open from the outside. Guo Yiyao looked at the swarming crowd rushing in; the one at the very front was none other than her stepmother.","Madam Meng pushed aside the maid who had rushed ahead and took Guo Yiyao's hand, asking with concern, \"The maid said you just started your monthly courses. Are you feeling unwell anywhere?\"","Guo Yiyao's delicate brows slightly furrowed, a look of confusion in her eyes. \"I haven't started my courses. Who said I had?\"","Liu Fufeng stepped forward, raising her voice. \"The maid said you were bleeding heavily. If it's not your monthly courses, could it be a miscarriage?\"","Guo Yiyao's tone was cool, tinged with anger as she retorted, \"Mother, please watch your words. This concerns your daughter's reputation. How can you casually utter such slanderous words about me being with child before confirming the truth?\"","Everyone looked at Liu Fufeng in unison.","That's right. Just a moment ago, she insisted Guo Yiyao hadn't miscarried, so why is she now suspecting a miscarriage?","Liu Fufeng covered her eyes with a handkerchief, feigning distress. \"It was Mother's fault. I heard something had happened to you and panicked, speaking too hastily.\"","Guo Yiyao raised her injured arm. \"I have neither started my courses nor had a miscarriage. The bleeding is because I accidentally knocked over a vase, and a shard cut my hand.\"","As her sleeve fell back, everyone finally saw the bright red wound.","Madam Meng's heart ached as she held her arm, not daring to touch it for fear of causing her pain.","\"Such a large gash, does it hurt? You silly child, why didn't you say so earlier? Aunt Meng will have a servant fetch a physician right away.\"","Liu Fufeng shot a dark, venomous look at Nanny Lu's face, chilling as a serpent's tongue.","Nanny Lu stared fearfully at the wound on Guo Yiyao's arm. How could this be?","She had clearly administered the medicine. Guo Yiyao should have started her courses immediately. How could it be blood from her arm?","Liu Fufeng spoke up. \"The wound is so deep, we mustn't let it scar. We should quickly invite a physician to take a look.\"","Whether she had her courses or not, the ultimate goal was to reveal her difficulty conceiving. By following Madam Meng's suggestion to call a physician, everything would proceed naturally.","Old Madam Meng said, \"Physician Song is right here in the residence. Have her come over.\"","Bihe was just about to turn and summon someone when she saw Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue sitting on the bench by the railing under the corridor, looking relaxed and pleased, as if watching a play."]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: The One Who Was Drugged Was Guo Yishu","paragraphs":["Meeting Bihe's gaze, Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together, stood up, and walked through the crowd to Guo Yiyao to examine the wound on her arm.","\"The cut isn't too deep. Apply ointment for a few days and it will heal without scarring.\"","Seeing that Song Jinzhao had dismissed Guo Yiyao's injury with just a few casual words, Liu Fufeng quickly spoke up. \"I've long heard of Physician Song's exceptional medical skills. Yiyao has been experiencing some irregularities with her monthly courses lately. Could you please take her pulse and see if there's any underlying issue?\"","Song Jinzhao raised the corner of her mouth meaningfully and gestured for Guo Yiyao to extend her hand.","All eyes were fixed on them, as if eagerly hoping something was wrong with Guo Yiyao.","After two months of recuperation, the acne on her face had noticeably improved and was barely visible under makeup.","When Qiu Ye had come alone to the clinic to fetch medicine earlier, she had mentioned Guo Yiyao's condition; her monthly courses had clearly arrived just last month.","Liu Fufeng thought Guo Yiyao had missed her courses for two months, which meant this scheme had been in the works for at least a month.","Song Jinzhao released her hand and said with a smile, \"Miss Guo is in perfect health. The recent irregularity over the past two months is likely due to stress. Getting proper rest for a while should resolve it.\"","Liu Fufeng's breath hitched, her pupils constricting sharply.","\"How is that possible? Are you sure you didn't misdiagnose?\"","Song Jinzhao feigned confusion, raising an eyebrow. \"I didn't misdiagnose. Miss Guo is not ill. Why do you sound almost disappointed, Madam Liu?\"","\"Do you wish for her to be ill, or not?\"","Madam Meng narrowed her eyes at Liu Fufeng, finding her behavior strange.","Liu Fufeng's expression changed, forcing an awkward smile. \"You jest, Physician Song. Of course, I hope Yao'er is well and healthy.\"","Seeing Guo Yiyao escape unscathed, Guo Yishu, who was standing beside Liu Fufeng, was just about to speak when a sharp pain seized her lower abdomen. She clutched her stomach and bent over, squatting down.","Liao Xiwen, standing behind her, pointed in horror at her backside and cried out, \"Blood! Second Miss Guo is bleeding!\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. It seemed the drugged soup had been consumed by Guo Yishu instead.","\"Mother, my stomach hurts,\" Guo Yishu whimpered, grabbing Liu Fufeng's skirt, unable to stay crouched due to the pain.","Seeing the blood stain on her daughter's skirt spreading, Liu Fufeng pushed Nanny Lu and shouted, \"Quick, help Shu'er to a bed!\"","The ladies present were now thoroughly bewildered. One incident had just ended, and now another began?","Old Madam Meng's eyes held clear displeasure. This constant disturbance at her birthday banquet was a slap in her face.","Suppressing her anger, she spoke slowly to Song Jinzhao, \"Physician Song, I must trouble you to examine Second Miss Guo as well.\"","This banquet trip was truly worth it.","She had met people, established connections, watched a drama unfold, and even earned some consultation fees on the side.","Just as she was about to step forward, Guo Yiyao silently gave her a meaningful look.","Song Jinzhao's brows lifted slightly. Was it time for the big reveal?","Guo Yishu thrashed violently on the bed, sweating profusely from the pain, her fringe completely damp.","After finishing her examination, Song Jinzhao exited the inner chamber and announced, \"Second Miss Guo appears to have ingested something that induced her monthly courses.\"","\"Forcibly inducing menstruation harms the vital energy and blood, intensifies menstrual pain, and could lead to further irregularities or even a temporary cessation of menses.\"","Liu Fufeng's face turned deathly pale, and she shot a fierce glare at Nanny Lu.","Didn't she say the medicine would be undetectable by pulse diagnosis? Why did Song Jinzhao identify it at a glance?","Old Madam Meng demanded sternly, \"How could such a thing appear at a birthday banquet?\"","Madam Meng hurriedly apologized. \"Mother, this substance was likely brought in from elsewhere. If the banquet food were tainted, more than just Second Miss Guo would be affected.\"","Old Madam Meng slammed her prayer beads onto the floor. \"Investigate this immediately! To consume such a thing at a birthday banquet is inauspicious!\"","Madam Meng's mind was now completely at ease. As long as it wasn't Yiyao in trouble, all was well.","\"Then let's first examine what Second Miss Guo consumed. Physician Song, would you please assist us in checking?\"","Liu Fufeng could find no reason to object and could only watch helplessly as they returned to the main hall.","Song Jinzhao picked up the bowl of soup, mostly finished, and smelled it.","\"It's this soup. It contains safflower, achyranthes root, peach kernel, and other herbs that promote blood circulation and break blood stasis. Fortunately, the dosage was light, otherwise it could have caused severe hemorrhaging and endangered her life.\"","\"So, someone deliberately poisoned it?\"","Meng Hechuan arrived with some servants from the neighboring men's section. He had wondered at Old Madam Meng's prolonged absence and, upon inquiry, learned of trouble among the female guests.","Song Qiming watched Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue with a worried expression. How could such a thing happen at a birthday banquet?","After checking the other soup bowls, Song Jinzhao stated, \"Only this bowl was drugged. It was definitely intentional.\"","Meng Hechuan's face darkened, his hands clenched into fists at his sides. \"To dare poison someone at my Meng family's birthday banquet... the culprit must be found.\"","\"Everyone who handled this soup, from start to finish, bring them all here.\"","Old Madam Meng sat stiffly in her chair, face ashen. A birthday banquet turned into a poisoning scene—who knew what rumors would spread?","Liu Fufeng, who had rushed over after settling Guo Yishu, saw that Meng Hechuan was involved and even men from the other banquet were peering over, causing her heart to race and panic to flash across her face.","Her gaze locked onto Song Jinzhao, who was inspecting the food.","It was all her fault.","The physician had clearly said this medicine wouldn't be detected. But Song Jinziao was here. Why did her medical skills have to be so exceptional?","The birthday banquet had turned into a courtroom. The Meng family's expressions were the most grim.","Soon, the kitchen staff and the maid who served the soup were all brought forward.","The chef responsible for the soup knelt on the ground, pleading his innocence. \"Sir, everyone in the kitchen was present when I made the soup. They can all testify I didn't add anything.\"","The maid who served the soup, Yunqiao, knelt pitifully, wiping her tears. \"Sir, I'm innocent. What grudge could I possibly have against Second Miss Guo to poison her?\"","Another maid standing in the hall narrowed her eyes in recollection, frowning hesitantly.","When serving the dishes, Yunqiao seemed to walk a bit slowly and fell behind for a stretch.","Upon questioning the kitchen staff, it was confirmed everyone was present during the soup's preparation, and the chef himself had even tasted it during final seasoning.","Meng Hechuan fixed his gaze on the maid. \"Did any stranger touch it along the way? Was the soup ever out of your sight?\"","Yunqiao hesitated for a moment before looking up. \"This servant... had to use the privy midway. I placed the soup tray on a railing bench. When I returned, I didn't notice anything different.\"","Madam Meng reprimanded her unhappily. \"Couldn't you have held it? The distance from the kitchen to the main hall is so short!\"","Yunqiao immediately kowtowed in apology, the sound sharp and rapid, her forehead nearly breaking. \"It was this servant's fault. I truly couldn't hold it any longer and went quickly, thinking it would be fine. I never imagined a villain would seize the opportunity. Please forgive me, Madam.\"","Seeing her being so quick-witted, Liu Fufeng inwardly breathed a sigh of relief.","The soup had been left unattended, and with so many guests at the Meng residence today, it would be very difficult to trace who administered the drug."]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: Mutual Accusations Without Evidence","paragraphs":["Meng Hechuan narrowed his eyes. \"Men, search the rooms of all the servants who served in the main hall and the back kitchen today. If you find any poison, report back to me immediately.\"","This matter had to be investigated thoroughly to clear the Meng family of any suspicion.","The incident happened in their manor. If the culprit was not found, the Meng family would be the one to take the blame.","Liu Fufeng stood calmly by Guo Qishi's side. The menstruation-inducing powder had only been brought over today, and all of it had been poured into the soup.","The paper packet that held the powder had already been torn to pieces and thrown into the pond by Nanny Lu. Even if they searched every servant's room, they would not find any poison.","Song Shixue grasped Song Jinzhao's fingers, her eyelids lifting slightly.","Sister, should we tell them what we saw?","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod.","Since Guo Yiyao could swap the drugged soup, it meant she definitely knew Liu Fufeng was going to poison her and must have a backup plan.","They just needed to stay quiet and watch the show.","Not long after, the guards who went to search ran back, holding a lacquer box.","\"My Lord, your subordinate found this in Yunqiao's room.\"","When the lacquer box was opened, it was half-filled with expensive pearl hairpins and earrings. At first glance, it was obvious that these were not things a maid could afford to use or buy.","Madam Meng's face darkened with anger as she sharply questioned, \"Speak, where did you get all these things?\"","Yunqiao stared blankly at the items in the box. Once she realized what was happening, she quickly shook her head and cried out.","\"You wrong me, Madam! These things are not mine at all. I don't know how they ended up in my jewelry box. Someone must have planted them to frame me!\"","Meng Hechuan reached out to motion Madam Meng to step back. \"Then tell me, who is trying to frame you?\"","Yunqiao's eyes darted around helplessly. Her hesitant demeanor sent Meng Hechuan into a rage.","\"I think you are full of lies. Bring the staff and give her fifty heavy blows. I will force the truth out of her.\"","Everyone present was shocked. Fifty blows would definitely claim this maid's life.","Hearing that she was going to receive fifty blows, Yunqiao instantly burst into terrified wails.","\"My Lord, these pieces of jewelry are really not mine! Only the fifty taels of silver inside belong to me, which was the money Nanny Lu used to bribe me. Nanny Lu administered the medicine herself; it has nothing to do with me!\"","Those who didn't know instinctively asked the people around them, \"Who is Nanny Lu? Is she a servant of the Meng manor?\"","Those in the know used their chins to point at the nanny standing next to Liu Fufeng. \"She's no servant of the Meng manor. Nanny Lu is a servant of the Guo manor, a trusted confidante of the Guo family's matriarch.\"","Guo Qishi heard Yunqiao's accusation, swung his sleeve, and slapped her hard across the face, tearing a cut at the corner of her mouth.","\"You wretched maid, how dare you make such wild accusations! How could my wife possibly poison her own biological daughter? There should be a limit to your nonsense!\"","Liu Fufeng stood calmly in place, but the trembling fingertips exposed beyond her cuffs betrayed her nervousness and unease.","Standing beside her, Nanny Lu froze completely. A chill ran down her spine, and her breath caught in her throat.","Yunqiao's face quickly swelled up. In order to survive, she no longer even feared Guo Qishi, a magistrate.","\"Guo Yishu is her biological daughter, but Guo Yiyao is not! That medicine was originally meant to be put into Guo Yiyao's soup bowl. Somehow there was a mistake, which led to the current situation.\"","She reached out, pointed at Nanny Lu, and said, \"She also told me to deliberately say at the birthday banquet that Guo Yiyao was bleeding heavily. Madam Guo would play along on the side, leading everyone to believe she had a miscarriage.\"","\"Once Guo Yiyao's reputation was ruined, the old madam would no longer let the young master marry Guo Yiyao. After Guo Yishu married over, they would promote me to a senior maid.\"","She crawled on her knees to Madam Meng and kept kowtowing and begging, \"I was blinded by greed and accidentally took the wrong path. I beg you for mercy, Madam! Please spare my life! I will never dare do it again!\"","The main hall fell into a deathly silence.","Guo Yiyao, unable to bear the blow, collapsed to the ground.","Her face was deathly pale, as if she were about to die at any moment. She muttered helplessly to herself, \"Impossible. Mother couldn't possibly do this to me.\"","Seeing her like this, Madam Meng couldn't help but get red-rimmed eyes.","Her heart aching, she stepped forward to embrace Guo Yiyao, gently stroking the back of her head to comfort her. \"It's alright. With Aunt Meng here, no one can bully our Yaoyao. Aunt Meng will back you up. Aunt Meng will protect you.\"","Thinking back to the scene where her good friend lay dying on the bed, holding her hand and entrusting her orphaned daughter to her on her deathbed, Madam Meng had to grit her teeth hard to keep the tears from falling.","The observing madams whispered among themselves as they looked at Liu Fufeng and Guo Yiyao.","\"Stealing the first wife's daughter's marriage for her own biological daughter. No wonder Liu Fufeng seemed to be protecting Guo Yiyao's reputation on the surface just now, yet blurted out that she had a miscarriage. She was practically wishing for something to be wrong with her body. So she had an ulterior motive all along.\"","Watching this deceitful farce unfold before her eyes, Song Shixue fearfully grasped Song Jinzhao's hand, pressing her body tightly against her sister's.","Noble households were too terrifying. Living under the same roof, they schemed against each other like enemies. It was simply horrifying.","Guo Qishi looked at Liu Fufeng in disbelief. How could his usually considerate and gentle wife commit such a vicious and wicked act?","Under everyone's accusing and disgusted gazes, Liu Fufeng spoke her first words since Yunqiao started pointing fingers at her.","With trembling eyelashes and a twitching mouth that seemed to hide unspeakable suffering, she perfectly established the image of a solitary and brave figure who had suffered a massive grievance yet stubbornly defended herself.","\"Drugging and falsely accusing Yao'er of having a miscarriage—the truth would immediately come to light as soon as a doctor was invited to check her pulse. Why would the Meng family despise her and agree to a marriage swap under those circumstances?\"","Yunqiao roared loudly, \"That's because you believed Guo Yiyao was infertile! That's why you wanted to use this miscarriage incident to have a doctor expose her in front of everyone. By then, this marriage would have to be annulled whether they wanted it or not, and you could logically have your own biological daughter marry in her place!\"","\"Nanny Lu told me all of this herself! If I am telling a single lie, let me be struck by lightning and die a horrible death! Let me descend to the eighteenth level of hell after death and never be reincarnated!\"","A sudden clap of thunder exploded in the sky, shocking everyone to the point of dizziness and making their minds go blank.","But Liu Fufeng, as if clutching at a life-saving straw, sharply questioned, \"What baseless lies! Doctor Song clearly stated that Yao'er is in good health. Where did this infertility come from? If you want to pin your own evil deeds on someone else, you should at least make up a better lie.\"","There was no evidence, only empty words.","Almost in despair, Yunqiao screamed at the top of her lungs, \"Who knows, maybe the heavens just couldn't bear to see you harming people like this!\"","\"The medicine meant for Guo Yiyao's bowl was drunk by your daughter. If Guo Yishu becomes infertile, that is retribution!\"","Seeing the situation becoming increasingly chaotic, Meng Hechuan rubbed his forehead, squeezed his eyes shut, and opened them again.","\"Men, take Yunqiao and Nanny Lu to the government office and lock them in the dungeon first. I will try this case carefully and uncover the truth.\""]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: The Hidden Truth, Accidentally","paragraphs":["For the second half of the birthday banquet, people were discussing what had just happened. Sitting on his stool, Guo Qishi felt like he was sitting on pins and needles under the prying eyes of the crowd.","Liu Fufeng picked up her chopsticks to serve herself some food. It tasted like sawdust in her mouth, but her face showed no sign that anything was amiss.","After the banquet ended, Song Jinzhao was about to leave when Bihe took the initiative to run over and see her off.","When they reached a secluded area, she stopped and shoved a coin purse into Song Jinzhao's hands, asking in a low voice, \"This is the consultation fee for the two Misses of the Guo family today. The Old Madam also has one more thing she wants me to ask Dr. Song: is the eldest Miss Guo's body truly healthy?\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight tug at the corners of her mouth and replied, \"The Old Madam doesn't need to worry. Eldest Miss Guo's body is perfectly normal, and she is capable of bearing children.\"","Hearing this, Bihe breathed a sigh of relief and hurriedly went back to report to Old Madam Meng.","When her carriage was nearing her home, Song Jinzhao remembered that she had forgotten to buy the date paste cake she had promised to bring Song Anhao. She asked Fushun to turn around and head to the pastry shop. Halfway there, however, she noticed the Guo family's carriage speeding toward the government office. It was moving so fast that the entire carriage looked as if it were about to shake apart.","The next day, the outcome of the incident spread.","The drugging incident was orchestrated entirely by Nanny Lu from start to finish, and had nothing to do with Liu Fuyun.","Rumor had it that Guo Yiyao had inadvertently offended Nanny Lu. Harboring a grudge, Nanny Lu used Liu Fufeng's name to order the manor's servants to send Guo Yiyao various mutually incompatible foods that would cause a cold womb and infertility. She also secretly bribed Yunqiao in an attempt to ruin Guo Yiyao's marriage.","As for the matter of swapping the brides, it was a lie fabricated by Nanny Lu to successfully bribe Yunqiao.","But she never expected that Guo Yiyao was kind-hearted and considerate of her servants, giving her daily meals to her personal maid as a reward. This was why the incompatible foods hadn't affected her.","Meng Hechuan also tracked down the medical clinic where Nanny Lu bought the drugs.","It was said that ordinary people wouldn't be able to detect the drug, but she hadn't anticipated Song Jinzhao's superb medical skills, which allowed her to spot it immediately, thus exposing the conspiracy.","Because no lives were lost and neither of the two Misses of the Guo family suffered serious harm, Nanny Lu and Yunqiao were respectively dragged back by the Guo and Meng families after being beaten with heavy staffs.","It was said that they were beaten to death as soon as they entered the manor gates, and their bodies were thrown into a mass grave with no one to even collect them.","The clinic was empty. Song Shixue, who was preparing medicine, looked at Song Jinzhao hesitantly upon hearing the news.","\"Sister, is that really what happened?\"","Song Jinzhao chuckled softly and asked in return, \"What do you think?\"","Song Shixue pursed her lips. After pondering for a couple of seconds, she put down the medicine packets, walked over, and sat beside Song Jinzhao.","\"I think the mastermind behind the scenes is Guo Yiyao's stepmother. Sending her incompatible foods to eat was real, ordering Nanny Lu to bribe Yunqiao to drug her was real, and the bride-swapping plot to marry her own biological daughter to Young Master Meng was also real. Nanny Lu is just a scapegoat.\"","Sitting opposite them, Liu Xuanqing stroked his long beard and looked at Song Shixue with a face full of smiles.","His little master was quick-witted and smart; she hadn't been fooled by the lies these wealthy households used to cover up the truth.","Without someone pulling the strings, how would a servant dare to frame her master? Not to mention drugging someone at the birthday banquet of Prefect Meng's mother.","What kind of deep-seated grudge would make her risk her life like that? These so-called truths that had been investigated were nothing but fabrications made by official families to maintain their reputation of an upright family tradition.","If the matriarch of the Guo family really bore the infamy of harming the legitimate daughter of the first wife, Guo Rongzhi and Guo Yishu's futures would be ruined. In serious cases, it would even affect Assistant Prefect Guo's official career. Of course, they had to quickly find a scapegoat to take the blame.","However, with things having reached this point, Guo Yishu's reputation was already half-ruined.","These tricks could deceive the common people, but they couldn't fool those well-informed, prominent families of similar status to the Guo family.","With Liu Fufeng as the mastermind, no one would believe that her daughter, Guo Yishu, was kept in the dark.","Poisoning her own sister and coveting her future brother-in-law—with such a reputation hanging over her head, her future marriage prospects would be extremely difficult.","\"Two months ago, Guo Yiyao came to our clinic for a consultation. She dressed like that because she didn't want to be seen, probably to guard against her stepmother.\"","Song Shixue's voice grew firmer and more forceful as she spoke.","\"At that time, you wrote her a list of cold and raw foods to avoid. That's why when her stepmother gave her those dishes, she didn't eat them, but rewarded a portion to her maid.\"","Song Jinzhao rubbed her chin with her fingers, looked up, and teased, \"And what about the soup she consumed by mistake?\"","Song Shixue froze. Staring at Song Jinzhao's playful gaze, her eyes flickered twice before her pupils suddenly dilated. \"Sister, do you mean that bowl of soup was deliberately switched by Guo Yiyao?\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. Seeing a patient come in, she stood up and left behind a breezy, \"What do you think?\"","Song Shixue stood frozen in place, her brows tightly knitted as her mind plunged into deep thought.","Liu Xuanqing hadn't known that Guo Yiyao had visited the clinic. Hearing the two sisters talk like this, he couldn't help but grow suspicious as well.","Guo Yiyao seemed to be about the same age as his grandmaster; it wasn't impossible for her to beat them at their own game and scheme against them in return.","A month later, when Guo Yiyao got married, Liu Fufeng didn't even show her face.","The reason the Guo family claimed to the public was that she had caught a chill and was afraid of infecting the guests who came to congratulate them, so she couldn't leave her room.","Less than a month after Guo Yiyao's marriage, Liu Fufeng died of her illness. It was said that the cold caused a high fever, and she breathed her last in just one night.","But all this was a story for later.","On the third day after Song Jinzhao attended Old Madam Meng's birthday banquet, Liao Xiwen personally came to her door to invite her to the Liao Manor to treat Madam Liao.","Liao Xiwen's father was the Sub-Prefect of Anyang; in terms of official rank, he was second only to Meng Hechuan, the Prefect.","In the carriage, Liao Xiwen furrowed her brows, her heart filled with anxiety. \"To be honest with you, Miss Song, my mother has been disappointed too many times. She has long since given up hope on doctors and even harbors some aversion toward them.\"","\"During today's consultation, if she has a poor attitude, I beg for your forbearance.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled and nodded. \"It's no trouble. As a healer, I've seen all sorts of patients. This is nothing.\"","Twelve pregnancies and twelve miscarriages—if this were the modern era, a person would likely have gone mad from the blow long ago.","The fact that this Madam Liao hadn't gone mad and only had a bad temper meant her psychological endurance was already astonishingly strong.","On the bustling street, the commoners saw the carriage and hurriedly stepped aside to make way.","For some reason, the customers at a noodle stall suddenly started arguing. After a few words, the quarrel grew louder and louder until they simply came to blows.","Seeing this, the stall owner hurriedly went up to break up the fight. In the chaos, a man with a thick beard was bumped and stumbled backward rapidly. Unable to stop his momentum, his back slammed heavily into the stove used for boiling wontons.","Blazing firewood scattered all over the ground, sending sparks flying everywhere. The boiling water in the pot splashed entirely onto the horse's legs.","\"Neigh—!\" The horse's body shuddered violently as it let out a sharp, frantic whinny.","It reared its scalded hooves high into the air, tossing its mane wildly and bucking in panic.","The carriage jolted violently. The tea and pastries on the low table were overturned onto the floor, scattering everywhere.","Liao Xiwen's eyes widened in horror, and she screamed at the top of her lungs, on the verge of being thrown out of the carriage.","\"Miss!\" The maid tried to reach out to support Liao Xiwen, but she lost her balance. With a loud thud, she crashed into the corner of the carriage, her mind going completely blank.","Song Jinzhao gripped the long wooden plank beneath her tightly with her left hand, leaned forward, and wrapped her arm around Liao Xiwen's slender waist, pulling the girl into her embrace.","Outside the carriage, a chorus of gasps and screams erupted as the commoners scattered in panic to dodge out of the way.","The rough reins had dug into the webbing and palms of the coachman's hands, leaving two dark crimson bloody gashes. Despite pulling with all his might, he still couldn't bring the horse under control. Amidst the violent jolting, half of his body was dangling precariously, looking as if he would fall from the carriage at any moment.","Song Jinzhao pried Liao Xiwen's hands off herself and placed them on the long bench beneath them, shouting sternly, \"Hold on tight with both hands and don't let go. I'm going to control the horse.\"","Liao Xiwen's limbs turned to jelly, her heart practically leaping out of her throat. \"Don't go! You won't be able to control a spooked horse.\"","Even the coachman was about to be thrown off. With Song Jinzhao's slender arms and legs, if she left the carriage, she would be sent flying until she was completely out of sight.","Song Jinzhao ducked out of the carriage. Her legs clamped onto the carriage frame like iron tongs. Her left hand snatched the reins flailing in the air, while her right hand grabbed the coachman by the shoulder, hauling him up from under the frame.","She exerted force in her arms, causing the horse to rear its head high. Accompanied by the rapid, heavy snorts from its nostrils, its front hooves kicked wildly in the air, struggling forward.","Under the force of inertia, the carriage let out a harsh, grating creak, and the right wheel, unable to withstand the pressure, snapped off and flew away.","An intense feeling of weightlessness swept over Liao Xiwen and her maid sitting inside the carriage. In the nick of time, the fierce horse's hooves slammed heavily onto the ground. Its head tossed from side to side a few times before finally drooping down.","Liao Xiwen leaned against the carriage wall, still reeling from the terror. Her chest heaved erratically, and she looked as though her soul had left her body, unable to recover her senses for a long time.","Once the carriage had come to a steady halt, the coachman stumbled and rolled off.","Seeing that Liao Xiwen was still panting heavily, Song Jinzhao grabbed her hand and led her down.","The maid crawled out of the carriage, dizzy and seeing stars. The moment her feet touched the ground, she pitched forward.","\"Linglong!\" Liao Xiwen's unfocused pupils suddenly contracted.","Song Jinzhao turned, took a step to the right, and reached out to catch the maid, gently laying her on the ground.","The maid raised a trembling hand and shook her head. \"Miss, I'm fine. Just a little dizzy.\"","Song Jinzhao placed her fingers on the maid's radial artery. The rise and fall of her chest was normal, and the whites of her eyes were a healthy porcelain hue.","When her fingers pressed against the back of her head, Linglong furrowed her brows, grabbed Song Jinzhao's arm, and groaned, \"It hurts a bit.\"","Liao Xiwen bent down and crouched beside them. \"Did she hit her head?\"","The impact inside the carriage just now had been no small matter.","\"Don't move, let me take another look.\"","There were no open wounds or depressions, but there was a swelling, no larger than two centimeters.","\"We'll observe her for a while first, but it shouldn't be a major issue.\"","Hearing Song Jinzhao say this, Liao Xiwen felt a slight wave of relief wash over her.","The coachman walked around to inspect the carriage and discovered that not only had one wheel rolled off, but the axle had also cracked open.","\"Miss, this carriage is no longer safe to ride in. Please allow this humble servant to pull it back to the manor and drive another carriage over to pick you up.\"","Liao Xiwen, still gripped by lingering fear, shook her head and waved her hands, swallowing hard to calm her nerves.","\"I don't want to ride in a carriage right now. You drag the carriage back. I will walk back to the manor with Doctor Song.\"","Song Jinzhao turned around to look back. The wonton stall that had been knocked over was already about a hundred meters away from them.","The stall owner, afraid that the noble ladies in the carriage would come over to hold them accountable, tightly grabbed a bearded man with both hands, refusing to let him leave.","The bearded man struggled to break free, repeating constantly, \"If that person hadn't pushed me just now, I wouldn't have crashed into it. If you want to blame someone, you should blame him.\"","The stall owner refused to let go, his spit spraying all over the man's face as he spoke.","\"That person has already run away! If you hadn't been arguing with him, how could a fight have broken out and knocked over my stove? I can't do any business today, so you have to pay for the damages.\"","The coachman looked hesitantly at Liao Xiwen. \"Miss, should we...?\"","Liao Xiwen shook her head. \"Forget it, they didn't do it on purpose. You go back first; we'll sit for a while before leaving.\"","The coachman nodded, picked up the reins, and slowly pulled the broken carriage away.","Liao Xiwen led Song Jinzhao and her maid into a nearby teahouse to sit down.","After calming down, she recalled the heroic way Song Jinzhao had tamed the horse just now, and she turned her head, her eyes brimming with curiosity.","\"Miss Song knows how to ride a horse?\"","\"I do.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at Linglong, who was wiping the table for Liao Xiwen. The maid had completely regained her energy and seemed to be perfectly fine.","Liao Xiwen picked up her teacup and took a sip, her tone filled with envy and a hint of regret. \"When I was young, I wanted to learn how to ride too. Later, when I was twelve, my father specially hired a riding master to come to the manor to teach me, but I ended up falling off the horse.\"","\"If the manor's guards hadn't caught me in time, I might have lost my life. After that, I never tried to learn again.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"How many days had you been learning before the riding master let go and allowed you to ride alone?\"","Liao Xiwen tilted her chin up in thought. \"Three days. He was right there beside me but didn't take control. My father said his riding skills were poor and that his reputation was unearned, so he kicked him out.\"","She leaned forward, resting her arms on the table.","\"Miss Song, your riding skills are so excellent. Could you teach me how to ride someday? If I encounter something like today again, there might be no one to save me.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"I have many chores at home, and the medical clinic sees quite a few patients every day. I cannot spare any extra time to teach Miss Liao how to ride.\"","Liao Xiwen lowered her head in disappointment. \"That really is a pity.\"","The teahouse was still quite a distance from the Liao Manor; walking there would take about an hour.","Song Jinzhao intended to speed up her pace, but whenever she walked just a bit faster, Liao Xiwen and her maid would be left behind. After a few attempts, she had no choice but to resign herself to a leisurely stroll beside the two of them.","Liao Xiwen's mouth simply couldn't stop. She talked as they walked, gossiping about almost every young lady from the inner courts of the prominent families in Anyang Prefecture.","When the topic turned to what had happened at the birthday banquet a few days ago, she said, \"Guo Yiyao's stepmother fell ill right after returning from the Meng Manor. I heard it was an invasion of evil wind. Did the Guo Manor ask you to come over for a consultation?\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a faint smile and shook her head. \"They probably wouldn't invite me.\"","Liu Fufeng most likely hated her to the core by now, so how could she possibly ask her to treat her illness?","She had been full of vigor just a few days ago, but today she was bedridden from an invasion of evil wind.","Whether it was a sickness of the heart or just pretending to be ill remained to be seen.","Seeing how Madam Meng had defended Guo Yiyao that day, it was absolutely certain that she wanted this daughter-in-law.","If Guo Qishi failed to handle this matter properly, not only would he break his biological daughter's heart, but he would also offend his future in-laws. This illness likely had an ulterior motive.","In an alleyway by the street, a man dressed in gray coarse clothing and wearing a bamboo hat fixed his gaze firmly on Song Jinzhao. Only after she had walked far away did he turn and leave.","Song Jinzhao stopped in her tracks and narrowed her eyes, glancing toward her right rear. The bustling street market was filled with people coming and going, each minding their own business. There didn't seem to be anything out of the ordinary.","Seeing her suddenly stop, Liao Xiwen asked in confusion, \"What's wrong?\"","Song Jinzhao turned back around and shook her head. \"I felt like someone was watching us.\"","Liao Xiwen's eyes curved into crescents as she smiled brightly and said, \"Everyone has an appreciation for beauty. Both of us are quite good-looking, so it's perfectly normal for people to stare. Next time, we can wear veiled hats when we go out.\"","Song Jinzhao parted her lips slightly, feeling as if her throat were blocked, leaving her momentarily speechless.","How had she never noticed before that this girl was so narcissistic? Weren't the young ladies of prominent families supposed to be reserved?"]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Two Accidents, the Liao Mansion","paragraphs":["As she turned the corner and passed a two-story building, that familiar sensation washed over her once more. Every cell in Song Jinzhao's body was vibrating with rapid intensity.","She quickly lifted her head, her gaze shooting like a sharp arrow toward the direction the malice emanated from.","A flowerpot fell from the sky, completely blocking Song Jinzhao's line of sight.","Tapping her toes lightly on the ground, she spun around and swiftly darted away from the spot, the hem of her fluttering skirt billowing out like a dancing, blooming pink lotus.","\"Crash.\" The flowerpot smashed onto the ground, shattering into pieces. Dirt, branches, and leaves were scattered all over in a messy heap.","Before Liao Xiwen could react, Song Jinzhao dashed into the adjacent eatery in the blink of an eye.","\"Guest, what would you like to... eat?\" Before the approaching waiter could finish his words, Song Jinzhao turned into a phantom-like blur and disappeared up the staircase leading to the second floor.","He stopped in his tracks, blinking at the empty staircase. Did someone just pass by?","Song Jinzhao stood at the top of the stairs on the second floor. There were only six tables up there; three were empty, and the other three were occupied.","Faced with the girl who had suddenly rushed up, the dining guests looked over at her in confusion.","How did she shoot up here so fast? It was as if she had appeared out of thin air.","Her sharp eyes locked onto the person sitting at the very last table wearing a bamboo hat. He did not even take it off while eating and kept his head lowered. Very suspicious.","Song Jinzhao stepped forward and walked toward him.","The man swallowed uneasily. His hands, hidden beneath the table, were clenched tightly into fists. His palms began to sweat, and it was so quiet in his ears that he could only hear his own breathing and heartbeat.","How was her reaction so fast? She was not hurt either time, and she even discovered his presence.","Fair, slender yet strong fingers landed on the tabletop. The man suppressed his pounding heartbeat and looked up at Song Jinzhao.","Feigning astonishment, he blurted out, \"Miss Song, is there something the matter?\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows, increasingly certain that the man before her was the one who had been spying on her all along and had just tried to smash her with the flowerpot.","\"How do you know my surname is Song?\"","A drop of cold sweat slid down the man's temple.","He scratched his head with his hand and offered an unnatural compliment, \"Miss Song's medical skills are famous throughout the entire Anyang Prefecture. Everyone knows you.\"","\"Are you here to eat, Miss? There is an empty table right next to me,\" he said, pointing to the adjacent vacant table.","\"Wang Zhong, why are you here?\"","Liao Xiwen, who had caught up, walked to Song Jinzhao's side and stared at the man in surprise.","The man hastily stood up, stepped out, bowed his head respectfully, and called out, \"Eldest Miss.\"","Song Jinzhao turned to look at her. \"Miss Liao knows him?\"","Liao Xiwen nodded. \"Wang Zhong is a guard from my family.\"","\"Why aren't you in the manor at this hour? What are you doing here?\" she asked, staring at Wang Zhong.","Wang Zhong replied, \"Concubine Su ordered me to come out and buy roasted squab. I had just sat down when Dr. Song arrived.\"","Liao Xiwen looked around, frowning in confusion.","\"You came here to buy roasted squab? Why didn't you go to the Haoyue Restaurant?\"","Such a simple eatery definitely could not match the delicious flavors of the Haoyue Restaurant.","Wang Zhong: \"Concubine Su said she was tired of eating from the Haoyue Restaurant and told me to buy from somewhere else, so I came here.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at the two of them with deep, dark eyes, a hidden gleam flickering in the depths of her pupils.","Haoyue Restaurant was the most famous restaurant in Anyang Prefecture. To be able to say she was tired of eating there meant this Concubine Su must have sent people out to buy food quite often.","With the legal wife still alive, a concubine could so easily dispatch the manor's guards, yet Liao Xiwen did not find it inappropriate at all. Concubine Su's status in the Liao manor must be quite extraordinary.","After hearing Wang Zhong's words, Liao Xiwen nodded to show she understood, then turned her head to ask Song Jinzhao, \"Did you find the person who knocked over the flowerpot?\"","The flowerpots on the second floor of the eatery were placed right on the windowsill. If someone accidentally bumped into them, the pots could easily fall.","Song Jinzhao neither nodded nor shook her head. Instead, with a half-smile, she said, \"I didn't see anyone else after coming up here. Wang Zhong, did you see who knocked the flowerpot down?\"","Wang Zhong's back was already half-soaked in sweat. His mouth twitched unnaturally. \"This servant just arrived and didn't see either.\"","Song Jinzhao turned and walked toward the other two tables of dining guests, politely asking, \"Gentlemen, a flowerpot just fell from the windowsill. Did any of you happen to see who pushed it off?\"","The eyes of the four men revealed sixty percent confusion and forty percent bewilderment. They shook their heads and replied, \"No idea, we didn't notice.\"","The windowsill was behind them, and they were too busy keeping their heads down and eating to notice if anyone had passed by behind them.","Wang Zhong breathed a sigh of relief upon hearing this.","Liao Xiwen stomped her foot and frowned, saying, \"They must have seen the flowerpot almost hit someone and ran away out of fear of taking responsibility.\"","Song Jinzhao rolled her eyes inwardly in speechlessness. From the moment the flowerpot fell to when she rushed up to the second floor, not even three seconds had passed. How could the other party run away that fast?","Even if they had run, she would have bumped into them on the stairs, but the stairs had been empty.","Unless someone jumped directly from the second floor, the perpetrator was undoubtedly Wang Zhong.","The question was, why did he attack her?","They had no grudges, no enmity, and had never even met before. Thinking of the accident that had just occurred at the wonton stall, Song Jinzhao could not help but connect the two incidents.","A concubine? A legal wife?","The only connection was probably that Liao Xiwen had invited her to the Liao manor today to examine her mother.","Twelve miscarriages, a mix of natural and accidental losses. It seemed the situation was far from as simple as she had described.","Song Jinzhao cast a meaningful glance at Wang Zhong, then spoke to Liao Xiwen, \"If we can't find them, we'll leave it for now. It is getting late, so let's head to your manor as quickly as possible.\"","To be capable of injuring and killing someone just to prevent her from conducting a medical consultation, one could well imagine that there was definitely something suspicious about Liao Xiwen's mother's illness, and it was inextricably linked to Concubine Su.","Wang Zhong watched the three people walk away. His shoe soles felt glued to the spot, unable to move a single step for a long time.","Her gaze just now clearly showed she was suspicious. If he made another move, he would definitely be caught.","The mission was not completed. What should he do now?","Wang Zhong hurriedly called the waiter to pack a roasted squab, grabbed it, and hastily took a detour toward the back door of the Liao manor.","On the way, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Does Concubine Su have any children?\"","Liao Xiwen nodded, biting her lip as a trace of disappointment surfaced on her face. \"My eldest brother, Liao Tingjun, was born to Concubine Su. He was born just a quarter of an hour before me. My mother has always been very disappointed that I am not a boy.\"","Song Jinzhao's grip on her medicine chest's shoulder strap tightened. \"Does your father have any other children?\"","Liao Xiwen shook her head. \"Concubine Su is just like my mother. After giving birth to my eldest brother, she got pregnant three times and miscarried each time. After that, she never conceived again. The doctor said the three miscarriages damaged her body, making pregnancy difficult.\"","Song Jinzhao shifted her gaze forward. Adding them up, there had been a total of fifteen miscarriages in a single manor. Those who didn't know better would think this was the Emperor's inner palace, given the sheer number of miscarriages.","She continued to probe, \"How many concubines does your father have in total, and have they ever miscarried?\"","Liao Xiwen smiled and said, \"My father only has one concubine, Concubine Su. She is my father's distant cousin. If it weren't for the fact that she was newly widowed and all her relatives had passed away, leaving her with no one to rely on, my father wouldn't have married her.\"","Song Jinzhao blinked, a stunned expression crossing her face.","Newly widowed? Could she have killed her own husband?","Because of the detour, both parties entered the Liao manor almost right on each other's heels.","Liao Xiwen led Song Jinzhao straight to Madam Liao's courtyard in the backyard for a medical consultation, while Wang Zhong sprinted toward Concubine Su's courtyard, panting heavily.","Seeing him running over, the maidservant hastily stepped aside to let him into the room.","Reclining on an arhat bed covered with a sheepskin rug was a woman of rather bewitching beauty.","The corners of her eyes slanted upward slightly like a fox's tail, and her delicate oval face was powdered with bright red blush. A purple gauze sash accentuated her soft, seemingly boneless waist, making it look even more slender and alluring.","\"Is the matter settled?\" Even her voice carried a lilting upward inflection at the end.","Wang Zhong rested his hands on his knees and knelt before her. He kept his head bowed, but from the corners of his eyes, his upward gaze remained fixed on the woman.","\"Song Jinzhao is agile and highly vigilant. This humble servant used a trick to spook the horse, but not only was she completely unharmed, she also saved the Eldest Miss. I almost got caught trying to smash her with a flower pot. Now, she has already entered the manor.\"","Concubine Su lowered her legs from the bed. As she stood up, a cold light glinted in her slender eyes.","\"Is she currently with the Old Madam, or at the Spring Water Courtyard?\"","Wang Zhong kept his head down and remained silent.","A maidservant walked into the room from outside. \"To answer Concubine, the Eldest Miss took her directly to the Spring Water Courtyard.\"","\"Useless trash!\"","A teacup from the table was hurled at Wang Zhong's shoulder, bringing with it a strong, pungent fragrance.","Outside, the bright sun beat down in broad daylight, yet the Spring Water Courtyard felt like a pool of stagnant water. Upon entering, everyone kept their heads bowed in silence.","When they saw Liao Xiwen, they merely curtsied, breathed out a faint \"Eldest Miss,\" and then silently retreated with their brooms and rags.","The doors to the main room and the two side chambers were shut tight. Two maidservants stood on either side of the entrance like ghosts, as if they were barely even breathing.","Liao Xiwen whispered, \"Ever since my mother suffered a miscarriage, she hasn't been able to tolerate loud noises. She refuses to see anyone or leave her room. Over time, the servants in the courtyard have become like this.\"","Song Jinzhao scanned the tightly sealed room. It was so suffocating that even if someone didn't already harbor a death wish, they would be stifled to death by this oppressive environment.","It would be better to throw a massive tantrum and vent all those emotions.","Liao Xiwen waved her hand to dismiss the servants, slowly pushed the door open, and brought only Song Jinzhao inside.","A foul, bloody stench immediately assaulted their faces. Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows as she surveyed the lit candles in the room.","With the windows shut, no ventilation, and no sunlight, who knew how severe the bacteria buildup was. A person with a weak immune system could fall ill just by staying here for an extra day.","\"Mother, I've brought Miss Song to see you,\" Liao Xiwen said softly to the woman lying in bed.","A face so pale it was almost transparent met Song Jinzhao's eyes. The blood vessels on her neck were clearly visible, as if she were merely draped in a layer of human skin.","Her dull, unfocused pupils didn't shift in the slightest at Liao Xiwen's call. She looked like a soulless zombie clinging to her last breath.","Seeing that Madam Liao remained unresponsive, Liao Xiwen signaled with her eyes for Song Jinzhao to approach.","Placing her medical box on the table and opening it, she took out a pulse pillow and walked toward the bed. The closer she got, the heavier the stench became.","The lochia from her miscarriage had likely never been fully cleared, and it had been over a month.","She reached out to take the woman's emaciated wrist. It was truly nothing but bone, with only the thinnest layer of skin left.","Her fragile neck turned mechanically outward, and her pale, unfocused eyes landed on Song Jinzhao. She lay motionless, allowing Song Jinzhao to do as she pleased.","Seeing Song Jinzhao begin to check the pulse, Liao Xiwen parted her tightly pressed red lips and slowly exhaled the breath she had been holding in her chest.","She unclenched the fists hanging by her sides and wiped the sweat from her palms against her thighs.","Even though her mother hadn't said a word to refuse when she suggested bringing Song Jinzhao for a consultation, she had been terrified that her mother would chase the doctor out once she arrived.","Thankfully, she didn't lose her temper today and seemed fairly cooperative.","Song Jinzhao frowned. The situation was much more severe than she had anticipated.","Her limbs were freezing, her spleen and stomach were failing. Consumed by excessive grief, her liver and kidneys were congested, and her depletion of qi and blood was exceptionally critical.","Her pulse was extremely weak. Without careful touch, it seemed to vanish several times in between, barely there at all. It was the undeniable sign of a lamp running out of oil.","She looked up at Liao Xiwen. \"Has the patient not been taking any of the medicine prescribed by the previous doctors?\"","Liao Xiwen nodded. \"She drank it for a few days at the beginning, but later...\"","She squinted meaningfully. \"...she stopped taking it.\"","All the doctors who came to see her said she could never bear children again. Since she no longer wanted her body to recover, she naturally stopped taking the medicine.","\"What does she eat every day? A bowl of watery white congee?\"","She was reduced to skin and bones; it was worse than being on an IV drip.","Liao Xiwen glanced toward the door.","The closed door blocked the view of the maidservants standing outside.","\"Just the thin layer of rice water skimming the top of the congee. She can only manage half a bowl per meal.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up to fetch a pair of gloves from her medical box.","No wonder she was so weak. A bowl of rice water a day, let alone a grown adult, even an infant couldn't survive on that.","The fact that she hadn't starved to death was a testament to her sheer tenacity.","Putting on the gloves, Song Jinzhao walked back to the bed and said calmly, \"Madam Liao, I am going to examine your lower body now. Tell me if it hurts anywhere.\"","She drew the bed curtains. Just as her hand grasped the blanket, Madam Liao's hand, as thin as a chicken claw, blocked Song Jinzhao's wrist.","Her throat sounded as if it had been half-severed by a knife, so hoarse it seemed to leak air.","\"What do you think you're doing?\"","Kong Wanru knew better than anyone the condition of her lower body hidden beneath the covers.","It was too filthy to be seen, and the stench disgusted even herself, it was practically no different from a cesspit.","Lifting the blanket meant exposing her most wretched state to another person, trampling her dignity. It was no different from dying on the spot.","Song Jinzhao did not let go. Holding her ground, she said in a deep voice, \"Madam, you are not even afraid of death, yet you are afraid of being seen by me?\"","\"In the eyes of a healer, there is no distinction between men and women. Furthermore, I am a female doctor. You can set your mind at ease.\"","Kong Wanru stared into Song Jinzhao's eyes with a deathly pale face. The hand resting on her wrist trembled incessantly, as if she were about to use up whatever little strength she had left just to keep it raised.","\"Can you cure my illness and allow me to conceive and safely give birth to a child?\"","Song Jinzhao gritted her teeth. She desperately wanted to ask her: was a woman born solely for the purpose of bearing children?","Would she die if she didn't have a child?","Having one wasn't enough; she had to have another.","If she couldn't give birth to a son, would she keep trying until menopause, only stopping when she was completely bereft of the ability to reproduce?!","But she also knew there was no reasoning with these ancient people. Their mindsets had been rigidly molded since childhood. Especially for someone like Madam Liao, the toxic brainwashing ran too deep to ever be undone.","\"If you don't let me examine you, Madam, how will I know if you can still be saved?\"","Kong Wanru's gaze shifted to Liao Xiwen's face. \"Xiwen, step outside.\"","Liao Xiwen bit her cherry-red lips until the skin peeled. After a moment of hesitation, she pulled the door open, stepped outside, and closed it behind her."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: Treating Mrs. Liao","paragraphs":["Seeing that Kong Wanru was still holding on tightly and refusing to let go, Song Jinzhao straightened her back, walked to the door to slide the latch into place, and then returned. \"No one can come in. Can I examine you now?\"","Kong Wanru's arms relaxed, her slender limbs losing their tension as she fell back stiffly onto the bedding.","Song Jinzhao lifted the quilt. There was a strong, foul odor, but her trousers were clean.","This meant her maid was changing Kong Wanru's trousers every day; otherwise, they would have long since rotted into a blackened, unseeable mess.","Lifting her top, Song Jinzhao saw many old stretch marks on her loose, sagging belly. She pressed her hand against it. \"Tell me if it hurts.\"","Kong Wanru clenched her back teeth and stared at the canopy above the bed in silence.","When Concubine Su led her people into the Spring Breeze Courtyard, she saw that all the maids and Liao Xiwen were standing outside. The only person missing was that female doctor, which meant she was already inside the room.","A breath caught in her throat, refusing to go up or down. She ought to be just like me, unable to bear children for the rest of her life.","Wanting to be cured so she could give birth to another child to steal my son's position? Don't even think about it. Keep dreaming!","She raised the corners of her lips, then stepped forward with a face full of worry to ask Liao Xiwen, \"Eldest Miss, is Doctor Song examining Madam inside? I wonder how the situation is?\"","Liao Xiwen looked back at the tightly shut door, sorrow covering her youthful and tender face.","She shook her head and said, \"Mother told me to come out. I don't know how things are going inside either.\"","Concubine Su gently brushed the corner of her eye with her hand. \"I have long heard that Song Jinzhao's medical skills are unmatched in the entire Anyang Prefecture. She even cured Old Madam Meng's incurable disease, so Madam's illness will surely be cured as well.\"","Seeing her so sad that she shed tears, Liao Xiwen thought of her eldest brother Liao Tingjun's health and couldn't help but speak up, \"Rest assured, Concubine Su. Once Miss Song cures my mother's illness, I will have her go and take a look at Eldest Brother. Perhaps Eldest Brother's health can be cured too.\"","The fingers Concubine Su used to hold her handkerchief tightened slightly, as if she were about to crush the thin silk. A dark glint flashed through her lowered eyes, but by the time she looked up, it had vanished without a trace.","\"For over ten years, what kind of medicinal soups hasn't he taken? He's been nourished with ginseng and lingzhi mushrooms, yet Tingjun's health has never shown any improvement.\"","\"Madam's illness is more important. Let Doctor Song focus on treating Madam. As for Tingjun, I think we should just let it be. I don't expect him to be as lively and vigorous as an ordinary young man, wielding swords and spears. As long as he can live a little longer, I will be completely satisfied.\"","When she fell silent, Concubine Su's gaze landed on the tightly shut door. To think that even a biological daughter was kicked out during the consultation.","Recalling the words those doctors had said before leaving, an idea formed in Concubine Su's mind.","Tilting her head, she used her right hand, which held the handkerchief, to stroke the corner of her eye. With a shift of her gaze, the maid standing beside her looked up, met her eyes, and instantly lowered her head.","Concubine Su widened her eyes, suddenly remembering something, and spoke up, \"Oh, right. The roasted squab Wang Zhong bought today might not be as delicious as the ones from Bright Moon Pavilion, but it was marinated with sour plums, making it refreshing and appetizing. I'll have the maid bring it over for Madam to taste.\"","Liao Xiwen smiled bitterly and shook her head. \"Mother doesn't have the appetite to eat these things right now.\" If she could stomach meat, her health wouldn't have deteriorated to this state.","Concubine Su said, \"Perhaps Madam will have an appetite after Doctor Song's diagnosis. Hongtao, hurry and cut the roasted squab, then bring it over.\"","The maid named Hongtao immediately curtsied and turned to leave, but she ended up bumping into another maid standing behind her, sending her entire body crashing toward the door.","Amidst a chorus of gasps, Song Jinzhao pulled her bloodied hand out from between Kong Wanru's legs. The bleeding wasn't heavy, similar to the last day of a menstrual cycle, but the color was a dark, almost blackish red, and the foul odor was pungent.","It was highly likely that a portion of the placenta or fetal membrane was still retained inside her body.","Her body had suffered too many miscarriages, causing severe depletion. It was simply no longer fit for pregnancy.","It was truly quite unbelievable that she had managed to carry this pregnancy to six months before miscarrying.","Startled by the screams, Kong Wanru instinctively grabbed the quilt to cover herself.","The impact didn't cause the doorframe to collapse or break; instead, Hongtao clutched her head, bent over, and slid down against the door to sit on the floor.","Before she could even sit steadily, her shoulders slumped to the right, and she curled up, collapsing onto the ground.","Bright red blood flowed onto the floor tiles. Turning to look at the protruding ring-shaped door handle, one could see fresh bloodstains lingering on it.","There was no sign of the door being broken open, but the person had already laid down.","Concubine Su clenched her jaw, her eyes darkening with gloom.","With so many people guarding outside, they still had to lock the door from the inside. They were simply sick.","Seeing Hongtao close her eyes and lose consciousness, Liao Xiwen immediately began to cry out, \"Quick, go fetch a doctor! Hurry!\"","Concubine Su grabbed Linglong's hand and pointed toward the room. \"There's a doctor right inside. Once Song Jinzhao finishes treating Madam, she can take a look at Hongtao. There's no need to make another trip.\"","Hearing the conversation outside, Song Jinzhao shook her head and sneered. They really never rested.","Kong Wanru asked aloud, \"How does it look? Can I still have children?\"","Song Jinzhao, who was taking off her gloves, found it exceptionally grating the moment she heard her talk about having more children. This entire family was sick, courting death without taking a break.","\"When Madam miscarried, the baby's placenta was not completely expelled from your body. Leaving it inside for a long time will cause infection and inflammation. First, we will use acupuncture combined with three months of medication to cure the illness.\"","\"The damage caused to your body by twelve miscarriages over the years won't heal anytime soon. It will require a long period of conditioning. As short as a year, or as long as two to three years, and perhaps you might have a chance to conceive again.\"","As for how big this chance was and whether it would actually happen? Song Jinzhao couldn't guarantee that.","Kong Wanru excitedly propped up her upper body with her arms, her severely sunken, emaciated eye sockets widening. \"You mean I can still bear children?\"","Song Jinzhao closed her medical box, walked over to the bed, and stared at her.","\"Given Madam's physical condition, it should have been very difficult for you to conceive previously, let alone safely carry it to six months before miscarrying. Have you taken any fertility-promoting prescriptions?\"","What answered Song Jinzhao was pure silence. Without saying a single word, she had already given her answer.","\"Do not use them anymore. With Madam's physical condition, even if you conceive, you won't be able to give birth.\"","\"Even for a normal person, giving birth to a healthy baby is a rare feat. If you're not careful, it could result in two lives lost. It's not worth the risk.\"","Kong Wanru buried her head in the quilt and remained silent. As long as she could give birth to a child, she was willing to do anything.","Even if her health was poor, the estate could afford to support her.","At the very least, she still had her dowry. She would never let him lack medicinal herbs or run out of silver to spend.","Opening the door, what greeted her eyes was the bright red blood on the floor tiles. By the looks of it, her head was definitely busted open.","Song Jinzhao's gaze fell upon Concubine Su, sliding from her face down to the hem of her skirt. She was a bewitching concubine, perfectly exuding the charm of a thirty-year-old woman.","Amidst the rich scent of roses, there was a trace of musk so faint it was almost imperceptible. She must have used it last night, and now it had almost entirely dissipated.","As she scrutinized Concubine Su, the other party was also observing her.","Such a young girl, about the same age as Liao Xiwen, yet she was quite capable. She had turned the Guo family upside down, and now she had come to the Liao estate. She truly was a meddlesome scourge who caused chaos wherever she went.","Liao Xiwen took a large stride forward, grabbing Song Jinzhao's hand and asking anxiously, \"Miss Song, how is my mother's condition?\"","Concubine Su fixed her gaze intently on Song Jinzhao's face, desperate to know if Kong Wanru's infertility could be cured.","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes, her expression grave. \"The illness has been dragged out for too long and has become quite severe. Let's focus on saving her life first.\"","Liao Xiwen stood frozen, her mind racing. Did this mean Song Jinzhao could actually cure her mother's infertility? Otherwise, why would she agree to treat her in the first place?","A stray lock of hair by Concubine Su's ear fluttered in the wind, sticking to her cheek until she brushed it away with her hand.","Gritting her teeth, she forced a smile and pointed to the maid who had been carried off to the corner. \"Doctor Song, please take a look at Hongtao. She accidentally bumped into the door handle just now and seems to have cracked her head open.\"","Linglong stepped aside. Song Jinzhao walked over under the eaves and lifted the maid's head. The back of her head was covered in blood, her hair matted into a bloody mess that obscured the wound.","To fake a fall only to smash into a door handle—was this not the very definition of poetic justice?","Karma had rarely struck so quickly.","Pressing a piece of gauze against the bleeding wound, Song Jinzhao instructed, \"The cut is deep. Find a room and carry her inside first.\"","She used acupuncture to revive the maid, treated the wound, and wrote out a prescription.","Liao Xiwen was waiting outside the side room for Song Jinzhao. Seeing her emerge, she immediately rushed over with a wide smile. \"My mother just asked the servants to open all the doors and windows in her room, and she even said she was hungry! Can her infertility really be cured?\"","Song Jinzhao paused and looked deeply into Liao Xiwen's eyes. \"Do you want a younger brother, Miss Liao?\"","She seemed a little too invested in whether Kong Wanru could bear children.","Liao Xiwen glanced around. \"My father has few heirs, and my eldest brother is not my mother's biological son. If I am ever bullied by my future in-laws, I fear there will be no one to back me up.\"","Song Jinzhao's lips twitched slightly. She averted her gaze and looked toward the doorway.","Pregnancy did not guarantee a boy, and even if it did, how could a brother nearly twenty years her junior possibly back her up?","Her own mother had endured twelve pregnancies just to have a son. Having a little brother was essentially like having a son of her own to raise. Let alone backing her up, it was far more likely she would end up sacrificing her own well-being to support him for the rest of her life.","Liao Xiwen was sixteen this year and would undoubtedly marry within a year or two. At this rate, it was anyone's guess who would be having a child first."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: The Eldest Son of the Liao Family with Heart Disease","paragraphs":["Passing by the garden, they encountered a man draped in a plain white gown walking towards them with a sluggish gait, supported by two young manservants on either side.","Liao Tingjun stopped in his tracks, pulled his arms out of the servants' grasp, and nodded in greeting to the two of them. \"Sister Wen.\"","Liao Xiwen returned the greeting and exchanged a few pleasantries. \"Have you had lunch yet, Big Brother?\"","A weak, faint smile appeared on Liao Tingjun's face. \"I just ate. I had a bit too much and felt bloated, so I came out for a walk. I assume this is Doctor Song?\"","Song Jinzhao suppressed the surprise in her heart and nodded at him. Why did this Young Master Liao look like he was bound to have a short life? His breathing was unsteady, and he even needed people to support him when walking.","A head of the household's legitimate wife who had miscarried twelve times, a cousin-concubine who had miscarried three times, and a frail, sickly only son.","Her gaze turned to Liao Xiwen. Could she have some hidden medical problem too?","Liao Tingjun bowed to Song Jinzhao with cupped hands, pointing to the pavilion in the garden. \"I wonder if Doctor Song could take a look at me, so my sickly and useless body can become a bit stronger.\"","Inside the pavilion, Song Jinzhao's fingers pressed lightly on the radial artery of Liao Tingjun's wrist.","Liao Tingjun was tense all over, his gaze fixed intently on Song Jinzhao's face.","After a long while, she lifted her eyelashes, took a listening tube from her medical box, and walked behind Liao Tingjun. \"Take off your outer clothes and leave only your inner garments.\"","The manservant waiting in the pavilion caught Liao Tingjun's eye and immediately came over to help him undress.","Looking at Song Jinzhao, who remained silent after finishing the examination, Liao Tingjun's heart sank to the bottom of a cliff.","He touched his face, pulling up his cheeks to force a smile. \"I've heard too many doctors' words, so I'm already used to it. Doctor Song, you can speak your mind frankly.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at him, shaking her head as she replied, \"My skills are shallow. Please forgive me, but I am powerless to treat Young Master Liao's illness.\"","\"What are you doing?\" An angry roar that seemed to pierce the sky exploded in their ears.","Concubine Su ran over furiously, the corners of her alluring eyes turning cherry-red from extreme anxiety.","Liao Tingjun propped his trembling hands on the stone table to help himself stand up. \"Concubine Su, I heard Doctor Song's medical skills are superb. I just wanted her to take a look at me.\"","Concubine Su looked at the closed medical box, her sharp nails digging into her palms, but she couldn't feel a hint of pain.","She forced the corners of her mouth up, but there was no trace of a smile in her eyes. \"Your illness has always been treated by Physician Jiang. I was afraid that your body wouldn't be able to adapt to a sudden change of doctors.\"","\"But since you've already examined him, I wonder if Doctor Song has a solution?\"","Song Jinzhao stood up, picked up her medical box, and slung it over her shoulder. \"Your son's illness is too rare. It is beyond my abilities.\"","Concubine Su's tightly clenched fists loosened for a couple of seconds before clenching even tighter than before.","\"We've heard the same words countless times. Thank you for your hard work today, Doctor Song.\"","Liao Xiwen sensed the atmosphere was off. Thinking that Concubine Su, like her mother, had experienced too many disappointments and was on the verge of losing control of her emotions, she quickly ushered Song Jinzhao to leave.","\"I've already had the servants prepare a carriage. It's waiting at the door right now. I'll walk you out.\"","It wasn't until they turned the corner and stepped through the circular stone gate that the intense, staring gaze behind them finally disappeared.","Just before getting into the carriage, Song Jinzhao turned her head and asked, \"Was Young Master Liao born prematurely?\"","Liao Xiwen shook her head without a second thought. \"No, my eldest brother was carried to full term.\"","Song Jinzhao didn't say a word. She ducked into the carriage, sat down, and fell into deep thought.","She truly couldn't cure Liao Tingjun's illness. He suffered from congenital heart defect brought from the womb. Unless he underwent heart surgery, there would never be a way to completely cure it.","With the legitimate wife and a concubine pregnant at the same time, it wouldn't be surprising if Concubine Su had wanted to give birth to the eldest son first.","If that was really the case, she must be full of regret now, knowing that Kong Wanru had given birth to a daughter.","After returning to her room, Concubine Su dismissed the servants, leaving only the maid who had grown up with her since childhood. Her voice trembled slightly.","\"Nanny, do you think Song Jinzhao diagnosed it?\"","Nanny Diao spoke in a low voice, \"Rest assured, Miss. So many years have passed. How could that female doctor find out just by checking the Young Master's pulse once? Just put your heart at ease. The Young Master will never know.\"","The already cold teacup in her hands was gripped so tightly by Concubine Su that it felt scorching hot. Her eyes were slightly wet, and her usual alluring charm vanished without a trace, leaving only bitterness and self-blame.","\"I know how much Tingjun has cared about his health all these years. Whenever he hears of a famous doctor somewhere, he sends people to travel day and night to invite them back and treat them like royalty. I'm just afraid that one day he'll find out the truth and hate me. Even more so, I'm afraid he'll be so heartbroken that he'll be disappointed in me.\"","Nanny Diao knelt by Concubine Su's legs and held her trembling knees. \"You did all of this for the Young Master, Miss. Back then, everyone in the manor said the Madam was pregnant with a boy, which was why you resorted to such a desperate measure. Who knew she would end up giving birth to a girl in the end? This is all fate; you didn't want this either, Miss.\"","Concubine Su closed her eyes to cool her mind. When she opened them, her gaze looked distantly ahead.","\"Send someone to keep an eye on the Spring Water Courtyard. Whatever medicine Song Jinzhao prescribes, tell Physician Jiang. Kong Wanru can linger on with her last breath, but she absolutely must not have another child.\"","\"I can't give birth, and neither can she.\"","Nanny Diao's lips moved, and after hesitating a few times, she finally spoke.","\"If Song Jinzhao can truly cure the Madam's infertility, perhaps she can cure you too, Miss.\"","Concubine Su's eyes were as firm as iron. \"There's no need. Having Tingjun alone is enough for me.\"","Nanny Diao asked, \"Should we still have Wang Zhong continue to deal with Song Jinzhao?\"","Concubine Su shook her head. \"He can't deal with Song Jinzhao. If he gets exposed and she catches a vulnerability, it will only be detrimental to us.\"","\"Keep a close watch on the Spring Water Courtyard. No matter how brilliant her medical skills are, it's useless if they can't be applied to Kong Wanru.\"","Seeing that Song Jinzhao had been gone for so long before returning, Song Shixue asked curiously, \"Sister, is Madam Liao's illness very serious?\"","Song Jinzhao put down her medical box and tapped her head with her finger. \"Illnesses of the heart are hard to cure, but what's even harder to cure is someone's mindset. If she can't figure things out, she can never be saved.\"","Liu Xuanqing, who was practicing suturing techniques, stopped his movements and looked at Song Jinzhao. Thinking of Kong Wanru's condition, he couldn't help but nod in agreement. \"Actually, as long as she doesn't have children and is willing to cooperate with the treatment, living to sixty will definitely not be a problem.\"","He sighed and chimed in, \"But she insists on giving birth. It's understandable, though. After all, having no heir is not a long-term solution.\"","Song Shixue looked at Liu Xuanqing in confusion. \"Isn't Miss Liao born to Madam Liao?\"","Liu Xuanqing opened his mouth and closed it again. A girl can't carry on the family line.","Song Jinzhao shot a cold glare over, and Liu Xuanqing instantly lowered his head.","He hastily picked up the pigskin with his hands and started changing the subject. \"Why does this stitch seem crooked?\"","Song Shixue walked over to take a look, clicking her tongue in disgust. \"How come your suturing isn't even as good as mine when I was eight? This is all twisted outward like a splayed character. How ugly will it be when it heals?\""]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Massive Purchases of Poultry and Livestock","paragraphs":["After Fushun rode back from the outskirts of the city to report to Song Jinzhao that the farmstead had been completed according to her plans, Song Jinzhao took Fushun and Lanxi to the livestock market the next day.","Song Anhao wrinkled his sparse, pale crescent-shaped eyebrows. Crossing his hands over his slightly upturned little nose and mouth, he mumbled, \"It stinks. There's so much poop.\"","Song Jinzhao covered her younger brother's nose with a scented handkerchief. \"I told you it was dirty and told you not to come, but you insisted on following. Regret it now, don't you?\"","Song Anhao plopped his head onto Song Jinzhao's shoulder, pouting with a voice full of deep grievance.","\"Eldest Sister is home today, so I want to be with Eldest Sister.\"","Ever since Lanxi's hands and feet had mostly healed, coupled with the increasing number of patients at the clinic, Song Jinzhao had stopped bringing Song Anhao to the clinic every day.","As a result, Song Anhao could only see Song Jinzhao and the others in the mornings and after dusk. Over time, he naturally started to feel a bit unhappy about it.","Song Jinzhao rested her hand on her younger brother's back. \"Don't you like playing with Lanxi? Are you upset?\"","Walking behind them, Lanxi looked up at Song Anhao.","Song Anhao shook his head, his smooth, tender cheek gently rubbing against Song Jinzhao's shoulder, his hot breath hitting her neck.","\"I like him, but I like being with my older brother and sister even more.\"","As Lanxi stared at Song Anhao's face full of dependence and his spoiled manner, the bloody scenes deeply suppressed in his mind were dug back up, causing his hands hanging by his sides to tremble uncontrollably as they clenched into fists.","He hurriedly lowered his head so no one would notice the fear, hatred, and the faint trace of sorrow in his eyes.","Song Jinzhao patted the back of Song Anhao's head, gently bouncing him in her arms. \"In the future, if you don't want to stay at home, just have Lanxi take you to the clinic.\"","Song Anhao wrapped his arms around Song Jinzhao's neck, revealing two small dimples on his face. \"I'll go tomorrow.\"","The livestock market was bustling every day with many livestock vendors and poultry sellers setting up stalls. Cages lining both sides of the street were filled with all sorts of live animals, while cows, sheep, donkeys, and horses were tied to ropes, occasionally letting out sorrowful cries.","Song Jinzhao had asked around beforehand. She led her group into a small shop with a banner reading All Creatures Poultry. Inside, Yang Qing was sound asleep on a chair.","Hearing footsteps, he lazily opened his eyes, his pupils hazy as if he hadn't fully woken up.","Once he clearly saw Song Jinzhao's face and the two servants standing behind her, he quickly stood up, smiled enthusiastically, and bowed. \"Honored guest, you grace my humble shop. Forgive my negligence.\"","\"Please have a seat, miss. Are you looking to buy poultry or livestock?\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"I heard that Master Yang in the livestock market has the most goods and can procure any amount requested. I wonder if that's true?\"","Yang Qing burst into hearty laughter and picked up a teapot to pour water for Song Jinzhao. \"I may not be much, but I do alright in Anyang Prefecture. However much you want, miss, I can definitely have it delivered within three days.\"","\"Two hundred piglets, fifty young sheep, and ten plowing oxen in their prime. Half male, half female for all.\"","\"Five hundred adult hens, five hundred adult ducks, five thousand chicken eggs, and five thousand duck eggs. The eggs must have been laid within the last seven days, as I intend to hatch chicks and ducklings. Add two hundred goslings to that as well.\"","Yang Qing stared blankly with his mouth agape. The tea overflowed the rim of the cup and burned his hand, causing him to grimace, shake his hand, and blow on it.","\"Miss, what do you need so many for? The quantity is too large; I can't gather it all in three days. I'll need at least seven.\"","Song Jinzhao leaned back in her chair, tilting her head with a light chuckle. \"Just a moment ago, Master Yang was boasting about his great abilities, claiming you could deliver any amount within three days. Giving up already?\"","The spilled tea on the table was much like Yang Qing's busted bragging, too full, it spilled over, burning his own hand.","He poured a fresh cup of tea and pushed it in front of Song Jinzhao.","\"I have poor eyesight and failed to see that you are doing big business, miss. How about six days? I'll give you a one percent discount.\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips and stared into his eyes. A one percent discount. He really had the nerve to offer that.","Standing on either side, Fushun and Lanxi speechlessly curled their lips and rolled their eyes. Buying so much for a mere one percent discount, this merchant was truly stingy.","Song Jinzhao held up her fingers. \"A twenty percent discount. I'll pay a thirty percent deposit first. Deliver the goods to my farmstead outside the city in five days. If everything is in order, I'll pay the balance.\"","Yang Qing suddenly felt his tea had lost its flavor.","She was a major client. If he took this deal, he could kiss a good night's sleep goodbye for the next five days.","\"Five days it is. Tell me the location of the farmstead, and I will deliver every single one to you in five days without a single one missing.\"","Being able to make a big profit before winter set in, he would be a fool not to do it.","Yang Qing brought out his abacus and clacked away to calculate the cost. Song Jinzhao casually jotted down a few equations on a piece of paper, calculated the price, and put down her brush.","A quarter of an hour later, a freshly drafted contract was placed before them. Song Jinzhao looked it over, found no issues, and signed it.","Yang Qing asked in astonishment, \"Aren't you going to calculate it, miss?\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her thumbprint onto the paper. \"I already calculated it. There are no problems.\"","Yang Qing furrowed his brows. When had she calculated it?","She had eaten half a plate of walnut pastries; could she do mental math while eating?","After paying the deposit, Song Jinzhao left with her servants. Yang Qing picked up the paper she had left under her teacup. Some characters were already blurred beyond recognition by spilled tea.","But the circled amount at the very end matched the figure written on the contract down to the last copper coin.","\"What kind of arithmetic method is this? How could she be so fast?\"","Ever since Ye Liangyu appeared at the Meng family's birthday banquet leaning on a crutch, more and more people had come to visit him. Some even blocked the academy entrance until Mu Hongyue chased them away.","\"You shouldn't have gone with a crutch. Now everyone knows your leg will recover. What if those people in the capital refuse to let you off?\"","\"You only have one life. Haven't you learned your lesson yet?\"","Ye Liangyu set down his wolf-hair brush and picked up the letter filled with writing, setting it aside to dry.","\"I will never regret what I have done. The assassins haven't been caught, and the true mastermind behind the scenes hasn't been brought to justice. I have to go back. I will avenge this myself.\"","Mu Hongyue gritted his teeth, furious enough to die. \"What if you die before you even get back? They dared to brazenly kill you once; what makes you think they'd fear doing it a second time?\"","His fist slammed heavily onto the desk, splashing ink from the inkstone everywhere.","Ye Liangyu gritted his teeth and said, \"I'm only afraid they won't try a second time.\"","Mu Hongyue's eyes grew tense and red. He was always this stubborn, unrepentant to the death.","Using himself as bait. If he really died, having never married or had children in his life, he wouldn't even have anyone to wear mourning clothes, smash the clay basin, or hold the spirit banner for his funeral.","All alone. In a few years, who would even remember Ye Liangyu? He would just be a wandering ghost, a handful of yellow earth offered to heaven and earth.","Seeing Mu Hongyue silent and so upset he looked ready to cry, Ye Liangyu smiled and said, \"Don't worry. Qiming hasn't passed the imperial examination to become an official yet. I won't die that easily.\"","Mu Hongyue gave a cold snort, a bitter mock on his lips. \"That's the only right thing you've done in your entire life.\"","Ye Liangyu picked up the dried letter, folded it in half, slipped it into an envelope, sealed it with wax, and handed it to Yunhe. \"Arrange for someone to send this out immediately.\"","Yunhe took the envelope with both hands and quickly left the manor.","After school, Song Qiming, who was packing his things, suddenly sneezed. The rush of air out of his nose made his throat feel dry and achy.","Su Luobai asked with concern, \"Did you catch a cold?\"","Song Qiming shook his head, rubbing the tip of his nose with his index finger. \"No, it just suddenly felt a bit itchy.\"","Su Luobai said meaningfully, \"Someone is probably thinking of you. Ever since Mr. Ye came to teach at the Inner House, the students of the Upper House have been pining for him every day, desperately hoping you'll pass the exam into the Inner House and bring Mr. Ye along with you.\"","Song Qiming shouldered his book box and headed outside. \"There's still over a month before the academy's annual examination. I'll do my best.\""]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Is the Loss of Liao Xiwen a Retribution","paragraphs":["Five days later, Yang Qing and his men drove all the livestock and poultry Song Jinzhao had requested, including two hundred piglets and fifty lambs, to the farmstead in the suburbs.","\"I've never seen animals live in such a nice place. They are sheltered from the wind and rain, and it's cleaned every day. Is your master really this particular about raising chickens and ducks?\"","\"My lady said that hygiene is very important. If it's too dirty, they can easily get sick, and they will die in droves,\" Fushun said, holding a brush with a struggling expression as he checked the numbers and kept records.","Reading and writing were truly exhausting for him. Lanxi had taught him for over a month, but to this day, he only knew how to write his own name and do the most basic accounting and arithmetic.","He was slow with the abacus, needing to double-check everything twice to feel at ease. A task that Chunxing could finish in the time it took to drink one cup of tea took him two.","But Fushun had no choice but to learn; otherwise, if he were replaced by someone else one day, he would truly regret it.","Yang Qing stood on a small hillside, gazing into the distance as if pondering something.","After a long while, he approached Fushun. \"Pass a message to your lady. When the pigs, sheep, chickens, and ducks on the farmstead are ready to be sold next year, come find me. I guarantee I'll give you a good price.\"","Fushun handed the final payment to Yang Qing and said with a smile, \"Master Yang, there's no need to mention it. What we raise here isn't even enough for my lady's own shops, so we still have to buy from outside, let alone sell them.\"","Yang Qing frowned in confusion. \"Raising so many... can your master's household finish eating them all? How many people do you have?\"","Fushun puffed out his chest, his voice seventy percent louder than before, the ending notes rising high with pride.","\"Does Master Yang know of the Song Family Delicacy Shop? That was opened by my lady.\"","Yang Qing's brow relaxed in sudden realization. \"The one that sells braised food?\"","Fushun nodded vigorously. \"That's right, the very one that sells braised food.\"","Yang Qing took a deep breath and looked down the hill at the rows upon rows of pigsties and poultry sheds. No wonder she bought so many; it really wouldn't be enough.","\"It seems your master is planning to open branch shops?\"","Fushun smiled and scratched his head. \"It seems she has that intention.\"","At the earliest, they had to wait for this batch to grow up. After the beginning of spring, the numbers would have to increase. However many were slaughtered, that many would be replenished. Raising them themselves would definitely be lower in cost than buying from outside.","At Chunshui Courtyard in the Liao Residence.","After the acupuncture session ended, a maid immediately brought over a bowl of herbal medicine and fed it to Kong Wanru.","Seeing Song Jinzhao using chopsticks to poke through the medicinal dregs in the pot, Liao Xiwen whispered, \"I had the maids take the prescription you wrote to Song's Clinic to get the medicine. We didn't buy it anywhere else.\"","Song Jinzhao's right hand paused. She pressed her lips together and took two deep breaths, truly feeling a bit exasperated.","She looked up with a sharp gaze. \"I am checking to see if anyone has tampered with the medicine.\"","Liao Xiwen froze, then hastily waved her hands to explain. \"The maids in this courtyard are all my mother's dowry servants. It's impossible for anyone to tamper with it. With so many miscarriages before, my mother has thoroughly investigated it long ago.\"","Song Jinzhao turned her head to look at Kong Wanru lying on the bed. The woman's face was completely expressionless. Both mother and daughter were foolish.","\"The fact that you were born, and your mother could get pregnant so many times, proves that her body is not prone to miscarriages. To be pregnant twelve times and miscarry twelve times... only a fool would believe it was an accident.\"","Kong Wanru's voice was hoarse and feeble. \"But I've investigated many times. The doctors who came to examine me all said that I miscarried because my body hadn't recovered properly from the previous miscarriages. Even after several accidents, no problems were found.\"","Song Jinzhao packed her medical box, preparing to leave. \"Just because nothing was found doesn't mean nothing is there.\"","Liao Xiwen saw her out with worry in her eyes, her footsteps somewhat erratic.","\"Miss Song, do you know something? Can you tell me?\"","Song Jinzhao stopped in her tracks. \"I haven't discovered anything; I just have my doubts.\"","\"It is inconvenient for me, an outsider, to interfere in Miss Liao's family affairs. Your mother is currently my patient, and a healer's duty is to treat illnesses and save lives. As for anything else, it is not my place as a doctor to meddle.\"","The dark secrets of the Liao family's inner quarters were even messier than those of the Guo family. If they were truly uncovered, who knew what kind of storm it would cause.","Song Jinzhao couldn't be bothered to waste her time interfering. With that kind of free time, she might as well open a few more shops and make more money.","Watching the figure of Song Jinzhao riding away on horseback, Liao Xiwen furrowed her delicate brows, biting her lip and smudging her exquisite rouge.","Returning to Chunshui Courtyard, Kong Wanru asked, \"Did you find out anything?\"","Liao Xiwen shook her head. \"Miss Song just has her doubts. She believes it's impossible for you to miscarry so many times for no reason.\"","Thinking of how Guo Yiyao had been schemed against in every possible way by Liu Fufeng, she hesitated before speaking. \"Mother, if the previous miscarriages were truly the result of someone's schemes, could it be Concubine Su?\"","As soon as she said it, she felt it was unlikely and couldn't help but speculate, \"She has always been very respectful to you over the years. Besides eldest brother, she hasn't given birth to any other children and has also miscarried three times. Could it be someone else?\"","When Kong Wanru thought of the children she had lost over the years, her chest ached as if pierced by thousands of needles.","\"There are only so many people in the manor. Anyone who should have been investigated has been investigated long ago. You can leave first. Perhaps the heavens simply don't want me to have another child.\"","Liao Xiwen lowered her eyes and silently left the room. They both had only one child, yet Concubine Su's and her mother's attitudes were completely different.","After her eldest brother turned four, he was taken by their father to be personally cared for. Concubine Su would visit him three times a day to deliver things and ask after his well-being, terrified that he might feel the slightest bit unwell.","But she herself, staying by her mother's side, received far less maternal love than her eldest brother did.","Just because she was a girl, her mother didn't like her as much.","If her mother truly gave birth to a boy, would the tiny bit of care she had left disappear entirely?","Liao Xiwen supported her stomach and slowly sat down on the railing bench. Her eyes were lifeless, and deep within her pupils lay a trace of disappointment as she stared blankly at the wild grass in the courtyard.","The night was hazy. Lying in bed, Kong Wanru stared out the window with dark, gloomy eyes.","The cold wind blew against the thorny rose vines. The branches swayed, and the sharp thorns gleamed in the candlelight.","With just a light touch, they could pierce the skin and become tainted with the scent of fresh blood.","She muttered to herself, \"Hasn't all these years of retribution been enough?\"","\"Four for one. The sinful debts of the past should have been paid off by now.\"","Just a quarter past the beginning of the Xu hour, Lanxi drove the carriage bringing Song Qiming back from the Ye Residence.","Song Jinzhao, who was getting ready to wash up, stood up to welcome him. \"Why are you half an hour earlier than usual today?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"Teacher said the weather has been getting colder these past few nights. He also said that since we see each other at the academy every day, I don't need to go over in the evenings anymore. I just need to stay for half an hour after school to discuss essays. He will give me more coursework after I enter the Upper House next spring.\"","Song Jinzhao looked out the window to gauge the temperature. Winter hadn't even begun yet; it didn't seem that cold.","\"Since that's the case, reading at home in the evenings is the same. When you want to relax, you can practice martial arts with Qingshuang and Lanxi.\"","Song Qiming's path in the imperial examinations was already progressing much faster than Song Jinzhao had anticipated. With his current grades and Ye Liangyu keeping an eye on him, the provincial examination in two years wouldn't be a big problem. The only question would be his ranking.","Thinking of the winter vegetable seeds currently being cultivated at the farmstead, they would have to return to Song Family Village for the New Year this year. Neither Chunxing nor Fushun had the talent for management, Qingshuang's ambitions lay elsewhere, and Lanxi was too young. She had to find a capable steward to take charge as soon as possible."]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: The Boy Who Went in Search of His Mother","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao browsed the slave market but failed to find anyone suitable. Qian Sanya, having talked until his mouth was nearly dry, picked up a teapot and chugged it empty straight from the spout.","\"Miss, the kind of person you're looking for is truly rare. They would have to be seasoned servants sold off by prominent families, or perhaps bankrupt merchants selling themselves into servitude voluntarily. It all comes down to luck. Why don't you lower your standards a bit? I thought the two we just saw were quite decent.\"","The slow tapping of Song Jinzhao's index finger against the table came to a halt. \"I already have people like them at home. There's no need to buy more.\"","Someone like Fushun was perfectly fine at following orders, but when it came to managing household affairs and coordinating the bigger picture, he fell far short.","He could only take orders, not give them.","Upon returning to the clinic, Song Shixue handed a wedding invitation to Song Jinzhao. \"The Meng family had this sent over. They are inviting you to attend the wedding banquet of Young Master Meng and Miss Guo, Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao opened it, took a brief glance, and tossed it aside. \"Prepare a gift and have Qingshuang deliver it. We are busy at home, so we won't be attending the banquet.\"","Their relationship with the Meng family had reached a sufficient level; there was no need to deepen it any further.","Song Shixue nodded. Deep down, she didn't want to go either. It would not only be boring but also potentially dangerous; they wouldn't even be able to eat in peace.","On the way home that evening, Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes, glancing behind her.","It had only been peaceful for a few days. Who had sent someone this time?","After she returned home and the front gates were shut, a distance away, Xu Geng pressed himself against the pillar of a thatched cottage, his burning gaze fixed intently on the Song family's tightly closed doors.","Heading to the shop the next morning, Song Jinzhao once again detected that faint, elusive gaze. Unlike Wang Zhong, whoever was sent this time did not seem to harbor any malice.","Wanting to uncover the person's true motives, Song Jinzhao did not expose them right away. To her surprise, this tailing lasted for seven whole days.","She stared at the youth standing in the corner dressed in tattered clothes. He looked to be about the same age as Qiming.","Whenever she went out alone, he never followed. He only shadowed the route back and forth between the shop and the Song residence in the mornings and evenings, waiting outside the rest of the time. His target was not her.","On the eighth day, as Song Jinzhao was returning alone from a medical consultation at the Liao Manor, the youth suddenly darted out from a side alley and stopped right in front of her.","Song Jinzhao stared at him. \"You've been following for seven days. You're finally willing to show yourself.\"","The youth was taken aback. Upon recovering, he spoke with a hint of reluctance, \"My name is Xu Geng. Zhang Xialian is my mother. She works in your shop and goes by the name Qingshuang now.\"","Song Jinzhao looked the youth up and down. The age matched, and his eyes did bear a slight resemblance to Qingshuang.","\"Has your mind recovered?\"","Xu Geng nodded vigorously.","\"Do you want to take your mother back with you?\"","Xu Geng clenched his jaw, his eyes growing stinging and wet.","He had no money to buy her freedom. Originally, he had planned to trade himself for his mother, but now...","Xu Geng clenched his fists and shook his head. His throat tightened as he forced the words out of his mouth, syllable by syllable.","\"She is living a good life now. Better than she did at home.\"","His eyes turned red. After a moment of silence, he abruptly dropped to his knees before Song Jinzhao, tilting his head up to gaze at her.","\"I am leaving today. I want to beg you to take good care of my mother. Please do not beat or scold her. My mother is a good person, and she works very hard.\"","He fought back his tears, refusing to let them fall. \"When the day comes that I can provide her with a good life, I will come back to get her. When that time comes, I will give you a lot of money—more than you could spend in a lifetime.\"","Looking at his worn-through soles, she realized he had walked all the way from Haoyue City. To find Qingshuang, he must have endured unimaginable hardships.","A twinge of sorrow tugged at Song Jinzhao's heart. \"You don't need to beg me. Your mother is a servant of the Song family now, and I have always valued her highly.\"","Through his observations and inquiries over the past few days, Xu Geng knew that Song Jinzhao was not a wicked master who would abuse her servants without cause.","Seeing her earnest tone and solemn expression, Xu Geng wiped away his tears and scrambled up from the ground. \"Please don't tell my mother I was here. She will be sad if she knows.\"","Watching the frail, solitary figure of the youth as he walked away with absolute resolve, Song Jinzhao stood rooted to the spot for a long while before finally taking her leave.","A husband killed by mountain bandits to save his wife. A son beaten into a simpleton to save his mother.","If it hadn't been for those bandits, this family might have lived a very happy life.","Honoring Xu Geng's request, Song Jinzhao did not tell Qingshuang that her son had come looking for her upon her return.","The boy had already left, and she had no intention of returning to her old home anyway. Why shatter the peace of her current life?","If it was meant to be, there would come a day for them to reunite. For now, Xu Geng was still incapable of protecting his mother.","And perhaps the current Qingshuang had never expected her son to protect her in the first place.","Ever since Song Jinzhao expressed concerns about the medicine being tampered with or swapped out, Kong Wanru had assigned two extra people to keep a close eye on the medicine pot while it was being brewed.","After more than half a month passed without incident, everyone's vigilance slowly began to relax.","In Concubine Su's courtyard, Nanny Diao's brows were furrowed so deeply they resembled a centipede. \"Song Jinzhao comes every day to administer acupuncture to the Madam, and her medical skills are exceptional. If we tamper with the medicine, others might not notice, but I fear she will. The step-wife of the Guo family met her downfall right at her hands.\"","Wang Zhong knocked excitedly on the door and waited to be let in.","\"Answering Concubine Su, I have found out that Song Jinzhao's family might return to their hometown in Xining City for the New Year. During that time, Doctor Liu Xuanqing should be the one taking over the medical consultations. That will be the perfect opportunity to swap the medicine.\"","Concubine Su's voice lifted with a hint of smugness. \"Anyang Academy historically goes on holiday in the early twelfth lunar month. In a month and a half, Kong Wanru's illness shouldn't be fully cured, right?\"","Nanny Diao lowered her head and placed a peeled orange by her hand, curling her lips into a fawning smile. \"Word from the Chunshui Courtyard is that she won't be able to stop taking her medicine for at least a year or two.\"","A fleeting glint of murderous intent flashed in Concubine Su's eyes. Trailing her red-painted fingernails up her leg to her lips, she crooked a finger, beckoning Wang Zhong closer.","Wang Zhong crawled forward on his knees and bowed his head before her.","\"Go out and ask around. See if there are any assassins in the underworld who kill for money. Wait until Song Jinzhao leaves Anyang Prefecture, then silence them. Leave no survivors.\"","A flicker of dread passed through Wang Zhong's eyes. Concubine Su had never ordered him to kill anyone before.","Song Jinzhao was the first. Originally, the plan wasn't to kill her, but merely to injure her severely enough that she wouldn't be able to visit the Liao Manor.","Hiring an underworld organization to wipe out an entire family was no small matter.","A thick stack of banknotes was pressed against Wang Zhong's chest. Glancing down, he saw that it had to be at least several thousand taels.","With trembling fingers, Wang Zhong accepted the banknotes and kowtowed. \"I will definitely see this matter done. One strike, no misses, and no survivors.\"","Nanny Diao stared at Wang Zhong's retreating back as he left in excitement, voicing her displeasure. \"Miss, isn't ten thousand taels a bit too much to give?\"","Years ago, when Concubine Su was newly widowed and traveling a thousand miles to seek refuge with the Liao family, she had witnessed an underworld organization committing murder. Since Wang Zhong was incapable of dealing with Song Jinzhao, she would simply find someone who was.","Concubine Su leaned back. \"As long as Song Jinzhao is killed, it will all be worth it.\"","\"If we don't get rid of her, what happens when she returns to Anyang Prefecture after the New Year and checks Kong Wanru's pulse again? It's better to just kill her and be done with it once and for all.\"","If she hadn't been worried that Liao Wangshu would take a new wife if Kong Wanru died—perhaps someone clever whom she wouldn't be able to control—she would have killed Kong Wanru a long time ago.","After causing her to miscarry so many times, she had finally rendered Kong Wanru barren. She absolutely could not allow a stumbling block like Song Jinzhao to ruin everything now."]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: The Annual Exam is Approaching, Under Attack","paragraphs":["Barely ten days after the ducklings on the farmstead had hatched, the temperature in Anyang Prefecture plummeted.","Song Qiming also began his final sprint of preparations for Anyang Academy's annual year-end examination.","Outside the Inner House lecture hall, Upper House student Wang Xu pulled along He Feixuan, the top student of the Upper House. They used the excuse of visiting Wang Xu's younger brother, but in reality, they were observing Song Qiming's study state.","Seeing the two men's gazes locked onto Song Qiming without a moment's deviation, Wang Rui couldn't help but step forward to block their line of sight.","\"If you keep staring, you'll be noticed. Don't worry, Song Qiming is guaranteed to test into the Upper House this time. He's already surpassed Hu Fengye.\"","Hu Fengye was a mountain who had occupied third place in the Inner House for a full eight months, yet Song Qiming had snatched his position after being here for only three months.","Having one-on-one guidance from a renowned master truly made a difference. His speed of improvement was something others couldn't catch up to even on stilts.","Hearing this, Wang Xu let his gaze fall upon his younger brother, Wang Rui's face. \"There's only half a month left until the year-end exam. You must not slack off; there are only three spots to enter the Upper House.\"","Wang Rui tilted his head and smiled. \"Don't worry, Big Brother. Song Qiming won't be able to surpass me for the time being. I will definitely be one of those three.\"","Passing by, Yan Baoyi heard the trio's conversation and ground his teeth until they audibly clicked.","He returned to his seat in the third-to-last row, his gaze landing on Song Qiming's back as if it had been steeped in poison.","Over three monthly exams, his grades had slipped to thirty-seventh place in the Inner House. Even Song Gaoli had climbed over his head.","When they first entered the academy, he was second and Song Qiming was first. One up and one down—now there was a world of difference between them.","He blamed all of this on Song Qiming. If not for Song Qiming's constant provocation, how could he have focused all his attention on him, resulting in a lack of concentration in class? By not advancing, he had fallen behind.","Now, even Ding Weiyue had taken on a new disciple, acting as if he was ready to give up on him.","Seeing Song Qiming's status in the academy rise higher and higher, on the verge of testing into the Upper House, how could Yan Baoyi possibly be willing to accept it?","Song Gaoli was holding a book and about to approach Song Qiming for a discussion. As he turned his head, he noticed Yan Baoyi's damp, gloomy gaze that resembled a poisonous snake, causing his shoulders to twitch in an involuntary shudder.","He bent down, propped his arms on the desk, and leaned close to Song Qiming's ear to whisper.","\"We've been in the academy for so long, why does Yan Baoyi still find you an eyesore? Hasn't he stopped ever since Master Ye came to teach in the Inner House?\"","Song Qiming turned his head to look at him. As their eyes met, invisible sparks seemed to fly.","\"This person has too strong a sense of jealousy. Now that he has fallen into a slump, he's definitely resentful. No one has bullied you in the dormitory recently, right?\"","Song Gaoli clicked his tongue and gave a dismissive smile. \"I'm just a small fry. They don't even put me in their eyes.\"","\"By the way, has your older sister confirmed when she's returning to the village this year? Don't forget to take me along when the time comes.\"","Song Qiming said, \"The academy only gives thirty-five days of vacation in total. If the journey goes smoothly, a round trip will eat up half a month. My sister said we'll leave as soon as my break starts. Get your things packed, and I'll come call for you when it's time.\"","Song Gaoli nodded.","Ten days later at the farmstead, Song Jinzhao stared at the pea and bottle gourd vines beginning to climb up the ropes inside the greenhouse. Her heart surged with emotion, and she could hardly conceal the excitement and thrill on her face.","Winter greenhouse cultivation had finally been accomplished.","Fushun smiled so widely that several wrinkles bunched up at the corners of his eyes. \"Eldest Miss, according to the timeline, we can harvest the first batch before the New Year. The other leafy greens have also grown to a thumb's height. If you want to eat them tender, we can pinch them off in ten days.\"","It had to be said that their young miss was truly capable. As long as they did things according to her requirements, there was nothing that wouldn't succeed.","To be able to grow vegetables in the dead of winter—if word got out, people would think it was immortal magic bestowed by the heavens.","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"Fresh vegetables are scarce in winter. Let them grow a bit bigger before picking them, so they weigh more.\"","\"I've already rented the shop next to the gourmet food store. When the time comes, we'll sell them inside. Have Chunxing take someone to keep an eye on it, and Lanxi will come to the farmstead to help you.\"","\"This is a list of all the restaurants in Anyang Prefecture. Once the vegetable shop opens, they will definitely come to discuss cooperation. The price must be standardized and cannot fall below this number.\"","Fushun took the list, read it over, and nodded. \"I understand.\"","Anyang Academy's year-end exam would last for two days, and tomorrow was the first day.","After school was dismissed in the evening, Song Qiming carried his book box on his back and headed home. Thinking about the holiday starting in a few days, even someone as diligent and studious as him couldn't help but feel a bit of anticipation.","As he quickened his pace and turned a corner, three masked men suddenly rushed at him.","Song Qiming's pupils shrank drastically, and he instinctively spun around, using his book box to ram into them.","The first masked man to charge clutched his aching chest and roared, \"Get him! Pin him to the ground and cripple his fingers!\"","Song Qiming reached his left hand to his right arm. A short, compact sleeve arrow was gripped in his hand, ready to fire. With a vigilant and stern expression, he demanded, \"Who are you?\"","The man raised a fist. \"I am your absolute master!\"","One against three, the four of them engaged in a chaotic brawl.","Song Qiming threw a punch with his left and a kick with his right, aiming entirely at the most vulnerable parts of the human body where the pain would be the most excruciating.","A man who had nearly had his mask ripped off cursed gruffly, \"This kid knows martial arts! Grab your weapons!\"","Three daggers gleaming with a cold light were drawn from their waists. Seeing this, Song Qiming pressed his thumb against the trigger mechanism. Taking the initiative, he raised his hand and unleashed a volley of iron needles like a celestial maiden scattering blossoms.","To make it more convenient to carry, Song Jinzhao had specially modified the sleeve arrow, replacing the short arrows with iron needles.","Although they couldn't pierce very deeply, the iron needles had been steeped in venom. As long as they pierced the skin, they would take effect within seven seconds."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: Knock Down Three, Then Bring Eight More","paragraphs":["Seeing this, the three men immediately dropped into a crouch, shielding their faces with their arms.","A volley of iron needles flew straight at them. With nowhere to hide, several needles pierced their skin, sending a wave of numbness spreading through their flesh.","One of the men tried to reach up and pull the needles out. He had barely plucked one free when a wave of severe dizziness hit him. His legs gave out, and he collapsed to the side. \"They're poisoned...\"","\"Too late to realize that now!\"","Song Qiming tore the veils from the three men's faces. He didn't recognize a single one of them; he had absolutely never seen them before.","He planted the sole of his shoe squarely on the face of the man who had been barking orders and demanded harshly, \"Speak. Who are you? Why are you coming after me?\"","\"Who sent you?\"","The man clamped his jaw shut, refusing to utter a word. His gaze shifted to something behind Song Qiming, a dark glint flashing in his eyes.","Song Qiming delivered a vicious kick to the man's face with his right foot. A premolar snapped at the root, filling the man's mouth with the metallic taste of blood.","\"If you won't talk, I'll hand you over to the magistrate.\"","The man clawed at the ground, dirt packing beneath his fingernails.","Not only did this kid carry hidden weapons, but he was also completely ruthless. Had he known, he would have demanded a lot more money for this job.","Seeing the man still wouldn't speak, Song Qiming was just about to pull his foot back and go fetch the authorities when a heavy club smashed violently into his back.","He stumbled forward, barely catching himself with his hands before hitting the ground.","A sudden gust of wind whipped past his ear, ruffling his loose hair. Song Qiming's eyes snapped wide open. Using his momentum, he immediately tucked into a forward roll, tumbling twice before springing swiftly to his feet.","Before he could even make out the figures, the overlapping shadows of two clubs swung toward him simultaneously.","He threw up his arms to block the blow. Taking a closer look, he realized there were far more than just two attackers. A dark mass of men loomed before him—at least seven or eight of them.","With his path home completely blocked, Song Qiming spun around and sprinted in the opposite direction.","Two alleys away on a narrow path, Ji Youming frowned slightly, a faint trace of worry weighing on his mind.","\"The annual exams are tomorrow. Are you confident?\"","Since Hu Fengye hadn't managed to outscore Song Qiming in the last monthly exams, Ji Youming was genuinely worried that his friend wouldn't make it into the Upper Academy.","Hu Fengye shook his head with a sigh. \"If only they would open up two more spots this year.\"","Ji Youming glanced up at the sky. \"Not a chance. The quota hasn't changed in decades.\"","\"Help!!!\"","The desperate cry echoed from a distance. Both boys immediately snapped their heads toward the sound.","They caught a fleeting glimpse of a youth in a dark cyan short jacket darting from the left side of the street to the right. A second later, seven or eight masked men sprinted after him, vanishing into the alleyway.","Hu Fengye froze in his tracks. Pointing toward where the figures had disappeared, he asked, his voice laced with uncertainty, \"Was that Song Qiming just now?\"","Ji Youming nodded. \"I think so.\"","The two exchanged a single glance. In the next second, they took off as if their feet were on fire, sprinting madly in the direction Song Qiming had vanished.","It was the bitter cold of winter, and it had snowed that morning. With the freezing wind howling through the streets, the roads were already completely deserted by evening; not a single soul was in sight.","The townspeople, huddled around their hearths indoors, heard the cries for help. Cracking their windows open just a sliver to peek outside, they only saw the receding backs of a group of people running frantically down the street.","One woman shot a fierce glare at her husband and muttered bitterly, \"It's definitely the thugs from the gambling den out hunting someone down again. Heaven knows how much debt was racked up this time.\"","Her husband silently turned his head away, not daring to utter a word.","\"Don't run! Stop right there!\" Ji Youming bellowed, dragging a broom behind him. The snow kicked up by his boots splattered right into the peering woman's face.","Hu Fengye gripped a heavy rock tightly in his hand. Plumes of white vapor puffed from his mouth in rapid succession as he gasped for air. His voice came out in broken fragments, his throat burning from the frigid air.","\"They're running too fast... I can't keep this up.\"","Ji Youming grabbed his friend's sleeve, practically dragging him along. \"Hurry! They're going to beat Song Qiming to death!\"","Staring at the backs of the two boys as they disappeared down the road, the woman wiped the snow from her face and raised a brow in confusion. \"Why are there two scholars chasing them? What on earth is going on?\"","Rounding yet another corner, Hu Fengye braced his hands on his knees. His chest heaved as he gasped for breath, his face completely numb from the cold.","\"I really can't go any further.\"","He pointed toward the alleyway on the right. \"Let's cut through the side path and climb the wall. I seriously can't run anymore.\"","It made sense that the masked thugs had incredible stamina, but how was Song Qiming such a fast runner? They had been running for ages and he still hadn't stopped!","He might as well have stopped and fought them—at least then he and Ji Youming would have been able to catch up.","Meanwhile, the masked men were growing increasingly anxious as they failed to close the distance on Song Qiming.","Even though the streets were empty, if the boy kept screaming for help like that, there was no telling how many people he would alert.","In a panic, one of the thugs completely disregarded their employer's strict orders to only cripple the target and spare his life. He hurled his dagger straight at Song Qiming's back.","\"Watch out!\" Ji Youming leaped down from the top of the wall, swinging his broom to swat the flying dagger away.","Song Qiming skidded to a halt, his face registering pure shock. \"What are you guys doing here?\"","Hu Fengye jumped down from the wall next and took his place beside Ji Youming, raising his rock, ready to strike at a moment's notice.","\"Your screeching was so awful it was hurting my ears,\" Hu Fengye quipped.","Three against eight. The odds were heavily against them.","Song Qiming stepped out from behind his friends to stand at the front. He lowered his voice and said, \"I'm their target. You guys get out of here. Go find my sister and tell her to come save me.\"","Neither of his friends looked like they knew the first thing about fighting; they were going to get themselves killed.","Ji Youming only gripped his broom tighter. The veins on the back of his hands bulged, and the muscles beneath his thick winter coat visibly tensed.","\"If we leave, you'll be dead long before your sister gets here.\"","Hu Fengye pulled Song Qiming back behind him, his eyes locked fiercely on the eight thugs. \"The youngest stays in the back. Get ready... we charge on my mark.\"","The lead masked man sneered. \"You really think we're a bunch of pushovers? Get them! Cripple all three of them!\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: No Match, Quickly Go Find My Elder Sister","paragraphs":["Ji Youming and Hu Fengye clenched their jaws, their eyes fierce, and rushed forward to fight without hesitation.","Song Qiming reached back, snatched a long stick from one of the men, and smashed it over a thug's head.","The head split open, and drops of blood splattered outward.","Seeing his underling's head busted open, the masked leader lunged toward a dagger dropped by the wall.","Song Qiming fiercely pounced over, striking the man's shoulder with the stick, the impact leaving his own palms numb.","\"Don't hit my face!\" Hu Fengye shielded his handsome features with his hands. A fist smashed into the back of his hand, bringing a bone-shattering pain.","Ji Youming was besieged by three men. In just a dozen blinks of an eye, he had already taken several heavy blows from their cudgels all over his body.","Song Qiming pushed off the wall with his right foot and launched himself into the air. Like a sharp sword, he flew in front of Hu Fengye, his sturdy and powerful leg kicking a thug three meters away.","He pulled Hu Fengye up with one hand, his face filled with urgency. \"You can't beat them. Run and find my older sister.\"","Half of Hu Fengye's earlier bravery had already vanished. He asked in a panicked rush, \"Where is your sister?\"","While carving out a path with his stick and rushing to Ji Youming's back, Song Qiming shouted his reply, \"The Song Residence in Qingyun Alley!\"","Hu Fengye swiftly bolted backward. \"Hold them off, wait for me to return!\"","Song Qiming and Ji Youming stood back-to-back facing the enemy, one holding a broom and the other gripping a wooden stick. The solid feeling against their backs made their eyes grow increasingly calm.","Hu Fengye stumbled and crawled along the way, not daring to stop for even a second.","The cold wind howled past his ears, freezing his face bright red.","At this moment, his mind was solely focused on the words \"Song Residence in Qingyun Alley\", terrified that a second's delay would cost his good brother and Song Qiming their lives.","When he finally saw the plaque of the Song Residence, it was as if he had grasped a lifeline. He pounded on the door like a madman, shouting, \"Is anyone there? Open the door, quickly!\"","Hearing the noise, Lanxi ran out from the kitchen to open the door.","The moment the door opened a crack, Hu Fengye threw himself in, squeezed through, and grabbed his hands. With an anxious expression, he said, \"Where is Song Jinzhao? Eight people are ganging up on Song Qiming, he's almost beaten to death! He said to get his sister to save him.\"","Lanxi's expression turned stern. \"Wait here a moment, I'll go call the Young Lady.\"","Song Jinzhao, who was instructing Chunxing on the opening preparations for the vegetable shop, heard Lanxi's shouts. She set down her brush and got off the heated brick bed.","Lanxi rushed in, stopping in the center of the main hall. Pointing outside, he said, \"Young Lady, a scholar came outside saying that the Young Master is being beaten and asked you to go save him.\"","Song Jinzhao lifted her eyelids, a sharp glint flashing through her eyes.","She turned back to her room, grabbed her sword, and ran outside.","Pacing back and forth at the door, Hu Fengye had never felt time pass so slowly; a mere few dozen seconds felt like decades.","Seeing a young woman rush out, he wondered: Is this Song Qiming's sister, that miracle doctor?","Recalling the street rumors that Song Jinzhao had beaten mountain bandits and northern thieves to death, he calmed his nerves a bit, his lips flapping as the words tumbled out.","\"It's in an alley not far from the academy. It takes half an hour to run there. I'll lead the way for you.\"","Lanxi ran over, pulling a horse out of the stable.","Song Jinzhao leaped onto the horse. Holding the reins with her left hand, she leaned slightly, grabbed Hu Fengye by the collar with her right hand, and hoisted him up onto the horse.","\"Show me the way.\"","Hu Fengye's eyes widened like a bull's. Reaching back to tightly grip Song Jinzhao's clothes, his heart leaped into his throat, pounding wildly.","She just lifted him up like that?","How could Song Qiming's sister be even more imposing than a man?","With a trembling finger, he forced himself to point ahead. \"Turn right at the second alley up ahead.\"","The biting cold wind poured down his collar, freezing Hu Fengye into a trembling mess, his nose running uncontrollably.","By the time the two arrived, the scene was completely deserted.","All that remained were hundreds of messy, disorganized footprints in the snow and strikingly eye-catching red blood on the ground.","Hu Fengye climbed down from the horse's back, wandered around the area, and looked up with a terrified expression. \"They must have been taken away by those masked men!\"","Song Jinzhao pushed off with both feet, flying up to the roof to survey the surrounding alleys, but she didn't see a single soul.","She jumped down from the eaves, observing the trail of footprints, and looked straight ahead. \"It's this direction.\"","Song Jinzhao was too fast; even using all his strength, Hu Fengye couldn't keep up with her.","He plopped down in the snow to rest for a long while before going back to fetch the horse.","Staring at the tall, majestic horse shaking its head and snorting hot air, he panted heavily and complained, \"If only I knew how to ride a horse.\"","\"No, when I get back, I have to ask my dad to find someone to teach me how to ride.\"","He never wanted to experience the feeling of being dangled in front of a woman on horseback like today ever again.","It was far too damaging to his masculinity; who knows how humiliating it would be if someone saw him.","Inside a cabinet in a narrow backyard, the heavy scent of rouge and powder enveloped the two of them. Song Qiming had to hold his breath to stop himself from sneezing.","With a loud bang, the courtyard door was forcefully crashed open.","Hearing the commotion, a heavily made-up madam with flowers pinned in her hair stepped out of the room with a scowl.","Seeing six burly men barge in, the anger on her face instantly transformed into a passionate, fawning smile.","She waved her handkerchief with graceful charm and spoke in an affected, high-pitched voice, \"Why didn't you fine gentlemen come through the front door? The girls of my Beauty Pavilion are all waiting at the front.\"","A man interrogated the madam, \"Did you see two scholars run in here?\"","Hiding in the old cabinet, Song Qiming furrowed his brows in confusion.","Beauty Pavilion? What kind of place is that?","These thugs wouldn't lay their hands on a woman, would they?","Ji Youming pressed down on his hand and gently shook his head.","He leaned close to Song Qiming's ear, speaking with nothing more than the sound of his breath. \"Don't worry, the Beauty Pavilion has quite a few bouncers. Otherwise, I wouldn't have brought you in here.\"","Song Qiming asked silently, mouthing the words, \"What kind of place is the Beauty Pavilion?\"","Ji Youming blinked, remembering that the boy was only twelve years old, and lightly spat out two words: \"A brothel.\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: The Courtesan, Exposed","paragraphs":["Song Qiming's pupils suddenly shrank, his breath caught, and he sat stiffly in place like a mummy.","A brothel?","This place wasn't far from the academy, but how did they end up in a brothel?","The Madam twirled the handkerchief in her hand like a flower and joked, \"I haven't seen anyone. Are you gentlemen looking for someone?\"","The man's gloomy gaze swept over every corner of the courtyard, stopping when his eyes landed on a cabinet placed in the corner.","As his soles ground against the coarse dirt, the Madam followed his gaze in confusion.","\"Madam, may I take a secret peek at the esteemed guests you mentioned?\"","The newcomer's jet-black hair was swept up in a high chignon, adorned with a kingfisher feather hairpin. A red peony painted between her brows was as bright and delicate as blood. In terms of looks, she was a thousand times more beautiful than Concubine Su of the Liao Manor.","Aside from the similar style of her clothes, she didn't have a trace of the seductive or frivolous air of a woman of the night.","Pei Yuyan's gaze swept over the faces of the six thugs. Her eyes crinkled as she offered a gentle smile.","The Madam excitedly stepped forward and grabbed Pei Yuyan's hand. \"Xiyan, have you thought it through?\"","Pei Yuyan suppressed the disgust in her heart and didn't pull away. \"Madam is right. Once you enter a brothel, there's no way out. It's better to make myself comfortable.\"","The six men stared blankly at Pei Yuyan, looking as if their souls had been snatched away.","The leading man changed direction and walked towards Pei Yuyan, asking the Madam, \"Is this a new girl?\"","The Madam's expression shifted slightly. She immediately shielded Pei Yuyan behind her and spoke politely, \"Gentlemen, this is the top courtesan I bought from the capital, thousands of miles away. She is proficient in the zither, chess, calligraphy, and painting, and she is still a virgin. You must definitely come to her debut ceremony in three days.\"","The leading man licked his thick lips with a yellowed tongue, his Adam's apple bobbing. \"Why wait three days? I'll pay. This girl's first night belongs to me today.\"","The Madam tightly gripped her handkerchief, a trace of coldness appearing on her face.","She had spent a fortune to buy this girl. Her first night was worth its weight in gold and had to be maximized in value. How could she hastily sell it to a street thug?","\"You must be joking, sir. The news of the new top courtesan's debut ceremony at Beauty Pavilion in three days has long been announced. How could I dare to go back on my word?\"","Hiding inside the cabinet, Song Qiming clenched his hands tightly. His palms were sweating, and his brows were furrowed into a tight knot.","Why haven't these people left yet?","Has Hu Fengye found my sister yet?","The leading man shoved the Madam roughly aside. Pei Yuyan's eyes darted like a startled bird as she quickly backed away in alarm.","Seeing this, the Madam shouted, \"Men, come out here! Throw these unruly bastards out of my place!\"","Five burly, thick-waisted men armed with wooden clubs rushed out from the room behind her.","The two groups instantly clashed in a chaotic brawl.","Hiding behind the door, Pei Yuyan cast a subtle glance at the discarded cabinet in the corner.","Inside the cabinet, Ji Youming whispered, \"Once they beat each other half to death, we'll make a run for it.\"","Song Qiming shook his head. \"If the people of the brothel find out we brought this trouble here, we'll be in deep water.\"","\"We'll wait until everyone leaves, then sneak out.\"","Unable to see outside, the two could only judge the progress of the battle by the sounds.","With their ears just a fingernail's width away from the cabinet door, they concentrated intently, silently cheering for the brothel's thugs to beat the men up and throw them out.","A heavy force crashed into the cabinet door. The already flimsy wood shattered into four pieces.","Song Qiming and Ji Youming simultaneously covered their ears and dodged to the side.","\"Boss, they're here!\" a man shouted toward the brawling crowd.","Song Qiming kicked the man flying, decisively grabbed Ji Youming's hand, and scrambled out of the broken cabinet. \"Run!\"","The Madam looked astonished. Two scholars had actually sneaked in. When did they hide there?","Seeing them trying to escape, the leading man ignored the brothel's thugs and turned to attack the two scholars.","The cold gleam of a blade flashed across Song Qiming's eyes. His heart trembled, and his body reacted instinctively, faster than his brain could process.","In a split second, he yanked Ji Youming behind him with his left hand while his right hand attempted to snatch the dagger from the man.","The prepared leading man twisted his wrist and slashed out forcefully with the blade, looking as though he meant to chop off Song Qiming's arm.","The sharp edge tore through Song Qiming's thick padded jacket. Even though he reacted fast enough, the opponent still managed to slice a ten-centimeter gash on his arm.","Seeing it was only a light wound, the man lunged at Song Qiming with his dagger again.","Song Jinzhao, who had followed their footprints all the way here, locked her eyes onto the bloody dagger and forcefully threw the longsword in her hand.","With a sharp whistling sound piercing the air, the blade of the sword sank into the man's right arm, causing the dagger to drop to the ground.","\"Sister!\" Song Qiming turned his head. Seeing the figure he had been praying for, his eyes trembled with emotion, and he cried out in pleasant surprise.","Song Jinzhao pushed off the ground, closing the distance in a few strides, and pulled her sword out of the man.","After kicking him to the ground, she stepped on his fingers with her boot and drove her longsword forcefully through the palm of his hand.","\"Ah!\" The man's face twisted in agony as he shrieked, rolling and struggling on the ground.","Shielded behind the Madam and the brothel's thugs, Pei Yuyan stood with her mouth agape. Her body seemed frozen, her soul seemingly sucked out of her in an instant.","The other five men rushed forward to gang up on Song Jinzhao, but she struck them down in a few quick moves, drawing blood from every single one of them.","Ji Youming froze completely in place, his mind going entirely blank.","At this moment, his eyes held nothing but the heroic figure of Song Jinzhao standing with her sword, looking like a goddess descending to the mortal realm to save him from the abyss."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: Bring to Justice","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao sheathed her sword and walked over to Song Qiming. She grabbed his hand and, seeing that the wound was still bleeding, furrowed her brows tightly.","\"I'm fine, Sister. The wound isn't deep. It'll be fine once we go back and bandage it,\" Song Qiming said, pulling his arm away and hiding it behind his back.","Where did this demoness come from, taking on six men all by herself? Even with her own men, they probably wouldn't stand a chance.","The brothel madam clutched her handkerchief tightly and stuttered, \"If you all have no further business, could you please take these people away? My Beauty Pavilion still needs to stay open for business, so I won't entertain you any longer.\"","By the time Meng Hechuan heard the news, Song Jinzhao had already dragged the six men to the government office.","Everyone except Song Jinzhao was covered in blood, especially the six thugs. After inspecting them, the yamen runners stated that their right hands were completely crippled.","Meng Hechuan looked at Song Jinzhao. \"What happened here?\"","Song Qiming stepped forward first and recounted the entire incident in detail, with Ji Youming chiming in from time to time to agree.","\"Your Honor, you have no idea. When these people couldn't beat us up, they pulled out their knives. If Song Qiming and I hadn't run fast enough, we would have lost our lives before his sister even arrived. They must be severely punished.\"","Meng Hechuan asked Song Qiming, \"Have you offended anyone recently?\"","Song Qiming shook his head. He frowned and pondered for a long while before answering, \"Tomorrow is the academy's annual examination. Their initial goal was to cripple my fingers, so I suspect the mastermind behind this might be someone from the academy.\"","\"It wasn't just these six men. The first three who attacked me were hit by my poisoned needles, and two others were injured and aren't here. Your Honor, you must capture them and bring them to justice.\"","Song Qiming was no longer a commoner without a title. Moreover, with three scholars involved, Meng Hechuan was determined to arrest the culprits and bring them to justice.","\"Rest assured. With these six men in custody, we will absolutely pry their mouths open tonight.\"","Stepping out of the government office gates, Song Jinzhao stopped and asked Song Qiming, \"Do you have any suspects in mind?\"","Song Qiming nodded heavily. \"I think it is Yan Baoyi. Ever since the academy exams ended, he has held a grudge against me. He even teamed up with his teacher to make things difficult for me at the academy at every turn.\"","\"It's highly likely that he hired these people to cripple my hands so that I could never hold a pen again, just to prevent me from testing into the Upper House.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes darkened, her voice growing cold. \"Why didn't you tell me any of this before?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"You're already so busy managing the medical clinic and the food shop, not to mention taking care of household matters. I can handle my own affairs.\"","He shrugged, pretending to be relaxed. \"Anyway, no matter how they target me, as long as I study hard, I can still leave him far behind. Besides, ever since my teacher went to teach in the Inner House, Master Ding hasn't dared to target me anymore.\"","Song Jinzhao grabbed Song Qiming's ear and pinched it tightly, her tone rising at the end. \"I am your eldest sister. If anyone bullies you in the future, you must tell me immediately. If you really resolved it, how did today's incident happen?\"","Song Qiming lowered his head. \"I didn't expect Yan Baoyi to dare to go this far.\"","Seeing the siblings talking endlessly, Ji Youming strolled over and asked in a low voice, \"Sister, where is my brother, Hu Fengye, the one who went to deliver the message to you?\"","Song Qiming looked up. \"Brother Ji, you should be older than my sister.\"","Ji Youming opened his mouth halfway and then closed it. He found it a bit difficult to call her younger sister.","The truth was, the imposing aura Song Jinzhao exuded could not be matched by the title of younger sister. Only calling her sister felt appropriate.","Just as he was about to speak, Song Qiming raised a hand to stop him. \"You can't call her younger sister. You have to call her Miss Song.\"","Ji Youming's mouth twitched imperceptibly twice.","Song Jinzhao spoke up, \"Qiming, take your classmate home first to treat his wounds. The other one was left behind halfway and couldn't keep up. I'll go find him.\"","Song Qiming nodded and led the limping Ji Youming toward home.","Song Jinzhao found Hu Fengye halfway there; he was in a standoff in an alley, tugging at a horse.","\"Miss Song, you're finally here. This horse won't listen to me. It stopped halfway and refuses to move.\"","\"How are Song Qiming and Ji Youming? Did you manage to save them?\"","Song Jinzhao vaulted onto the horse and hoisted Hu Fengye up once again. \"They're saved. The thugs were sent to the government office. Ji Youming should be at my house right now. I'll take you there.\"","Hu Fengye's tense shoulders slumped. \"As long as they're fine. Those men looked like vicious fiends. I was really terrified that something terrible would happen.\"","In the main hall of the Song family home, Ji Youming was pressed into a chair by Lan Xi, his body twisting like a maggot.","Song Shixue's hands, slick with medicinal wine, continuously rubbed his arm. \"Bear with it and don't move. If I don't rub away the bruised blood, you won't even be able to get out of bed tomorrow.\"","Ji Youming was sweating profusely from the pain, his neck glistening with moisture, as he cried out and begged for mercy.","\"Second Miss Song, could you be a little gentler? I'm dying of pain.\"","Song Shixue didn't lessen the force in her hands one bit. \"Being gentle won't work. I have to use some strength. It will be over soon.\"","Hu Fengye, who had just stepped over the threshold, fearfully pulled his leg back. He raised his left hand and touched himself all the way from his swollen eye down to his arm.","Would he be subjected to the same treatment?","Hu Fengye's injuries were much lighter than Ji Youming's.","Although those men's target was Song Qiming, Song Qiming had, after all, practiced martial arts with Song Jinzhao for over a year, so he was capable of dodging and fighting back.","This was unlike Ji Youming, who purely relied on his body to absorb the blows and fought without any technique.","Although Ji Youming didn't suffer any major injuries, he had sustained his fair share of superficial wounds from head to toe, making his condition even worse than Song Qiming's."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: The Intricate Song Mansion","paragraphs":["After all the wounds on the three of them were bandaged, Hu Fengye impatiently asked Ji Youming for the details of what had happened.","Stealing a glance at Song Jinzhao, who was washing her sword in the courtyard, Ji Youming lowered his voice and carefully recounted everything that had occurred after Hu Fengye ran off to get help.","\"You didn't see how incredible Song Qiming's older sister is! Six guys were taken down in less time than it takes to drink half a cup of tea. Song Qiming's martial arts were taught by her.\"","Hu Fengye coughed. How could he not know that Song Jinzhao possessed true martial arts skills? Just from her lifting him up and putting him down with a single hand, he knew exactly how much strength she had.","Song Qiming picked up his teacup, stood up, and respectfully cupped his hands to the two of them. \"Thank you both, Brother Ji and Brother Hu, for your righteous assistance today. I will never forget your kindness.\"","At the academy, he rarely spoke with Ji Youming and Hu Fengye. He had never expected them to risk their lives and rush forward to help, nearly getting themselves killed.","Ji Youming and Hu Fengye quickly stood up and supported Song Qiming's arms.","Enduring the pain all over his body, Ji Youming said straightforwardly, \"We are classmates. It was just a small effort, nothing worth mentioning.\"","Hu Fengye took the teacup. \"Since we saw it happening, how could we just sit back and do nothing? Besides, I didn't actually help much. In terms of skills, I'm far worse than you.\"","Song Shixue and Qingshuang entered the room carrying bowls of medicine and placed them on the table.","Song Shixue said, \"Let it cool for just a moment, then drink it while it's still hot. It will promote blood circulation, remove stasis, reduce swelling, and relieve pain. This way, you won't be too swollen when you go to the academy tomorrow.\"","They absolutely could not miss the annual examination. There were no make-up exams, so they had to go even with their injuries.","Hu Fengye had always cared deeply about his face. He didn't want to go to the academy with a swollen face and be laughed at, especially with bruised, purple eyes.","He picked up the medicine bowl and was about to drink from it.","The moment his fingertips touched the side of the bowl, the scorching heat caused him to let go, and he jumped up from his chair.","\"Hot, hot, hot!!!\"","Qingshuang, who was waiting nearby, quickly reached out and caught the medicine bowl. The liquid sloshed around in mid-air before settling back into the bowl.","Some of the medicine splashed onto her hand, but Qingshuang remained completely still, as if she couldn't feel the heat at all.","Song Qiming asked anxiously, \"Are you burned?\"","Standing on his chair, Hu Fengye shook his hand and shook his head. \"No, my fingers just feel a bit of a burning sting.\"","Ji Youming reached out and touched the rim of the bowl; it was indeed quite hot.","Just now, Song Shixue and the Song family's servant had carried the medicine over just like this. Were they not afraid of the heat?","Moreover, this maid's reaction speed was a bit too fast. She managed to catch the bowl without spilling the soup medicine. Could it be that even the servants in the Song family knew martial arts?","Song Shixue instructed Qingshuang, \"Go outside and get some crushed snow to apply a cold compress for Young Master Hu. He has to hold a pen tomorrow; his hand cannot get blisters.\"","Song Jinzhao put her cleanly wiped sword back into the inner room and said to the two of them, \"Dinner will be ready soon in the kitchen. After you eat, I'll have the servants take you back in a carriage.\"","Ji Youming cupped his hands and replied with a smile, \"I'll listen to you, Sis—no, I mean, I'll listen to you, Miss Song.\"","After Qingshuang wiped the medicine bowl clean and placed it back on the table next to Hu Fengye, and once only Song Qiming and the other two were left in the room, Ji Youming asked curiously, \"Song Qiming, does your maid know martial arts too?\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"Not only does Qingshuang know it, but my younger sister does too. They were both taught by my older sister.\"","Hu Fengye and Ji Youming exchanged a glance. Although the Song family wasn't extremely wealthy, they clearly weren't simple either.","With the eldest sister running the household, the women in the family were stronger than the men. Not a single one of them could be underestimated.","After a rigorous interrogation, the lead thug didn't say a single word. The other five didn't know who the mastermind was, but they confessed the hideout of the other five who hadn't been caught.","Meng Hechuan ordered the bailiffs to capture them overnight. One of them had a frozen face, looking like a zombie.","Another had half of his body paralyzed and was half-carried back by two bailiffs.","The other three either had busted heads or broken arms and legs. They looked even more severely injured than Song Qiming and the other two victims.","Eleven against three, and they still lost. With skills like that, daring to work in this line of business was practically courting death.","\"Coroner, what's wrong with these two?\"","Twirling his beard, the coroner examined them and concluded, \"They must have been hit with a paralyzing drug, and a heavy dose at that.\"","One of the thugs spoke with a crooked mouth: \"It was Song Qiming. He stabbed us with poisoned needles.\"","\"Your Honor, we never intended to kill anyone. Song Qiming was the one who truly showed no mercy. He used excessive self-defense! Your Honor, you must seek justice for us.\"","Meng Hechuan sneered. \"Masked, armed with clubs, and carrying knives—and you say you didn't intend to kill anyone? Who are you trying to fool?\"","\"Song Qiming and the others hold academic degrees. Assaulting scholars is an aggravated crime, not to mention that you drew knives. Once your masks were pulled off, you tried to silence them by killing them. And you want me to seek justice for you? You have some nerve saying that!\"","A red-hot branding iron was held right in front of the man's face as Meng Hechuan interrogated him, \"Speak! Who ordered you to ambush Song Qiming on the road and attack him?\"","The man kept his mouth shut tight and shook his head, hot sweat streaming down his face.","\"I don't know! Our boss takes all the jobs. We never saw the person who hired us.\"","Meng Hechuan handed the branding iron to a bailiff.","The next second, the branding iron was pressed against the man's bare chest. The scorching hot iron burned his skin, making a sizzling sound.","Agonizing screams echoed through the prison cell. The captured thugs huddled in the corners, not daring to peek out, terrified that they would be next."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: Ye Liangyu's Concerns, Qing Shuang's Secret Investigation","paragraphs":["\"What! Qiming was beaten up?\" Ye Liangyu, who had been waiting for Song Qiming to arrive for a long time, was just about to send a servant to the Song residence to inquire when Lanxi returned from seeing someone off and delivered the news.","Yunhe hurriedly comforted him, \"Don't worry, Master. The servants of the Song family said that Young Master Song only suffered minor injuries. No bones or muscles were harmed, and he can go to the academy as usual tomorrow.\"","Ye Liangyu gripped the armrests of his wooden chair and sat down, his heart heavy and completely in turmoil.","\"Have the attackers been caught?\"","Yunhe nodded. \"Miss Song has already apprehended them and taken them to the local magistrate's office. Prefect Meng has taken the case personally, so the mastermind behind this will surely be caught soon.\"","Ye Liangyu sat in his seat, clenching his right hand into a fist until his knuckles cracked.","\"Go keep an eye on the magistrate's office. See if the mastermind was sent by people from the capital.\"","Yunhe looked up and analyzed, \"Master, Young Master Song is currently only a scholar. He hasn't caught the attention of those people yet, so you don't need to be so worried.\"","To catch bandits, one must first catch the ringleader; grabbing a mere lackey would only alert the snake in the grass.","Ye Liangyu took a deep breath. \"I know they wouldn't, but I still can't put my mind at ease. Going by the time, they should have arrived by now.\"","Yunhe stole a glance at his master. Thinking of the young general who had visited a few days ago and was now living next door, he bowed and left the room to gather information at the magistrate's office.","The night was hazy, and a faint candlelight flickered in Song Jinzhao's room.","Qingshuang stood with her hands hanging by her sides, a broken blade tucked at her waist. The chilling aura around her had not yet dissipated.","\"Yan Baoyi's father went to Jiangnan to purchase goods three months ago and hasn't returned yet. The Yan family controls nearly half of the fabric business in Anyang Prefecture, and Jinxiu Boutique is theirs.\"","\"Yan Baoyi grew up in the lap of luxury and is the only son of his family. He has an arrogant and snobbish temperament, never paying any mind to those from families of lower standing than the Yans. He especially looks down on poor people trying to climb the social ladder.\"","\"Your servant also found out that Yan Baoyi verbally mocked the Eldest Young Master at the Flower Pinning Banquet, but the Eldest Young Master completely shut him down.\"","Song Jinzhao remained expressionless, her slightly calloused fingers resting on her arm and tapping lightly. \"So he became even more aggressive after entering the academy. And what is the background of that Master Ding?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"Ding Weiyue passed the provincial examination twenty-five years ago. After failing the metropolitan examination twice, he bought a minor official position in a poor county. He served as a county magistrate for three years, but his political achievements were mediocre, leaving him with no hope of promotion. Moreover, the area was so impoverished that they couldn't meet the tax quotas year after year. So, he simply resigned from his post and entered Anyang Academy as a teacher, where he has stayed for twenty-two years.\"","\"Ding Weiyue doesn't have much of a family background, but he has taken in many students over the years. Two of them eventually passed the highest imperial examination, though their rankings weren't high. Now they seem to be serving as county magistrates down in Jiangnan, with no influence reaching the north.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up and asked, \"He went to Jiangnan to purchase goods two months ago, so he should be returning right about now. Did you find out the exact timeframe?\"","Qingshuang shook her head. \"The exact time is unclear, but he will definitely return before the new year. This batch of goods is meant to be sold during the new year festivities.\"","Song Jinzhao asked, \"What's the situation at the magistrate's office?\"","Qingshuang replied, \"The bailiffs said the other five men have all been caught, but their lips are sealed incredibly tight. They haven't said anything else.\"","Early the next morning, Song Qiming, Ji Youming, and Hu Fengye entered the academy bearing their injuries, instantly drawing everyone's attention.","After entering the inner courtyard lecture hall, Song Gaoli quietly walked over to Song Qiming's side and asked, \"What happened? Did you guys get into a fight?\"","Today was the annual examination, and both Ji Youming and Hu Fengye were strong contenders for entering the upper courtyard. Could it be that they had started fighting each other last night?","As the unshakable first-place student of the inner courtyard, Wang Rui rested his hands on his desk and secretly peeked at Song Qiming.","If his performance was affected by his injuries and he failed to advance to the outer courtyard, Teacher Ye would remain in the inner courtyard to teach, which would certainly not be a good thing.","Song Qiming reached out his hand, gesturing for Song Gaoli to keep quiet. Turning his saviors into the perpetrators—if Ji Youming and Hu Fengye heard that, it would be incredibly hurtful.","\"No, on the way back from the academy yesterday, someone tried to cripple my hand. Ji Youming and Hu Fengye rushed in to save me, and that's why they took a beating.\"","Song Gaoli widened his eyes in surprise. \"You usually aren't very close to them. I didn't expect them to be so righteous.\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"If Hu Fengye hadn't gone to inform my sister in time yesterday, Ji Youming and I would have been in grave danger.\"","Yan Baoyi, who hadn't received any news all night, arrived late. Seeing that although Song Qiming had scratches on his face, his hands were perfectly fine, he couldn't help but clench his fists in anger.","Their eyes met, and a dark glint flashed through Song Qiming's eyes.","He wondered how Prefect Meng's interrogation was going, and whether the person who hired the thugs was really Yan Baoyi.","After having breakfast, Song Shixue headed to the medical clinic first, while Song Jinzhao went to the magistrate's office to request an audience with Meng Hechuan.","The bailiff struggled to keep his exhausted eyelids open and said, \"Miss Song, the prefect interrogated them until late last night and didn't even go home. He hasn't woken up yet. How about you come back this afternoon?\"","Song Jinzhao frowned and asked, \"Eleven thugs, and after a whole night of interrogation, not a single one opened their mouth?\"","Wealth cannot buy passage through the gates of hell.","How could money be more important than life? Logically speaking, they should have spilled everything by now. Could it be that someone has leverage over them?","The bailiff leaned against the door and explained, \"These thugs are repeat offenders. They make a living out of doing illegal things for money. Let alone chopping off a hand, they definitely have blood on their hands.\"","\"The others said that the person who hired them only ever met with their boss. The rest of them don't know who paid the money. But this ringleader is incredibly tight-lipped. The prefect used all kinds of severe torture, but he hasn't said a single word from last night until now.\""]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: I Can Make Him Talk","paragraphs":["Meng Hechuan walked out of the back residence of the government office, his left hand supporting his waist and his right hand adjusting his official hat. The moment he saw Song Jinzhao, he immediately straightened his back, transforming into the imposing and majestic prefectural magistrate.","Miss Song, what brings you here?","Song Jinzhao took a step back and bowed. I heard that the assassin who attacked my younger brother yesterday refuses to disclose the mastermind who hired him. I have a way to make him tell the truth.","Meng Hechuan explained, The leader of those men hasn't uttered a single word even after I subjected him to severe torture. What method could you possibly have, Miss Song?","Song Jinzhao's lips curled into a faint smile. I can make him beg for death, yet be unable to die.","The morning sunlight filtered through the tiny windows of the dungeon into the cells. The prisoners locked inside were all unkempt and covered in grime. Though they were alive, their spirit was worse than that of beggars.","Seeing Song Jinzhao enter, the five men whose arms she had slashed instantly tensed up, shrinking into the corners in fear that Song Jinzhao might strike again.","Meng Hechuan pointed at the leading thug, who was tied to a cross-shaped wooden stake and covered in blood, and said, This man's name is Xiao Hu. He and his brothers have been operating around Anyang Prefecture in recent years, making a living by taking people's money to eliminate their troubles. Because they are tight-lipped and highly secretive, those who hire them usually have to pay a hefty sum of silver to enlist their services.","Song Jinzhao asked curiously, Has no victim ever thought of reporting them to the authorities?","Meng Hechuan looked helpless. Many commoners are too afraid of retaliation to report to the officials. Furthermore, this group always covers their faces when they strike. Without knowing what they look like, we can't catch them.","Not everyone possessed Song Jinzhao's skills to capture them on the spot.","This time, Xiao Hu had failed completely. All of his subordinates were captured, without a single one spared.","Xiao Hu opened his sweat-drenched eyes, his bloodshot gaze fixed fiercely on Song Jinzhao. His crushed molars pierced his gums, and the wounds that had stopped bleeding began to ooze beads of blood once more.","If he had known Song Qiming was so troublesome, he should have killed him right at the beginning, and none of the subsequent events would have happened.","Seeing that his gaze was as stubborn as it had been last night, Meng Hechuan spoke up, Miss Song, what is this method you spoke of?","Song Jinzhao stepped forward and took a bamboo tube out of her sleeve, placing it on a rack. It was slightly thicker than a thumb and twice as long.","Untie him and bind him to the torture bed.","Receiving a glance from Meng Hechuan, the bailiffs in charge of the interrogation stepped forward, used a key to unlock the iron chains binding Xiao Hu's limbs, and strapped him to the torture bed.","Xiao Hu raised his chin and said stubbornly, The underworld has its own rules. Even if you kill me, I won't say a word.","Song Jinzhao took a white porcelain bottle from her robes, opened it, and poured out a black pill, which she then dissolved in a bowl of water.","Meng Hechuan and the others covered their noses and mouths, stepping back.","It was incredibly foul, worse than a latrine, so foul that it made one nauseous and want to vomit.","Force it down his throat.","A bailiff knitted his brows into a tight knot. Holding his breath, he pried open Xiao Hu's mouth and poured the unimaginably foul-smelling liquid from the bowl down his throat.","The stench overwhelmed Xiao Hu's senses of smell and taste, and a physiological reflex made him want to vomit.","The bailiff forcefully pressed down on his skull and squeezed his jaw.","Xiao Hu tried to open his mouth but couldn't. In the end, he was forced to swallow the liquid back down into his stomach, along with the vomit that had surged up into his throat.","Bitch, I'll kill you sooner or later! Xiao Hu felt as if he reeked from the inside out. Having been force-fed a belly full of what seemed like feces and urine, he felt that even his flesh tasted like excrement.","Song Jinzhao picked up the bamboo tube she had placed on the rack and opened it. That was just the appetizer. Now comes the main course.","For men who spent their days fighting and mingling among piles of corpses, pain was a commonplace occurrence.","Rather than killing them with a single strike, the dual torment of flesh and spirit was what truly instilled terror and dread in them.","Two twenty-centimeter-long centipedes crawled out of the bamboo tube and rested on Xiao Hu's face.","The touch, as light as a feather, made Xiao Hu's limbs go numb. He didn't dare to move a muscle, and the pores all over his body stood on end.","The cell was as suffocatingly quiet as being underwater, and everyone's gaze was fixed on the two centipedes.","They were larger than ordinary centipedes, with red, yellow, green, and black colors intertwining. Just looking at their colors gave off an eerie feeling.","Meng Hechuan didn't dare to swallow the saliva pooled in his throat. His voice was as faint as a gossamer thread, so quiet it was barely audible.","Miss Song, are these centipedes poisonous? Don't let the man die.","Song Jinzhao replied, These are the centipedes I use for making medicine. They are mildly venomous but not lethal.","Just as Meng Hechuan was about to heave a sigh of relief, the centipedes resting on the man's face began to crawl.","Xiao Hu watched helplessly as they stopped right over his eyes.","Seeing that the centipedes' legs were about to reach into his eyes, he frantically squeezed his eyelids shut. His eyelashes trembled in sheer terror, and his entire body shook.","This was nothing compared to the post-apocalyptic era, when humans were parasitized by various mutated insects and turned into living hives that triggered trypophobia, nausea, and intense discomfort. A mere two centipedes were nothing in Song Jinzhao's eyes.","One centipede crawled along his eyelid to the corner of his eye and slipped into Xiao Hu's ear, while the other stopped on his tightly shut mouth, attempting to burrow inside.","As the centipede crawled down his ear canal, the intense sensation made Xiao Hu writhe and twist his body violently. He could clearly feel exactly where the centipede was crawling.","The moment his eardrum was pierced, an agonizing pain swept through Xiao Hu's brain.","The instant his mouth relaxed slightly, the centipede clinging to his lips swiftly crawled inside.","His pupils dilated. Unable to bite down or spit it out, Xiao Hu began to struggle violently, rattling the iron chains with loud clanking sounds.","He opened his mouth wide, trying to fling the centipede out, but it was already too late.","The bailiffs with weaker psychological fortitude closed their eyes, turned their heads, and ran outside to vomit. Meng Hechuan fought back his nausea, feeling as though those two centipedes were crawling all over his own body.","He had never used such an interrogation method before.","Looking at the unfazed Song Jinzhao, Meng Hechuan hugged his own body tightly. His throat constricted, feeling as if he would throw up in the very next second."]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Begging to Speak","paragraphs":["The centipede crawled down his throat, its countless tiny legs skittering against his windpipe, inflicting a prickly sensation that was both agonizingly painful and maddeningly itchy.","Song Jinzhao walked over to the torture rack and crouched down. Her voice sounded like a ghoul crawling straight out of hell.","\"Next, they will feast on your internal organs. Once they have eaten their fill, they will lay eggs and multiply inside your body. Dense swarms of baby centipedes will eventually crawl out from your eyes, mouth, ears, nostrils, and even your nether regions.\"","\"You won't die right away. This process will last for a month or two. Take your time and enjoy it. I have all the patience in the world.\"","Xiao Hu, who now only had one good ear to hear with, shook his head frantically and struggled. He could clearly feel the centipedes slithering inside him. The mere thought of being a host to tens of thousands of centipedes caused uncontrollable tears to stream down from the corners of his eyes.","Meng Hechuan covered his eyes with his hands, too afraid to look, yet his curiosity compelled him to peek through the gaps between his fingers.","A spectacle like this was a once-in-a-century occurrence. If he missed it now, he might never get another chance to witness it.","Song Jinzhao straightened up and ordered everyone to step outside. The quieter the surroundings, the stronger the sense of isolation and terror the prisoner would feel.","The group sat on a long wooden bench outside the cells to rest. A prison guard hurriedly poured tea for Meng Hechuan and Song Jinzhao.","Meng Hechuan picked up his teacup, just about to take a sip, when he noticed the floating tea leaves looked uncannily like centipedes. Startled, his grip loosened. The tea spilled all over him, soaking his official uniform straight through.","\"Please forgive me, Your Excellency!\" the guard cried out in alarm and dropped to his knees, assuming the official was dissatisfied with the tea.","Seeing Song Jinzhao acting as if nothing had happened, still perfectly in the mood to sip her tea, Meng Hechuan stifled his exasperation and waved his subordinate away.","\"It's a bit hot, and I'm not thirsty. There's no need to pour me another.\"","The guard kept his head bowed, shuffled back on his knees, then stood up and leaned against a pillar in the corridor.","The tea had been brewed during the morning shift change; it had gone cold a long time ago.","Meng Hechuan swallowed hard and asked her out of sheer curiosity, \"Miss Song, wherever did you learn such an interrogation method?\"","Song Jinzhao set her teacup down and half-raised her eyelids. Her gaze was as placid as a deep abyss, completely devoid of ripples, yet carrying a faint, almost imperceptible smile.","\"There's no need to learn it. In the mountains, the carcasses of dead animals are swarmed by flies and maggots in less than an hour. If you slice open their bellies with a knife, they are entirely filled with insect eggs. That sight is far more thrilling than this.\"","The image of maggots infesting a brain stem flooded Meng Hechuan's mind. He clutched his chest and gagged audibly.","He managed to hold it down the first time, but as his mouth filled with saliva, the wave of nausea grew increasingly intense.","As his stomach convulsed, sour bile surged up his throat. With a loud retch, Meng Hechuan clamped a hand over his mouth and bolted out of the dungeon.","Song Jinzhao turned her head, watching his wretched, fleeing figure. She blinked, shook her head, then picked up the teapot to pour herself another cup and continued drinking.","If he couldn't even stomach a minor scene like this, he clearly didn't visit the morgue very often. Otherwise, he would have been thoroughly used to it by now.","Just over fifteen minutes later, agonizing pleas for mercy echoed from Xiao Hu's cell.","Meng Hechuan, pale and weak from throwing up, looked up with a pleasant surprise. \"Let's interrogate Xiao Hu right now.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head, stopping him. \"There's no rush. Let's wait another half hour. We'll question him when he's right on the brink of absolute despair.\"","A chill ran down the guard's spine. He had never seen a young woman employ such ruthless methods, let alone one who was supposed to be a doctor.","If she were to slip a few insect eggs into a patient's medicine, over time, their entire body would be infested with bugs. Experiencing that would be no different from a living death.","She was undoubtedly a dark physician.","Meng Hechuan asked cautiously, \"Can those two centipedes actually be taken out?\"","Since they had already burrowed deep inside the body, would she have to slice the man's belly open to retrieve them, then stitch him back up?","Song Jinzhao's lips curled into a smirk. She pulled a small medicine vial from her robes and gave it a gentle shake. \"Of course. It just needs a little bit of heat, and the centipedes will be lured out by the scent.\"","Meng Hechuan leaned back slightly. He couldn't shake the feeling that none of the various bottles and jars Song Jinzhao carried contained anything good. Just looking at them sent a shiver down his spine.","Hoarse, agonizing screams for mercy echoed throughout the dungeon. The other inmates huddled in the corners of their cells, completely terrified to even lift their heads.","The screams gradually grew weaker. Seeing that enough time had passed, the group finally made their way back to Xiao Hu's cell.","Xiao Hu was drenched in sweat from head to toe, looking as though he had just been fished out of a river.","The moment he saw Song Jinzhao, his body began to convulse. His vocal cords were so shredded that uttering a single word felt like a knife slicing his throat.","\"As long as you take the centipedes out, I'll tell you everything. I won't leave out a single word. You can know whatever you want.\"","\"You should have just spoken up earlier. Then you wouldn't have had to suffer so much.\"","Song Jinzhao uncorked the porcelain vial, poured the black granules into a bowl, and heated it.","As the black granules dissolved into the water, a stench a thousand times more putrid than before began to waft through the air. Meng Hechuan, who had only just recovered, spun around, braced himself against a wooden post, and began violently retching again.","His stomach was completely empty; all he managed to throw up was the water he had just drunk to rinse his mouth.","With the relentless sounds of gagging echoing behind her, Song Jinzhao brought the bowl to Xiao Hu's lips. \"Open your mouth.\"","Xiao Hu's eyes widened in sheer terror. \"I have to drink it?\"","Song Jinzhao tipped the bowl forward, glaring fiercely. \"Open wide. One more word of nonsense and I'll force it down your throat.\"","A few moments later, the two centipedes crawled out of Xiao Hu's mouth, one after the other.","Song Jinzhao uncapped a bamboo tube and sealed them inside. She then turned her head to look at Meng Hechuan. \"Your Excellency, you may begin the interrogation.\"","Meng Hechuan's steps were unsteady, looking as though he had just lost half his life.","His stomach was tied in knots, and he felt as if he had practically thrown up his gallbladder.","The air circulation in the dungeon was poor, meaning the foul stench wouldn't dissipate anytime soon. He had no choice but to press a handkerchief over his nose as he proceeded to interrogate Xiao Hu."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: It's Yan Baoyi, It's Him","paragraphs":["Huddled together in the corner of the opposite cell, Xiao Hu's ten subordinates raised their heads, their eyes gleaming with hope.","Now that their boss had confessed, the authorities would likely spare them from further torture.","Being sentenced to prison or exile was far better than enduring the horrifying, sickening agony of having centipedes burrowing through their bodies.","Xiao Hu shot a shifty glance at Song Jinzhao. Gritting his teeth to swallow his lingering resentment, he confessed, \"It was Yan Baoyi. He paid me five hundred taels of silver to take my men and cripple Song Qiming's hand, ensuring he could never hold a brush again and would be forced out of Anyang Academy.\"","Sitting on a stool with her legs crossed, a dark glint flashed through Song Jinzhao's eyes.","It was exactly as Qiming had guessed; the mastermind who hired the thugs was indeed Yan Baoyi.","Five hundred taels of silver just to ruin a hand—what an extravagant sum. Since the Yan family had so much money with nowhere to spend it, they might as well lose it all.","\"Yet later, you didn't just try to cripple my brother's hand; you intended to murder him and Ji Youming.\"","Xiao Hu lowered his voice. \"I didn't expect him to know martial arts, nor did I anticipate two other scholars jumping into the fray. During the fight, my mask was torn off, so my only choice was to silence them for good.\"","Meng Hechuan furrowed his brows and interrogated, \"When did Yan Baoyi approach you? Did he pay you in silver ingots or banknotes?\"","Xiao Hu closed his eyes. \"Three evenings ago. The banknotes are hidden at the Hongyun Inn. There is a secret compartment beneath the floorboards in my room; I sandwiched the notes between iron plates and stashed them inside.\"","Meng Hechuan pressed further, \"Did anyone else see Yan Baoyi besides you? Are there any other witnesses?\"","Xiao Hu shook his head. \"I always meet my clients alone when I take a job, and I never bring anyone else along. However, Yan Baoyi brought a servant with him that day, who looked like his study attendant.\"","\"He had a pair of beady, rat-like eyes and spoke in a sharp, mean-spirited tone. Just looking at him was repulsive.\"","Song Jinzhao stood up. \"My Lord, now that we have a witness, can we make the arrest?\"","Meng Hechuan nodded and issued orders to his subordinates. \"You, personally lead a team to Anyang Academy to apprehend Yan Baoyi and his attendant. The rest of you, go to the inn, retrieve the banknotes, and take them to the money house for verification. Find out who originally withdrew them and trace it back step by step.\"","A banknote worth five hundred taels was a large denomination. An ordinary commoner could not save that much money in a lifetime; only the wealthy would withdraw such sums from a money house.","By the time the Head Constable and his men arrived at Anyang Academy, the entire grounds were dead silent.","Seeing the approaching men dressed in official uniforms, the gatekeeper hurriedly rose to his feet and asked, \"What business brings you officers here?\"","The Head Constable replied, \"A student of your esteemed academy, Yan Baoyi, is suspected of hiring thugs to commit assault. The Prefect has ordered us to arrest him and bring him to justice.\"","The gatekeeper's face stiffened. \"Are you certain it is Scholar Yan?\"","The Head Constable nodded. \"Yan Baoyi of the Inner Dormitory. Is he currently in the lecture hall?\"","The gatekeeper led the officers to the entrance of the Inner Dormitory courtyard. \"Please wait a moment, gentlemen. I will fetch the master in charge of the Inner Dormitory.\"","Ding Weiyue listened to the constables with a dark expression. Forcing down the heavy heaving of his chest, he said, \"There must be some misunderstanding. Today is the academy's annual examination. Could you perhaps wait until the exams have concluded before summoning him?\"","During the exam invigilation, he had noticed that Ji Youming, Hu Fengye, and Song Qiming all bore injuries on their faces and hands, with Ji Youming's being the most severe.","He had initially assumed they had gotten into a brawl over the limited spots in the Upper Dormitory. Never did he imagine that one had been attacked while the other two had come to his rescue—and that the mastermind behind the assault was his own student.","If Yan Baoyi were convicted and word got out, Ding Weiyue's own reputation in Anyang Prefecture would be utterly ruined.","Catching sight of someone eavesdropping behind the bamboo grove out of the corner of his eye, the Head Constable gripped the sword at his waist and charged forward.","Seeing this, the eavesdropper turned and fled, but another constable vaulted over a flowerbed and tackled him to the ground.","Grabbing the man by the hair and wrenching his face upward, he revealed a remarkably ugly pair of beady, rat-like eyes."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Yan Baoyi Arrested","paragraphs":["\"Are you Yan Baoyi's pageboy?\" The head constable rushed forward and roughly grabbed him by the collar, choking his neck until it turned bruised and purple.","The pageboy shook his head frantically. \"No, I'm not Yan Baoyi's pageboy.\"","The head constable looked at Ding Weiyue, who was frozen in place, and asked him to confirm, \"Master Ding, is he Yan Baoyi's pageboy?\"","At this moment, Ding Weiyue was on the verge of a mental breakdown.","His lips parted slightly as if to speak, but he stopped himself. The words swirled in his chest a couple of times before he gritted his teeth and nodded.","The pageboy's shoulders slumped, and he roared at Ding Weiyue in dissatisfaction, \"Master Ding, you are my young master's teacher~\"","Ding Weiyue put his hands behind his back and turned away.","The pageboy's voice carried into the lecture hall where an examination was taking place.","Hearing the familiar voice, Yan Baoyi looked up toward the window.","Several figures were partially obscured by the bamboo grove, though he could vaguely make out a few constables in official uniforms among them.","Upon seeing the blue-clad figure being forced to kneel on the ground, the brush in Yan Baoyi's hand dropped onto the desk with a sharp clatter.","Ink splattered from the bouncing brush tip onto his face. He frantically wiped it with his hand, turning half of his face black.","Sitting in the chair on the podium, Ye Liangyu swept his gaze over Yan Baoyi, his eyes sharp and piercing.","Hearing the noise, Song Qiming stopped writing and looked up at Yan Baoyi, noticing his nervous expression as he stared out the window.","Following his line of sight, he just happened to see two constables escorting Yan Baoyi's pageboy away.","A few constables stayed behind, walking over to the pavilion to sit down. They occasionally glanced toward the inner court lecture hall, as if waiting for something.","Ye Liangyu picked up the disciplinary ruler from the desk and tapped the table. \"There is half an hour left until the end of this exam. Those who haven't finished, hurry up.\"","The students whose attention had been drawn away, including Song Qiming, refocused their minds and continued copying their essays from their scratch paper onto the answer sheets.","His ink-stained answer sheet was already ruined, so Yan Baoyi hastily grabbed a new one and started copying all over again.","Distracted and anxious, his mind was completely consumed by the memory of paying Xiao Hu to hire thugs, as well as the sight of his pageboy being taken away just moments ago.","The more he wrote, the more rushed he became. His hands trembled violently, causing him to make mistake after mistake.","The classmates sitting around him were disturbed by the loud rustling of his pages and couldn't help but roll their eyes at Yan Baoyi in disgust.","Making such a racket, was he rushing to a funeral?","If they hadn't still been in the middle of an exam and Ye Liangyu hadn't been sitting at the front, they would have slammed their desks and lost their tempers at Yan Baoyi.","Ding Weiyue walked in from outside with a gloomy face, sat in his chair, and kept his head lowered the entire time.","Seeing that Ding Weiyue refused to look at him, Yan Baoyi clenched his hands tightly. The brush snapped into two pieces under the pressure, and the lower half flew out, hitting the back of the student sitting in front of him.","The young man gritted his teeth and turned his head to glare at him. Answering the exam required quiet, and especially during the copying phase, no mistakes could be afforded.","This guy had caused a disturbance time and time again—what exactly was he trying to do? Once the exam was over, he would definitely have to give him a piece of his mind.","As soon as the half hour passed, Ding Weiyue stood up and said, \"Pens down. Leave your papers on the desks. The morning exam is over.\"","Yan Baoyi, his eyes burning like wildfire, stared intently at his answer sheet, on which he had only managed to copy three columns.","Seeing that he was dawdling, Ding Weiyue closed his eyes and helplessly raised his voice, \"Leave the papers on the desks and everyone get out.\"","As soon as the other students stepped out of the lecture hall, they saw several constables walking toward them.","Ji Youming walked up to Song Qiming's side. \"Has the government office reached a conclusion about the thugs? Yan Baoyi is acting very strangely, and he still hasn't come out.\"","Song Qiming nodded, turning his head to look at Yan Baoyi, who was still sitting in the lecture hall and hadn't gotten up. He was the only one left inside.","\"Just now, I saw the constables take his pageboy away. Those thugs were most likely sent by him.\"","Hu Fengye gently touched his slightly swollen eye corner. \"I knew Yan Baoyi was highly jealous and vindictive, but I didn't expect it to be this extreme!\"","\"He even dared to commit a crime like hiring thugs to hurt people, and he almost cost the two of you your lives. Master Ding won't be able to protect him this time.\"","Ji Youming glanced at Ding Weiyue standing on the podium and shook his head. \"I'm afraid Master Ding has no intention of protecting him this time either.\"","Seeing that Yan Baoyi was taking a long time to come out, the head constable simply led his men and barged into the lecture hall.","\"Scholar Yan, you are suspected of hiring thugs to injure others, committing a serious felony. By the order of the prefect, we have come to arrest you and bring you to justice!\"","The student from the front row, who had planned to confront Yan Baoyi, froze in his tracks.","Hiring thugs to hurt people? Did he hear that right?","The students lingering outside the lecture hall widened their eyes one by one, watching in disbelief as Yan Baoyi was taken away.","The pageboy who had been taken away earlier hadn't even lasted an hour before he confessed everything.","Meanwhile, the constables discovered at the bank that the five-hundred-tael silver note was one of twenty notes withdrawn by Yan Baoyi's father a year ago.","With conclusive physical and testimonial evidence, Yan Baoyi was thrown into prison immediately upon arriving at the government office.","During the exam that afternoon, looking at the empty desk and chair, the students of the inner court felt a turbulent mix of emotions.","\"Did you hear? The injuries on Song Qiming, Ji Youming, and Hu Fengye were all caused by thugs hired by Yan Baoyi.\"","\"Where did you hear that? Has Yan Baoyi gone mad? Even if he injured Song Qiming and the other two, with his level of learning, he still wouldn't be able to pass into the upper court.\"","...","Facing the whispering students, Yang Yanfeng knocked the disciplinary ruler with a stern face. \"Quiet! The afternoon exam is about to begin. The exam papers will now be distributed.\"","Too ashamed to show his face at the academy, Ding Weiyue took a temporary sick leave.","Ye Liangyu simply didn't show up at all.","Having injured his precious disciple, even if Master Yan rushed back right now to save him, it was highly unlikely that his son would be getting out this time."]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: Deprived of Scholarly Honor and Sentenced to Exile","paragraphs":["On the morning of the first day after the annual examinations concluded, Meng Hechuan held a court session at the local magistrate's office.","The eleven thugs, led by Xiao Hu, were sentenced to exile three thousand miles away.","As the principal offender, Yan Baoyi should have been sentenced to hanging according to the penal code. However, due to his status as a Xiucai scholar, his sentence was reduced to being stripped of his scholarly honors and exiled three thousand miles away.","In the courtroom, Ji Youming and the others stared at the disheveled Yan Baoyi as he was escorted away, feeling only that he deserved his punishment.","Instead of focusing on their studies and improving their talents, some scholars spent their days plotting crooked schemes to drag others down. There were so many outstanding people in the world; could he possibly ruin the hands of them all?","If such a person were to enter the imperial court as an official, he would spend every day thinking about stabbing others in the back.","It was for the best that he was ruined early on.","Outside the courtroom, Li Zien walked over to Song Jinzhao holding a hand warmer. \"Miss Song, when Yan Fengnian returns and learns that his son has been stripped of his honors and exiled, I'm afraid he won't let your brother off the hook.\"","The corners of Song Jinzhao's lips curled up slightly. She already had a plan in mind. She only feared that by then, he wouldn't even have the time to worry about his son.","\"Could the Yan family possibly prevent me from buying clothes to wear?\"","Watching Song Jinzhao walk away with complete indifference, Li Zien felt as if he had swallowed a fly. Why was she so stubborn, refusing to show even the slightest bit of weakness?","That afternoon, Song Qiming went to the Ye residence to bid farewell.","\"Teacher, tomorrow my family and I will set off for our hometown, and we won't return until the Lantern Festival. If the shop and the medical clinic encounter any trouble during this time, I ask that you please look after them.\"","Ye Liangyu rested his leg on a stool, shifting it slightly.","When Song Jinzhao had come for a follow-up consultation some time ago, she mentioned that his leg was healing very well.","It would take no more than three months at most for him to fully recover. As long as he avoided strenuous exercise that would increase the burden on his knees and legs, he would have no problem walking normally.","\"Rest assured. With your teacher here, no one in Anyang Prefecture will dare to bully your Song family. Furthermore, your elder sister has a good relationship with the Meng family. Even if I don't intervene, Meng Hechuan won't allow the Yan family to act recklessly.\"","\"You don't need to take the matter of Yan Baoyi to heart. When you pass the imperial examinations and become an official in the court in the future, as soon as you stand out, the schemes and plots you'll encounter will only be more ruthless than this. Your sister is right to teach you martial arts; you must practice hard to protect yourself.\"","Song Qiming's gaze swept over Ye Liangyu's leg. Lowering his eyes, he nodded and said, \"Thank you for your guidance, Teacher. Your student will keep it in mind.\"","As he was leaving, he caught a glimpse of the bare loquat tree in the neighboring courtyard out of the corner of his eye.","Seeing someone sitting in the tree looking in his direction, he felt as though he had seen the face peeking out from the thick velvet hat somewhere before.","He turned and said to Yunhe, \"Go and see who lives across the way. Who sits in a tree peeking around in the dead of winter?\"","Yunhe lowered his head with an unnatural expression. \"That is a guest invited by the master. Young Master Song, there is no need to worry.\"","Song Qiming raised an eyebrow and looked toward the man.","Qin Yunqian met his gaze, lifted his chin in greeting, and revealed a smile at the corner of his lips.","Song Qiming narrowed his eyes to look closely, and a flash of realization exploded in his mind.","He remembered now. It was the man who had taken the portrait of the Shuobei thieves the night his sister returned from the mountains.","Later, his sister had mentioned that one of them was the Duke of Qing, and the other was the son of General Qin.","Why was he here in Anyang Prefecture instead of staying at the border? And he was even living next door to his teacher's house.","Suppressing the doubts in his heart, Song Qiming mounted his horse and headed home.","In the main hall of the Song residence, the first four servants they had bought stood neatly in a row before Song Jinzhao.","Fushun had rushed back from the estate outside the city that morning, his rough face flushed red from the cold wind.","\"While I am away from Anyang, everything must proceed according to plan. If you are unsure about any business matters, the four of you should discuss and handle them together. If you encounter difficulties that you cannot resolve, go to the Ye residence and ask Mr. Ye for help.\"","The four of them nodded solemnly.","The Eldest Miss's booklet spanned a full twenty pages. It covered every detail, leaving nothing out, and anticipated every possible mishap.","If the four of them still couldn't handle things well with all of that, then they would truly be incompetent."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: Like Father, Like Son: Enemies Cross Paths","paragraphs":["The carriage was lined with thick mattresses, and the charcoal in the brazier glowed a fiery red. Song Anhao lay buried deep within the quilts, fast asleep.","The snow on the road, nearly half an inch deep, slowed the carriage's progress. As they passed through the Fourth Mountain and neared their intended resting point, another carriage appeared ahead, sending sprays of slush and snow flying toward the roadside.","The Yan family's driver gritted his teeth, forcing his frozen hands and face to keep moving as he incessantly snapped the reins.","Yan Fengnian sat inside the cozy, warm carriage. Every time the speed dropped even slightly, he would begin to urge the driver on.","\"Faster! We must enter the city before dawn.\"","The verdict had come down yesterday. Any later, and his son would be hauled away.","Shivering with cold, the driver failed to notice the carriage approaching from the opposite direction in the distance. Song Jinzhao slowed down, but seeing that the other party was actually accelerating, she decisively pulled her carriage to the side of the road and stopped.","Song Gaoli, following behind, couldn't see what was ahead. Seeing Song Jinzhao stop, he followed suit and pulled over.","The official road was just wide enough for two carriages to pass side-by-side. The Yan family carriage was driving right down the middle of the road. Once the driver noticed the carriage parked at the side, he frantically pulled the reins to slow down and veer away.","However, the snowy ground was slick, and they were going much too fast. The horses couldn't find their footing and skidded straight toward Song Jinzhao and her group.","The driver waved his arms and screamed, \"Get out of the way!\"","Hearing the commotion, Song Gaoli craned his neck to look forward. When he saw the out-of-control carriage barreling toward them, his expression shifted instantly.","He twisted his wrists, rapidly turning his carriage's direction, and shouted at the top of his lungs to Song Jinzhao, \"Sister Jinzhao, run! They’re going to hit us!\"","At such a high speed, the carriage would surely be smashed to pieces upon impact.","Song Jinzhao gripped her Lingyun Spear and stood up on the carriage frame. The cold wind whipped at the rabbit-fur hat on her head, and the stray black hairs blowing across her brow felt icy cold.","\"It’s too late.\"","There were mountains on both sides of the road; there was nowhere to hide.","Turning the horse around wouldn't give them enough time to pick up speed and dodge, so she decided to force the other carriage to a halt instead.","The freezing wind blew the carriage curtain open, and the warmth inside vanished in an instant. Song Shixue pulled Song Anhao close, preparing to jump out at a moment's notice.","The other driver used every ounce of his strength, but seeing that he still couldn't pull the horses back, despair began to take hold.","Inside the carriage, Yan Fengnian was being tossed about. He gripped the bench beneath him and roared, \"You useless waste! Stop the horses now!\"","The driver bit his lip, his throat tight as he verged on tears.","Hurry, hurry, hurry—all he knew was how to hurry. Well, look at them now. They were about to hurry themselves right into the grave.","Song Jinzhao thrust the tip of her spear into the snow and used the momentum to vault several meters through the air, landing squarely on the back of the lead horse.","She grabbed the leather harness with her right hand and pulled back with all the power in her arm.","The horse’s front hooves reared up into the air, reaching an almost vertical angle.","The Lingyun Spear carved a twenty-centimeter-deep furrow into the ground as Song Jinzhao used the strength in her legs to force the horse to a dead stop.","The carriage behind them, propelled by its own momentum, slammed into the stone cliff with a thunderous crash, splitting right down the middle.","Yan Fengnian was thrown out, but Song Jinzhao caught him with the shaft of her spear.","After the driver was set down by his collar, his legs gave way, and he collapsed onto the ground, gasping for air in sheer terror.","\"Driving so fast in a snowstorm without looking at the road... are you in such a hurry to meet your—\" Catching sight of Yan Fengnian's face, Song Jinzhao abruptly pulled back her spear.","Yan Fengnian, who hadn't quite landed yet, fell flat on his face in the snow.","Qingshuang had previously found someone to draw a portrait of Yan Baoyi's father and had shown it to Song Jinzhao. This man was none other than Yan Fengnian, Yan Baoyi’s father.","It truly was a small world for enemies.","There was no convoy of cloth being escorted behind them, so it seemed he had learned of his son being thrown into prison and was rushing back to save his life.","Since he was here, the Yan family's cargo convoy shouldn't be far off—perhaps they were in Nankou Town.","The task she had previously instructed Qingshuang to handle could now be dealt with by her own hand.","His backside aching from the fall, Yan Fengnian stood up and pointed an accusing finger at Song Jinzhao. \"You girl! Not only did you wreck my carriage, but you nearly killed me! Are you trying to take my life?\"","Song Jinzhao pulled the corners of her mouth down and said coldly, \"You’re too heavy; I couldn't hold you up.\" If she could take his life, she certainly would; it would be better than letting him come back for revenge later.","\"You were driving too fast and weren't watching the road. You were distracted and nearly hit my carriage. I haven't even settled the score with you, and I saved your life to boot. Instead of being grateful, you turn around and bite the hand that feeds you. You're just like the dog that bit Lu Dongbin—totally incapable of recognizing a person’s good intentions. You deserved that fall.\"","Yan Fengnian was left speechless by Song Jinzhao’s retort. He could only glare hatefully at his driver. \"Useless thing! You can't even drive a carriage properly. When we get back, I’m selling you off!\"","The driver knelt in the snow, kowtowing repeatedly. The slush made his head wet and filthy.","\"Please, Master, have mercy! It was my fault, I’ll never do it again!\"","Song Jinzhao had no interest in dealing with the master and servant. She turned back to her carriage, preparing to drive away.","She had to reach Nankou Town before dark to see if their goods were there.","Song Gaoli, having turned his horse around, quickly followed.","Seeing them about to leave, Yan Fengnian stepped out to block Song Jinzhao’s carriage.","He pulled a banknote from his robe and commanded haughtily, \"Here is a hundred taels. I’m buying your carriage. My horse is yours.\"","Song Jinzhao looked straight ahead, completely indifferent.","\"Not selling.\"","He was just like Yan Baoyi, with his eyes on the top of his head. Let him ride his horse back through the freezing night wind then.","Yan Fengnian gritted his teeth and pulled out another hundred taels. \"If you won't sell, someone else will.\"","He thrust the two hundred taels worth of banknotes in front of Song Gaoli. \"Two hundred taels. Sell me your carriage.\"","Song Gaoli’s mouth twitched awkwardly as he pointed ahead. \"I’m just the driver. The carriage isn't mine.\"","Song Qiming pulled back the curtain and said expressionlessly, \"Don't talk about two hundred taels. If you upset my sister, we wouldn't sell it for twenty thousand.\"","Watching the back of the carriage disappear heartlessly into the distance, Yan Fengnian closed his eyes in frustration, the two banknotes in his hand feeling light and useless.","The driver asked in a small voice, \"Master... should we go back to Nankou Town to find another carriage before continuing?\"","Yan Fengnian kicked him. \"How much time would we waste going back and forth? Take off your padded coat and give it to me. You’ll ride the horse and carry me.\"","The driver’s face went deathly pale. Riding a horse was cold enough as it was, and now his coat was being taken? Was he meant to freeze to death?"]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: The Same Inn: Design of Spontaneous Combustion for Goods","paragraphs":["They arrived at the only inn in Nankou Town before dark.","A waiter clearing the tables spotted two carriages approaching from afar. He quickly put down the bowls and chopsticks, wiping his hands on a cloth as he hurried out to greet them.","\"Honored guests, there's a stable in the rear courtyard. Let me show you the way.\"","Winding around the side of the building to the backyard, they saw dozens of cargo-laden carts parked in the yard.","A man, bundled up in thick cotton clothes and a hat, sat guard in the nearby woodshed.","Song Jinzhao scanned the surroundings. Confirming there were no other guards, she picked up her Lingyun Spear and alighted from the carriage.","Seeing two men, two women, and a young child of just a few years step down from the two carriages, a flicker of surprise crossed the waiter's eyes.","They all looked quite young. Were their families really at ease letting them travel so far?","Entering the main hall, the innkeeper behind the counter greeted them warmly. \"Honored guests, the inn is quite full today. We only have two superior rooms left. Would you like one or two?\"","Superior rooms cost twice as much as simple ones. Judging by their attire, these guests could likely afford two.","Song Jinzhao took silver from her purse. \"We'll take two.\"","She asked casually, as if making conversation, \"How come there are so many guests in the dead of winter?\"","The innkeeper grinned in explanation. \"The Yan family cloth merchant convoy from Anyang Prefecture is staying the night. It's fortunate their master hurried on ahead after dark, otherwise you honorable guests might have had to squeeze into just one room.\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight smile and nod, then pointed to the menu board on the wall. \"We'll have a lamb and tofu hotpot, a Three-Crisp Soup Pot, and send a steamed minced pork with egg to the room.\"","Innkeeper: \"Right away, I'll have the kitchen prepare it.\"","Going upstairs, Song Gaoli nudged Song Qiming's arm and whispered, \"Is the Yan family the innkeeper mentioned Yan Baoyi's family? They are in the cloth business.\"","Song Qiming's eyes held a thoughtful look. \"If it is, then the master and servant we encountered on the mountain path half an hour ago might have been Yan Baoyi's father.\"","His son was about to be imprisoned and exiled, so the man would have rushed through the night, leaving the convoy behind.","Song Gaoli frowned uncertainly. \"His father shouldn't have the power to make Prefect Meng change the verdict, right?\"","Song Qiming shook his head, his tone firm. \"The judgment has been passed. With our teacher keeping watch, no one can save Yan Baoyi.\"","Song Gaoli nodded hesitantly, setting his mind at ease.","When resting that night, Song Jinzhao mixed the ground iron powder and salt in a precise ratio, then added water to form a paste.","She divided it into fifteen portions, wrapped each in oiled paper and dipped them in oil, then wrapped them again in silk handkerchiefs thoroughly soaked in oil.","In the middle of the night, when everyone in the inn was asleep, Song Jinzhao stood by her room's window. Peering through a crack, she looked down at the backyard.","Once the man guarding the goods was snoring soundly on a pile of straw, she changed into black clothes, covered her face, and left her room.","Silently, she slipped the packets into the cloth bundles on every cart.","Oxidizing iron powder releases heat; the precise ratio controlled the time until ignition.","Cloth is highly flammable. Once the ignition point was reached, the fire would start from within, reducing all the goods to ashes in no time.","It would be done without a trace. Given the knowledge of this era, no one would ever discover the cause.","The sky gradually lightened. Watching the faint glow of dawn behind the mountains, she knew today would be clear and sunny.","After breakfast, Song Jinzhao and her four companions left the inn almost simultaneously with the Yan family convoy.","One headed south, the other north, in completely opposite directions."]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: Two Hundred Thousand Taels, No Deal","paragraphs":["Yan Fengnian, who had rushed back to Anyang Prefecture overnight, headed straight for the Yan residence the moment the city gates opened.","Half an hour later, before Meng Hechuan had even left for his duties at the magistrate's office, Yan Fengnian arrived for a clandestine visit through the back door, clutching an exquisite mahogany box.","Meng Hechuan, who was currently having breakfast, listened to his servant's report. After a moment's reflection, he said, \"Invite him into the main hall for tea. I will be there shortly.\"","Sitting nearby, Meng Xiaozhe spoke up hesitantly, \"Father, Yan Fengnian has come to see you at such an hour and even used the back door to avoid being seen. It must be for his son's sake. Do you still intend to see him?\"","Meng Hechuan set down his chopsticks and rinsed his mouth with tea. \"The Yan family is one of the top merchant families in Anyang Prefecture. They have donated a great deal of silver to the imperial court over the years. I cannot release Yan Baoyi, but I must show the man some respect.\"","\"If Anyang Prefecture suffers another disaster in the future, or if funds need to be raised for a war in the north, we will still need to rely on the Yan family.\"","Meng Xiaozhe’s brows rose slightly in a frown. \"Yan Baoyi is Yan Fengnian's only son. After what has happened, will he still be willing to donate?\"","Meng Hechuan replied with righteous conviction, \"Commoners do not fight with officials. Yan Fengnian hasn't spent years in business being a fool; he knows what is important.\"","Watching his father's departing figure, Madam Meng, who was sitting nearby, spoke to comfort him. \"Don't worry, your father has been an official for many years; he knows how to handle things.\"","Guo Yiyao sat quietly, silently placing a goose-fat bun into Meng Xiaozhe's bowl. \"Eat it before it gets cold.\"","Meng Xiaozhe looked at his wife tenderly and took a bite of the bun.","Madam Meng felt relieved seeing the young couple getting along so well. Her son would return to the capital for his studies after the New Year, and this time, with his wife accompanying him, there would finally be someone attentive to care for him.","Yan Fengnian sat restlessly in the guest chair in the main hall, his eyes fixed urgently on the doorway. When he saw Meng Hechuan approach, he hurried to his feet to salute.","\"This humble subject pays his respects to Lord Meng.\"","Meng Hechuan nodded in response. \"Master Yan, there is no need for such formalities.\"","Before Meng Hechuan could even sit down, Yan Fengnian dropped to his knees before him.","His knees hit the bluestone floor with a heavy thud that sounded painful.","\"My Lord, I know my son has committed a grave error, but he is my only son. I rely on him to carry on my family line. I beg you to spare his life—strip him of his scholarly titles if you must, but please do not exile him.\"","The servant kneeling behind him saw Yan Fengnian reach out and immediately handed over the box.","Yan Fengnian opened the lid, his expression grief-stricken and his voice full of pleading.","\"If your Lordship agrees, I am willing to donate all two hundred thousand taels of silver notes in this box to the prefecture office.\"","A thick stack of five-hundred-tael notes was piled inside the box.","Two hundred thousand taels—that was equivalent to the entire tax revenue of Anyang Prefecture for the previous year.","No matter how firm Meng Hechuan's resolve was, his heart skipped a beat at the mention of such a sum, and a restless heat surged in his chest.","He picked up his teacup and took a sip, then reached out to close the lid, pushing Yan Fengnian's hand away.","\"Yan Baoyi hired thugs to injure people. He used a blade and nearly took a life. No matter how much silver you donate, I cannot grant your request.\"","Yan Fengnian was instantly plunged into despair, tears streaming down his aged face.","He held the box and kowtowed repeatedly to Meng Hechuan. \"My Lord, after all, no lives were lost. My son is still young, and it was all due to my lack of discipline. Please, My Lord, think of a way. My Yan family cannot be left without an heir!\"","Meng Hechuan blurted out, \"You are only in your early forties; you can still have another child.\"","Yan Fengnian froze in shock.","Meng Hechuan continued, \"It is not that I am unwilling to help you, but the imperial court has laws. How can a crime be settled privately through donations?\"","\"The Ji, Hu, and Song families are not the type to let things go quietly. If I do not judge this case according to the law, someone will surely file a complaint against me.\"","A glimmer of hope flickered in Yan Fengnian's eyes as he asked urgently, \"If the three victims are willing to drop the charges, would my son be alright?\"","Meng Hechuan's expression tightened. \"The verdict has been passed. The Anyang Commissioner of Education has already stripped Yan Baoyi of his scholarly status. There is no room for reversal in this case.\"","The box slipped from Yan Fengnian's hands, and silver notes scattered across the floor.","A few of them landed on Meng Hechuan's official robes, looking strikingly eyesore in contrast.","Yan Fengnian had to be supported by others as he left the Meng residence. Upon returning home, he collapsed and lost consciousness.","He had gone a day and a night without sleep to rush back in the freezing winter. Had it not been for the sheer will to save his son, he would have collapsed long ago.","Physician Gu arrived carrying his medicine chest.","\"The patient is suffering from a surge of internal heat due to extreme agitation, coupled with a severe cold. I will prescribe a dose of medicine to bring down the high fever first, otherwise, his mind might be damaged by the heat.\"","Master Yan's wife covered her eyes with a handkerchief. She had been crying since Yan Baoyi was taken away. Her eyes were red, swollen, and stinging; she felt as if she were going blind.","\"Physician Gu, you must heal my husband quickly. My son is still in prison!\"","Physician Gu's salt-and-pepper eyebrows twitched as he silently turned to write the prescription.","The news of Yan Baoyi hiring thugs to injure people had spread throughout Anyang Prefecture. The verdict was final. Did the Yan family still think they could save him?","It was already evening when Yan Fengnian woke up.","Yi'er's mother rushed to the bedside, wailing, \"Master, you're finally awake! News just came from the prefecture office that Yi'er is to be exiled tomorrow morning. You must think of something!\"","Yan Fengnian could barely catch his breath upon hearing this. He stared blankly at the ceiling beams, his heart as cold as dead ashes.","\"What can I do? Lord Meng wouldn't budge even for two hundred thousand taels. Yi'er cannot be saved.\""]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: The cargo worth one hundred thousand taels of silver was completely burned.","paragraphs":["As twilight descended, the Yan family caravan pressed on, making the most of the clear weather. They were less than an hour’s journey from Anyang Prefecture.","Everyone was filled with anticipation, looking forward to a well-deserved two-day rest upon their return. However, in the middle of the line, the temperature deep within the folds of fabric on one of the flatbed carts had been steadily rising after a full day of scorching sun.","The friction of the goods during the journey generated heat, causing iron filings to spark into a faint flicker of fire. The flame licked against oiled paper, quickly igniting the oil-soaked silk handkerchiefs packed within.","Silently, the fire began to spread from the heart of the cargo.","The faint scent of burning wood and the acrid stench of scorched feathers began to drift through the air.","A driver twitched his nose and asked in confusion, \"Do you smell that? It smells like something's burning.\"","His companion took a long swig from his wineskin and shook his head tipsily. \"What smell? I don't smell a thing.\"","\"Fire!\" A deafening cry echoed across the plains.","Startled, everyone halted and looked ahead, only to see the second carriage near the front engulfed in roaring flames.","The drivers and guards braved the heat, desperately clawing at the goods that hadn't yet been touched by the fire, shoving them onto the ground.","Just as the others were about to rush forward to help, more cries broke out.","\"Fire!\"","\"Mine is on fire too!\"","Terrified screams rang out one after another, and the entire group was instantly plunged into chaos.","\"Put it out! Find some water, quick!\"","But there were no rivers nearby; water was nowhere to be found.","They were forced to use snow to quench the flames. But after a day of bright sunshine, there was precious little snow left on the ground. They could only watch helplessly as the fire grew larger and fiercer.","The draft horses, feeling the searing heat against their hindquarters, grew restless, tossing their heads and struggling against their harnesses.","Seeing this, the drivers scrambled to hack through the leather traces. Thick, billowing smoke rose into the sky, and to the onlookers, it felt as though the world was ending.","The head steward’s face went deathly pale. He collapsed to his knees, his very soul seeming to have fled his body in shock.","He wailed toward the heavens, \"How could this happen? How could it just catch fire out of nowhere? What are we going to do?!\"","This was a shipment worth a hundred thousand taels of silver. It had been burnt to nothing. The Master would surely have his head for this.","The servant with the wineskin had never been more sober. Eyes wide with terror, he pointed at the charred skeletons of the carts and bellowed.","\"Heavenly fire! It must be heavenly fire! The Heavens are angry; this is a divine punishment!\"","His words were like a boulder dropped into a still pond, sending ripples of panic through the crowd.","In an instant, everyone was shouting, \"Heavenly fire!\"","They clung to the phrase like a drowning man to a straw, desperate for a convincing excuse that might save their lives. For a fire to break out for no reason in the dead of winter—if it wasn't heavenly fire, what else could it be?","They dragged the charred wooden frames and a few scraps of soot-stained fabric back to the Yan Manor. There, Yan Fengnian lay in bed, his eyes wide with fury as he glared at the steward kneeling before him.","\"What did you say? Everything... burned?\"","The steward held up the blackened scraps of silk, tears streaming down his face.","\"Everything was going smoothly, but then, just as we neared Anyang Prefecture, heavenly fire suddenly descended. Over a dozen carts ignited all at once!\"","\"The fire moved with unnatural speed, eerie and strange. In less than the time it takes to drink a cup of tea, everything was incinerated. The men risked their lives to save what they could, but we only managed to pull these few scraps from the flames.\"","Yan Fengnian’s eyes turned bloodshot. A surge of heat boiled in his chest, and a metallic sweetness rose in his throat before he spat out a mouthful of fresh blood.","His heart turned to ash. Blood continued to trickle from his mouth as he rasped, \"One hundred thousand taels... that would have turned into two hundred thousand. Only one day... and you tell me it's gone?\"","The steward, his face splattered with the Master's blood, froze, his body as stiff as a wooden puppet.","Throughout the room, the servants remained knelt on the floor, too terrified to make a sound.","In contrast to the chaos back at the Yan estate, the second day of travel for Song Jinzhao and her companions was remarkably smooth. A campfire crackled in a quiet clearing deep within the mountain woods. Song Gaoli rubbed his hands together, his eyes fixed on the clay pot bubbling away on the iron rack as he swallowed hungrily."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: Night Assassination","paragraphs":["Song Gaoli sighed, \"If only someone could open an inn here. Spending the night in the wild during winter is just too cold.\"","Song Qiming shoved a scorching hot flatbread into his hand. \"Just get through tonight. We won't have to sleep outside after this.\"","The bright firelight reflected on the faces of the five people, their shadows dancing like monsters as the cold wind blew.","Song Anhao, who was bundled up tightly, reached out to touch the fire, but Song Shixue held him firmly in her arms, kneading his chubby little hands.","\"You want to touch everything. Careful, or you'll turn those hands into roasted pig trotters.\"","Song Anhao turned and threw himself toward Song Jinzhao. \"I don't want roasted pig trotters, I want braised trotters with beans.\"","Song Jinzhao pinched his soft, tender cheek and pulled gently, laughing dotingly. \"If you eat any more, you're going to turn into a little ball.\"","Song Anhao tilted his head against Song Jinzhao's hand and acted spoiled. \"Anhao is small, I have to eat a lot to grow up.\"","The cold wind swept through the mountain forest, making the withered yellow leaves rustle loudly.","Song Jinzhao’s ears twitched slightly. She stopped what she was doing and turned her head, looking solemnly into the pitch-black forest.","In the darkness where she could not even see her own fingers, the sound of dry branches being trampled caught her attention.","She pulled Song Anhao into her left arm, holding him tight, while her right hand alertly gripped the Lingyun Spear resting on the ground. She said coldly, \"Qiming, Shixue, get your swords.\"","Song Qiming and Song Shixue looked up, their gentle expressions vanishing as they picked up the longswords beside them.","Song Gaoli, confused and having no idea what was happening, looked at the three of them with a bewildered expression.","\"What's wrong? Is it a wolf?\" In winter, when wolves in the mountains couldn't find food, they would come down to eat people. Could they really be so unlucky as to run into one?","The sound of footsteps drew closer; there were four or five people.","Song Jinzhao stood up and moved toward the carriage. \"It’s not wolves, it's people. Gaoli, get in the carriage.\"","Song Qiming quickly hauled Song Gaoli up from the ground. \"It’s dangerous, go hide in the carriage first.\"","Watching the three Song siblings standing guard with their weapons, Song Gaoli was ushered into the middle and climbed onto the carriage.","Song Jinzhao handed him a dagger along with Song Anhao. \"Stay in the carriage and don't move. Protect my brother.\"","The ice-cold dagger made Song Gaoli's palm stiffen. He held Song Anhao tightly in his arms, the dagger trembling in front of his chest.","It wasn't wolves, but people. If Jinzhao was this nervous, could it be mountain bandits?","Song Jinzhao’s hand rested on the bow and arrows on the carriage frame. Five masked men dressed entirely in black descended from above.","Three arrows were fired simultaneously, accompanied by a sharp whistling sound as they tore through the air.","Huangquan Ghost’s eyes flickered. His body twisted mid-air, his toes tapping lightly against the flying arrows. With a wave of his hand, several flying daggers shot toward Song Jinzhao.","The shaft of the spear moved like a shooting star across the night sky. Sparks flew as all the daggers were knocked away.","Huangquan Ghost landed on his feet, holding a long whip covered in sharp thorns. His narrow, cold eyes held a chilling smile.","\"A job worth five thousand taels of silver indeed requires some skill.\"","Song Qiming, guarding the side of the carriage, knit his thick brows into a knot. These people were here to kill; could it be the Yan family?","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes. These five men were filled with a thick aura of killing intent and the scent of blood. They were different from the previous useless thugs; these were professional assassins.","\"Five thousand taels of silver to buy the lives of my family of four? I'll give you five thousand taels to kill the employer instead.\"","Huangquan Ghost gave a wicked laugh. \"My Suoming Sect never breaks a contract, but we also never refuse business that comes to our door.\"","\"This deal can be done. For five thousand taels, once I've killed you, I'll go and kill the buyer.\"","Anxiety and worry filled Song Shixue's eyes. If she had known, she should have brought Qingshuang and Lanxi along.","Three against five—they were at a disadvantage in numbers."]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: Fierce Battle in the Forest: The Siblings' First Kill","paragraphs":["Her elder sister must have discovered something; otherwise, she wouldn’t have offered five thousand taels of silver to settle the matter.","“It seems this deal is off,” Song Jinzhao said coldly, the killing intent in her eyes intensifying.","Song Qiming and Song Shixue gripped their swords in their right hands. The hidden arrows tucked inside their left sleeves were primed and ready, poised to claim the lives of the five assassins from the Suoming Gate at any moment.","Inside the carriage, Song Gaoli held Song Anhao tightly, not daring to poke his head out.","When did his own life become worth a thousand taels of silver?","The long whip in Huangquan Ghost’s hand hissed like a soaring serpent, striking directly at Song Jinzhao’s face.","Song Jinzhao neither dodged nor retreated. The tip of her spear, like a cold star streaking through the pitch-black night, accurately struck the handle of the whip.","With a forceful upward flick, she forced him back. A sharp, ruthless glint flashed in Huangquan Ghost’s eyes as his toes tapped the ground, his body spinning twice in a rapid retreat to break free from Song Jinzhao’s pursuit.","“The girl has quite some strength,” he thought. The impact had nearly shattered his wrist.","Once Huangquan Ghost was forced back, two other assassins swung their swords at Song Jinzhao, while the remaining two launched an attack on the carriage from different directions.","Song Shixue summoned her courage and raised her sword to meet the enemy. Since she had begun her martial arts training, this was her first real combat experience involving bloodshed.","Having survived one such encounter before, Song Qiming’s gaze was significantly more determined.","In a situation like this, it was kill or be killed.","Hearing the continuous, sharp clanging of metal from outside the carriage, Song Gaoli’s heart leaped into his throat.","Song Anhao reached out his short, chubby hand to lift the window curtain.","Song Gaoli immediately grabbed the small hand and pulled it back. “My little ancestor, how can you be as bold as your eldest sister?”","“Look, outside!” Song Anhao waved his fist, his upper body leaning outward.","Song Gaoli covered the boy’s ears and rested his chin on top of the child's head.","“You mustn’t look. If you have nightmares tonight, your brother and sister will skin me alive.”","Of the four Song siblings, this little one had the best luck; he hadn’t suffered a day since the moment he was born.","Raised fair and chubby, anyone who saw him would take him for a child of a wealthy, noble house.","The Lingyun Spear swept out with the force of a thousand-strong army. The shaft slammed into the chests of three men, the resulting vibration sending a persistent hum through the air that left their ears ringing.","Huangquan Ghost’s face paled as he clutched his chest and dropped to one knee. He had never seen a woman wield a spear with such mastery. Even more shocking was that every one of Song Jinzhao’s strikes was aimed at a lethal point.","She was more cold-blooded than a professional assassin like himself. Her hands must have been stained with many lives.","This was not the behavior of a sixteen-year-old girl; even the Suoming Gate couldn't train an assassin like this.","Song Qiming struggled to withstand a heavy blow from his opponent. His left hand flicked, firing a sleeve arrow at the man.","The assassin’s pupils constricted as he dodged frantically.","Song Shixue was not as strong as her opponent. As the assassin pressed his blade against hers, her body slid backward, the soles of her shoes scraping against the ground until they felt as thin as paper.","“Remember, if a man attacks you, lift your leg and use all your strength to strike his most vulnerable spot.”","Her sister’s words from their close-quarters combat training echoed in her mind, the scene playing out vividly before her eyes.","Song Jinzhao’s face—sharp as a blade during her stern lessons—seemed to overlap with the assassin’s black mask. As the two images merged, Song Shixue raised her leg and delivered a heavy knee strike between the man’s legs.","It felt as if something had exploded.","“Argh!” His features contorted, his eyes above the mask bulging in agony.","His longsword clattered to the ground as the assassin collapsed, rolling back and forth while clutching his groin, howling in pain.","The sound carried for miles, echoing through the entire mountain.","Song Jinzhao glanced over, a sharp glint of approval flashing in her eyes at the sight.","While fending off Huangquan Ghost’s attacks, she roared in a low voice, “Shixue, kill him!”","Song Shixue looked at Song Jinzhao, who was currently fighting off three men at once. She swallowed nervously, took a deep breath, and stepped toward the fallen assassin.","Seeing the man still doubled over in pain, she gripped her sword tight and raised it high.","The tip of the sword pierced through the man’s hand and drove deep between his legs.","An earth-shattering scream pierced the sky, waking a pregnant wolf sleeping in her distant den.","Driven by an intense curiosity to know how the battle was faring, Song Gaoli pressed Song Anhao’s face into his chest while he cautiously peeled back the curtain with his other hand. The scene he witnessed was one he would never forget.","A flash of cold steel, and a drop of warm blood splattered onto his face.","Song Gaoli recoiled in terror against the carriage wall, his breath hitching. The horrifying image of Song Shixue slitting the assassin’s throat, blood spurting everywhere, flashed repeatedly in his mind.","Through the corner of his eye, via the swaying curtain, he saw Song Qiming seize the moment as the poison took effect, plunging a sword vertically into another assassin’s chest.","Song Gaoli opened his mouth but couldn't make a sound; it was as if he had lost his voice.","Just as Song Anhao managed to pull his head free and was about to turn around, Song Gaoli instinctively covered the boy’s eyes, his voice as faint as a mosquito’s buzz. “Don’t look.”","From now on, he would never worry about Song Qiming being bullied at the academy again. Ultimately, it was his own lack of experience and narrow-mindedness that had misled him.","He wondered if this little toddler would grow up to catch up to his siblings. He had a feeling the boy would be a formidable character as well."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Dealing with the Netherworld Ghosts, Looting the Bodies","paragraphs":["Seeing his two subordinates taken down by the Song siblings, Huangquan Ghost spat out a mouthful of blood, his eyes fixed on Song Jinzhao with a look of intense wariness.","He had initially thought this mission was an easy way to earn some quick coin, but he hadn't expected to run into such a hard target.","How was this woman so strong?","And that long spear in her hand—after so many clashes, there wasn't a single scratch on it. Who had given it to her?","Having killed for the first time, Song Qiming and Song Shixue felt their hearts pounding violently, as if they were about to leap out of their chests.","Their eyes met, and Song Qiming pulled his sword from the assassin's chest. His steps were slightly unsteady as he said, \"Let's go help Sister.\"","Song Shixue nodded.","As the Song siblings blocked the other two subordinates, the tip of the spear streaked toward Huangquan Ghost's eyes like a bolt of lightning.","He ducked quickly, ignoring the strands of hair sliced from his forehead, and swung his whip to entwine the Lingyun Spear.","Song Jinzhao's arms tensed, the fine, lean muscle definition showing beneath her fair skin.","The spikes on the whip were shaken into tens of thousands of silver-black afterimages by the force of her vibration.","Huangquan Ghost gritted his teeth and gripped the whip with both hands, his palms feeling as though the bones were cracking from the shock; only by holding on with all his might did he avoid being thrown back.","Watching his strained effort in their literal tug-of-war, Song Jinzhao’s cherry-red lips, untouched by rouge, curled into a faint, wicked arc.","She suddenly let go with her right hand. The massive momentum sent Huangquan Ghost flying back dozens of meters.","In a flash, Song Jinzhao gripped the Lingyun Spear and hurled it with all her strength toward Huangquan Ghost.","Just as he was struggling to steady himself and catch the spearhead with his whip, a swift figure appeared behind him like a sudden storm.","Several hidden sleeve-arrows fired simultaneously, riddling his body like a sieve.","Song Jinzhao rushed forward, snapped his limbs, and leapt up to seize the Lingyun Spear, thrusting it vertically into the top of Huangquan Ghost’s head.","The hard skull seemed incredibly fragile at that moment, shattering instantly into a massive, bloody hole.","Seeing Huangquan Ghost killed, the two assassins still entangled with the Song siblings immediately turned to flee.","The target was highly skilled in martial arts; they needed to return to the sect as quickly as possible to have the Sect Master send higher-level experts.","Pulling the spearhead free, a cold light flashed in Song Jinzhao’s icy eyes. The sharp tip of the spear acted like an armor-piercing shell, piercing through the hearts of the two fleeing men.","The moment Huangquan Ghost had rejected her proposal, these five people lost any chance of leaving alive.","If anything was unexpected, it was the performance of Song Qiming and Song Shixue.","For their first real combat experience, their performance was truly remarkable.","Especially the fact that they actually dared to kill.","Looking at the five corpses lying around them, Song Shixue’s palms were sweaty. She looked at Song Jinzhao with a dazed expression, her voice a mere murmur: \"Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao walked over to the two of them with the blood-dripping Lingyun Spear. Her eyes crinkled with a smile as she offered a satisfied compliment. \"Not bad. Your year of training hasn't gone to waste. Remember this feeling; it should be the same even when I’m not around.\"","Seeing that there was no more movement outside, Song Gaoli peeked through the curtains, his heart trembling as if he were having a heart attack.","Perhaps he should ask Song Qiming to teach him a few moves one of these days—not to kill, but just for self-preservation.","Otherwise, acting like a shrinking violet like he did today—especially when Song Shixue was younger than him—would truly damage his masculine pride if word got out.","After calming down, Song Qiming thought for a moment and said, \"Sister, we are still a day’s journey from Kaikang City. Since lives have been lost, we should report this to the authorities first.\" Otherwise, they might be framed by someone else.","Song Jinzhao walked over to Huangquan Ghost and pulled back his clothing, discovering a skull-shaped tattoo on his chest near the armpit.","Checking the other four bodies, she found identical tattoos in the same spot. This was likely the mark of the Soul-Claiming Sect.","\"Those from underworld assassin organizations are usually orphans. Even if they lose their lives, no one will report it to the officials.\"","\"However, since the Soul-Claiming Sect took the money for this assassination, if the mission isn't completed, this likely won't be the end of it.\" There would probably be another wave.","Song Qiming and the others felt heavy-hearted. Was it the Yan family?","To avenge Yan Baoyi, they had actually gone so far as to contact an assassin organization from the underworld.","Song Gaoli wanted to say something to lighten the mood and suggest traveling through the night, but then he saw Song Jinzhao squatting by the corpses, looting them.","Opening the money pouches she took from the five men, she raised an eyebrow and sighed in disappointment. \"I thought the whole five thousand taels would be on them. After all that work, there's only a bit over two hundred taels.\"","Tossing the empty pouches aside, she tucked the banknotes and silver pieces into her robe. She cut off Huangquan Ghost’s tattoo and walked toward the carriage. \"We won't stay the night here. We're going to Kaikang immediately.\"","The clay pot on the fire was covered in blood splatters, so the food was definitely inedible.","Song Qiming extinguished the fire and climbed onto the carriage to follow Song Jinzhao.","Song Gaoli held the door curtain open and said, \"Qiming, you hold your younger brother. I'll drive the carriage.\"","Song Qiming gripped the reins and didn't let go. \"You stay inside tonight. I'll do it.\"","There was no guarantee there wouldn't be another round of attacks, and he didn't feel safe with Song Gaoli being outside."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: Waiting for Gains without Pains, All Are Death Warriors","paragraphs":["Anyang Prefecture. Moonlight cast a pale, grayish-white glow upon the snow.","A few short, crisp taps sounded from the roof. A figure in black slowly crouched down and carefully pried up a roof tile.","Inside the room, a charcoal brazier burned with a bright red flame, sending a wave of heat outward.","Thick quilts swaddled Ye Liangyu tightly, leaving only a coarse, long strand of white hair trailing over the bedside—its poor quality evident at a glance.","The black-clad figure turned his head to signal to his companions behind him.","Dozens of black-clad figures dropped from the eaves like the wind, rolled twice on the ground, and sprang up.","They swiftly dispersed, rushing toward various rooms within the estate.","Their master had given the order: not a single servant of the Ye household was to be spared.","To avoid suspicion, after the killings, the Ye estate was to be set ablaze, disguising the deaths as an accidental fire.","Soporific smoke was fed through the small hole pierced into the rooms of Ye Liangyu and his attendant.","After waiting a moment, one of them slid a blade into the door crack and shifted the bolt. Five men, weapons in hand, barged into Ye Liangyu's chamber.","Just as a longsword was about to pierce Ye Liangyu's body, the quilts were abruptly thrown aside. A flash of silver light shot into the attacker's pupils as a sword thrust straight for his throat.","\"Been waiting for you,\" said Qin Yunqian, tossing aside the white wig he had been wearing, his sharp gaze fierce as a vulture's.","Yesterday, soldiers disguised as street vendors had noticed people frequently loitering around the Ye estate. Upon learning of this, Qin Yunqian immediately decided to set a trap, waiting for the assassins to walk right in.","Sure enough, on the very night they finished casing the place, they couldn't restrain themselves from acting.","In the courtyard, the clang of blades suddenly erupted, mingled with the thuds of hand-to-hand combat. In the neighboring room, Ye Liangyu clenched his fists, the hatred in his heart surging like a furious tide.","Knowing his legs had been healed, they couldn't wait to try and kill him again.","Was the mastermind behind this Prince Qi, Prince Ying, or someone else entirely?","Today, he would finally have his answer.","The black-clad leader, seeing the courtyard filled with armed, robust men, furrowed his brow in dismay. \"It's a trap.\"","Qin Yunqian, having dealt with two minor lackeys, charged toward him. \"Too late to realize that now.\"","The leader swung his sword to parry, gritting his teeth as he demanded, \"Who are you? Why are you helping Ye Liangyu?\"","A former Vice Censor-in-Chief who had resigned and returned home due to illness couldn't possibly have trained so many guards in such a short time. Whose side were they on?","Seizing an opening, Qin Yunqian kicked him squarely in the chest. \"That's my question for you. Who sent you?\"","The scent of blood grew heavier in the courtyard. Warm blood splashed into the pond, blocked by the ice on the surface, forming a strange tripartite layer of black, white, and red.","Outnumbered five to one, and caught off guard by the number of guards at the Ye estate, the dozens of black-clad assassins were soon whittled down to just three.","\"Take them alive,\" Qin Yunqian ordered his subordinates, pressing the lead assassin to his knees with his leg.","A command token fell from Qin Yunqian's chest. The black-clad man's pupils constricted. \"You're from the Thunderclap Army!\"","The token was clearly engraved with the words 'Thunderclap Army'—their identities were now obvious.","Qin Yunqian commanded, \"Bind them with rope and take them to the woodshed. We must find out who's behind this.\"","\"Yes, sir!\" The resolute, unified response was unmistakably military; these men were clearly handpicked elites.","After the prisoners were taken to the woodshed, Qin Yunqian vaulted over the courtyard wall to fetch the person next door.","\"Lord Ye, the assailants have all been subdued. Three remain alive.\"","Ye Liangyu slowly rose to his feet, a thin layer of sweat dampening his palms.","\"My thanks to General Qin for today's intervention.\"","Qin Yunqian squared his shoulders, duty-bound. \"It was nothing. Lord Ye is a friend of my father's, which makes you an elder to me. I would have stood guard not just for two months, but for a year or more if needed.\"","Ye Liangyu's eyebrow twitched slightly. This temperament was completely unlike Qin Guo's.","They had only been connected for three months, and he was already claiming the status of a junior? Should one call him thick-skinned or highly perceptive?","No sooner had he stepped into the courtyard, his back foot yet to land, than someone came rushing out from the woodshed, nearly colliding with them.","\"Bad news, Young General! Those three have taken poison and died.\"","Qin Yunqian's expression turned grim. He strode quickly into the woodshed and looked at the three bound figures lying on the ground, black blood staining their mouths.","A subordinate frowned, deeply distressed. \"The poison was hidden in their mouths. They died in an instant—there was no way to save them.\"","Their key witnesses were dead, and the mastermind remained unknown.","Qin Yunqian's face was dark with fury.","Two soldiers entered from outside. \"Reporting, Young General. All the corpses outside also had poison packets hidden in their mouths.\"","Qin Yunqian's face turned as black as a pot's bottom. \"They were all death warriors.\"","Ye Liangyu gazed at the bodies on the floor, his eyelashes trembling uncontrollably.","He closed his eyes, took a deep breath, and said with a tone of self-mockery, \"They certainly think highly of me.\"","He had already resigned and returned home, yet they sent death warriors for an assassination.","How utterly determined they were to kill him—it was a fight to the death!"]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: The Timid and Overcautious County Magistrate Kaikang, a Potential Danger","paragraphs":["It was high noon when Song Jinzhao and her companions finally arrived in Kaikang City after traveling for sixteen hours straight.","Song Gaoli was dizzy and bleary-eyed; by the time he stepped down from the carriage, his entire lower body felt stiff and numb.","The sound of drums echoed as the Magistrate of Kaikang straightened his official robes and headgear before taking his seat in the hall.","\"Who stands before me? What grievance do you bring?\"","Song Qiming explained the sequence of events with absolute clarity, while Song Jinzhao handed over the piece of tattooed skin she had cut away to the bailiff.","The Magistrate stared at the skull tattoo on the human skin, his thick lips parting slightly. His eyes flickered with unease, as if he were terrified of something.","\"This official is now fully aware of the case. You may leave for now. Once the mastermind is found, I shall send men to inform you.\"","Song Qiming opened his mouth to say more, but the gavel suddenly slammed down.","\"Court adjourned!\"","Watching the Magistrate of Kaikang flee the hall as if running for his life, Song Qiming muttered, \"He didn't even ask where we’re staying. How is he going to inform us?\"","Moreover, they had no intention of lingering in Kaikang; they planned to rest for one night and depart first thing tomorrow morning.","Song Jinzhao folded the petition, now bearing the official crimson seal, and tucked it back into her bag. \"They never intended to investigate. Those were merely excuses to stall and brush us off.\"","She shook her head. \"They say all under heaven belongs to the Emperor, but the delicate line between the martial world and the imperial court is one that not every official dares to cross. The Magistrate of Kaikang fears for his life; he doesn't dare provoke them.\"","If the investigation truly led to the Suoming Gate, the organization could take his life just by sending a few assassins. He didn't dare investigate, nor did he plan to.","Song Qiming knit his brows, worried. \"What do we do next? If this happens a few more times, it will be impossible to guard against.\"","Song Jinzhao set off with calm steps. \"If one comes, I’ll kill one. If ten come, I’ll kill ten. Let’s see how many lives of Suoming Gate assassins five thousand taels of silver can buy.\"","The strongest assassin had focused solely on her, which proved that she was their primary target. If that was the case, the likelihood of the Yan family being the employer was relatively low.","Who could produce five thousand taels and held a grudge against her?","Liu Fufeng was dead, but her children were still alive. Then there was the Liao family—could it be Concubine Su?","Back at the inn, Song Gaoli was slumped over the table in Song Shixue’s room, sleeping fitfully. He shifted, nearly sliding off the stool.","Song Shixue, who was sitting on the couch reading, shook her head helplessly at the sight.","Startled awake, Song Gaoli forced his eyes open and craned his neck around, asking disappointedly, \"Are they back yet?\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, the door was pushed open from the outside.","Seeing Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming enter, Song Gaoli stood up excitedly. \"Well? What did the Magistrate say?\"","Song Qiming narrowed his eyes. \"Why are you in my sister’s room?\"","Song Gaoli shrank back pitifully. \"I didn't dare stay in my room alone while you were gone.\"","Song Qiming pursed his lips. He should have just brought him along earlier. Although Anhao was also in the room, the boy was only two years old. Propriety between men and women had to be maintained, even with a trusted brother.","\"The Magistrate has no intention of investigating. He just accepted the case to get us out of there.\"","Song Gaoli flopped back onto the stool. \"If even the government is afraid to touch it, this Suoming Gate must be a very powerful organization.\"","Song Qiming sat down and poured some water. \"Don't worry, their target likely doesn't include you. Once we’re back at the village and you aren't with us, you’ll be safe.\"","Song Gaoli had always been well-behaved at the academy and never offended anyone. If he hadn't been traveling with Song Jinzhao and the others, he wouldn't have encountered this mess.","Song Gaoli suddenly snapped his head up, staring intently at Song Qiming.","\"That's not what I meant! Fearing death is human nature, but I’m no coward. I’m just worried about what happens next. If they strike at you and Shixue while Jinzhao is away, it’ll be over for you.\"","Song Qiming and Song Shixue turned to look at Song Jinzhao simultaneously.","\"Sister, once we’re back in the village, I want to double the time Shixue and I spend on our daily training.\"","\"And hidden weapons—we want to prepare more of them.\"","Song Jinzhao’s lips curled into a smile as she held up three fingers.","\"Make it triple. Train as if your lives depend on it.\""]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: Back to Songjia Village","paragraphs":["A few days later, at the manor outside Anyang Prefecture, Chunxing gazed at the lush green vegetables in the greenhouse, her face beaming with delight.","“The shop is all set up. When can we harvest the first batch of vegetables?”","In the northern winter, where temperatures dropped to more than ten degrees below zero, the sight of fresh greens would surely stun everyone once the news got out.","Fushun plucked a broad bean and peeled it open. “In three days. According to the Eldest Young Lady’s instructions, it will be just in time for the Little New Year.”","Chunxing nodded and took a deep breath, her heart racing with anticipation for that day to arrive.","Even though Song Jinzhao was away, everything in the Song household was proceeding according to her plan, moving as smoothly as well-oiled gears.","Meanwhile, Old Man Song, wearing two layers of worn-out padded cotton coats, pushed open the door with a head full of snow.","Old Lady Song stood up and took a cloth to brush the snow off him. “Still no sign of them?”","Old Man Song shook his head. “I just went to the Village Head’s house to ask. They said it should be in the next day or two. They should be back soon.”","The letter Song Jinzhao sent three days ago had clearly stated their departure time. Based on the distance, they should be home any moment now.","Oldest Song, who was busy weaving bamboo baskets in the main hall, looked up and said, “The roads are difficult to travel when it snows, so it’s normal to be delayed by a day or two. With Jinzhao there, you can rest easy, Father.”","Old Man Song took off one of his cotton coats and sat by the stove to warm himself.","“It’s been five months. I wonder how the third branch is doing. Have they gained weight or gotten thinner?”","“They don’t have any relatives out there to help them, and they are so young. If they get bullied, they don’t even have an elder to stand up for them.”","Oldest Song pursed his lips helplessly. It was hard to say who would be bullying whom.","With his eldest niece’s skills, she could take on three people at once with energy to spare. Anyone who dared to provoke her would be lucky to escape with their life.","As the surrounding scenery became increasingly familiar, Song Jinzhao, who hadn't spent much time in Song Village, felt a touch of \"homesick apprehension\" as she neared her destination.","Song Shixue leaned against the carriage window, her eyes sparkling with an excitement brighter than the spring sun.","“Sister, can we go see Father and Mother as soon as we get home? I miss them.”","Song Jinzhao’s hand tightened slightly on the reins. She pressed her lips together and nodded. “We’ll go as soon as we arrive. We’ll stop in the city first to buy some joss paper.”","After a quick sweep through the city, as the sky began to dim, the two carriages headed straight for Song Village.","Song Dazhuang, who was eating dinner, suddenly put down his bowl and chopsticks and pricked up his ears. “I think I hear the sound of horse hooves.”","“Grandpa, Grandma, I’m back!”","A thunderous shout shattered the peace of the Village Head’s house.","The sound reached the neighbors, and curious villagers stepped out to see two carriages parked on the road.","Rubbing their eyes, they realized the person driving the carriage looked like the eldest daughter of the third Song brother?","Village Head Song Mancang was the first to react. He dropped his bowl and rushed to open the door.","Song Gaoli, carrying a bundle and the goods he had just bought from Xining City, dashed into the courtyard. The joy on his face was even more radiant than when he had passed the scholar exams.","“Grandpa!”","Everyone inside the house rushed out, joyfully grabbing Song Gaoli to check on him.","Song Mancang said with a smile, “You’ve gotten thinner, but you’ve grown quite a bit taller. You’re almost as tall as your father.”","Song Gaoli scratched his head sheepishly as he set down his things. “I’m not thinner, just leaner and stronger.”","Song Mancang glanced toward the courtyard gate, where Song Qiming was walking in with the rest of Song Gaoli’s luggage.","He didn't hesitate to praise him. “It’s only been a few months, but Qiming has grown to be even more handsome and dignified.”","Song Qiming gave a gentle nod to everyone in the house. “Village Head, Uncle Dazhuang, Grandma, Auntie.”","Dazhuang's Wife warmly took the items from Song Qiming’s hands. “Where is your sister? It’s just in time for dinner. You must stay and eat with us today.”","Song Mancang immediately chimed in, “Yes, yes! Wife, take Dazhuang's Wife to the kitchen and cook a few more dishes. They must be hungry after traveling all day.”","Song Qiming smiled and shook his head, already stepping back toward the door.","“No need, we bought food in the city. My sister is still waiting for me outside. I’ll come over another day.”","Gaoli's grandma and mother couldn't hold Song Qiming back. They followed him out of the courtyard and saw another carriage parked on the road.","Gaoli's grandma waved and ran over, looking at Song Jinzhao with admiration.","“Jinzhao has grown into such a fine young lady. Thank you for bringing my Gaoli back this time. You must come to my house for dinner tomorrow.”","Song Shixue poked her head out of the carriage and called out politely, “Gaoli's grandma.”","In just a short while, more and more villagers opened their doors to see the commotion.","The only two scholars in the village had returned. Looking at the carriages, they were even more beautiful than those belonging to the wealthy Master Zhao.","Looking at their clothes and appearance, they looked like the young ladies and masters of a great noble family in the city. Life for the third branch of the Song family in the prefectural city must be very prosperous indeed.","“Jinzhao! Qiming! Shixue!”","Old Man Song came running over in his old cotton coat, not even having time to fasten the top two buttons.","Song Jinzhao jumped down from the carriage, and Song Shixue climbed out holding Song Anhao.","Three cries of “Grandpa!” rang out one after another.","Looking at the four siblings gathered together, Old Man Song’s heart completely melted."]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: Visiting the Grave, First Day at Home","paragraphs":["The room was spotlessly clean, not a speck of dust in sight.","Old Lady Song came in carrying a large teapot and poured three bowls of steaming hot water.","\"Knowing you were coming back, the day before yesterday I took your Eldest Aunt and Second Aunt to clean the place from front to back three times, so you could move right in when you arrived.\"","Old Man Song held the soft and chubby Song Anhao, \"The grain in the kitchen is the new rice harvested this year, and there's chopped firewood in the woodshed.\"","\"Tomorrow, I'll have your grandmother kill a chicken and send it over. You can cook for yourselves or come to the old house to eat, whichever you prefer.\"","Oldest Song stood to the side, nodding. \"If you're short of anything, just go to the old house to get it. Father has prepared everything well, he's been looking forward to your return.\"","Second Song's eyes roamed over the four members of the third branch. After taking off his heavy cloak, he revealed the silk-padded jacket embroidered with flowers, birds, and beasts underneath.","The white jade hair crown on Song Qiming's head, the beaded flowers and silver hairpins in Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue's hair—everything about them screamed expense.","They seemed even more refined than the wealthy Master Zhao in the village.","In just half a year, the third branch had transformed once again.","This was all the benefit that studying had brought.","Once his own son passed the imperial examination and became a scholar, he too could go to the prefectural city and live such an idyllic life.","Thinking that Song Yaozu would advance to the advanced class next year, Second Song said to Song Qiming, \"Qiming, after the New Year in February, Yaozu will take the county-level examination. While you're home, you must give him some guidance.\"","His eldest nephew's literary talent was now even higher than Scholar Zheng's. With half a month of his tutoring, next year's county exam would be a sure success.","After two years of study, Old Man Song was perfectly clear about what kind of performance Song Yaozu had shown at the Zheng family's private school.","\"Scholar Zheng said, this time, Yongnian and Yaozu are just taking the county exam for the experience. The main focus is really the year after.\"","Second Song argued discontentedly, \"Yaozu is clever. With Qiming's guidance for half a month, he might just pass.\"","Old Man Song rolled his eyes. \"Always dreaming of pies falling from the sky. If the imperial examinations were that easy, scholars would be everywhere.\"","\"Qiming has finally come home and needs to rest properly. Don't just think about ordering people around.\"","Second Song opened his mouth to say more, but Oldest Song stepped in front of him, blocking his way and glaring to stop him.","Causing trouble on the very first day back? Be careful, Father will lose his temper.","Second Song unhappily closed his mouth.","Seeing Song Anhao yawning with sleepiness, Old Man Song placed him on the kang and said to Song Jinzhao, \"You rest first. When Oldest and Second's wives have the meal ready, Grandfather will come call you.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded and stood up to see them out. \"Thank you, Grandfather. We'll come over ourselves once we're settled.\"","After the four left, Song Qiming put on his cloak and fetched the spirit money from the carriage.","Outside, the sky was gradually darkening. Song Jinzhao took a torch in case they couldn't see the path on the way back.","Song Shixue, carrying the sleepy Song Anhao, walked in the middle. The cold air blowing on their faces instantly chased away any drowsiness.","The snow at the foot of the mountain was thicker than elsewhere, crunching loudly under their feet.","Song Jinzhao stuck the torch in the ground and, together with Song Qiming, used large bamboo brooms to clear the snow around the tombstone.","The spirit money burned with a piercing light in the charcoal basin. The young Song Anhao looked at the tombstone and called out \"Father, Mother\" along with Song Jinzhao and the others.","Even though less than half a year had passed, both Song Qiming and Song Shixue felt a sense of change and impermanence in their hearts, as if everything had become different.","By the time the meal was ready, the sky had turned completely dark. Seeing the third branch hadn't arrived, Old Man Song took Oldest Song with him to fetch them.","Arriving at the courtyard gate, he found it closed. Puzzled, he peered through the crack—the room inside was pitch black, nothing visible.","Old Man Song sighed with heartache. \"They're probably all asleep. They must be exhausted from traveling for so many days.\"","Oldest Song turned his head and noticed a flickering light in the direction of the path leading to the back mountain. He muttered, \"Who would go up the mountain at this hour?\"","In winter, no one in the village dared go into the mountains; even the foothills were avoided at night.","Old Man Song's right hand, which had been about to knock and call out, froze as if paused. He took a step back, gazing toward the end of the light. The guess forming in his mind made his heart ache with a sour feeling.","As the distance closed, faint figures became visible. Old Man Song's voice sounded a bit distant. \"Jinzhao.\"","Song Jinzhao responded, \"Grandfather.\"","As they approached, Old Man Song took the torch to light their way.","\"You went to see your father and mother without telling me. Had I known, I wouldn't have left earlier.\"","Oldest Song walked beside them and said, \"It's the same if we go tomorrow. It's not safe at night.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled faintly. \"Qiming and Shixue were both longing to go. They wouldn't have been able to sleep tonight without seeing them.\"","Old Man Song looked into the distance without a word, the cold wind chilling his eyes.","During the meal, the old couple and the families of Oldest Song and Second Song chattered nonstop. Song Anhao leaned over a cradle, staring at the infant who couldn't yet speak and giggling.","That was Oldest Song's youngest son, Song Yongshi, only two months old, and now the youngest grandchild in the Song family.","Oldest Song's wife smiled, her eyes curving. \"Time flies. In just over two years, Anhao has grown so much. He looked a bit like Yongshi when he was born.\"","Song Anhao frowned, his soft little hands cupping his own cheeks. \"Not alike. Anhao is better looking than him.\"","\"Pfft.\" Song Jinzhao couldn't help laughing, poking Song Anhao's forehead with her finger. \"So vain at such a young age. I wonder who you learned that from.\"","Song Anhao put his hands on his hips, chin held high. \"Eldest Sister and Second Sister are both good-looking, so of course I'm not bad either.\"","Song Qiming teased, \"What about your big brother?\"","Song Anhao gestured with a tiny gap between his fingers. \"Just a little bit worse than me.\"","Old Lady Song chuckled and praised, \"Anhao speaks so fluently, not at all like he's only two.\"","Quick-witted, clever, and smart, with good looks too—just like the child sitting beneath the Goddess of Mercy.","Song Jinzhao said, \"He's met many people and talks a lot. It's all from practice.\"","Song Shixue picked up Song Anhao and placed him on her lap. \"When you were just born, you were thin and small, not even half Yongshi's size. Eldest Sister, Big Brother, and I were all afraid to hold you. Not like now, eating so much every day, I can hardly lift you.\"","The expressions of Oldest Song and Second Song and their wives tightened slightly. Their hearts skipped a beat, feeling as if these words were somehow aimed at them.","Back then, when Anhao was born premature, their handling of the arrangements for the children had indeed been less than proper, but there had been no other choice.","Now, the third branch was completely different from before. The events of that year were like a thorn, forever impossible to remove. To say they didn't regret it would be a lie."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Jinzhao's Marriage is Beyond Our Interference, The Gift","paragraphs":["The next morning, the entire Song Village was abuzz, with almost everyone discussing the return of Song Qiming and Song Gaoli the previous evening.","The men envied their ability to study and pass the imperial examinations to become xiucai, while the women's conversation centered entirely on the clothing and appearance of Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue.","When Old Lady Song came to deliver breakfast, the three children were still asleep.","Song Jinzhao took the basket and said, \"Grandma, you don't need to make lunch for us. The house is almost tidied up, and we'll make our own lunch.\"","Looking at her eldest granddaughter, as bright and beautiful as a plum blossom standing proudly in the snow, Old Lady Song's thoughts began sprouting one after another.","Returning to the main house, she pulled Old Man Song into the room. \"After the New Year, Jinzhao will be seventeen. I'm thinking of asking a matchmaker about her marriage.\"","Back then, Jinzhao had promised not to marry until Qiming started a family, but that was to support her three younger siblings.","Now, the third branch of the family has no worries about food or clothing. Even if Jinzhao married, it wouldn't be a big issue.","Qiming has passed the xiucai examination and has the ability to support the third branch. Old Man Song's previous idea of having Song Jinzhao take in a live-in son-in-law had also become unnecessary, greatly expanding the pool of potential candidates.","With her eldest granddaughter's qualities, just putting out the word would surely have a line of suitors encircling the village four or five times. Would they fear not finding a good one?","Old Man Song remained silent for a long time before shaking his head. \"We can't meddle in Jinzhao's marriage. With her qualities, she deserves at least a xiucai master. How many unmarried ones are there within dozens of miles?\"","\"Qiming definitely won't live in the village in the future. I'd say it's best if Jinzhao can marry into the provincial capital.\"","Old Lady Song's mouth opened and closed. Her husband's words weren't without reason, but...","\"They don't have any elder relatives in Anyang Prefecture. We can't possibly let Jinzhao find a matchmaker and meet prospects on her own.\"","Leaning on the kang, Old Man Song couldn't help but think of Third Song and his wife.","If Third Song were still here, they would be more concerned about Jinzhao's marriage than anyone.","\"How about I ask Qiming another day? After the New Year, he'll be thirteen and should understand things.\"","\"The Anyang Academy is full of xiucai masters. We can pick a few good ones to introduce. Later, if they pass the provincial or imperial examinations, Jinzhao would become an official's wife. That would be truly marrying well and rising in status.\"","Old Lady Song frowned. \"Is Qiming reliable? I just don't feel at ease.\"","Old Man Song pulled the quilt over his legs. \"He would just arrange for them to meet. The final decision is still in Jinzhao's own hands. I trust her judgment.\"","Old Lady Song pressed her lips together, her heart still uneasy.","The most important thing in a woman's life is to marry a good man. If she chooses wrong, her whole life could be ruined.","No matter how capable and competent Jinzhao is, she ultimately hasn't experienced romantic love. She mustn't be deceived by anyone.","It was past 8 a.m. when Song Qiming and the others woke up. After breakfast, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming brought the things bought from Xining City to the main house.","Returning home for the New Year, one must always bring gifts for the elders, especially since Old Man Song and Old Lady Song had been looking after their house.","Just take the courtyard; if left unswept for a month, it would be overgrown with weeds and shrubs.","Being able to move in directly upon returning home, with everything prepared so well, Song Jinzhao felt she had to show her appreciation.","The first branch family stared at the bundle spread open on the table—a thick stack of new clothes, all ready-made garments that required no sewing.","Old Lady Song's cloudy eyes shone brighter than obsidian. Her rough hands gently stroked the soft fabric, her joy almost overflowing like water.","\"Just coming back is enough. Such fine material is wasted on an old woman like me.\"","Old Man Song opened the wine jar's stopper. The rich aroma of wine rushed into his nostrils, intoxicating him before he even took a sip.","Song Jinzhao smiled in response. \"Clothes worn on a person are never wasted. The deep red suits you, Grandma. It looks beautiful.\"","Song Yongnian and Song Qiaoniang held their new clothes, happily thanking Song Jinzhao. \"Thank you, Sister Jinzhao.\"","Song Yongshi, still in swaddling clothes, received a bolt of new cotton cloth.","\"The child grows fast. Yongshi's clothes will have to trouble Elder Aunt Song to make herself.\"","Although she didn't receive a gift herself, Elder Aunt Song was overjoyed holding the cloth.","\"You traveled so far to come back and even brought clothes for the children. I'm delighted, it's no trouble at all.\"","\"Next time you come back, don't buy things for them. These things are very expensive. These kids are tough, coarse cloth is enough for them.\"","The ready-made clothes Song Jinzhao bought weren't made of overly expensive material either, but for farming families, having new clothes to wear was already a great gift.","Carrying the remaining three pieces of clothing, they went to the second branch. When Second Aunt Song saw the clothes, her eyes instantly lit up.","She reached out to open them, but seeing the size, she asked puzzledly, \"Jinzhao, it seems I can't fit into these clothes. Why didn't you buy fabric?\"","Standing beside her, Song Qiming's face darkened, remembering the scene from two years ago when they sent steamed buns. He snatched the clothes back and handed them to Song Laidi.","\"These are for Laidi and Pandi. Only Yongnian and Qiaoniang in the uncle's family got some. If Second Aunt wants new clothes, you can have Second Song buy them for you.\"","Second Aunt Song awkwardly withdrew her hand, a slight look of disdain on her face.","\"Girls are fine as long as they have clothes to wear. What's the point of buying new ones? It's a waste even if they wear them.\"","Song Jinzhao pulled the clothes back, her face stern.","\"You're a woman too. Since it's a waste, why don't you just go outside naked? If you don't want them, I'll give them to Qiaoniang to wear. Their figures are about the same anyway.\"","Second Aunt Song hurriedly grabbed the clothes and hugged them to her chest, replying with an ingratiating smile.","\"That's not what I meant. I just feel it's a pity if such nice clothes get worn out.\"","Song Jinzhao didn't want to waste more words. She turned to Song Laidi and Song Pandi and said, \"The new clothes were specially bought for you two. Remember to wear them for the New Year. Yongnian and Qiaoniang will also be wearing new clothes for the New Year's Eve dinner.\"","Song Laidi tightened her grip on Song Pandi's hand, her gaze meeting Song Jinzhao's intently.","She nodded in response. \"Thank you, Sister Jinzhao. My sister and I like them very much.\"","As they were leaving, Song Qiming turned his head and shouted into the room, \"Second Uncle, you didn't give me New Year's money last year. Don't forget this year.\"","Second Song wanted to say something but stopped himself. Your family is so well-off now, do you still lack my bit of New Year's money?","Third Song and his wife have passed away; giving New Year's money to their children is a one-way gift with no return.","Second Aunt Song sat down heavily with a huff, staring at the clothes, her heart aching.","Seeing this, Second Song said, \"If you can't wear these clothes, you can give them to Yaozu to wear. If they're too big, just take in the sleeves and pant legs.\"","Song Yaozu, who was trying on his new clothes, said disdainfully, \"I won't wear them. You can tell at a glance these are girls' clothes. I'd be laughed at if I wore them outside.\"","Second Song looked at the two sets of clothes—one peach red, one light purple—indeed unsuitable.","Second Aunt Song, fuming, threw the two sets of clothes at the sisters. \"Jinzhao deliberately picked such bright colors. She obviously prefers girls. The outfit on Shixue is worth more than Qiming's put together.\"","If Song Jinzhao were there, she would definitely retort.","Girls should be raised with ample resources, with higher standards and broader horizons. Otherwise, when they grow up, they might be fooled by the first man who beckons, and then there would be nowhere to cry.","Song Laidi and Song Pandi suppressed their joy, holding the new clothes carefully, not daring to grip them too hard, worried the thick calluses on their hands might wrinkle or tear the fabric.","Second Song: \"If you really like them, after the New Year when Jinzhao and the others leave, you can combine these two sets to make a new one for yourself. Then you can wear it.\"","The sisters' backs stiffened. They clenched their teeth, their hearts full of grievance.","Second Aunt Song thought for a moment and shook her head. \"One red and one purple, the colors don't match. It would look awful pieced together. Jinzhao even suggested they wear them to the old house for the New Year. If people found out I was wearing my daughter's clothes, who knows how much gossip there'd be behind my back.\"","\"If Father and Mother sent a letter to tell Jinzhao, we in the second branch could forget about getting any nice things from now on.\"","Anyway, he had no silver to buy Second Aunt Song new clothes. With both his suggestions rejected, he felt he'd done his part just by voicing them."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: The Startled Village Chief's Family Goes into the Mountains to Practice","paragraphs":["After clearing the snow from the courtyard, Song Jinzhao expanded the daily martial arts practice time to three hours, making it the routine for each day's twelve hours, aside from sleeping, eating, and reading.","The main room was covered with thick sheepskins by Song Jinzhao. Song Anhao sat on the floor watching his older brother and sister practice outside, occasionally standing up to mimic their movements.","When he fell, it didn't hurt at all; instead, he would laugh heartily.","The old house sent over two cleaned old hens—one for stewing soup, the other for braising in soy sauce. They were finished in three days.","Watching the brother and sister sparring back and forth, Song Jinzhao turned to face the rear.","Their bouts were too restrained, lacking enough lethal intent. They needed more real combat experience.","Song Gaoli gulped down a whole piece of braised pork. Song Mancang watched, his heart aching.","He claimed to be doing well at the academy, but his eating manners showed he hadn't had much meat.","Seeing the whole family staring at him, Song Gaoli swallowed the savory sauce in his mouth.","\"I really am doing fine at the academy. Qiming often brings his family's marinated dishes for me, and he invites me to his home for meals now and then. I just missed Mother's cooking—it tastes like home.\"","Gaoli's mother brushed the back of her hand across the corner of her eye and picked up a large chicken drumstick, placing it in Song Gaoli's bowl. \"If you like it, eat more. While you're home, your mother will cook for you every day.\"","Song Mancang asked, \"What marinated dishes? Is Qiming's family taking good care of you in the prefectural city?\"","Song Gaoli nodded. \"Qiming and I are good brothers now. Sister Jinzhao opened a shop in the prefectural city selling marinated food and drinks. She makes a lot of meat dishes to sell every day, and sometimes Qiming brings some to the academy for me to share.\"","Song Mancang raised his eyebrows in surprise. \"Jinzhao bought a shop in Anyang Prefecture?\"","Song Gaoli affirmed with a nod, taking a bite that consumed half the drumstick meat.","\"Sister Jinzhao is amazing. She bought two shops at once—one for food and one for a medical clinic. Now the whole of Anyang Prefecture knows her as the best physician; they call her the Divine Healer.\"","Song Mancang was stunned. \"Two shops? Qiming has to study. Can the two sisters manage all that?\"","Song Gaoli shook his head. \"Shixue is learning medicine from Sister Jinzhao. The food shop is managed by servants.\"","Song Dazhuang exclaimed in shock, \"They bought servants too?\"","Song Gaoli nodded, feeling satisfied with his family's astonishment. Finally, someone could share the surprises Song Jinzhao had brought him over the past six months.","Unlike in Anyang Prefecture, where his classmates found it all ordinary, he was the only one who thought it remarkable.","\"They bought them not long after arriving in the prefectural city. There are six just at home. From what Qiming says, there are over a dozen more on their estate outside the city.\"","Song Dazhuang was dumbfounded, as if struck by lightning.","\"They bought an estate too?\"","Song Gaoli replied, \"Most likely. I didn't ask for specifics. But their three-courtyard house was bought, and I even helped with the move.\"","The village chief's family sat frozen like sculptures, mouths slightly agape, almost drooling.","After a long while, Song Mancang couldn't help but sigh in admiration. \"I knew Jinzhao was capable, but I never imagined she was this capable. In such a short time, she has everything in Anyang Prefecture.\"","Gaoli's mother thought for a long time, then scrutinized her son from head to toe.","As the saying goes, marrying an older woman is like embracing a gold brick. An age difference of two years doesn't matter.","The only difficulty is that he's only fourteen, too young to marry.","By the time he grows a couple of years older, Song Jinzhao will probably already be married. Should they try to arrange a betrothal first?","Having finished showing off, Song Gaoli began to focus wholeheartedly on his meal, completely unaware of his mother's peculiar gaze.","If he had known, he would have jumped right off his stool.","Old Lady Song reached out to hold Song Anhao's hand and voiced her disapproval with concern.","\"Why go to the mountain in such cold weather? I heard wolf howls just a few days ago. You absolutely cannot go.\"","Old Man Song blocked the path of the three. \"Is the meat at home all gone? I'll have Grandma kill another chicken.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"No need to kill a chicken. I just want to take Qiming and Shixue to the mountain to test their skills. Practicing without real danger is no fun.\"","She noticed there weren't many chickens left in the coop; killing another would empty it.","Old Man Song saw that Song Qiming and Song Shixue showed no fear on their faces; instead, they looked eager.","He felt torn, neither able to agree nor refuse outright.","Seeing his hesitation and silence, Song Jinzhao simply took the two siblings and left. \"We'll be back by afternoon at the latest.\"","Back home, the three geared up fully, leaving only their faces exposed.","The heavy snow had sealed the mountain. On the narrow path leading to the back hills, not a single bird could be seen. It was so silent it felt as if only the three of them remained between heaven and earth.","Once in the mountains, Song Jinzhao walked at the back, watching the two bend down to search for animal tracks on the ground.","It hadn't snowed after midnight yesterday, so animal footprints and droppings on the snow should not yet be covered by fresh snow, making them easier to find.","Song Shixue sniffed and twitched her nose. Besides the fresh, cold scent of snow and the earthy smell of withered grass, she couldn't detect anything else.","After a good while, Song Qiming straightened up.","\"We're still too close to the village. We need to go further in.\"","They both looked at Song Jinzhao, seeking her opinion.","Song Jinzhao spread her hands, not moving her feet. \"Today, you two decide for yourselves. Unless there's danger, your older sister won't intervene.\"","Their eyes met. Song Qiming gave a slight nod. \"Then let's go further in.\"","Song Shixue agreed.","The further in they went, the thicker the snow became. Their boots sank into the snowdrifts, submerging half their calves.","Entering a pine forest, they saw a large gray tail swishing left and right in the snow, with a pile of excavated snow beside a burrow entrance.","The air and snow crystals rubbed together, emitting a soft, rustling sound.","A squirrel digging for its winter stores alertly poked its head out of the hole. Upon seeing Song Qiming, its body froze for an instant, and its tail puffed up like a flower.","It didn't bother with the pinecone it had dropped, scrambling up a nearby tree like a brown flash of lightning.","It leaped from one tree to another and vanished without a trace in the blink of an eye.","Song Qiming walked over and used his dagger to dig open the entrance. Seeing inside, he smiled and said, \"It has stored quite a lot.\" The hole was filled with pinecones.","Song Shixue covered the hole again with snow. They didn't eat squirrels.","These creatures were small and fast. Catching them was too much effort for too little meat—not worth it.","\"Let's keep going forward. If we can see squirrels, other prey shouldn't be far either.\""]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: Capture Alive, the Black Bear That Does Not Hibernate","paragraphs":["Looking at a string of footprints left in the snow, which resembled a dog’s paws, Song Shixue reasoned that there shouldn't be any dogs deep in the mountains during such heavy snowfall.","\"They should be wolf tracks,\" Song Shixue judged.","Song Qiming reached out to measure the size of the prints with his hands, shaking his head in disagreement. \"Wolf prints are at least two or three times larger than this. Besides, there’s only one set of tracks. Wolves are pack animals; this isn't a wolf.\"","A meter away from the two, Song Jinzhao stood with her arms crossed, a faint smile on her face.","Keen observation, heightened alertness, excellent decision-making and judgment, and strong psychological and emotional control—these were all traits that had to be cultivated one by one. This world was far more dangerous than she had imagined.","Initially, her requirements for the siblings hadn't been so high. She simply wanted them to be physically fit and have a certain level of self-defense capability.","However, after surviving various crises, the training had to be elevated to the highest standard.","The higher one climbs, the harder the fall. With so many wolves, tigers, and leopards lurking in the world, there was no guarantee they wouldn't meet with disaster if she wasn't by their side one day.","One’s life had to be held in one's own hands.","Song Shixue followed the tracks forward and discovered several long, hard lumps in a snowdrift.","As she leaned in closer, a pungent, musky odor hit her, making her stomach churn with nausea.","\"It's fox droppings.\"","The oval footprints, with an inverted U-shape in the center of the palm, matched those of a fox.","Song Qiming looked up and scanned the surroundings, his eyes lighting up with joy.","\"A fox is good. We can use the fur to make scarves for you and Ah Jie.\"","The two of them gripped their bows, eager to try. They followed the direction of the tracks all the way forward.","Suddenly, a flash of grayish-white lunged out from a snowbank, leaping high and arching its body like a bow.","It pounced and hopped with its powerful hind legs, its bushy tail swaying like a feathery fan, exuding a touch of elegance as it moved.","It was a white fox.","Song Qiming quickly drew his bow and aimed at the fleeing white fox. The long arrow released with a sharp whistle through the air.","\"Oh, no!\"","Just as the arrow was about to strike, the white fox leaped, narrowly dodging the shot. Song Qiming furrowed his brows in frustration.","Just as he was preparing for a second shot, a feathered arrow whistling with the wind pierced through the white fox as its paws were just touching the ground.","Bright red blood bloomed like a brilliant plum blossom on the white fur.","Song Qiming looked to his side in surprise.","Song Shixue lowered her bow, her face filled with the joy of hitting her prey.","She trudged through the snow, running over to pick up the white fox.","It was quite heavy. The fur was a bit dirty and tinged with gray; otherwise, it would have been nearly impossible to spot in the snow.","Song Jinzhao’s eyes curved like crescent moons as she offered unreserved praise. \"Not bad. You knew how to anticipate the prey's movement. You're better than your brother.\"","Song Qiming’s eyes drooped, and he drawled, \"Ah Jie~ It was my first time and I lacked experience. I’ll definitely hit it next time.\"","Song Shixue tilted her head, showing off. \"It was my first time, too.\"","Song Qiming’s cheeks puffed out like a hamster's. He took a deep breath and said with determination, \"Again!\"","Song Shixue pulled the arrow from the fox, wiped it clean with snow, and followed after him.","Song Jinzhao followed behind the two, carrying the sack containing the fox. Raising children was quite fun.","Watching them succeed gave her a unique sense of accomplishment.","As she stepped past the spot where the white fox had first jumped, Song Jinzhao caught a glimpse of a hole beneath the snowdrift. It looked as if something had burrowed through the snow and escaped.","Looking in the direction of the hole, there was an almost invisible ripple on the ground.","She leaned down and picked up a few tufts of brownish-yellow fur. It wasn't fox fur; it was rabbit fur.","Turning around and noticing that Song Jinzhao hadn't kept up, Song Qiming called out in confusion, \"Ah Jie?\"","Song Jinzhao walked over and held the rabbit fur out to the two of them. \"One got away. A rabbit escaped.\"","Seeing the tuft of rabbit fur, Song Qiming shut his mouth in frustration. After a moment of silence, he said, \"It must still be nearby. Let's find it.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"The snow is too thick, and rabbits can burrow. It’s been gone for a while; there's no trace left. Keep looking for other prey.\"","A clump of snow fell from a tree, landing right on Song Qiming’s hat. The three of them looked up, only to see a figure flash away like lightning.","Song Qiming asked uncertainly, \"Was that the squirrel from earlier?\"","They hadn't even stolen its pinecones, yet it was actually holding a grudge.","Song Shixue nodded. \"Likely. The color looks similar.\"","Just as they were about to cross the pine forest, Song Qiming grabbed Song Shixue and suddenly crouched down. A snow slope hid their bodies completely.","Not far away was a herd of roe deer, nearly ten of them, both large and small.","Song Jinzhao stopped behind a tree like a silent phantom. A roe deer that was digging through the snow with its hooves looked up at Song Jinzhao.","Its round eyes paused for three seconds before it lowered its head to continue eating the withered grass and lichen buried under the snow.","After a moment, the siblings cautiously poked their heads out.","They glanced at Song Jinzhao, and after receiving her nod of approval, they crawled in two opposite directions, planning to perform a pincer maneuver.","The fox's carcass had grown cold, and the small amount of blood that had leaked onto the sack had frozen into a thin layer of ice.","The scent of blood spread much slower than usual in the cold.","Upon reaching their target positions, they slowly drew closer. Song Shixue gave a wave of her hand, and the two of them fired their arrows simultaneously.","The deathly silence of the snowy mountain was instantly shattered.","The sudden danger sent the herd of roe deer into a panic, and they began to scatter in all directions.","Ignoring the two roe deer that had been shot through the throat, Song Qiming and Song Shixue had already released their second arrows.","The distance was too great, and the prey was moving fast; the feathered arrows struck nothing but the ground.","The siblings' expressions turned solemn. They quickly discarded their bows, drew the daggers tucked into their waists, and charged directly toward the two fleeing roe deer to surround them.","Song Jinzhao climbed a tree to look out over the hunting grounds ahead.","Roe deer have strong hind limbs and explosive speed; their first instinct when facing danger is to flee. Now, it remained to be seen if the two children could catch up.","Realizing they couldn't block all four directions, the siblings decided to join forces to kill one after seeing one of the deer escape the perimeter.","Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes and shouted toward them, \"I want one live roe deer without any wounds.\"","Without a moment's hesitation, Song Qiming and Song Shixue sheathed their daggers and lunged at their prey barehanded.","Due to the harsh winter, this male roe deer was at its lowest weight of the year, estimated at about twenty kilograms. However, its developed leg muscles allowed it to leap to a height of 1.5 meters repeatedly, and a defensive kick from a single leg could pack dozens of kilograms of force.","Capturing such an agile and powerful creature alive tested not only the siblings' physical flexibility but also their strength and coordination.","Song Qiming took the lead, leaping up to lock his arms around the deer’s thick neck, pressing it toward the ground with all his might.","Song Shixue pounced, throwing her weight onto its body.","The roe deer twisted its neck and struggled violently, desperate to stand back up.","Song Shixue was tossed aside by a massive surge of strength, her body slamming heavily into the snow.","Song Qiming’s face contorted as he held onto the deer’s neck for dear life. Despite the freezing winter, he was drenched in sweat, exerting every ounce of strength he possessed.","\"Shixue, hurry!\" he roared urgently.","Song Shixue looked around but couldn't find a rope. Looking down, she saw the belt tied around her waist. She decisively untied the knot and rushed toward the deer's hind legs.","The vibration of the powerful muscles made Song Shixue’s arms tremble, while Song Qiming gritted his teeth and squeezed the deer's throat.","Unable to breathe, the roe deer’s hind legs lost their power. Song Shixue seized the opportunity to quickly bind its two hooves together with her belt.","\"Use mine too! The front hooves need to be tied!\"","Song Shixue deftly reached out and pulled off Song Qiming’s belt as well. After binding the front hooves, she sat astride the deer’s belly to pin it down.","The struggling grew weaker and weaker until the animal beneath them went completely still. Only then did Song Qiming dare to slowly let go.","He collapsed into the snow, his neck sticky with sweat and his face as red as a monkey's bottom.","Up on a pine branch, the crossbow Song Jinzhao had aimed at the deer’s brainstem was slowly lowered. She jumped down from the tree carrying a sack. \"Well done. Your reaction speed was very fast.\"","Thinking to use their belts when there was no rope showed that Shixue’s mind was sharp.","Song Jinzhao added, \"You can slaughter it now.\"","Song Qiming pulled out his dagger and plunged it straight into the deer's heart.","The belly, bloated with meat, gave a sudden twitch and then went silent.","Song Jinzhao walked in front, carrying the sack and one roe deer with a single hand. Song Qiming and Song Shixue followed behind, each dragging a deer, leaving three half-meter-wide trails in the snow.","The flowing blood stained the surroundings a deep crimson, looking much like a gruesome crime scene.","Panting heavily, Song Qiming and Song Shixue’s backs were soaked with sweat. They looked up at Song Jinzhao’s back with eyes full of envy.","Even though the deer in Ah Jie's hand was the heaviest, she carried it as if it weighed nothing at all.","If only they had that kind of strength.","A cold wind blew the white snow off the pine branches, falling like scattered flower petals.","Song Jinzhao’s nose twitched as she caught a whiff of a strong, musky scent.","Song Shixue stopped in her tracks, her eyes lighting up. she took the bow from her arm and scanned the surroundings.","\"It must be another fox, and a male one at that.\"","Heavy footsteps crunched the dead leaves buried under the snow; the creature was not small.","Song Jinzhao said coldly, \"It's not a fox. It's large, and it's approaching.\"","Sensing the alertness in Song Jinzhao’s tone, Song Qiming let go of the deer hooves and stood up, ready for a fight.","The sound grew louder. The three held their breath and looked to the left.","First to appear were a pair of black, furry ears, followed by dark eyes, a upturned snout, and a gaping, drooling maw.","Song Qiming murmured in disbelief, \"Don't black bears hibernate in the winter?\" Why was it appearing now?","Song Jinzhao scanned the black bear’s relatively thin frame. \"It's a 'starving bear.' It didn't store enough fat before winter, so it's forced to come out and forage.\"","Song Shixue said, \"Then it must have no strength. It should be much easier to kill.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"A starving bear is more dangerous than a normal black bear. Extreme hunger makes them incredibly perilous; their behavior becomes frantically unpredictable.\"","This opponent had arrived at just the right time.","Seeing how highly Song Jinzhao spoke of the starving bear, Song Qiming assumed she would handle it herself. However, out of the corner of his eye, he saw that she hadn't moved forward—in fact, she had taken a step back.","\"The two of you take it. Whether we get to eat steamed bear paws tonight depends on you.\"","A famished black bear, driven by the scent of blood, tracked them through the wilderness. Having gone without food for a long time, it had already marked Song Jinzhao and the others as its prey, determined to tear them apart and turn them into the fat it needed to survive.","The bear, which had not eaten for many days, saw nothing but food; it wanted to shred anything edible in its path.","The two siblings had inherited all their martial skills from Song Jinzhao. Watching the approaching black bear and bolstered by Song Jinzhao’s encouragement, there was no trace of fear in their eyes—only an impatient desire to challenge a powerful foe.","They had come up the mountain today specifically looking for ferocious beasts. If they couldn't find wolves, a black bear would do just fine.","Song Qiming gripped his dagger tightly, summoned his courage, and charged toward the bear.","Song Shixue stood to the side with her bow, providing cover. Whenever she saw an opening, she loosed an arrow to draw the bear's attention.","\"Brother, it hasn't eaten in days. No matter how fierce it is, its stamina won't last. We can wear it out!\"","Regardless of how violent and savage the bear was now, its weakness was undeniable. It could only maintain such an explosive burst for a short time; once its energy was spent, its combat effectiveness would inevitably plummet.","Song Jinzhao stood with her hands behind her back in the snow. She appeared relaxed, but her sharp eyes were fixed unblinkingly on the battle.","On one hand, she was looking for flaws in the siblings' fighting techniques; on the other, she was there to protect them, ensuring the bear didn't land a lethal blow.","Song Qiming gripped his dagger, constantly circling and maneuvering around the bear. He rolled and dodged through the snow, and several deep gashes had already been torn into his thick cotton coat by the beast's sharp claws.","The biting cold seeped into his chest—a jarring mix of heat from the exertion and the icy chill against his skin.","Suddenly, an arrow struck the black bear precisely in the eye. The massive frame shuddered as an explosive pain radiated from the socket throughout its body.","After a brief, stunned pause, a piercing roar echoed through the mountains like a collapsing sea, a sound thick with fury and madness.","The bear shook its head violently, swatting at its face with its massive paws in a desperate attempt to pull the arrow out.","Under the force of its own strength, the shaft snapped and fell to the ground, leaving only the arrowhead lodged in its right eye to torment it.","With its optic nerve damaged and its vision blurred, the bear began to thrash about blindly. Two small pine trees snapped under its weight, and snow cascaded down from the larger branches.","As its strength drained rapidly, its movements began to slow.","Song Qiming and Song Shixue drew their bows simultaneously. In moments, the black bear had been turned into a pincushion.","Despite this, it continued to struggle feebly, clinging to life.","Its sunken belly rose and fell weakly, and its pupils lost focus. The ferocity and bloodlust from moments ago had vanished without a trace.","The siblings did not lower their guard.","They approached cautiously. Seeing that it was lying on the ground with its breath coming in shallow gasps, they each delivered a swift, final strike, ending the black bear's brief life with lightning speed.","Only then did Song Qiming feel the cold—a bone-deep chill as the wind whistled through the tears in his clothes.","Song Jinzhao nodded in satisfaction. Shixue was not only skilled with silver needles, but her archery precision was also far beyond the norm. In the modern world, she would have been prime material for a sniper.","As they began their descent, snow started to drift lazily from the sky. Near the entrance of the village, Song Shuanzhu, who had been sitting by a fire weaving straw rain capes, stood up to close his courtyard gate.","Song Jinzhao happened to pass by the gate, carrying a black bear in one hand and a roe deer in the other.","Song Shuanzhu turned his neck stiffly, his gaze following Song Jinzhao in a daze.","\"Huff—huff—\"","The sound of heavy breathing reached Song Shuanzhu’s ears. He turned to the left and saw Song Qiming and Song Shixue, each dragging a roe deer along the road.","Their faces were flushed bright red, sweat poured off them like rain, and thick white clouds of vapor billowed from their mouths with every breath.","After a moment of hesitation, Song Shuanzhu ran toward Song Shixue and grabbed one of the deer's hind legs to help pull.","\"This is so heavy, how can a young girl like you drag this? Let go, I'll do it.\"","Song Shixue did not let go. Beads of sweat rolled down her chin and disappeared into her collar.","Panting heavily, she shook her head. \"Thank you, Uncle Shuanzhu, but I can drag it myself.\"","Ah Jie had set this task specifically to build their strength; she couldn't accept help.","Song Shuanzhu insisted on helping Song Shixue drag the deer back, leaving Song Qiming to struggle alone against his own catch. Before long, he was left far behind."]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Selling Meat in the Village, Flyer","paragraphs":["The Song Shuisheng family living next door to Song Jinzhao stared dumbfounded as a black bear and a roe deer were carried into the neighboring courtyard, with a couple of drops of blood left at the entrance.","Song Shuisheng's father, Song Datian, said, \"They must have gone hunting in the mountains.\"","In winter, villagers didn't dare go near the foot of the mountains, yet Song Jinzhao actually dared to go up. This was a black bear, worth nearly a hundred taels of silver.","When Old Man Song heard the news and rushed over, Song Shixue had just finished bathing. Her padded clothes had blood on them, and her inner clothes were soaked with sweat; she would have disliked it herself if she hadn't washed.","\"Where are your brother and sister?\" Not seeing them, Old Man Song felt uneasy, worried they were injured.","Why was the black bear out before spring had even begun? Testing one's skills wasn't done like this.","Song Jinzhao walked out of the kitchen carrying two bowls of steaming hot brown sugar ginger tea, handing one to Song Shixue. \"Drink it while it's hot.\"","She hadn't shed a single drop of sweat, only her hands were stained with blood, so a simple hand wash was enough.","Song Shixue drank while answering Old Man Song's question. \"Brother is bathing.\"","Seeing that the two sisters were unharmed, Old Man Song's heart, which had been in his throat, finally settled.","Looking at the prey in the yard, Song Shixue asked uncertainly, \"Elder Sister, we can't finish all this meat. Should we take it to sell at a restaurant in town?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"Skin them, keep two roe deer, and sell the rest to the villagers.\"","They would be going up the mountain every day from now on. They definitely couldn't finish all the meat, so selling it was necessary.","It was the first day, the snow was falling heavier, and it was getting late. Selling to the villagers to earn some goodwill was a good idea.","The villagers watching the commotion outside the courtyard heard this and joyfully rushed in. \"Jinzhao, how much are you planning to sell the meat for per jin?\"","Pork was too expensive. Villagers usually couldn't bring themselves to buy it, only getting a couple of liang or half a jin for a taste during holidays. Now there was fresh meat available, and from a fellow villager, the price was sure to be cheaper than in town.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Fox meat is fifteen wen per jin, roe deer meat is twenty-five wen per jin, black bear meat is thirty-five wen per jin.\"","Fox meat not only had a strong gamey smell but also poor texture. Without the fur, just selling the meat, even restaurants wouldn't take it, so the price was much cheaper relatively.","Although roe deer meat tasted better than black bear meat, it was common.","Black bear was considered a high-end item on the dining tables of wealthy families, so the price was much higher.","However, for the villagers, cheap was the real deal. The fifteen-wen-per-jin fox meat was their first choice.","Pork sold for thirty wen per jin, so this price was a real bargain.","After chopping off the four bear paws, Song Jinzhao began teaching her younger brother and sister how to skin the fox, roe deer, and black bear completely.","\"Shixue, keep the bear gallbladder for medicine.\"","Song Shixue nodded, neatly cutting out the bear gallbladder alone and placing it in a basket.","The news that the third branch of the Song family was selling meat quickly spread throughout the entire village.","After clarifying the prices, every household grabbed their money and rushed towards Song Jinzhao's house, afraid they would miss out if they were late.","The skinned fox only had ten jin of meat and sold out first, followed by the roe deer meat. Most families chose to buy half a jin or a jin to save for the New Year.","Song Gaoli stood in the crowd and said to his father, \"Dad, I've never eaten bear meat in all my years. Let's buy a jin.\"","In the prefectural city, Song Gaoli couldn't afford bear meat, and it was scarce even at a price. Now he could buy a jin for thirty-five wen, an opportunity not to be missed.","The villagers chattered noisily, the shouts and cries making one's ears ache.","Old Mrs. Song, who had hurried over, along with Oldest Song, his wife, and the second son Song Erlang and his wife, couldn't even squeeze their way in.","Besides, there were enough people; they weren't needed to help.","Being held, Song Anhao saw his older brother and sister and wanted to get down from Elder Aunt Song's arms, but she held him tight, not letting him move.","\"They're busy right now. Wait until they finish selling before you go over.\"","Old Man Song and Song Qiming used knives to cut the meat, while Song Jinzhao and Song Shixue calculated the bills and collected money beside them.","Song Daniu pointed at the piece of roe deer meat with the most fat, his eyes gleaming.","\"Qiming, cut this piece for me, with more fat.\"","Song Shixue, who was collecting money, looked up. \"No picking. If you pick, it's five wen more per jin.\"","Meeting Song Shixue's clear, bright eyes, and remembering how he had once wanted her to marry his son for a \"fortunate match\" to cure his illness, Song Daniu quickly lowered his head and averted his gaze, his voice weakening.","\"Then just cut any piece, two jin will do.\"","The copper coins in the earthenware basin piled higher and higher. Standing not far away, Song Erlang saw the meat on the ground dwindling and anxiously paced on the spot.","\"It's almost all sold out. Will there be any left for us?\"","Second Aunt Song stopped him and whispered, \"Jinzhao kept two roe deer. She'll definitely give some to Father, but whether she gives us any is unknown.\"","Song Erlang frowned in annoyance. \"We should have run faster. If we had helped, she would have been too embarrassed not to give us any.\"","After all the villagers had left, there were still over ten jin of black bear meat left on the ground.","Song Jinzhao told Song Qiming to cut half and give it to Old Man Song to take back.","Old Man Song repeatedly refused, trying to return the meat to her.","\"It's too much. Just cut a jin or two.\"","Song Qiming lowered his hands and didn't take it back.","\"Grandpa, our family can't finish this much meat either. Take it back and eat well these next few days.\"","Song Shixue, holding the earthenware basin filled with copper coins, nodded.","\"Yes, eat more meat to nourish yourselves. You and Grandma look a whole lot thinner than when we left in the summer.\"","The elderly couple's hearts clenched, feeling heavy.","That their own sons weren't as concerned about them as their grandchildren was truly saddening.","A slightly bittersweet smile appeared on Old Mrs. Song's face.","\"We know you're filial. I never thought your grandpa and I would get to eat black bear meat in our old age. This life can be considered worthwhile.\"","Seeing Song Qiming about to take the remaining meat back into the courtyard, Song Erlang, empty-handed, began to panic.","He was just about to speak when a fierce glare from Old Man Song scared him into silence.","Full of grievances he couldn't voice, he was on the verge of tears.","What was wrong with giving him a little of all that meat? They couldn't finish it anyway.","Seeing this, Second Aunt Song pulled Song Erlang along to follow the two elders and the eldest branch.","If they couldn't ask Jinzhao for it, Father had so much. Surely, a few soft words would get them a share.","In the kitchen, Song Jinzhao was using fire to singe the fur off the bear paws. Song Shixue grabbed her younger brother's hand, not letting him go over.","\"Be careful not to burn your clothes.\"","Song Anhao was wearing rabbit fur. If it caught even a single spark, the fur would catch fire.","After burning the bear hair clean, Song Jinzhao poured a little wine into some rice-washing water, mixed it well by hand, and soaked the bear paws in it.","\"Alright, soak them overnight to draw out the blood and any off-flavors. We can cook them tomorrow at noon.\"","\"Ah, I thought we could eat them tonight.\" Song Qiming, who had been eagerly waiting, really wanted to know what steamed bear paw tasted like.","Song Jinzhao said, \"No, making them now wouldn't be perfect. Tomorrow morning, just the steaming will take one or two hours.\"","\"Tonight, we'll eat roasted roe deer meat. Tomorrow, when it's done, we'll take some to the graves first to let Father and Mother have a taste. This is a bear you two hunted with your own hands.\"","The siblings immediately perked up.","\"Yes, we must tell Father and Mother, let them have some too.\" Let them know how capable we are.","The second branch managed to take a jin of black bear meat from the old house. Back home, Second Aunt Song fixed her dark, gleaming eyes on Song Laidi and Song Pandi.","\"If the third branch goes hunting again tomorrow, both of you go over to help.\"","Song Laidi bit her lip, unwilling to go.","This wasn't about them going to help; it was about them going to ask for meat.","After a long internal struggle, Song Laidi mustered her courage and spoke up loudly, \"Pandi and I have to wash clothes and cook, we don't have time. We could send our brother instead.\"","Aunt Song (the second wife) immediately snapped, \"No! Yaozhu needs to focus on his studies without any distractions.\"","\"If you don't have time, just get up earlier and do it. They won't be back from hunting until the afternoon. You two should finish all the chores in the morning, that's all there is to it.\"","Song Laidi clenched her fists, lowered her head, and said nothing.","Fine, I'll just finish the work and run off. Forget the meat. I'll just endure a few scoldings anyway.","The second branch of the family had thought too wishfully, for the next day, Song Jinzhao and the others did not go up the mountain to hunt.","Oldest Song's second son lurked outside the courtyard for half an hour, finally returning home with a disappointed and sullen face.","The bear's paw, soaked overnight, had only a trace of its gamey odor left. After washing it clean, it was placed in a deep dish, topped with ham, shiitake mushrooms, and winter bamboo shoots. A little broth was poured over it, along with various seasonings, and then it was steamed for four hours.","The siblings had trained all morning, and their stomachs were already growling with hunger.","Despite this, the three of them first took the wine and meat, along with Song Anhao, to the graves at the foot of the mountain.","It was said to be for Song Sanlang and his wife to have a taste, but it really just meant kowtowing a few times before the tombstone and burning some paper offerings. Except for the wine which was poured out, the offered food would be brought back after being presented.","Song Jinzhao dipped her chopsticks into the soft, sauced meat and let Song Anhao have a taste. Unexpectedly, the little boy loved it. Having one bite wasn't enough; he wanted to take a spoon and dig in himself.","\"No, you can't have too much of this. You won't digest it well and will get diarrhea. Just one bite.\"","Song Anhao knelt and lay across Song Jinzhao's lap, shaking his head. \"Big sister~ I'm hungry. Let me have one more bite—just one more bite will be enough.\"","\"Your food is here. Your elder sister went to the river early this morning specifically to catch this fish for you.\" Song Qiming came over from the kitchen carrying a bowl of fish-paste porridge.","Song Anhao stared at the pale-colored fish porridge, his chubby little mouth pouting sadly as he shook his head.","\"When I grow up, I'm going to eat all the delicious food from every corner of the land.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled and tucked the spoon into his hand. \"Let's talk about that when you're grown up and can travel to every corner of the land.\"","Here, there were no high-speed trains or railways. To travel across the land would take at least several years.","Anyang Prefecture, Sweet Snow Pavilion.","Li Zien sipped the warm milk tea from his cup, his eyes fixed unmoving on the flyer in his hand.","\"Are you sure this was handed out by servants of the Song family?\"","In winter, every family's dinner table was dominated by cabbage, radish, and some rehydrated dried goods. Yet this flyer was printed with the names and pictures of over twenty types of vegetables: chives, spinach, chili peppers, pea shoots, fava beans, and more.","It even specially emphasized in bold that all vegetables were picked that very day and absolutely fresh. Wasn't this just deceitful?","The servant nodded vigorously. \"I saw with my own eyes. The person in charge was called Chunxing, she's a clerk at the Song family's food shop.\"","\"They said sales start tomorrow morning. The shop is right next to the food shop.\"","Li Zien bit down on a tapioca pearl, tasting no sweetness.","He put down his cup and said discontentedly, \"Who made today's milk tea? They didn't add any sugar.\"","The servant glanced at the remaining milk tea in the cup. He's drunk half of it before saying there's no sugar?","He pretended to be angry and accused, \"It must be that the clerk was too busy and forgot. I'll go have them remake it right away.\"","Li Zien irritably furrowed his brows, took two deep breaths, and stood up.","\"No need. Let's go take a look at the Song family's shop.\"","The servant put down the teacup and quickly picked up an umbrella to follow Li Zien.","Arriving at the door, the shop next to the Song family food shop was open.","On the walls to the left and right of the main door hung plaques with the five large characters 'Song Family Vegetable Shop'. Inside were two rows of empty wooden shelves, looking ready for business.","The servant stopped Qingshuang, who was coming out of the food shop. \"Excuse me, may I ask what time the vegetable shop next door opens tomorrow morning?\"","Qingshuang's gaze shifted from the servant's face to Li Zien.","Young Master Li. He seems to have some issues with the young mistress.","\"It opens officially at 7 a.m. tomorrow morning. We close when sold out. You'll have to get up early, sir.\"","Li Zien's face was dark as water as he voiced his skepticism. \"Your flyer says the vegetables are fresh, picked that day. They're not from an ice cellar, are they?\"","Qingshuang retorted, \"What leafy green vegetable can stay perfectly fresh in an ice cellar for several months?\"","She took out a flyer and pointed at the words on it. \"See here? 'Counterfeit items compensated tenfold.' If it says picked that day, it's picked that day. Absolutely fresh.\"","Li Zien: \"In such cold weather, even weeds don't grow. You say they're fresh. How were they grown?\"","Qingshuang pressed her lips together speechlessly, feeling this person had ill intentions.","\"That's our family's trade secret. Young Master Li, would you tell others yours?\"","Li Zien gritted his teeth and frowned. Sure enough, a servant taught by Song Jinzhao, as bold as her master.","Even a servant spoke so impolitely.","Staring at the plaque of the Song Family Vegetable Shop, Li Zien took a deep breath and said, \"Take two people with you tomorrow morning and queue up early. If it's real, buy out the entire shop for me.\"","The servant hurriedly nodded. If they could grow vegetables in such cold weather, they definitely had to buy a lot.","The Li family's restaurant alone would need a large batch of goods.","The next day, just as the hour of Yin (3-5 a.m.) arrived, the greenhouses at the Song family's estate outside the city lit up.","Dozens of bright lanterns were lit, illuminating the surroundings clearly.","Twenty people, holding shovels or scissors, began to work busily.","Outside the greenhouses, three ox-carts stood ready, waiting only to be loaded before setting off.","Fushun's excitement was indescribable. After all, they had been waiting for this day. Their Song family was bound to astonish everyone in Anyang Prefecture.","The first hint of morning light emerged from beneath the distant mountain range. Everyone covered the carts with straw to prevent the vegetables from freezing.","By the time they arrived at the shop entrance, many commoners holding flyers had already gathered outside.","Fushun and the others removed the straw, revealing the lush green assortment of vegetables beneath.","Gasps of surprise arose. They really were fresh vegetables!","They looked absolutely freshly picked, some roots still caked with mud.","Lanxi and the others quickly carried thirty bamboo baskets filled with vegetables into the shop. Before they could even place them on the shelves, customers had already rushed in and started grabbing.","Chunxing raised her voice and shouted, \"The bundled vegetables can't be taken apart! They're only sold in bundles! The prices are posted on the wall, everyone take a look!\"","An auntie who was reaching for fava beans looked up, drew a sharp breath, and immediately stopped her movement.","She blurted out, \"Why is it so expensive!\"","It was nearly three times the usual price for vegetables. The fava beans were almost as expensive as meat.","A female clerk standing in the aisle keeping watch explained with a smile, \"Our proprietor went to great lengths to grow these vegetables in winter. Not only are the costs high, but the quantity is also limited.\"","\"To let everyone have a taste of fresh vegetables, we're already selling at a loss.\""]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: The Vegetable Shop Opens, and the Rakshasa Approaches","paragraphs":["The elderly woman clutched her money pouch, thinking of her little grandson at home who loved eating broad beans. With a pang of heartache, she poured out half of the coins and picked up a bundle of flowering cabbage hearts to take to the counter to pay.","She handed the money to Chunxing, her face etched with painful reluctance.","Two vegetables costing the price of a whole jin of meat—truly unaffordable.","Young Master Li Zi'en's servant, gripping his silver, stared at the prices posted on the wall. He hadn't brought enough money to clear out the shop.","After pondering for two seconds, he walked towards Chunxing with heavy steps.","He slapped the silver onto the table and declared with bold bravado, \"Give me a hundred jin of each variety for now!\"","Chunxing pointed to a temporary notice pasted on the wall behind the counter. \"Our shop's vegetable supply is limited. Each customer is limited to two jin per variety. For bulk purchases, please register next door.\"","\"Huh?\" The servant was puzzled. \"But you have so much right here in the shop? Just sell it to me directly.\"","Chunxing raised her voice and shook her head. \"If I sell it all to you, others won't get any. Please register first. We'll notify you as soon as stock is available.\"","While the servant was still hesitating, several restaurant workers standing behind him had already turned and rushed into the food shop next door.","By the time Li Zi'en's servant went over, he was already seventh in line.","When it was his turn, Lanxi took out a blank contract. \"Bulk purchases qualify for a ninety-nine percent discount. The minimum order is ten thousand jin, requiring a fifty percent deposit.\"","\"The winter vegetable supply is limited. The first batch is only two hundred thousand jin. First come, first served, until sold out.\"","The servant held the contract. \"Ninety-nine percent off? That's practically no discount at all.\"","Lanxi offered a thin, insincere smile. \"The customer may also choose to forgo the discount and purchase at the original price.\"","The servant pressed his lips together, utterly speechless. Seeing that a familiar restaurant manager was already signing a contract, and realizing he didn't have enough money for the minimum fifty percent deposit on ten thousand jin, he thought for a moment, then turned and went back next door. He bought five jin of each type of vegetable and hurried home.","He had to rush back and tell the young master—only two hundred thousand jin. If they were late and it sold out, it would be a disaster.","Bang! Bang! Bang! The knocking on the door was so forceful it seemed like someone wanted to break it down. \"Young Master! Young Master!\"","Li Zi'en, not yet fully awake, was jolted from his sleep and nearly fell out of bed.","\"What's all the shouting? You scared me half to death!\"","Eyes still closed, he roared, \"Get in here!\"","The servant pushed the door open forcefully, rushed in, and placed the vegetables before Li Zi'en.","\"Young Master, the vegetables are real. Several restaurants are buying them. The Song family's servants said the first batch is only two hundred thousand jin. If we don't buy, they'll be gone.\"","Li Zi'en opened his eyes, picked up a vegetable in front of him, broke it, and sniffed it.","Fresh. Absolutely freshly picked.","His voice immediately grew louder. \"Did you buy any?\"","The servant answered with a bitter face. \"Young Master, the prices are three times the usual. For bulk purchases, they require a minimum order of ten thousand jin, plus a fifty percent deposit. The silver you gave me wasn't enough.\"","Li Zi'en scrambled up and started putting on the clothes from the rack.","\"Why didn't you say so sooner? Hurry and withdraw silver from the accounts, a thousand taels for now.\"","\"Prepare the horses. Be quick!\"","Li Tianchong, clutching a contract, walked into the room from outside. He glared at the flustered master and servant and scolded, \"By the time you two get there, the opportunity will be long gone.\"","He tossed the contract onto the table with a thud.","Li Zi'en was stunned for a moment, then picked up the contract and opened it.","Black on white, it was an order for a hundred thousand jin, stating delivery over three days. The payment had already been made.","He relaxed, his shoulders sinking. \"Father, you're truly far-sighted.\"","Li Tianchong placed his hands on his hips. \"It seems your business sense is regressing. Get up quickly. The vegetables will arrive tomorrow, and the restaurant needs to start selling them.\"","\"And arrange for shipments to our restaurants in the various county towns this morning. We paid a high price for these vegetables. If they freeze and spoil, the loss will be significant.\"","Li Zi'en swiftly finished dressing and headed out. \"Don't worry, Father. I'll have everything arranged within an hour.\"","By the time he had arranged the transport carts and went to take a look at the Song family vegetable shop, it was already completely empty—not even a single leaf of vegetable remained.","In the tranquil main hall of the Ye residence, serene as an ink wash painting, Ye Liangyu sat in a chair carefully examining a stalk of vibrant green celery.","Fushun had just delivered a whole bamboo basket of fresh vegetables to Ye Liangyu, and the kitchen was already preparing them.","\"Growing vegetables in this weather is truly a miracle.\"","Qin Yunqian, who was using a vegetable leaf to wrap roasted lamb, nodded in agreement. They were incredibly fresh, bursting with moisture with each bite.","\"In warmer parts of the south in winter, one can grow spinach and chives, but in the north, this is absolutely unheard of.\"","In his memory, Song Jinzhao was highly skilled in martial arts and meticulous in thought. He hadn't expected her not only to have ingenious ideas in engineering but also such great talent in agriculture.","Ye Liangyu placed the celery on the table. \"I heard the shop sells them at a very high price. The cultivation cost must be quite substantial.\"","The capital's climate is similar to Anyang Prefecture. Perhaps there's something that can be done with this matter.","If this were reported to the imperial court and the cultivation method promoted nationwide, it would undoubtedly be a great achievement.","But if that happened, Song Jinzhao would find it very difficult to make money next year.","Returning home from his official duties in the evening, Meng Hechuan picked up a broad bean with his chopsticks, puzzled. \"Is this a fresh bean?\"","Old Lady Meng lifted her chin, preening with pride. \"The Song family sent it over this morning. They said they grew it themselves.\"","\"Before Dr. Song returned to her hometown, she specifically instructed her servants to send some for me to taste. I heard their shop sold out in less than two hours.\"","Meng Hechuan put the broad bean in his mouth and chewed. A fresh, fragrant flavor.","Very tender, no different from what they ate in July or August.","The Meng family's servants brought out three more dishes one after another, all made with fresh vegetables.","\"How much did the Song family send?\"","Lady Meng answered, \"Over twenty varieties, about a jin of each.\"","Upon hearing this, most of Meng Hechuan's attention was no longer on the meal.","Since the start of winter, the weather had grown colder and colder. In the past half month, it had snowed every few days. There was even still unmelted snow on the ground. How were these vegetables grown?","Thinking that Song Jinzhao was not currently in the city, whom should he ask?","Although the Song family vegetable shop had only been open for two hours before closing, its fame spread like the wind, quickly reaching the homes of the common people.","Along with the fame came the prohibitive high price, different from ordinary vegetables, which certainly put them out of reach for poor families.","But farmers who heard the news began to feel puzzled.","They had farmed all their lives and had never grown vegetables in winter. How did the Song family vegetable shop manage it?","Some, disbelieving and defiant, even tried sowing seeds themselves, only to have them freeze to death in less than two hours.","On the third day after the vegetable shop's opening, Lanxi, who was sorting contracts in the food shop, received an unexpected visitor.","Seeing Meng Hechuan enter in his official robes, Qingshuang, who had been weighing braised delicacies behind the display counter, quickly finished her task and stood beside Lanxi.","\"Your humble servants pay our respects to the Prefect.\" The two knelt and bowed. They remembered what the young mistress had instructed them before leaving. They hadn't expected it to happen so soon.","Meng Hechuan looked at the two. \"Rise.\"","He asked, \"Your employer is away. Who is in charge at the residence now?\"","Qingshuang raised her head to look at Prefect Meng. \"Replying to Your Excellency, the young mistress instructed the four of us to discuss and decide matters together. May I ask what business brings Your Excellency here?\"","Meng Hechuan said, \"The vegetables in your shop are picked fresh daily. I presume the place where you grow them is within Anyang Prefecture. I, as the prefect, would like to see it.\"","Lanxi bowed and replied, \"Your Honor is most astute. The farm is at the estate outside the city. This humble one will take you there immediately.\"","Upon the group's arrival at the estate, Fushun, who was busy leading the harvest, quickly washed his hands and came to greet them.","\"Your humble servant pays his respects to the Prefect.\"","Not long after entering the estate, Meng Hechuan saw from a distance many large, arched, pale-yellow structures standing in the fields, looking almost like houses.","He curiously asked Fushun, \"What are those?\"","Fushun walked alongside, slightly bent at the waist. \"In reply to Your Honor, those are vegetable greenhouses.\"","Hearing this unfamiliar term, Meng Hechuan quickened his pace with curiosity.","Drawing closer, he squinted for a better look. \"Are these made of oiled paper?\"","Fushun nodded. \"Our young mistress said oiled paper has good light transmission, waterproofing, and flexibility, making it suitable for greenhouses.\"","Opening a small door supported by a wooden frame, they saw servants inside harvesting broad beans, dressed in autumn clothing and working diligently.","With two hundred thousand catties of vegetables needing delivery within three days, everyone was working overtime.","The first batch of vegetables had already ripened. If not harvested promptly, they would become tough and delay the maturation of the second batch.","A wave of heat hit them, causing the frost on Meng Hechuan's official hat to begin melting.","Upon entering, Meng Hechuan noticed many bamboo poles inside the greenhouse, each with numerous small holes from which the warm air emanated.","\"What is this?\"","Fushun stood beside him and explained, \"In reply to Your Honor, these are flues.\"","\"The winter is cold. Sometimes, even with sunshine, the temperature inside isn't sufficient for vegetable growth. When it gets too low, we light the stoves. The hot air travels through these bamboo tubes, naturally raising the temperature.\"","Intrigued, Meng Hechuan placed his hand above a bamboo tube; it was pleasantly warm.","\"Was this Song Jinzhao's idea?\"","The person who could invent a waterwheel was indeed remarkable.","Fushun nodded. \"Everything on this estate was conceived by our young mistress. She said the winters are long and she didn't want the land to lie idle.\"","After inspecting every greenhouse thoroughly, Meng Hechuan, wearing thick cotton padding beneath his official robes, had begun to sweat.","\"In addition to growing vegetables in greenhouses, you also raise so much livestock?\"","He looked at the rows upon rows of chickens and ducks in the wooden pens, with eggs—seemingly freshly laid—filling the trays below.","Fushun replied with a smile, \"The restaurant requires a significant number of chickens and ducks daily. The young mistress said we must control our own supply. Moreover, the animal manure improves the soil and provides nutrients for the crops. It serves a dual purpose.\"","After seeing everything, Meng Hechuan stopped and looked at Fushun.","\"You brought me here today to see the greenhouses and explained the principles in detail. Aren't you afraid I might leak the method?\"","According to information gathered by the yamen runners, these vegetables were priced comparable to pork. Selling ten thousand catties in bulk to restaurants fetched four hundred taels of silver.","The first batch totaled two hundred thousand catties. Selling it all would bring in eight thousand taels.","Considering many vegetables could yield several harvests, it meant Song Jinzhao could earn tens of thousands of taels in a single winter.","But if the cultivation method became known to others, this goldmine would be ruined.","Fushun relayed the words Song Jinzhao had instructed him to say.","\"To be frank with you, Your Honor, bringing you here today was specifically arranged by the young mistress before she returned to her hometown. She insisted that I must hold nothing back and tell you everything.\"","\"The world is vast, and Anyang Prefecture is not the only place. Although this cultivation method is not low in cost, if popularized, it would be a great boon for the common people.\"","After speaking, Fushun glanced at Lanxi.","Lanxi then took a letter from his robe and respectfully presented it to Meng Hechuan with both hands.","\"This is a letter from my young mistress to you, Your Honor. All matters are detailed within. Please consider reading it at your leisure.\"","Meng Hechuan stared at the six characters on the envelope: \"For the Esteemed Prefect's Eyes Only.\" Recalling how Song Jinzhao had specifically arranged for vegetables to be sent to his residence, he couldn't help but chuckle softly.","\"She wrote this letter before leaving. Your young mistress truly leaves nothing to chance.\"","Lanxi bowed his head and flattered, \"That is because the young mistress knows Your Honor possesses a benevolent heart dedicated to governance for the people. You would do anything that benefits the populace.\"","The praise was so lofty it left Meng Hechuan both pleased and feeling put on the spot.","After seeing Meng Hechuan off, Fushun moved closer to Lanxi and asked quietly, \"Has the young master's letter been delivered to the Ye residence?\"","Lanxi nodded. \"Aunt Qingshuang has surely delivered it by now.\"","Fushun sighed. \"The young mistress didn't tell us what was in the letter either. We worked so hard to develop these greenhouses. Earning more silver would be good, but it seems the young mistress doesn't think that way.\"","Lanxi, having experienced too much deceit and intrigue, looked up at the vast white sky.","\"The greenhouses are built on the estate. The method couldn't have been kept secret for long anyway. It's better to offer our goodwill proactively. There's no need to offend the prefect.\"","Fushun plopped down on the frame of an ox-cart. \"In a few years, when the young master passes the imperial examination and becomes an official, no one will dare to bully our Song family so easily.\"","Lanxi walked around to the other side of the ox-cart and sat down, remaining silent.","Above officials, there are always higher officials. To avoid being bullied, one must aim for the highest ranks, like becoming a marquis or a chancellor.","Meng Hechuan didn't wait until returning to the yamen; he opened the letter right in the carriage.","From the letter, it seemed Song Jinzhao made no specific requests. She only expressed hope that he would report the cultivation method to the imperial court.","Only with an imperial decree from the Emperor could the vegetable greenhouse method be popularized among thousands of households at the fastest pace.","Meng Hechuan held the letter up against the sun, obscured by clouds, for a long time, confirming no other requests were written.","But he felt something was odd. All this scheming, just for this?","Upon returning, Meng Hechuan pondered for a whole night before beginning to draft his memorial.","The next day, he even summoned Fushun to the yamen and had him explain the greenhouse construction method and vegetable cultivation precautions in meticulous detail from start to finish.","It took him three days to complete the memorial.","What he didn't know was that three days prior, Ye Liangyu's personal letter had already been dispatched to the capital and was now speeding along the road.","In a gloomy, secluded valley between deep cliffs, the tremulous cries of birds pierced the eardrums. Their eerie gaze seemed to harbor human consciousness, inspiring fear.","The master of the Life-Snatching Sect, having waited in vain for the Huangquan Ghost to return and report on the mission, showed a puzzled expression.","\"So many days have passed. Why hasn't the Fourth Hall Master returned yet?\"","By his calculations, the return should have occurred three days ago.","He issued an order to the subordinate standing at the foot of the steps. \"Third Hall Master, go out and gather information.\"","The masked Rakshasa Ghost stepped forward and knelt on one knee. \"Your subordinate obeys the command.\""]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: New Year's Eve of the Third Year: Question After Question","paragraphs":["In Xining City, Song Jinzhao and her two siblings hauled a cartload of game to the entrance of a restaurant.","Manager Li of Shi You Ji and Manager Ma of Ting Yun Lou, who had been waiting for some time, immediately gathered around to pick over the goods.","To hone the siblings' practical skills, Song Jinzhao had been taking them up the mountain to hunt almost every day these past few days.","They had caught so much game that they couldn't possibly eat it all themselves, and the village market was already saturated, so they brought it to the city to sell.","Each time, the two restaurants would take the entire lot, and on the rare occasion there was any extra, the surrounding townsfolk would quickly snatch it up.","Song Jinzhao addressed the two restaurant managers, \"Tomorrow is New Year's Eve, so we won't be coming for the next few days. Our next trip up the mountain probably won't be until four days later.\"","The two men checked the goods and settled the accounts simultaneously.","Ma Baichuan said, \"You're too kind, Miss Song. The mountain beasts have nearly been hunted clean by you these past days. You should take a good rest at home for the New Year.\"","Her younger brother had already passed the imperial examination at the county level, yet he still went hunting every day during the New Year holiday. With such diligence, it was no wonder Song Jinzhao was prospering.","Manager Li respectfully handed over the silver to Song Jinzhao. While Ma Baichuan might not know the full situation of the Song family in Anyang Prefecture, Manager Li knew it clearly.","The Song siblings were no longer the impoverished farm children of two years ago.","They had long since secured their footing in Anyang Prefecture; even his own employer dared not easily offend them.","What was truly commendable was that despite the change in their status and position, Song Jinzhao still seemed to carry not a hint of arrogance.","Even Song Qiming, who had passed the imperial examination at the county level and studied under a renowned teacher, never acted condescendingly or put on airs.","Compared to him, the young master of his own household was worlds apart.","Miss Song had truly raised her younger siblings very well.","After selling the game, Song Jinzhao took Song Qiming and Song Shixue around the city to buy many things needed for the New Year.","Thinking of the turnips and cabbage from the old house back home, she couldn't help but feel annoyed that she hadn't stopped by the estate to pick a batch of the tenderest greens to taste before leaving Anyang Prefecture.","After spending so much silver and brainpower, she wasn't even the first to taste the fruits of her labor. What a loss.","She also wondered how the vegetables grown in the greenhouses were selling and if things were proceeding according to plan.","For the New Year's Eve dinner, the third branch of the family, as usual, all gathered at the old house to eat.","Song Laidi and Song Pandi, wearing new clothes, moved very awkwardly. While eating, they rolled their sleeves up high, worried about dirtying their garments.","Old Man Song took small sips of wine from his bowl, looking at the whole family gathered around the table with deep satisfaction.","The grandsons from the first and second branches, while perhaps not the best scholars, were at least literate.","Even if they couldn't pass the preliminary imperial exams, they could still find work in the city later, giving their future days some hope.","But what pleased him most was still the third branch. Jinzhao was highly capable and could earn money; Qiming was now a scholar and very likely to become an official someday; even Shixue was literate and had a skill. This could already be considered bringing honor to the ancestors and elevating the family's standing.","If Third Son and his wife were still here, they wouldn't know how overjoyed they'd be.","Having been poor, Old Man Song hadn't drunk much wine in his life. After one bowl, he was drunk.","Taking advantage of Old Man Song being drunk and asleep in his room, Second Aunt Song sidled up and sat down next to Song Jinzhao.","\"Jinzhao, I heard from folks in the village that you've set up quite a few businesses in the prefectural city and even bought servants?\"","The mouths of Song Dazhuang and his wife were never that tight to begin with. After holding it in for a few days, and with villagers having free time around the New Year and visiting each other everywhere,","they ended up revealing most of the situation about Song Jinzhao and the others in the prefectural city.","How much money they'd made, how many servants they'd bought, how well they were living.","Word spread from ten to a hundred, and so Second Aunt Song found out.","Song Jinzhao nodded nonchalantly, not uttering a single word in reply to Second Aunt Song.","The second branch couple were the type to become presumptuous if given an inch. The best approach was to ignore them completely, paying them no mind.","Second Aunt Song continued, \"Servants can't be as reliable as family. How about letting your Second Uncle go and help you?\"","Last year, when Mother-in-law watched the stall for Song Jinzhao, she got such good wages. If she could get her own man over there this time, it would mean at least several dozen taels of silver a year. They wouldn't have to worry about Yaozu's tuition for years.","The main room fell quiet, except for the children chattering away.","A playful smile curled at the corner of Song Jinzhao's mouth. \"The servants I bought all signed deeds of sale. I can beat or even kill them as I please; their lives are in my hands. They really are more reliable than Second Uncle. How about Second Uncle signs a deed of sale too?\"","The smile froze on Second Aunt Song's face. She twitched her cheek in shock. \"Your Second Uncle is your elder. How could he sign a deed of sale?\"","\"If that's really too inconvenient... we still don't have the money for Yaozu's tuition next year. Could you lend us some?\"","Second Song quickly chimed in, \"Jinzhao, your Second Aunt is right.\"","\"Your father, your First Uncle, and I grew up together. If he knew Yaozu had to abandon his studies because we couldn't pay the tuition, he would definitely lend us the money.\"","Song Qiming, who had been telling his two younger cousins about the academy, suddenly looked up and spoke loudly.","\"My own father never paid my tuition, let alone had any to spare for Yaozu.\"","Song Shixue retorted, \"Why doesn't Second Uncle have any money? I see First Uncle and First Aunt weaving bamboo baskets to sell every day for Yongnian's schooling. Why don't you weave any? Is it because you're too lazy?\"","\"A father sets the example. Children's words and actions unconsciously follow their parents'. No wonder Yaozu is always lagging far behind others in the private school. He must have learned it from you.\"","Song Jinzhao leisurely helped Song Anhao put on her clothes. \"If my father knew of this in the netherworld, he should have crawled out of the underworld on the very day he was buried.\"","\"Second Uncle, Second Aunt, since my parents passed, they've never once appeared in our dreams. Have they visited you?\"","Their smiles stiffened on their faces. It was as if a pair of blood-stained hands had tightly locked around their necks. A chill drilled from the top of their heads down to the soles of their feet, their hearts pounding so hard they could barely breathe.","First Aunt Song shot First Uncle Song a look, pretended the child needed feeding, and pulled him back to their room.","If Second Brother was rushing to court misfortune, he shouldn't drag their first branch into it. They had to leave quickly, and not let Jinzhao implicate their family too.","Song Jinzhao stood up holding Song Anhao. Her icy gaze was like a blade's edge, scraping against their hearts and filling them with dread.","\"Don't covet what isn't yours to covet. Although we are relatives, we've already divided the household. It's enough to maintain appearances in our daily interactions.\"","\"If you insist on tearing off the fig leaf and laying everything bare, we won't even be able to remain relatives.\"","People here treated reputation as their life, not daring to defy elders, constantly wearing the word 'filial piety' on their heads. But Song Jinzhao didn't care about any of that.","Song Village was remote, far from the emperor's reach. Even if Song Qiming entered court as an official in the future, the two branches of the Song family couldn't stir up much trouble.","If it weren't for the two elders still being alive, Song Jinzhao truly wouldn't want to engage in this pretense with them.","When Old Lady Song finished tending to Old Man Song and came out of the room, she sensed something was off about the atmosphere in the main room. It was quiet in a frightening way.","\"Where are Jinzhao and the others?\"","First Uncle Song forced a bitter smile and glossed over it. \"Anhao was getting sleepy. They just left.\"","Causing such a scene during the New Year festivities... if Father and Mother found out, they'd be upset for days.","It was bad enough that Second Brother was lazy himself, but to expect his eldest niece to raise his son for him? That was pure nonsense.","Second Song, unable to save face, stood up, bid Old Lady Song farewell, and left.","On the way back, Second Aunt Song's face was ashen with anger. She never expected Song Jinzhao to tear off all pretense of cordiality.","The third branch of the family had money now; that bit of tuition was nothing to them.","Things had escalated to this point, and Second Aunt Song had no idea how they would even face each other next time.","Outside Kaikang City, at the mass graves.","The Rakshasa Ghost looked at the five corpses frozen solid like blocks of ice, his face hidden beneath the mask appearing extremely grim.","Five thousand taels of silver to kill a few people, and to think they'd still fail.","Staring at the black wound where the tattoo had vanished—even the Life-Seeking Sect's mark had been gouged out—what a wretched way to die.","A sharp whistle sounded, and a pigeon, jet-black all over, landed on the Rakshasa Ghost's pale finger.","On the second day of the Lunar New Year, the old house called everyone for a meal. After arriving, Old Man Song keenly sensed something was off between the second and third branches.","Before, they would at least exchange a few superficial pleasantries, but now his eldest granddaughter couldn't even be bothered to give them a glance, treating them like air.","After the meal, once everyone else had left, Old Man Song called Eldest Song into the room to demand an explanation.","\"What's going on? Did Second Son cause trouble for Jinzhao again?\"","Eldest Song knew he couldn't hide it from Old Man Song, so he simply recounted what had happened on New Year's Eve.","\"Second Brother heard Jinzhao bought many servants in the prefectural city and suggested going there to work for her. Jinzhao didn't agree. Then they said they had no money for Yaozu's tuition and wanted Jinzhao to lend them some.\"","\"They even mentioned that if Third Brother were still alive, he definitely wouldn't stand by and let his nephew's studies go to waste for lack of money. That's when Jinzhao lost her temper. Even Qiming and Shixue didn't look too happy about it.\"","The teacup on the table was hurled by Old Man Song, nearly hitting Eldest Song's face before clattering to the floor and shattering in two.","\"Wretched creature! Unfilial son! Ingrate!\"","Old Man Song stood up, pointing a finger right at Eldest Song's nose. \"An elder borrowing money from a junior to raise his own son? Does Second Song have no shame?\"","\"And how dare he use Third Son as an excuse? I'll skin him alive! Where was all that brotherly love when Third Son died back then!\"","Spittle flew like rain onto Eldest Song's face. He closed his eyes, swallowing his bitterness.","It wasn't him who had asked Jinzhao for money, so why was he getting the scolding?","Seeing Eldest Song standing there like a dumb gourd that wouldn't make a sound even if beaten, Old Man Song had nowhere to vent his fury. He slammed the door open with a bang.","\"You go and call Second Son over here right now. Today, I want to ask him personally just what this Second Uncle of hers intends to do!\"","Eldest Song turned and hurried out as if his backside were on fire.","When he reached the second branch's house, he saw Second Song lying on the kang, one leg crossed over the other, idly swinging it. Anger instantly flared in Eldest Song's heart.","Here he was, taking the scolding for him at home, while Second Song lounged around leisurely.","And he even had his two daughters fetching him tea and water, living more comfortably than an immortal.","Eldest Song rushed to the kang, grabbed Second Song by the ear, and yanked him down. \"All you know is lazing around, not doing any work! Do you really think silver falls from the sky?\"","Second Song frantically grabbed Eldest Song's hand. \"Big Brother, what are you doing? Let go, it hurts!\"","Hearing the shouts, Second Aunt Song ran out from the adjacent room, crying out in alarm, \"Big Brother, what are you doing?\"","Seeing the whole family—one adult and three children—gathered in the main room, Eldest Song closed his eyes and let go.","He took a deep breath and said to Second Song, \"Father wants you to go to the old house immediately. He has something to discuss with you.\"","Standing beside them, Second Aunt Song's heart sank. \"Father-in-law knows?\" she blurted out.","He hadn't specified what, but everyone present understood perfectly well.","Eldest Song rolled his eyes, snorting through his nostrils. \"Yes, Father knows, and he gave me a good cursing. I took that scolding for you.\"","Second Song felt a chill of fear but tried to refuse. \"I'll go tomorrow. My stomach's upset after just eating.\"","Ever since Third Brother passed away, Father's temper had grown worse, and he seemed to particularly dislike him.","Going now would definitely mean getting an earful.","Eldest Song glared, grabbed his arm, and started dragging him out. \"You're going today. If your stomach's upset, why did you eat so much meat? That was all brought by Jinzhao.\"","Watching the two brothers' grappling figures recede, Second Aunt Song's eyes darted back and forth twice before she turned and shut the main door firmly.","Since she wasn't called, she didn't have to go.","When they arrived at the old house, only Old Man Song was in the main room, sitting on a chair with a dark expression.","Not a shadow of anyone else could be seen, nor even the sound of voices. The silence was enough to make one's heart pound.","In the side rooms, Old Lady Song and Eldest Aunt Song stayed quietly inside. Even Song Yongshi, lying in his swaddling clothes, kept his eyes open without making a sound.","After delivering Second Song, Eldest Song immediately wanted to retreat to his room.","\"Eldest, you stay too.\"","Eldest Song's just-lifted foot fell back down, feeling as heavy as if bound with dozens of pounds of sandbags.","Old Man Song's gaze burned into Second Song, as if trying to see right through him.","Selfish, greedy, expecting rewards without work, reaping benefits without sowing.","When all three sons were poor, these flaws weren't apparent. Now that the third branch was doing well, all these shortcomings had begun to surface.","Now, even the last remaining bonds of blood kinship were being worn thin, and he was trying to drag the eldest branch down with him.","Old Man Song's deep gaze held a touch of weariness, and a thought of giving up on this son flickered in his mind.","Under the relentless stare, Second Song began to feel unsteady on his feet.","He played dumb. \"Father, what did you have Big Brother call me over for?\"","Old Man Song's tone was calm. \"After Third Son and his wife passed, you two brothers didn't want to care for your nephew and nieces. You wanted to have Anhao adopted out and send Shixue off as a 'bliss bride'.\"","\"Jinzhao went hunting in the mountains. Eldest, I forced you to go once. Jinzhao shared half a goat with you. Second, you never went once.\"","\"When I asked you to help carry water for the fields, Jinzhao, upon finding out, sent you plenty of food. Later, she even took you up the mountain to gather mushrooms, earning you quite a bit of silver.\"","\"In the harsh winter, fishing—she hauled the catch to the city and still gave you two taels of silver.\"","\"For going to the private school, she never charged for the two children riding in her carriage. Second, you secretly used the carriage for your own side jobs to make money, and Jinzhao, being magnanimous, didn't hold it against you.\"","\"Selling cold-skin noodles and tea in the city during the sweltering heat, and all you could think about was your wages.\"","The hearts of the two brothers standing in the middle of the main room pounded wildly.","Every word from Old Man Song was like a needle, drilling into their ears with a buzzing sound, lashing at their consciences.","The words continued, as if they would never end.","\"The third branch moved to the prefectural city, and the village land was rented to you first, with no grain tax and lower rent than anyone else.\"","\"Before they returned, I asked you to help chop firewood and clean the house. You got new clothes and ate plenty of meat.\"","After saying all this, Old Man Song walked up to Second Song and stared hard into his eyes. \"Second Son, just who is the elder here, you or Jinzhao?\"","His voice grew louder, his tone heavier. \"Jinzhao didn't want to break relations completely, she left you face. Did that just make you greedier, pushing you to become so insatiable?\"","A slap landed on Second Song's face. Old Man Song, eyes blazing with anger, said, \"I'll pay half of Yaozu's tuition. And you have the nerve to ask Jinzhao to borrow the other half? Too lazy to support your own son, and you drag your dead Third Brother into it? If he could crawl out of his grave, he'd strangle you first.\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: Threatening to Sever Father-Son Relationship, Only Surviving White Tiger Cub","paragraphs":["Second Song's face was slapped crimson red, swelling rapidly.","Oldest Song, standing beside him, trembled all over, frightened. In all these years, their father had never hit them.","His right cheek burning hot, Second Song steeled himself and said, \"How can things be divided so clearly between family? As juniors, it's only right to show regular filial respect. If I had Jinzhao's abilities, I'd be willing to support not just four, but even eight people.\"","Another slap landed abruptly on his left cheek.","Old Man Song's face was livid, his aged and cloudy eyes now burning with fire, his heart filled with utter disappointment.","\"You refuse to repent even facing death. Look at yourself, is there any trace of an elder about you?\"","\"As a son, you are not filial to your parents; as an uncle, you do not care for your orphaned nephew and niece; even as a father, you fail in your duty.\"","\"Don't covet what isn't yours to covet. From now on, except for coming to the old house, your second branch need not interact with the third branch. I will tell Jinzhao to take back the five mu of land rented to you and lease it to others.\"","Second Song's eyes widened in disbelief, and he wailed, \"Father, you can't do this! How will our second branch survive without those five mu?\"","Old Man Song's tone was unyielding. \"You managed just fine before you had those five mu.\"","Second Song's hands shook violently, a pang of regret in his heart.","\"Yaozu still needs to study. We'll only need more silver in the future. Everything I did was for him.\"","Old Man Song snorted coldly. \"If you truly cared for your child, you wouldn't laze around at home during the farming off-season instead of finding work in the city. In the harsh winter, how many families in the village weave bamboo baskets and raincoats to earn money? Only you and your wife lie at home enjoying your ease.\"","\"Now you claim it's for the child? It's too late. I will definitely have Jinzhao take back the land. Better that than helping you only to inflate your ambitions and raise an ingrate.\"","\"And don't even think about causing trouble for Jinzhao. If you dare, I will sever our father-son ties.\"","A thunderclap exploded in Second Song's mind.","He collapsed to the ground, body trembling slightly, face deathly pale, throat dry and gasping for air.","Oldest Song stood rigid, not daring to make a sound.","He never imagined things would come to this. Severing father-son ties—such words had been spoken. He was serious.","In the room, Old Lady Song sat on the bed, her expression dazed, her tightly clenched hands icy cold in the palms.","On the other side, Elder Aunt Song covered her young son's ears, hoping he wouldn't cry.","She certainly didn't want her own family to end up like the second branch.","No amount of pleading made Old Man Song relent. On the way home, Second Song's legs were weak, and he nearly slipped three times.","He collapsed just inside his door and remained dazed for a long time. No matter how Second Aunt Song called to him, he didn't speak.","The words \"sever our father-son ties\" kept circling in his mind, hammering at his skull, making him increasingly uneasy.","It felt as though something very important was drifting away, with nowhere to land, about to fall and shatter.","Old Man Song returned to his room somberly.","Old Lady Song looked up and said, \"Weren't your words a bit too harsh?\"","Old Man Song gritted his teeth. \"If I don't speak harshly, he won't learn. If he and his wife dare to make trouble in front of Jinzhao again, the third branch might not be willing to come back at all in the future.\"","Second Song didn't speak all night. It wasn't until the next day when Old Man Song came for the lease agreement that Second Aunt Song learned they had lost the five mu of rented land.","Second Aunt Song kept shoving Second Song, wailing, \"Say something! What on earth happened?\"","Second Song said nothing. He turned, went back to the room, took out the lease, and handed it to Old Man Song.","This time he was afraid. Afraid Old Man Song would truly sever their ties.","To lose one's parents is to lose one's roots.","When Old Man Song brought the lease agreement to Song Jinzhao, a flicker of surprise passed through the young woman's eyes.","She hadn't expected Old Man Song to go this far, after all, Second Song was his son.","Old Man Song's gentle voice held a trace of weariness. \"From now on, you don't need to pay any mind to whatever the second branch says. The eldest branch has enough land. Whether you rent these five mu to Tudan's family or someone else is up to you.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the black and white lease, stamped with Second Song's red fingerprint.","\"To Tudan's family. They had the highest yield last year.\"","Old Man Song nodded.","Watching his aged, retreating back, Song Jinzhao tapped her fingers rhythmically on the table.","Song Qiming came out of his room and asked, \"Elder Sister, when are we returning to Anyang?\"","Apart from being able to see their parents' graves, coming back wasn't all that interesting.","In Anyang, they never had to trouble themselves with such trivial matters.","Song Jinzhao gave a faint smile. \"We leave on the sixth. Four more days.\"","Song Qiming nodded and went back to his room to read.","Song Shixue walked to the doorway and looked toward the back mountain. After a long moment, she came and sat down beside Song Jinzhao.","\"Elder Sister, when we return to Anyang, let's make new memorial tablets for Father and Mother, okay? Then we can offer incense to Father and Mother every day.\"","\"Alright,\" Song Jinzhao agreed without hesitation.","The siblings' attachment to their hometown was gradually fading. They were already considering not returning for several years, or even longer.","To give them something to do, and not waiting until the fourth day, Song Jinzhao took them up the mountain again.","This time, they didn't leave Song Anhao at the old house but brought him along.","Dressed in a white rabbit-fur coat, Song Anhao stood tiny in the snow, as if blending into heaven and earth.","His large, bright, smiling eyes sparkled with liveliness, the two little dimples by his mouth seeming capable of lighting up the whole world.","His small hand, clutching snow, suddenly shot into Song Qiming's collar, giving him an icy shock.","\"Anhao, what are you doing!\" Song Qiming shivered from the cold on his chest, pulling open his collar to find the snow already melted.","The little one giggled with delight, turned over, and began rolling on the ground. The whole mountain was his playground.","Song Jinzhao strode over and lifted him up. His face was covered in snow, some even in his mouth.","\"You don't mind it being dirty?\"","Song Anhao shook his head. \"No taste.\"","\"Of course it has no taste.\" Worried he might catch a cold, Song Jinzhao held him in her arms and didn't let him down again.","At just over two years old, he understood nothing. Many things were driven by instinct and unreasonable.","He was undoubtedly adorable, but sometimes truly boisterous.","The game in the back mountain had been hunted clean by the three siblings. The survivors had fled deeper to relocate.","Following the tracks along the path, Song Jinzhao looked at the familiar cliff. Across the ravine was North Mountain.","Song Qiming turned his head and said, \"Elder Sister, didn't you say before that North Mountain has the most game?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement. \"Quite a lot. There's also an enormous female tiger, one I wouldn't dare confront head-on.\"","After many consecutive days of hunting, having killed bears and fought wolves, the siblings' courage was far from what it used to be.","Ordinary beasts, apart from being killed for money, no longer posed a challenge. Hearing Song Jinzhao say this suddenly piqued their curiosity.","Elder Sister had killed tigers before. Was this one really that formidable?","Seeing their expressions, Song Jinzhao knew what they were thinking. Holding Song Anhao with one arm, she freed her right hand to gesture.","\"That female tiger's size is nearly double that of an ordinary tiger. Its limbs are strong and powerful, capable of leaping dozens of meters in a single bound.\"","\"I've encountered it twice. The first time was on North Mountain, the second time was deep in the old-growth forest far behind the mountains. It ambushed and killed a soldier from Shuobei and ate his flesh.\"","Song Qiming shook his head, trying to clear the gruesome image of the tiger devouring the corpse from his mind.","Song Shixue tightened her grip on the long sword in her hand, her eyes brimming with fighting spirit.","\"Only a powerful opponent can temper our will and martial arts. Sister, should we go look for it?\"","Song Qiming stared blankly at his younger sister. \"You're becoming more and more like Elder Sister.\" Her courage was even greater than his, actually thinking of delivering themselves to its doorstep.","Song Shixue was not ashamed but rather proud. She lifted her chin high and declared proudly, \"I was taught by Elder Sister hand-in-hand. Isn't it only right that I resemble her?\"","Song Jinzhao gave a gentle smile. \"That tiger roams all over the mountains and wilderness. It might have long since changed its territory.\"","\"We didn't bring the Lingyun Spear today, and Anhao is with us. We should still be careful.\"","If a real fight broke out, someone would have to protect the child.","Hearing this, the two simultaneously shifted their gaze to their younger brother, who was shaking his head and grabbing at Song Jinzhao's hair. He was a bit of a hindrance.","Out of consideration for Song Anhao, they didn't go to North Mountain.","They walked along the cliff edge, hunted two wild boars, and then began their return journey.","All was silent, save for the cold wind whistling through the bare branches, accompanied by the rustling sound of snow clumps falling.","Just as the three turned around, a sharp chorus of bird cries erupted from the woods across the mountain stream.","The next moment, countless black migratory birds flapped their wings into the sky, creating a scene reminiscent of \"dark clouds bearing down, threatening to crush the city.\"","A faint tiger's roar could be heard, carrying defiance mixed with a touch of mournful cry.","Song Qiming and Song Shixue both looked at Song Jinzhao. \"Elder Sister, that's a tiger's roar.\"","For it to carry this far, it must be an adult tiger.","On the mountain cliff, the three stood for a long while.","The tiger's roar gradually grew fainter, as if growing weaker, until it finally vanished completely.","\"Let's go take a look.\"","Song Jinzhao grabbed Song Anhao's hand and made him hold tight around her neck, then climbed down the cliff face using the large trees.","Leaving the wild boars behind, Song Qiming and Song Shixue quickly followed. The three crossed the mountain stream and ran towards the direction from which the birds had just startled.","Arriving at a sunny small hillside, the three halted their steps abruptly as if hitting brakes.","Not far away, two massive tigers lay in the muddy ground overgrown with withered grass. The surrounding snow was churned into a mess.","Blood was splattered all over the ground, the red glaringly conspicuous.","Clearly, a fierce battle had just taken place here.","Uncertain if the two tigers were still breathing, Song Jinzhao handed Song Anhao to Song Qiming. \"Stay here and don't move. I'll go check.\"","Sword pointed forward, she approached step by step. The tigers lying on the ground showed no reaction.","No breath. The bodies were still slightly warm. They hadn't been dead long.","One of them was the very tigress Song Jinzhao had encountered twice. Who would have thought it would die like this before they even had a chance to confront it.","She turned her head and called to the others, \"You can come over now.\"","Song Qiming and Song Shixue excitedly jogged over. \"Elder Sister, is it the tigress you mentioned?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded, pointing at the larger tiger. \"This is the one.\"","The two opened their eyes wide for a closer look.","Its size was that of two wild boars. No wonder Elder Sister was wary of it.","Song Jinzhao crouched halfway to examine the fatal wounds on the bodies.","The tigress had its throat torn out. The male tiger had a hole ripped in its belly by sharp claws and died from excessive blood loss.","But what puzzled Song Jinzhao was this: the male tiger's size was clearly about one-third smaller than the tigress. Given the tigress's lethality, it shouldn't have lost.","\"Elder Sister, look at this! What is this?\" Song Shixue's pupils contracted as she pointed in astonishment at the tigress's hindquarters.","Song Jinzhao stood up and walked over to the snow pile. She fixed her gaze downward, her chest suddenly heaving, her eyes filled with shock.","Stuck in the tigress's birth canal was a small tail, like that of an unborn tiger cub.","Tigers usually give birth headfirst. A tail presenting first meant a difficult birth?","No wonder it couldn't defeat the male tiger.","A mother tiger in the process of giving birth is exceptionally weak, let alone halfway through labor, struggling with a difficult birth while fighting an enemy.","She quickly used a dagger to slice open the tiger's belly, located the birth canal, and reached her hand inside.","Staring at the retrieved tiger cub, motionless... was it dead?","After checking, Song Jinzhao helplessly placed the cub on the mother tiger's belly, her eyes turning somber. \"It's already dead.\"","Looking at the two bodies, one large and one small, the siblings felt a heavy weight in their hearts, as if a large stone were pressing down.","They had just spoken about killing a tiger for practice, but now, facing the dead mother and cub, their feelings were complex and indescribable.","Attacked by a male tiger halfway through giving birth, she not only lost her own life but also failed to bring her child into the world.","Song Jinzhao frowned and began pacing around the area. Noticing this, Song Shixue asked curiously, \"Elder Sister, what are you doing?\"","Song Jinzhao searched as she answered, \"A tiger usually doesn't give birth to just one cub at a time. If there's none in the belly, it's possible some have already been born.\"","Hearing this, the siblings immediately scattered, searching everywhere.","\"Brother, loosen up a bit.\" Song Anhao uncomfortably patted Song Qiming's arm.","Song Qiming stopped and looked at his younger brother's scrunched-up face. \"What's wrong?\"","Following his gaze downward, he realized his arm was wrapped too tightly, pinching the child's leg.","\"Sorry, I used too much force. Does it hurt?\" Song Qiming quickly loosened his grip and rubbed Song Anhao's leg.","Song Anhao lifted his toes and wiggled them. \"Not too much. Put me down, I can walk myself.\"","Song Qiming scanned the surroundings, found a clean patch of snow, and set the child down. \"Stand here and don't move. Everywhere else is dirty.\"","\"Elder Sister, I found one!\" Song Shixue exclaimed excitedly, turning her head to call out.","She was lying over a dried-up tree trunk, half her body inside a hollow, stretching her arm to reach for a faintly moving grayish-white shape lying on a bed of straw.","The touch was wet, cold, and sticky. The tiny body was wrapped in a semi-transparent membrane, slippery and unpleasant.","After wiping the mucus clean with her clothes, Song Shixue said in surprise, \"Why is it white?\"","Shouldn't tigers be yellow and black?","Song Jinzhao stared at the cub cradled in Song Shixue's palms. Within the white fur, faint light black stripes could be seen. \"It's probably a genetic mutation.\"","Song Qiming looked puzzled.","Song Shixue asked, \"What's a genetic mutation?\"","Song Jinzhao frowned. This was a bit difficult to explain.","She thought for a moment and said, \"You can think of it as copying a recipe and writing the wrong character. It said to add salt, but you wrote to add sugar instead. Braised chicken becomes sweet chicken.\"","The two seemed to understand, yet not quite."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Decided to Take It Home to Raise, The Furious Death-Demanding Door","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao continued, \"Genetic mutations often bring about physical defects. Generally, white tigers suffer from severe strabismus, have relatively weak constitutions, and may even exhibit symptoms like cleft lips, palates, or scoliosis. In severe cases, it can even affect their lifespan.\"","Song Shixue’s expression froze. She looked down at the tiger cub in her hands with sadness. \"But it looks perfectly fine right now.\"","Song Jinzhao leaned over, lifting the cub’s head to examine it closely. \"The mouth is normal. As for the rest, we’ll have to wait until it grows a bit more to find out.\"","Hearing Song Jinzhao say this, Song Qiming and Song Shixue felt their hearts sink.","How could this be? Its mother had just died, not a single sibling had survived, and now the cub itself might have health issues.","It was hard to imagine how it would have survived if Anhao had been born and found not only that its parents were dead, but that they weren't there either.","It would have had no choice but to wait for death.","Song Shixue hugged the little tiger tightly, her voice pleading. \"Sister, can we take it back with us? If we leave it here, it will surely die soon.\"","Song Qiming added, \"The weather is so cold; it will definitely freeze to death quickly. Let’s take it back, Sister.\"","Song Jinzhao leaned down to pick up Song Anhao, who had walked over with eyes full of curiosity. She gazed seriously at the two siblings.","\"If we find out later that it’s cross-eyed, that its body is crooked and unattractive, or that it has other disabilities, it would be better not to raise it at all than to abandon it then. Consider this carefully. If you want to raise it, you must take responsibility for it.\"","The two siblings exchanged a glance and then nodded vigorously in unison. \"We’re sure. Even if it’s blind, we won’t let it go.\"","Seeing their serious attitude, Song Jinzhao’s eyes crinkled as she gave a gentle smile and a slight nod. \"In that case, we’ll take it back and raise it.\"","Song Shixue beamed with joy. She began unbuttoning her coat, intending to tuck the tiger inside her cloak to keep it warm.","Song Jinzhao stopped her quickly, pointing at the tigress’s carcass. \"There’s still milk. Let it have a few drinks before we head down the mountain.\"","While waiting for the cub to feed, Song Jinzhao cut down two trees to fashion a simple wooden stretcher, placing the bodies of the two adult tigers on top.","Half an hour later, the group made their way back up the cliff with difficulty. After retrieving the two wild boar carcasses, they finally descended the mountain.","In front of the Shiyouji Restaurant, Manager Li and Ma Baichuan stared at the two tigers with glowing eyes.","Ma Baichuan pointed at Manager Li and said firmly, \"One for each of us. We’ll split them.\"","Manager Li suppressed his internal reluctance and gritted his teeth in agreement. \"Fine. I want the female.\"","The tigress was significantly larger than the male, and its pelt was worth more.","Ma Baichuan replied, \"Deal. I’ll take the male.\"","While the pelt was valuable, the tiger penis was not cheap either.","Song Jinzhao watched the two of them divvy up the spoils with an expressionless face. \"I’m not finished yet. The pelt of the tigress is not for sale.\"","The little cub had already smelled its mother’s scent; she had to leave something for it to remember her by.","\"Ah? Then I want the male,\" Manager Li immediately recanted.","Ma Baichuan pointed at his nose, annoyed. \"I let you pick first. Now that you’ve picked, how can you go back on your word? The male is mine.\"","Manager Li argued, \"I didn't know the pelt wasn't for sale. What I said just now doesn't count.\"","Ma Baichuan pursed his lips in frustration. \"You bought the last tiger Song Jinzhao caught. This time, I have to get a pelt no matter what.\"","Looking at the two men arguing incessantly, Song Jinzhao said helplessly, \"I’ll sell the two wild boars along with the tigress to whoever buys her. Next time, that person can have the first pick of the prey.\"","The scene instantly fell silent as neither man wanted to be the first to make a move.","Feeling a movement against her chest, Song Shixue pulled back her cloak to check on the white tiger cub. \"Sister, it’s hungry again.\"","The tigress’s body had already frozen stiff; there was certainly no more milk.","Song Jinzhao said, \"We’ll buy some goat milk for it in a moment.\"","The sharp-eyed Ma Baichuan walked over to Song Shixue. Once he saw the cub clearly, his pupils dilated slightly.","He had never seen a white tiger before. He pointed at it to confirm, \"Was it born from that tigress?\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"Yes. There was another one, but unfortunately, it died before it could be born.\"","Ma Baichuan suggested, \"Sell it to me. A white tiger is rare, and since it’s still a cub, someone will definitely want it.\"","Song Shixue pulled her cloak shut and took a step back, saying warily, \"No, this one isn't for sale. We’re going to raise it ourselves.\"","Sister had said it might have defects. If she sold it to someone else and they grew to dislike it, what if they killed it? She wouldn't feel at ease leaving it with anyone else.","Ma Baichuan sighed in disappointment. Why weren't there two? What a pity.","In the end, Manager Li bought the tigress and the two wild boars, while Ma Baichuan bought only the male tiger.","After finishing the transaction, the four of them went to buy goat milk. They left the tiger pelts with Manager Li to be processed, planning to collect them the day they departed.","As they passed by the old house, Old Man Song stared at the nanny goat they had brought back from the city. \"Why did you buy another goat?\"","\"Is there not enough meat at home?\"","The tiger cub was hidden inside Song Shixue’s cloak, so Old Man Song didn't notice it. He simply assumed they hadn't caught any prey today and had bought a goat from the city to roast.","Song Jinzhao used an excuse. \"Shixue and the others wanted to drink goat milk, so we just bought one.\"","Old Man Song raised an eyebrow, unable to understand. \"If you want to drink goat milk, just buy the milk. You’re leaving in a few days; what will happen to the goat?\"","Song Shixue cradled her chest with both hands and hurried forward. \"We’ll take it with us when we leave. That way, we can have something warm to drink on the road.\"","Watching the three of them leave in such a hurry, Old Man Song looked puzzled.","Buying a whole goat just to have a warm drink seemed a bit excessive.","Back at the house, Song Shixue made a nest for the white tiger cub out of wolf skin. Looking at the tiny ball of fur and thinking about its future, she felt a pang of sadness.","Song Anhao squatted nearby, pointing at the little tiger lying in the middle of the wolf skin and questioning Song Shixue in his childish voice, clearly jealous.","\"Second Sister, who do you like more, me or it?\"","Song Shixue’s mind went blank for a moment. Once she realized what was happening, she didn't know whether to laugh or cry as she picked up Song Anhao and walked toward the heated brick bed.","\"You, of course. Second Sister just thinks it’s as pitiful as you were when you were born. If it died, its mother would be so sad.\"","Song Anhao pouted and turned his head away stubbornly.","\"I’m not pitiful. My cousins say I’m the luckiest kid; they’re all very jealous of me.\"","Song Shixue’s eyes felt slightly moist. She smiled, hugging Song Anhao tightly and resting her chin on top of his head.","\"Your brothers and sisters will make sure you stay lucky forever.\"","Song Anhao grabbed Song Shixue’s collar half-knowingly and closed his eyes as sleepiness took over.","A black pigeon flew into a stilt house hidden deep within a valley. A hand wearing a black glove reached out from the window.","The man untied the secret message from the pigeon’s leg. After opening it, his expression changed, and he hurried downstairs.","\"Sect Leader, the Third Hall Master has sent word. The bodies of the Fourth Hall Master and four others were discovered in Kaikang City. There were no survivors.\"","The atmosphere around the Sect Leader of the Suoming Gate turned heavy and cold. His knuckles turned white as he gripped the secret message. As his dark, sinister eyes snapped open, the paper in his hand fluttered down like snowflakes.","\"Five people, and they couldn't even handle one woman. If word of this gets out, how can my Suoming Gate maintain its standing in the martial world?\"","\"Second Hall Master, I order you to take ten elites to Kaikang City to rendezvous with Rakshasa Ghost. Bring back Song Jinzhao’s head to fulfill your mission.\"","The man known as the Second Hall Master, holding an iron fan, cupped his hands and accepted the order. \"Your subordinate obeys the Sect Leader’s command.\"","Song Gaoli was practicing his horse stance in his courtyard when his nose suddenly twitched. \"Achoo!\" He couldn't hold it back, and his lunch nearly sprayed out of his nostrils.","Song Dazhuang poked his head out from the doorway of the main hall. \"Get inside this instant! Standing out in the freezing cold in the middle of winter—what will we do if you catch a chill?\"","Song Gaoli readjusted his stance. \"I'm fine, Dad. It was just a sneeze.\"","\"Qiming practices martial arts at home every day and goes hunting in the mountains. I need to exercise too, otherwise next time I encounter...\" He cut himself off abruptly.","Song Dazhuang pressed him, \"Encounter what?\"","Song Gaoli shook his head. \"Nothing. I just feel like my constitution is a bit weak. I need to train.\"","Song Mancang said to Song Dazhuang, \"I think more practice isn't a bad thing. Song Qiming is two years younger than Gaoli, yet he's almost as tall as him.\"","\"The other day, I even saw those two siblings dragging a wild boar weighing several hundred pounds down the road. They've got more strength than you do.\"","Song Dazhuang clicked his tongue. \"Dad, it’s not that I don't want him to practice, but it's so cold outside. He can do his horse stance inside just the same.\"","Song Gaoli lifted his chin and gazed into the distance. \"When Heaven is about to confer a great responsibility on a person, it must first exercise his mind with suffering, toil his sinews and bones, and expose his body to hunger...\"","\"This bit of cold is nothing. If I do catch a chill, I can just go to Sister Jinzhao for treatment. After a few visits, I’ll probably be immune to it.\"","Song Dazhuang didn't understand the first part of the speech, but the second part made him think his son was mental. Who on earth looks forward to getting sick?","Inside the house, Dazhuang's wife, who was stitching shoe soles, let out a heavy sigh as she overheard the commotion.","Before the New Year, she had asked her son if he wanted to marry Song Jinzhao. She thought it was a sure thing, but Song Gaoli had rejected the idea immediately.","What did he mean by \"treating her like an older sister\" or \"not being worthy of her\"? They weren't born of the same parents, so why couldn't it work?","Hearing him call her \"Sister Jinzhao\" over and over again made her want to sigh in frustration.","On the fifth day of the first lunar month, the day before all the businesses were set to reopen, Song Jinzhao took Song Qiming into Xining City to purchase supplies for their journey the next day.","Song Gaoli, who was hitching a ride, sat outside with Song Qiming to drive the carriage.","\"Qiming, I've been practicing for an hour every day just like you said. Look, have my arms gotten a bit more muscular?\"","Song Qiming stared at his friend's arms, which were wrapped in five or six layers of clothing. He reached out to pinch the muscle on Gaoli's shoulder and said, half-laughing, \"It feels like nothing but fat. Have you gained weight?\"","Song Gaoli jerked his arm back and rubbed his belly, retorting awkwardly, \"My family was worried I wasn't eating well at the academy, so they thought they’d fatten me up while I was home.\"","More than half of the bear and roe deer meat purchased from Song Qiming's house had ended up in his stomach. Combined with the chickens and ducks raised at home, he was almost sick of eating by the end of the New Year festivities.","Song Qiming continued, \"If you follow my method and practice for another hour every day, all that fat will turn into muscle within two months. It’s just like when my sister first started training Shixue and me.\"","Song Gaoli leaned back against the outer wall of the carriage and wailed, \"Then I'd have to get up two hours earlier every day!\"","The academy had classes every day; it wasn't as relaxed as being at home.","A cool, crisp voice drifted out from behind him, giving Song Gaoli a start.","\"Whining over just two hours? If you become an official in the future and get chased by villains, you won't even be able to run fast enough to save your life.\"","Song Gaoli’s back snapped straighter than a wooden board.","Song Qiming leaned close to Song Gaoli’s ear, covering his mouth as he whispered, \"I have to practice for six hours a day now.\"","Song Gaoli shut his mouth, his heart sinking into despair.","He truly had no hope of catching up to Song Qiming in this lifetime. With an older sister like that constantly pushing from the side, there was no room for laziness.","After the carriage entered the city, they passed the shop Song Jinzhao had bought in Xining. Customers were bustling in and out, and business seemed quite good.","The interior furnishings were all new, showing that a lot of thought had gone into it.","Song Qiming asked curiously, \"Sister, how many years is the lease for this shop?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Five years. The rent stays the same for the first two years, and starting from the third year, it increases by five percent annually.\"","When she had left Xining City, Song Jinzhao had entrusted the shop entirely to a middleman agency. Although they took a five percent management fee from the rent every month, it saved her a lot of trouble.","Before her return, the agency had already sent someone to deliver this year's rent to her. They had even brought along the rent from the village fields on their way.","Sitting nearby, Song Gaoli listened to the siblings discuss their family assets and couldn't help but marvel inwardly.","They had shops everywhere, and their land deeds probably formed a thick stack by now. If anyone was truly formidable, it was Song Qiming's sister.","They went to a shoe store and bought two pairs of leather boots. Over the past few days, the siblings had been practicing martial arts and hunting in the mountains every day, wearing through two pairs of soles already.","Just as the three of them stepped out of a general store, they saw a massive funeral procession occupying half the street.","A shop assistant who had come out to watch the excitement shook his head and sighed. \"To lose one's life by falling down the stairs at a brothel... Provincial Graduate Wang was truly cursed with bad luck.\"","Song Jinzhao turned to the assistant to confirm, \"Is that the same Provincial Graduate Wang from the Wang family private school whose son died last year?\"","The assistant replied, \"The very same. Ever since the young master of the Wang family was killed, this illustrious Provincial Graduate took several concubines, hoping to father another son. But not a single one of them got pregnant. Now that he's died in a brothel, his reputation is utterly ruined.\"","\"Hurry, hurry! Don't let the people from Shiyou Restaurant beat us to it!\"","Just as the funeral procession passed, Song Jinzhao saw Ma Baichuan sitting in a carriage, urgently prompting his servants to move faster.","The carriage whistled past, bringing a gust of cold wind that stung their faces.","Song Jinzhao watched the back of the carriage. \"Where are they going in such a rush?\"","The shop assistant craned his neck toward the north. \"The docks are opening for business today. I expect a merchant ship has arrived.\"","Fifteen minutes later, they arrived at the canal docks. People were swarming everywhere, and the air was filled with shouting.","At a glance, the docks were packed with boats; there was hardly any room to step.","Song Qiming’s eyes widened. \"It's only the fifth day of the new year, and there are already so many people.\"","The chants of the porters, the haggling of merchants, and the cries of street vendors intertwined. Compared to six months ago, the bustle at the Xining City canal docks had nearly doubled.","Song Jinzhao unconsciously rubbed her chin. Property prices in Xining City were bound to rise. Should she buy a few more houses in advance?","\"Come on, let's go see what they have.\"","As they walked, Song Gaoli said, \"If only the canal could reach Anyang City. Traveling by water would cut the journey time in half.\"","From the corner of his eye, Song Qiming saw a bamboo basket being carried off a boat by a porter. It contained high-quality charcoal transported from the south.","This kind of Chinese Tallow charcoal was smokeless and burned longer. It cost twice as much as northern charcoal and was only used by wealthy families.","\"The riverbeds in Anyang aren't wide enough for large ships. There are hundreds of mountains between the two rivers. Unless one could move mountains and fill the seas, it’s impossible.\"","Song Gaoli sighed and shook his head. \"Moving mountains and filling seas is the stuff of immortal arts in storybooks. Unless a god descends to earth, it would take thousands of years to do it with shovels, and it still might never happen.\"","Walking in front, a faint smile played on Song Jinzhao's lips. Thousands of years later, humanity really would be able to move mountains and fill seas.","It wasn't through immortal arts, but through the power of technology."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: Crew Members Who Mistakenly Ate Sprouted Potatoes, Potato Sprouts in Hand","paragraphs":["On the riverbank, wine jars of various sizes were being hauled off the ships.","As the lids were lifted, a fragrance blending light malted wheat and nutty notes wafted through the air. Attracted by the scent, Song Qiming stopped in his tracks and leaned in for a closer look.","Noticing his interest, the shopkeeper enthusiastically scooped out half a ladle of wine with a bamboo dipper for Song Qiming and Song Gaoli to smell.","\"Young masters, this is aged Huadiao wine, a specialty of the Jiangzhe region. The water used for brewing is a gift from heaven, sourced from the Great Lake. It has a mellow, fragrant taste and is perfect for warding off the winter chill. Would you like to buy some?\"","Song Qiming twitched his nose. It did smell wonderful. Both his teacher and the master liked to drink; it would be a good idea to bring some back.","\"How much is it?\"","The shopkeeper held up one finger. \"One tael of silver per liter.\"","Song Gaoli’s eyes widened. \"That’s so expensive!\"","The yellow wine his grandfather drank cost only twenty copper coins per liter. This price could buy fifty liters of that!","Thinking they couldn't afford it, the shopkeeper quickly opened another jar.","\"If that’s not to your liking, young masters, you can try this regular Huadiao. It’s only two hundred coins per liter.\"","Song Gaoli leaned in to sniff it, then frowned. \"The scent isn't right, and the color is much paler.\"","The shopkeeper smiled and said, \"You get what you pay for. Fine Huadiao wine needs to be buried underground for ten years to reach the standard of 'Aged Huadiao.' To be honest with you, this wine has even been served in the imperial palace—though that was the thirty-year variety, and this is ten.\"","\"What’s going on?\" Noticing the two of them talking by the wine stall, Song Jinzhao turned around and walked toward them.","Song Qiming turned his head and said, \"Sister, I want to buy some wine to bring back for my teacher, and some for the master as well.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at the various jars on the stall. \"Then buy it.\"","Song Gaoli pointed at the two jars of different colors. \"The regular Huadiao is two hundred coins a liter, but the aged stuff is a whole tael of silver.\"","Song Qiming nodded in agreement.","Song Jinzhao leaned down to catch the scent of both wines, then looked up and asked, \"Can we taste it?\"","The shopkeeper hesitated, his gaze falling upon the jade hairpin in the woman’s hair. \"The lady wishes to taste the aged Huadiao?\"","He had initially recommended the aged wine because Song Qiming looked like a scholar, but he hadn't expected them to complain about the price. If they tasted it and didn't buy it, a single sip of aged Huadiao was worth dozens of coins. If everyone wanted a free sample, he’d be ruined.","Song Jinzhao saw through his hesitation immediately. \"If the wine is good, I will buy it.\"","After a moment of consideration, the shopkeeper nodded. \"Very well.\"","He used the bamboo dipper to pour half a cup of each for Song Jinzhao to taste.","After two sips, Song Jinzhao pointed to the jars of aged Huadiao and asked, \"How many liters are in these?\"","Seeing a potential sale, the shopkeeper hurriedly pointed to the other jars on the rack. \"The largest is ten liters, the medium is three liters, and the small ones are one liter.\"","\"If it’s for a gift, I suggest the small ones. I had the bottles specially made at a porcelain workshop. It’s an extra ten coins per bottle.\"","Song Gaoli said in disbelief, \"You're charging a tael of silver per bottle and you still want to charge extra for the container?\"","The shopkeeper acted as if it were only natural. \"The price of the wine is one thing, but these bottles are top-grade celadon. Using these to hold the wine makes the gift look elegant and prestigious.\"","Song Jinzhao stepped in to bargain. \"I’ll take one three-liter jar and ten one-liter bottles. We'll waive the hundred-coin fee for the bottles.\"","The shopkeeper hadn't expected her to buy so much at once. He paused for a second before nodding in agreement.","\"Deal. I’ll find a wooden crate to pack them for you.\"","After walking a few more steps, Song Jinzhao saw someone selling fresh mandarin oranges.","The vendor unhesitatingly picked up an orange and handed it to her.","\"Try it, miss. I guarantee they are juicy and sweet. Look, even the leaves are still green.\"","Song Jinzhao peeled it, gave half to Song Qiming, who then gave half of his portion to Song Gaoli.","\"Is it sweet?\"","The two boys nodded. Being able to eat such fresh fruit in the middle of winter was something they wouldn't have dared to dream of in the past.","Song Jinzhao also found it sweet. Tossing the peel aside, she said, \"I'll take two crates.\"","She couldn't just bring wine to Scholar Zheng’s house; she would bring a crate of oranges as well, and the rest they could eat on the road when they set out tomorrow.","\"Move! Get out of the way!\" Anxious screams caused the noisy wharf to fall silent for a brief moment.","Song Jinzhao looked toward the source of the commotion.","On a ship at the far end of the dock, several men were being supported as they walked down the wooden gangplank, their heads hanging low as if they were vomiting.","\"Watch the things. I’m going to take a look,\" Song Jinzhao left them with those words and charged through the crowd.","\"Where is the nearest clinic?\"","\"Where is the nearest clinic around here!\"","The captain was supporting a crewman who was vomiting uncontrollably. He was asking passersby for directions to a doctor, frantic like an ant on a hot griddle.","At a glance, there were three others in the same condition.","\"Put him down. I am a physician.\"","The clear, sharp command cut through the captain’s panicked mind.","Seeing a young woman running toward him, he froze, unsure if he should trust her.","In that second of hesitation, Song Jinzhao had already taken the crewman from him and laid him flat on the ground.","She pulled his hand away from his abdomen and pressed down. \"Does it hurt here? What kind of pain is it?\"","The dizzy crewman could only hear a voice; he couldn't see Song Jinzhao clearly.","In a blurred state of consciousness, he shook his head and replied, \"Cramping... dizzy... my mouth feels like it’s burning and numb... I want to throw up.\"","Song Jinzhao noticed the other three had the same symptoms, accompanied by sweating and a slowed heart rate.","She looked at the captain and demanded, \"What did the four of them just eat?\"","The scruffy captain’s mind was a total blank, his heart pounding as if it were about to leap out of his chest. He shook his head, trying to calm himself. \"They just had lunch. It was just ordinary food; we’ve been eating it for days.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed further. \"How long ago did they eat? Is there any left? Bring it to me immediately.\"","A crewman guarding another patient responded, \"Yes, I’ll go get it right now!\"","He turned and ran back to the ship, his steps frantic and unsteady, nearly falling off the gangplank.","When he returned, he held three multicolored steamed buns and half a bowl of unfinished seaweed soup. The soup was mostly seaweed; most of the liquid had spilled on the way.","Song Jinzhao frowned as she pulled out a potato wedged between a black-flour bun and a yellow-flour bun. Since crossing into this world, she hadn't seen high-yield staples like potatoes or sweet potatoes; she hadn't expected to find them here.","The potato had been steamed soft, but Song Jinzhao could still see dark green sprouts on it.","\"Were these potatoes already sprouting before you steamed them?\"","The crewman asked in confusion, \"You call this a 'potato'?\"","Song Jinzhao’s voice grew stern. \"I asked you, were they sprouting?\"","Coming to his senses, the captain said, \"Yes, they were sprouting. But we ate some a few days ago and nothing happened.\"","\"They must not have sprouted as much then. Prop up his legs and let him lean forward to induce vomiting,\" Song Jinzhao commanded the captain coldly.","She reached into the poisoned man’s throat to induce vomiting. Undigested food sprayed out from his mouth and nose.","\"Do the same for the other three. Follow my method.\"","The onlookers at the wharf narrowed their eyes, unable to watch the grizzly scene. Being a female physician was truly not easy.","How could such a beautiful young lady endure the stench of vomit? The sight alone was revolting, yet she hadn't flinched. She had stayed right there, reaching down the man's throat to induce vomiting without a second thought for her own safety or comfort.","Even her sleek, luxurious fur cloak had been soiled in the process.","Song Qiming, who had rushed over after setting down his belongings, saw what his sister was doing and hurried forward to pull her away.","\"Sister, let me do it.\"","He couldn't bear to let his sister touch something so filthy.","When the man was finally retching nothing but bile, Song Jinzhao turned to the captain. \"Have everyone eat some croton seeds first to completely purge their stomachs. Then, brew two pots of licorice and mung bean soup for them to drink until the toxins are fully cleared from their systems.\"","\"If you turn right at the dock and run for fifteen minutes, you'll find a pharmacy that sells licorice. Send someone to buy some immediately.\"","Seeing that the complexions of the four crew members were already improving and their abdominal pain was subsiding, the captain’s trust in Song Jinzhao was now absolute.","He nodded vigorously. \"I'll send someone right away.\"","The four poisoned sailors were helped into the cabin to rest.","Song Jinzhao walked to the riverbank to wash her hands. She unfastened her cloak and used a handkerchief to wipe away the splatters of vomit.","Before long, the messenger returned with the croton seeds, licorice, and mung beans.","After half an hour of intense purging followed by the licorice and mung bean soup, the four men were exhausted and drifted into a deep sleep.","Down in the hold of the ship, Song Jinzhao stared at a basket tucked in a corner, filled with a mixture of straw and round tubers.","She sifted through them; every single potato had sprouted.","Salted fish hanging from wooden poles gave off a heavy briny scent, and in a basket next to the potatoes were dried strips of kelp.","These people had come from the coast.","The captain, having changed into clean clothes, walked out and glared at the basket of potatoes, his temper rising.","He kicked the bamboo basket over, cursing under his breath. \"If I’d known these things were poisonous, I never would have picked them up.\"","The potatoes rolled across the floor. The dense clusters of sprouts were enough to make anyone’s skin crawl.","Song Jinzhao explained, \"Potatoes themselves aren't poisonous, but sprouted ones are.\"","\"You said you found these?\" she asked.","The captain nodded. \"We came from Jinzhou. After the Imperial Canal was completed from north to south, we thought we’d bring some dried seafood from our hometown to sell.\"","\"Shortly after we set sail, we spotted a sinking vessel. It must have been overturned by the storm the night before. Those potatoes you mentioned were found on that ship.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed further, \"Were there any survivors?\"","The captain shook his head. \"The winds and rain were fierce those few nights, with waves over ten meters high. No matter how good a swimmer you are, you don’t survive falling into that sea.\"","\"We found two bodies in the cabin. They had curly hair, very high cheekbones and bridges of their noses, and yellowish-brown skin. They definitely didn't look like people of our Dongzhao Kingdom.\"","Song Jinzhao fell into deep thought.","From the description, they sounded like indigenous people from South America.","If that were the case, it explained why there were potatoes in the cabin. That was the birthplace of the potato.","With eyes full of hope, Song Jinzhao asked, \"Besides the potatoes, did you find anything else in the cabin? Anything at all.\"","The captain furrowed his brow and tilted his chin up in thought. After a long moment, he shook his head. \"Nothing else. The water was deep. If the box of potatoes hadn't been wedged between the cabin planks, it would have sunk through the hull long ago.\"","Song Jinzhao pressed her lips together, feeling a flicker of disappointment, but she quickly bolstered her spirits.","Having potatoes was already a miracle. It was better than having nothing at all.","Suddenly, the captain raised his hand, his eyes widening as if remembering something.","\"Wait! We found a parchment map on one of the bodies. The writing on it was gibberish to me. Now, where did I put it?\"","He looked around the cabin, his gaze eventually landing on the leg of a table. His eyes lit up as he pointed to a black, rectangular object wedged underneath. \"There it is! I used it to level the table.\"","Song Jinzhao lifted the corner of the table and picked up the parchment.","The parchment, having been soaked in seawater, had become brittle, its edges curled and deformed.","She carefully unfurled the map, but it still tore into three pieces.","The text and drawings were blurred and faded. While she couldn't make out the words, the black curved lines spread across it appeared to be coastlines and navigation routes.","\"Captain, could I buy this map and these sprouted potatoes from you?\" Song Jinzhao asked.","\"If you want them, just take them,\" the captain replied. \"They're useless to me anyway.\"","Just then, a sailor ran in through a small door. \"Captain, they’re awake!\"","The group moved to the adjacent room, where the four men lying on straw beds had opened their eyes.","Song Jinzhao stepped forward to examine them. \"Does your stomach still hurt? Are you dizzy?\"","\"How does your throat feel? How many fingers am I holding up?\"","The four men answered in raspy voices, \"My stomach doesn't hurt anymore. No dizziness. My throat is still a bit numb. Four fingers.\"","After the check-up, Song Jinzhao straightened up. \"There are no major issues; the poison is mostly cleared.\"","\"There are still some residual toxins in your systems. Keep drinking the licorice and mung bean soup, and you should be back to normal in a day or two.\"","The four men nodded gratefully. \"Thank you for saving our lives, Miss.\"","As she turned to leave, Song Jinzhao added, \"The patients are out of danger, but you must watch their diet over the next few days. Keep it light; no spicy food or seafood.\"","The captain nodded repeatedly while reaching into his robe for money. \"How much is the medical fee? I'll pay you now.\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"No need. The map and the potatoes are payment enough.\"","But the captain wouldn't hear of it. These were four lives saved; he couldn't let her leave without payment.","He pulled out a silver tael and pressed it firmly into Song Jinzhao's hand. \"One must pay a doctor for their services. I'm not a man who takes favors for free.\"","After a second of thought, Song Jinzhao accepted the silver.","As they left the cabin and reached the shore, she pulled out a banknote for one hundred taels and handed it to a sailor. \"Give this to your captain.\"","A clean break. She didn't want to take advantage of anyone either, lest complications arise in the future.","The sailor stared at the banknote in confusion. This was a hundred taels of silver—why give so much?","He turned back to the cabin and handed the note to the captain.","The captain froze. By the time he ran out of the cabin clutching the banknote, Song Jinzhao and her companions were nowhere to be seen.","Meanwhile, back on the carriage, Song Gaoli stared at the basket of potatoes, unable to wrap his head around it.","They weren't made of gold. How could they be worth a hundred taels?","He turned back toward the carriage interior, baffled. \"Sister Jinzhao, even if you didn't want to take them for free, you didn't need to give them a hundred taels. Forget that they're poisonous and inedible—even if they were fine, they’d only be worth the price of a few bowls of rice.\"","Sitting inside the carriage, Song Jinzhao gazed at the map in her hand, her voice perfectly calm. \"They are worth every penny.\"","In this era, depending on the quality of the land, the yield of rice was between one and three 'shi' per mu—roughly sixty to one hundred and eighty kilograms.","But the yield of potatoes could reach thousands of catties per mu. Depending on the soil, it could range from five hundred to nearly two thousand kilograms.","That was at least an eight-fold difference. An acre of potatoes could feed eight times as many people as an acre of rice.","Buying these seeds for a hundred taels wasn't just a fair deal—it was the bargain of a lifetime.","And then there was this parchment map; perhaps it would prove invaluable one day in the future."]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: Procurement of Weapons","paragraphs":["Song Gaoli’s eyebrows knitted together like two fuzzy caterpillars as he nudged Song Qiming’s arm with his elbow.","\"Aren’t you going to stop her?\"","To pay a hundred taels for something someone else didn't even want—no matter how you looked at it, it was a massive loss.","Song Qiming replied calmly, \"My sister has her reasons for everything she does. If she says it’s worth it, then it’s worth it.\"","Song Gaoli pressed a hand to his forehead, falling silent in resignation. He shouldn't have even bothered asking; Song Qiming was a hopeless sister-follower. If it were snowing right now and Song Jinzhao claimed the snow was red, Qiming would probably just nod and ask whether she meant crimson or pink.","Scholar Zheng’s daughter saw a familiar carriage stop at the gate and turned back toward the house. \"Father, Song Qiming is here.\"","When Song Jinzhao and the others had first returned before the New Year, they had come to pay their respects with gifts, riding in this exact same carriage.","Scholar Zheng stood up in confusion and walked toward the door, muttering to himself, \"They’re supposed to head back to Anyang Prefecture tomorrow. Why have they come at this hour?\"","Song Qiming walked in carrying a crate of mandarin oranges, bumping right into Scholar Zheng as he came out to greet them.","\"I happened to be in town today when the docks opened for trade,\" Song Qiming explained. \"I thought I’d pick up a few things to take back to Anyang and stop by to bring you some New Year’s gifts, Teacher.\"","Scholar Zheng looked at the crate of fresh oranges, which also contained two bottles of wine. \"There’s no need to bring gifts next time. You only just sent some before the New Year.\"","Song Qiming set the crate down. \"I still hold your earnest teachings close to my heart, Teacher. I bought these simply because I thought of you; please don't overthink it.\"","Outside, beneath a barren tree, Song Jinzhao lifted the carriage curtain. \"Since we’re already here, why aren't you going in?\"","Song Gaoli spread his hands and sighed. \"I’d feel embarrassed going in empty-handed. I’ll pass.\"","Besides, he had already paid his respects before the New Year. It would only be awkward to go in now and be compared to Qiming.","Song Qiming didn't stay at the Zheng residence for long. After dropping off the gifts and chatting for a few moments, he stepped back out.","\"All done, Sister. Shall we head to the blacksmith’s now?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded.","\"What are we going to the blacksmith’s for?\" Song Gaoli asked.","As Song Qiming turned the horse around, he explained, \"Sister is worried about the dangers we might face on the road back, so she ordered some extra weapons. We’re going to pick them up today.\"","The memory of the assassins they had encountered in Kaikang City flashed through Song Gaoli’s mind, sending a cold shiver down his spine. He had been so busy enjoying himself at home with food and drink over the past few days that he had completely forgotten about that ordeal.","The Life-Taking Gate, that underworld assassin organization, had accepted five thousand taels of silver to kill them. They certainly wouldn't give up easily.","Seeing his friend's fear, Song Qiming reached out and patted Song Gaoli’s shoulder to comfort him. \"Don't worry, I’ll protect you.\"","\"Or, I could find a merchant caravan or a security escort to take you back to the academy?\"","Song Gaoli shook his head frantically. \"Forget it. If I ran into danger while I was alone, I’d be truly helpless. No one would hear my cries for help.\"","It wasn't as if they hadn't encountered trouble on the road before the assassins showed up. The memory of those bloody, mangled corpses still made his skin crawl.","Sun Youli saw Song Jinzhao step down from the carriage. He set down his hammer and turned to retrieve a longsword from a rack.","\"Two swords, one crossbow, three hidden sleeve-arrows, and the seventy-two iron needles you requested. Give them a look.\"","Song Jinzhao picked up one of the longswords and handed it to Song Qiming. \"Try it out. See if the weight feels right.\"","The swords they had bought on the road previously had become too light for the siblings' growing strength. Moreover, since those had been bought in a hurry, the blades weren't nearly sharp enough.","To be safe, Song Jinzhao had specifically commissioned the blacksmith shop to forge two precious swords according to her exact requirements. While she couldn't claim they could slice through iron like butter, they were certainly sharp enough to kill without leaving a trace of blood on the blade.","Song Qiming gripped one of the longswords, first testing its weight; it was perfectly balanced and felt right in his hand.","With a sharp \"shink,\" he drew the blade from its scabbard. Accompanied by the piercing, metallic ring of the unsheathing, Song Gaoli hurriedly covered his ears, almost as if he had seen sparks fly from the friction.","One listen to that sound was enough to know it was a masterpiece.","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow at the sound. She picked up the other longsword, drew it, and inspected it closely.","She looked up at Sun Youli with a nod of approval. \"Master Sun, your forging skills have improved yet again.\"","Sun Youli grinned with pride, though he maintained a facade of humility. \"It’s all thanks to my father’s excellent teaching. Besides, the raw iron recently sold by the government has been of high quality; otherwise, I couldn't have crafted such fine swords.\""]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: Return Journey: This Wine Costs One Tael of Silver per Liter","paragraphs":["On the way back, Song Qiming handed the crossbow to Song Gaoli.","\"Come over to my house once we're back in the village. I’ll teach you how to use it. If we run into those assassins again on the road, you can use this to shoot them.\"","Song Gaoli took the crossbow, his face a mask of pleasant surprise. \"This is for me?\"","Song Qiming nodded. \"I had the blacksmith rush the order using the money I earned from hunting. Take a look and see if you like it.\"","Song Gaoli held the crossbow up against the sky, inspecting it closely. His eyes sparkled with excitement, not letting a single detail escape his notice.","\"I love it. I love it so much.\"","He threw an arm around Song Qiming’s shoulder and gave him a vigorous shake. \"Good brother, you really know exactly what I want.\"","Regardless of whether he knew how to use it yet, every man loved a good weapon—especially one that was actually capable of killing.","As they passed the old house, Song Qiming carried the three-liter wine jar inside and grabbed a few mandarin oranges along the way.","\"Grandpa, we bought these in the city today.\"","Old Man Song looked at the wine jar and grumbled, \"I haven't even finished the wine you gave me before. Why did you buy more? You're just throwing money away.\"","Song Qiming stuffed the oranges into the hands of Old Man Song and Old Lady Song.","\"Wine doesn't go bad anyway. You can keep it and drink it slowly, Grandpa. I’m heading out now; Shixue is waiting for us at home.\"","That afternoon, Song Gaoli practiced in Song Qiming’s courtyard for two full hours. He shot the target so many times it looked like a sieve, yet his success rate for hitting the bullseye was barely five percent.","Song Qiming offered some comfort: \"It’s okay if you can’t hit the bullseye. In a real fight, as long as you hit the person’s body, it gives you time to fight back or escape. At worst, just fire a few more arrows. Someone's bound to die.\"","Song Gaoli looked at the other target standing three meters away. Half of the arrows were buried in the bullseye, another forty percent were within the nine-ring, and the rest were all in the eight-ring.","How could anyone be so accurate? The difference was so vast that his self-esteem took a massive hit, leaving him feeling utterly crushed.","Following his gaze, Song Qiming hooked an arm around his neck and turned him away.","\"Don't compare yourself to Shixue. Her archery is better than mine. My sister says she has a natural talent for it, like she was born with it.\"","Song Gaoli’s eyes narrowed. \"So you're saying I don't have talent?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"Of course not. Being able to practice to this level in one afternoon is already very good. If you lack talent, you can make up for it with hard work. You'll catch up sooner or later.\"","Song Gaoli didn't feel comforted at all. With a gap at the starting line and a gap in the process, he felt like even having an extra pair of hands wouldn't help him catch up.","On the day of their departure, the two elders and the family from the first branch stood at the village entrance to see them off.","Song Jinzhao held Old Man Song’s hand and said, \"A house falls into disrepair easily if it sits empty for too long. You and Grandma can go stay there whenever you like. Just think of it as helping me look after the place.\"","Old Man Song gripped the keys in his hand, his heart a whirlwind of emotions.","Song Mancang, the village chief, watched until the carriage was out of sight. Seeing that Old Man Song and Old Lady Song were still standing there staring, he circled back and walked up to them.","\"Once children grow up, they have to leave home. Jinzhao and the others are not only successful but also filial. You should be happy.\"","Old Man Song looked down and gave a bitter smile, shaking his head. \"My grandchildren are filial and successful, but neither of my two remaining sons is worth a damn. How can I not worry?\"","Song Mancang, wanting to stay on good terms with Old Man Song, patted him on the shoulder.","\"Every generation has its own luck. At your age, you should just stay home and enjoy your golden years.\"","\"This morning, my daughter-in-law picked up a frozen fish by the river. Qiming left so early she didn't have time to cook it for him. Come over to my house for lunch today. Bring some wine so we two old men can have a proper chat. I've never even seen that aged Huadiao wine that costs one tael of silver per liter. Let me have a taste.\"","Old Man Song looked up blankly. \"What did you say? One tael of silver for what?\"","Song Mancang said in surprise, \"The aged Huadiao wine Jinzhao and the others bought in the city yesterday. I heard it was brought in by water from the Jiangsu and Zhejiang regions. It costs one tael of silver per liter. Gaoli said Jinzhao bought you three liters. Didn't they give it to you?\"","Old Man Song thought of the wine jar sitting in his room and felt as if he had been turned to ice.","\"You're saying that wine costs one tael of silver per liter?\" Three liters would be three taels of silver!","Song Mancang nodded. \"I heard even the Emperor himself has tasted it. Your Jinzhao is truly generous.\"","Old Man Song clutched his chest and swayed back a couple of steps. \"That child... I don't need to drink such expensive wine. This is way too much.\"","Song Mancang huffed. \"You old man, I want to drink it but I can't. Remember to bring it when you come for lunch.\"","Old Man Song didn't say a word. He turned around, went home, and spent a long time just holding the wine jar and smelling it.","Since the wine was so expensive, it had to be delicious.","However, when he went to the village chief's house for lunch, he brought the wine Song Jinzhao had given him on the first day she returned.","\"You couldn't even bring a little bit for me to taste?\" Song Mancang grumbled. After all, he was the village chief.","Old Man Song looked at the table full of good food, including meat and fish, and picked up the wine pot to pour a drink for his friend.","\"The seal on that jar hasn't even been broken yet. I can't even bear to drink it myself. This one is plenty good enough.\"","Song Mancang picked up his cup and took a speechless sip, but then his eyes lit up.","\"This isn't bad either. A bottle of this costs fifty wen in the city.\"","Old Man Song’s hand paused. His family had been poor, so he didn't drink often; he usually only got a taste when there was a wedding or a funeral in the village.","Fifty wen per liter was already an astronomical price to him.","Seeing that Old Man Song was starting to feel stingy again, Song Mancang clinked his cup against the other man's.","\"If it’s bought, it’s meant to be drunk. And it should be drunk happily. Otherwise, their kindness is wasted.\"","Old Man Song picked up his cup and took a hearty gulp. \"Village Chief, you're right. Let's drink!\""]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: The Scheming of the Second Hall Master of the Life-Seeking Sect","paragraphs":["On the driver’s seat at the front of the carriage, Song Gaoli turned his head to look at the small bamboo basket placed by the cabin door.","\"So that's why you brought a live ewe on this trip—it was for this little thing.\"","\"This is a tiger, you know. It looks small now, but it’ll eat people when it grows up. It’s dangerous.\"","Song Qiming held a rope in his hand, leading the tethered ewe as it walked alongside the carriage.","\"If we raise it from a cub, it shouldn't harm its own family. If it gets too dangerous when it's older, we’ll just build a big iron cage to keep it in.\"","Seeing that the tiny creature wasn't moving, Song Gaoli reached out and scooped it into his arms.","The little white tiger, startled awake, couldn't even open its eyes. It could only feebly bat at Song Gaoli's hand with its two small front paws.","\"I have to say, this fur is really warm. Its belly is toasty.\"","Song Qiming reached over to give it a pat. \"Don't mess with it. It’s only three days old and very weak.\"","Song Gaoli placed the cub back and casually ran his fingers over the tiger skin lining the bamboo basket.","It was smooth and glossy, the tiger stripes looking incredibly majestic and beautiful.","It really paid to know martial arts and how to hunt; you could get things like this without spending a penny.","Meanwhile, Phantom, the Second Hall Master of the Life-Seizing Sect, had arrived in Kaikang City with ten elites.","After meeting up with Rakshasa Ghost, the two began to discuss how to deal with Song Jinzhao.","Rakshasa Ghost shared the information he had gathered in Kaikang City during this time with Phantom.","\"The portrait provided by the sect for the mission only shows Song Jinzhao's face. According to what I’ve gathered, they went to the Kaikang City yamen to report the incident after the killings.\"","\"There are five of them in total: two males and two females, all only in their teens, plus a two-year-old baby boy.\"","\"I have examined the five bodies of our people. Two were killed by a longsword, and one of them was also poisoned.\"","\"The other three were killed by a spear. It should be the work of the same person—the technique was clean, decisive, and extremely heavy-handed.\"","\"Especially Huangquan Ghost. His body was covered in wounds, his limbs were all broken, and the spearhead was driven directly through the top of his head, shattering the skull. The battle must have been intense, but he was likely suppressed the entire time. I suspect Song Jinzhao was the one who did it.\"","The hand Phantom used to grip his teacup was hauntingly white, as if it had not seen sunlight for years.","The blue veins on the back of his hand were clearly visible, and something resembling insects seemed to be crawling beneath the skin, looking incredibly eerie.","\"Based on the start date of Anyang Academy, they should already be on the road. We’ll strike in Kaikang. I don't want to waste time on a mission worth a mere five thousand taels.\"","The masked Rakshasa Ghost cast a fleeting glance at the other's arrogant expression. \"Huangquan Ghost was killed. This is no longer just a five-thousand-tael transaction; it concerns the reputation of the Life-Seizing Sect. We must not underestimate the enemy.\"","Phantom’s sharp fingernails pierced his palm. Blood dripped into the teacup, and several tiny nematodes began to swim in the liquid.","Their bodies arched repeatedly, looking as though they might leap out of the water at any moment.","\"That was because Huangquan Ghost was incompetent and only knew how to use brute force. I will make Song Jinzhao wish she were dead.\"","The moment Rakshasa Ghost saw the nematodes, he instinctively leaned back, his scarred face hidden beneath the mask filled with loathing.","If it weren't for the Sect Leader’s orders, he would never have wanted to go on a mission with Phantom. He felt as though the man even had bugs in his mouth when he spoke.","As the carriage continued its journey, the closer the four got to Kaikang City, the more their vigilance grew.","Song Gaoli blew a breath onto the polished, gleaming tip of a crossbow bolt and wiped away the moisture with the hem of his robe.","\"I have a bad feeling about this.\"","Song Qiming glanced at him speechlessly and held up five fingers. \"Since we left Xining City, you’ve said that phrase no less than fifty times in three days. I’m almost tired of hearing it.\"","Song Gaoli shook his head with a heavy heart. \"I just feel a chill down my back, like someone is watching us.\"","Song Qiming tried to reassure him. \"When a person is too tense, they start seeing ghosts. If someone were following us, Sister would definitely be the first to notice. Since she hasn't said anything, it means we're fine.\""]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: There's a Bloody Taste in the Dish","paragraphs":["After arriving in Kaikang City, the four of them first drove their carriage to the entrance of the county magistrate's office. A yamen runner dismissed them with a flippant remark about not knowing the location of the Life-Seeking Sect.","Song Gaoli clutched his head and wailed, \"Just as I feared. Living in constant fear is unbearable. Is there any permanent solution?\"","Song Jinzhao looked into the distance. Before her stretched an endless vista of streets and houses, while behind her, a plaque hanging above the main gate clearly bore the words \"Kaikang County Magistrate's Office.\"","\"Either eradicate the Life-Seeking Sect, killing until they dare not make a move, or eliminate the one who hired them.\"","Song Gaoli immediately lifted his head and asked, \"Sister Jinzhao, do you know who hired the assassins? Was it Yan Baoyi's father?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"It's not confirmed yet. Too many people resent me for being in their way. These assassins probably aren't targeting Qiming.\"","Song Gaoli was puzzled. \"But you doctors are all about healing and saving lives. How could you be in anyone's way?\"","Song Shixue, sitting inside the carriage compartment, lifted the window curtain.","\"It's all because my elder sister's medical skills are too exceptional. No scheme or trick can escape her discerning eye. Naturally, that breeds resentment.\"","Song Gaoli frowned, only half-understanding.","What did that mean?","How could diagnosing illnesses reveal schemes and tricks?","They returned to the inn they had stayed at last time for the night. For safety, Song Jinzhao chose the largest room this time, so all five of them could sleep in one room.","Song Jinzhao, Song Shixue, and Song Anhao took the bed, while Song Qiming and Song Gaoli slept on the daybed.","In the chaotic yet orderly kitchen, a tall man dressed in coarse kitchen helper's clothing walked in with his head bowed.","His gaze swept over the tables holding the prepared dishes before he silently, like an invisible man, sidled up to a pot of braised crucian carp with tofu.","His pale fingers lightly brushed over it, and two drops of blood fell into the pot, instantly dispersing.","An inn waiter knocked on the door with a tray. \"Honored guests, the dishes you ordered are ready.\"","Song Qiming, who had been dozing on the daybed, opened his eyes, glanced sideways at the closed door, and got up to answer it.","The waiter made two trips, placing all the dishes and staple food on the table.","He bowed respectfully to Song Qiming. \"Just call out in the corridor when you're finished, honored guests, and I'll come to clear everything away.\"","Song Gaoli weakly climbed down from the daybed. \"After traveling all day, we can finally have something hot to eat.\"","Song Qiming first filled a bowl with chicken soup and handed it to Song Jinzhao before the others began to eat.","Song Jinzhao took a sip of the soup, then put the bowl down, picked up her rice bowl, and started serving herself some dishes.","Phantom, peeking through the window, curled his lips into a smug smile upon seeing all four of them eat the crucian carp with tofu.","No matter how capable they are, once the gu poison enters their bodies, they can only wait for death when it activates without the antidote.","The rich flavors of saltiness and spiciness spread on her tongue.","Song Jinzhao frowned, looking at the half-piece of tofu in her bowl, then brought it closer and sniffed carefully.","A very faint scent of blood.","\"Stop. Don't eat any more.\" Song Jinzhao stopped the three who were wolfing down their food.","Phantom's expression froze. He hadn't expected Song Jinzhao to discover it so quickly.","But it was too late; they had already eaten it.","The gu worms had crawled down their throats into their stomachs. In a few days, without the antidote, death was certain.","Song Jinzhao frowned and turned to look at the half-open window, but saw nothing except the corridor.","Song Qiming and the others paused, their hands holding their rice bowls, food still in their mouths, unswallowed.","Song Shixue blinked in confusion. \"Elder sister, what's wrong?\"","Song Jinzhao stood up and leaned closer to the crucian carp and tofu, sniffing carefully. \"There's a scent of blood in the dish.\"","The thought of human flesh flashed in his mind. A wave of nausea surged up his throat. Song Gaoli spat the food in his mouth back into his bowl, holding his breath to suppress the urge to vomit.","After inspecting all the dishes and tea on the table, Song Jinzhao found that only the braised crucian carp with tofu carried the faint scent of blood.","The fishy smell could mask the scent of blood. Those unfamiliar with the smell of blood or with less sensitive senses of smell would find it hard to detect.","Song Qiming's face was filled with dread. \"Elder sister, what do we do now? We've already eaten it.\"","Song Jinzhao said gravely, \"Go and make yourselves vomit.\"","The three immediately rushed out of the room and ran downstairs to vomit.","The waiter, who was attending to other guests, stood there helplessly upon seeing this.","What happened? Their food shouldn't be that bad.","Apart from those drunk on wine, he'd never seen anyone vomit like this.","\"Waiter, was the chef who prepared the braised crucian carp with tofu just now injured on his hand?\" Song Jinzhao's voice came from the top of the stairs.","The waiter looked up and hurriedly replied with a smile, \"You jest, honored guest. The kitchen masters have been cleaning fish for half their lives. Never mind a few crucian carp, even a large grass carp weighing over ten pounds can be scaled and gutted in the blink of an eye. It's simply impossible for them to get injured.\"","Song Jinzhao's expression remained impassive. She turned and went back to the room to put the sleeping Song Anhao down.","Using a spoon, she carefully fished out the fish meat and tofu from the clay pot piece by piece to examine them.","Finally, on a piece of pale yellow fish meat, she discovered two tiny, wriggling thread-like worms."]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: Gu Du (Sorcery Poison)","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao took out a white handkerchief and spread it flat on the table. She picked the pieces of fish meat with the threadworms from the pot and placed them on it.","The poisoner had dripped blood infested with parasites into the dishes; there were certainly more than just these two.","These parasites were too small and could easily latch onto any organ.","Given the few bites they had just taken, even vomiting everything from their stomachs couldn't guarantee no worms remained inside.","The three who had finished vomiting downstairs walked in, clutching their stomachs, their pale lips and faces looking awful.","Song Shixue fixed her gaze on the wriggling threadworms on the handkerchief, a thought dawning on her.","She asked in disbelief, \"Elder Sister, are these... from the dishes?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"It must be the work of the Life-Taking Sect, mixed into the food along with blood.\"","Song Gaoli drew a sharp breath, the nausea from vomiting rising in his throat again.","He staggered out of the room. This time, he didn't even make it down the stairs, bending over with his right hand braced against the wall, retching as if trying to expel his very organs.","Song Jinzhao had Song Shixue and Song Qiming sit down so she could check their pulses.","\"Nothing shows on the pulse for now. The worms can parasitize and reproduce inside the body. We must kill them as soon as possible.\"","Song Shixue bit her lip, her eyes filled with a mix of urgency, worry, and anxiety.","\"Elder Sister, ancient texts mention monsters called gu worms. Is this it?\"","Legend had it that those afflicted with gu poison were either controlled for life or faced certain death.","Moreover, the dying process was excruciatingly painful; most couldn't endure it and even resorted to suicide to end their suffering.","Song Jinzhao picked up Song Anhao and placed Huzai into Song Shixue's hands. \"Come with me to the pharmacy to buy medicine. I don't know if it's gu poison, but I know how to kill it.\"","Passing through the corridor, Song Qiming grabbed Song Gaoli by the collar and dragged him along. \"Let's go, to the pharmacy.\"","The Life-Taking Sect people were surely nearby. Even if he was useless, they couldn't leave him behind.","It was dangerous; without Elder Sister here, they felt insecure.","In the room at the end of the corridor, Phantom and Rakshasa Ghost were watching the street below through a crack in the window.","Rakshasa Ghost raised an eyebrow. \"Trying to flee?\"","A frivolous smile curled Phantom's lips as he sneered, \"Even if they run to the ends of the earth, they can't escape death.\"","\"Send someone to follow. Song Jinzhao is very alert; don't get too close.\"","Rakshasa Ghost nodded. \"Once Song Jinzhao and the others are dead, we'll eliminate that child directly.\"","Uproot the grass and remove the roots, leaving no future trouble.","In the carriage, Song Gaoli hugged his knees, trembling.","He had imagined a real fight with swords and spears, never expecting poison and being fed worms. It was utterly revolting.","Terrified, he clutched the hem of Song Jinzhao's skirt.","\"Sister Jinzhao, can we really kill all the worms? Could they already be eating my heart and liver, drinking my blood?\"","Disturbed by the noise, Song Anhao instinctively covered his ears with his hands, slowly opening his eyes to find himself in a carriage again.","He muttered to himself in confusion, \"It feels like I didn't sleep long. Is it already the next day?\"","He felt like he hadn't eaten yet.","Song Jinzhao held him by the back to steady him. \"It's not the next day. You only slept for two hours.\"","Song Anhao nodded groggily, lifted the window curtain to look outside; it was almost dark.","Finding a pharmacy, they went in. Song Jinzhao handed a written prescription to the apprentice in charge of dispensing medicine.","\"Please prepare five doses according to this formula.\"","The apprentice opened the prescription, glanced at it, then looked up at Song Jinzhao with suspicion.","\"One moment.\"","He walked over to an old man wearing a hat and handed him the prescription. \"Master, a customer brought this prescription, but it seems all the ingredients listed are poisonous.\"","The elderly physician took the prescription and peered at it closely, his sparse white eyebrows furrowing deeply.","He stood up and approached Song Jinzhao. \"Miss, who prescribed this for you? What illness is it for?\"","Song Jinzhao replied frankly, \"I prescribed it myself. I am a physician.\"","The old physician gently stroked his beard. \"I see. Miss, are you aware that all these herbs are toxic? If the dosages are incorrect, they could harm rather than heal.\"","Looking at this young girl, barely in her teens, her medical skills couldn't be that proficient. He worried she might have made a mistake without realizing it.","Song Jinzhao said, \"It is precisely to use poison to attack poison.\"","\"Physician, rest assured. I consider myself quite proficient in medicine. Please prepare the medicine quickly.\"","The old physician held the prescription, reading it over twice more, but still couldn't discern what illness it treated.","\"Very well. Since you seem confident, I'll say no more.\"","He handed the prescription back to the apprentice and instructed, \"Prepare the medicine for them according to the formula.\"","After leaving the pharmacy, Song Jinzhao and the others bought a medicine pot for decoction.","The Life-Taking Sect assassin who had been observing from afar quietly returned to the room and knelt to report.","\"Hall Masters, Song Jinzhao took people to a pharmacy, bought a medicine pot, and has now returned to the inn.\"","Rakshasa Ghost stroked his chin, saying gravely, \"Song Jinzhao is a physician, and I hear her skills are quite good. Could she actually neutralize the gu poison?\"","The hand holding the fan in Phantom's hand paused slightly. He lowered his gaze, a dark tide swirling in his pupils.","\"Our sect master searched the world for divine physicians and found no way to cure gu poison, let alone a girl in her teens. This is nothing but a deathbed struggle.\"","Sensing the disappointment in Phantom's tone, Rakshasa Ghost wisely kept his mouth shut."]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: Turning Their Own Trick Against Them","paragraphs":["Inside the room, a medicinal pot simmered over a charcoal brazier. Song Qiming stood by the window, keeping watch.","A figure clad in black embroidered with gold thread passed through the corridor. A complexion so pale it was almost translucent immediately caught his attention.","Has this man never seen the sun? He’s as pale as a ghost.","The pungent, thick scent of medicine wafted out from the window. Phantom walked past Song Qiming with his head held high, eyes fixed straight ahead.","Beneath that calm facade, a stormy sea of excitement was being suppressed.","After the initial surge of excitement, his subconscious made him shake his head.","No, he had searched the world for famous doctors, and all had said they were powerless. How could Song Jinzhao possibly have a solution?","That medicine must be useless. It was a futile effort.","Stopping halfway down the stairs, Phantom’s lips were pressed thin, his heart and mind caught in a desperate tangle of conflict.","But what if it really worked?","Once the medicine was brewed, Song Jinzhao poured a bowl for everyone.","The taste was overwhelmingly bitter, a bitterness so intense it induced nausea.","Song Gaoli forced back the urge to gag, swallowing every last drop in the bowl, terrified that drinking too little would fail to kill the parasites.","\"Sister Jinzhao, how many days do we have to drink this?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"One dose at midnight tonight, another tomorrow morning, and then it will be over.\"","Although the \"insecticide\" made from poisonous traditional Chinese medicine was fierce in its properties, it could thoroughly kill the parasites. The only thing to watch for was the dosage; a little too little wouldn't kill the bugs, but a little too much would kill the person.","Once the smell of charcoal in the room had mostly dissipated, Song Qiming closed the window.","He whispered, \"Sister, what do we do now?\"","\"The people from the Soul-Snatched Sect must be nearby. If they realize we're fine, they'll definitely strike again.\"","Song Jinzhao said, \"Parasites usually don't take effect immediately after entering the body. Their choice to use poison shows they don't want a head-on confrontation.\"","\"Perhaps even our trip to buy medicine just now was under their surveillance. Since that's the case, we'll beat them at their own game and lure the snake out of its hole.\"","Song Qiming and the others looked at each other, a chill running down their spines. This feeling of being watched was truly unsettling.","In the middle of the night, the members of the Soul-Snatched Sect, sitting cross-legged in their room, snapped their eyes open alertly.","Rakshasa Ghost opened the door to look out into the corridor. The sound of vomiting was coming from Song Jinzhao’s room.","He closed the door and turned to Phantom. \"As expected, it was useless. It's starting to take effect so soon.\"","Phantom spoke coldly, \"Wait for it. All the torment and pain are only just beginning.\"","He turned over to lie on his side facing the wall. The smile on his face vanished instantly, replaced by endless disappointment and coldness.","To lack the skill yet dare to prescribe medicine recklessly—they truly deserve to die!","Early the next morning, the sky was dim, with a hint of snow in the air.","Up on the second floor, watching the four people—pale-faced and clutching their stomachs—crawl into the carriage, Rakshasa Ghost suggested with a smile, \"Song Jinzhao has no power to resist now. I suggest we strike once they leave the city. Let's finish the mission early and head back to report.\"","Phantom used his fan to press against his itching chest. He had only one Poison Control Pill left; it was indeed time to head back.","\"Do as you say.\"","Inside the carriage driven by Song Jinzhao, Song Shixue sat close to Song Anhao. With one hand, she held the Three Character Classic and read softly to him; with the other, she gripped a long sword, standing ready for battle.","Behind them, the carriage driven by Song Qiming and Song Gaoli followed closely, the distance between the two carriages never exceeding one meter.","Fearing a long-range attack, Song Gaoli had been pushed into the carriage by Song Qiming.","Huzai, who had been sleeping in a bamboo basket, was held in Song Gaoli’s arms, as if doing so could alleviate his fear and tension.","To make the Soul-Snatched Sect believe them, Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming, sitting on the driver's seats, played the part of people suffering from the onset of the venomous curse.","As time passed, their complexions grew increasingly ghastly, and they could barely keep the carriages steady.","The woods on both sides of the official road were deserted. The two-inch-thick snow looked like freshly steamed sponge cakes, glowing white.","The sound of many footsteps treading on snow became increasingly obvious. Song Jinzhao, who was holding her forehead with her right hand pretending to be in pain, felt a dark intensity surging in her eyes.","\"Ugh!\" Song Qiming groaned. He let go of the reins with his right hand and slumped over, clutching his stomach.","Song Jinzhao stopped the carriage and turned back. \"Qiming, what's wrong?\"","Song Qiming moaned in pain, \"Sister, my stomach hurts. It’s cramping, it hurts so much.\"","Sitting inside the carriage, Song Shixue and Song Gaoli seemed to hear the signal. One raised her sword to her chest, while the other gripped a crossbow with both hands, ready.","In the path obscured by branches, the assassins stopped.","To avoid drawing attention, they had specifically changed into white clothes to blend in with the snowy ground.","Phantom stared at Song Jinzhao with cold eyes, the killing intent in his gaze so thick it almost overflowed.","\"Move. Leave no one alive.\"","Ten assassins instantly turned into a gust of wind, rushing from the woods toward the roadside. Rakshasa Ghost and Phantom stood on high ground with their arms crossed, watching the battle.","A Song Jinzhao afflicted by the venomous curse was no longer worth their personal intervention; commanding their subordinates would be enough to kill them all.","Song Jinzhao’s palm, which had been resting on Song Qiming’s back, retracted. The two pale-faced youths suddenly turned and looked up.","\"Do it!\"","The sleeve-arrows held in their hands were like lotuses blooming; silver needles soaked in deadly poison shot out toward the assassins like scattered flower petals.","It happened too suddenly. The unprepared assassins had no time to dodge, and their exposed faces were riddled with silver needles like sieves.","Song Shixue and Song Gaoli, staying in the carriage, pulled back the curtains to finish off the wounded.","Standing on the embankment, Rakshasa Ghost’s expression changed abruptly. \"Not good, it’s a trap! They weren't cursed at all.\"","He immediately drew his blade and rushed forward to help.","Phantom stared intently at Song Jinzhao, his eyelashes trembling, his heart already churning with massive waves.","Caught in a pincer attack, five of the ten assassins collapsed from the poison, while the other five swung their swords at Song Jinzhao.","Song Jinzhao’s toes pushed off hard to the right, using the momentum to flip through the air.","Landing on the carriage frame, she leaned down to draw the Cloud-Soaring Spear and swung it in a horizontal sweep, her momentum as surging and powerful as a tsunami.","\"Qiming, catch the sword!\" Song Gaoli threw a long sword down from the carriage with force.","Song Qiming looked up, his body moving like an arrow from a bow as he rushed over to catch the scabbard.","Blades clashed. The immense force made it impossible for Song Qiming to keep his footing; he dropped to one knee, his hands trembling as he gripped the sword hilt.","Seeing Rakshasa Ghost’s long blade about to hack into Song Qiming’s shoulder, he gritted his teeth and shouted with a contorted expression, \"Sister!\"","Three iron needles flew from Song Jinzhao’s hand. Rakshasa Ghost decisively pulled back his strength to dodge.","The remaining five assassins had already been reduced to two by Song Jinzhao.","The two sides quickly swapped positions, and Song Jinzhao and Rakshasa Ghost became locked in combat.","Sitting in the carriage, Song Shixue protected Song Anhao while firing arrows to support Song Qiming.","Looking at the assassins who kept shifting positions, Song Gaoli didn't know where to fire his crossbow; the moment he aimed, the person was gone.","Unable to hold out, Rakshasa Ghost roared heart-wrenchingly toward the man behind him.","\"Phantom, what are you doing? Help me!\"","Just as the words left his mouth, a spear shaft as thick as an arm struck his neck heavily.","Rakshasa Ghost’s eyes widened in terror. He kicked off with both legs, retreating rapidly.","Pfft!","Rakshasa Ghost looked down in disbelief.","An iron fan had pierced through his back, skewering his stomach."]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: Kill Auntie Su","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao narrowed her eyes at the man standing behind the Rakshasa Ghost. Weren't they supposed to be accomplices?","Phantom withdrew his iron fan with a swift motion, and scalding blood sprayed out.","The Rakshasa Ghost collapsed to the ground, his eyes filled with confusion.","\"Why?\" he managed to choke out, questioning his comrade.","Phantom’s face remained expressionless, his voice cold. \"The Gu poison in my body was planted by the Sect Leader himself.\"","The Rakshasa Ghost’s eyes widened in horror. \"How can that be? The Sect Leader was saving your life.\"","Phantom let out a sneer, his face twisted in mockery.","\"He poisons me, pretends to be my savior, and then uses the antidote pills to blackmail me into doing his dirty work. You call that saving a life? How laughable.\"","The two men who had been fighting Song Qiming exchanged glances when they saw Phantom kill the Rakshasa Ghost. They immediately chose to flee.","The Second Hall Master had betrayed the Life-Taking Sect; they had to get back and inform the Sect Leader at once.","Noticing their attempt to escape, Song Qiming prepared to give chase, but a slender figure in white moved faster, intercepting the two assassins.","The sharp edge of the iron fan sliced across their fragile throats. In less than the time it takes to finish a cup of tea, they were silent forever.","Song Qiming’s gaze remained locked on Phantom, unable to fathom the man’s true intentions.","Internal strife? What exactly was going on?","Song Gaoli climbed down from the carriage and hid behind Song Qiming.","\"Qiming, who is he?\" he whispered.","If he was an enemy, he had just killed three other assassins. But if he was a friend, the masked man’s words implied they had originally been part of the same group.","Phantom’s sharp gaze shot toward the carriage.","Song Shixue, who was aiming her bow at him, felt her arms stiffen. She looked toward Song Jinzhao with a lost expression.","Seeing this, Phantom folded his iron fan and walked up to Song Jinzhao. \"Hand over the prescription for the Gu poison's cure.\"","Song Jinzhao stared back at him fearlessly. \"All your helpers are dead. It would be easy for me to kill you now. Why should I give you the prescription?\"","The blood in that dish earlier must have belonged to this man. If a single drop contained so many parasites, his entire body must be riddled with them.","Phantom leaned in close, his white breath brushing against Song Jinzhao’s fluttering hair. \"If you don't give it to me, I will go to the pharmacy where you buy your herbs.\"","\"As a physician, I assume you wouldn't want to see innocent people die because of you.\"","Song Jinzhao’s left hand, hanging at her side, curled slightly. She tilted her lips into a faint smile. \"Even if you knew the prescription, you couldn't cure the Gu poison on your own.\"","\"Every herb involved is a toxin. The dosage must be adjusted according to the patient's specific condition. Otherwise, it will either be useless or the poison will kill you before the cure does. You’re welcome to try.\"","Phantom’s dark pupils grew even gloomier. He took a step back and said, \"I can tell you who wants you dead, provided you cure the Gu poison in me.\"","Song Jinzhao studied him. \"When were you poisoned?\"","Phantom clenched his jaw. \"Three years ago.\"","After a moment of thought, Song Jinzhao said, \"I can help you, but I have one condition.\"","\"What condition?\" Phantom pressed.","\"I want you to bring me the head of the person who hired you,\" Song Jinzhao replied.","Phantom frowned. \"It’s just a concubine in a back courtyard. Killing her would be easy for you. Why must I be the one to do it?\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. The only person she had offended in a back courtyard was Concubine Su of the Liao Manor. She hadn't expected the woman to be involved with an underworld assassin organization. Truly, one cannot judge a book by its cover.","\"I don't want to get my hands dirty.\"","Phantom’s brow twitched. That excuse was far too perfunctory. This woman had clearly killed many people; her hands were already stained. What difference would one more make?","\"I accept your condition. Give me the cure first.\"","\"I want to see Concubine Su’s head first,\" Song Jinzhao insisted.","The two remained in a deadlock for a moment before Phantom gripped his iron fan and turned to leave. \"Remember your word. I will return with the head within seven days.\"","Watching the white figure gallop away, Song Qiming stepped forward. \"Sister, are you really going to cure him?\"","He was a professional killer who had attacked them. What if he decided to kill them after being cured?","Song Jinzhao thrust her spearhead into a snowbank to clean it.","\"Concubine Su is not only favored, but she is also the cousin of Liao Xiwen's father. If she is killed, Liao Wangshu will definitely investigate to the end. Rather than risking ourselves, it’s better to let an assassin from the Life-Taking Sect do it.\"","\"It's called shifting the trouble. We’ll see if the authorities can trace it back to the assassin organization and if they have the courage to wipe them out.\"","\"He said himself that the Sect Leader poisoned him. Once he's cured, he will surely go back for revenge. Why refuse a blade that delivers itself to your door? An organization that kills for money shouldn't exist anyway.\"","The three people standing before her stared in stunned silence, their mouths hanging open.","This move—using a borrowed knife to kill two birds with one stone—their sister played the game far too well.","Phantom rode day and night without stopping, entering Anyang City two days later.","Under the cover of darkness, he slipped into the Liao Manor and decapitated Concubine Su. He also killed every servant in the courtyard for good measure. Before leaving, he dropped a token representing his status as a Hall Master of the Life-Taking Sect in the middle of the yard.","Shifting the trouble—he would let the government throw the Life-Taking Sect into chaos while he sought his own revenge. Three years of false kindness, deception, and threats needed a final resolution.","The next morning, when no one from Concubine Su's courtyard came to the kitchen for hot water, the staff sent someone to check.","A servant wearing a headscarf stepped through the archway and froze instantly.","\"AHHHH!\" A piercing scream shattered the morning peace of the Liao Manor.","Liao Xiwen's father was livid as he looked at the corpses littering the yard. When he saw Concubine Su’s headless body, his eyes bulged with fury. He had gone completely mad with rage.","\"Who did this?\" he roared at the sky.","\"Report this to the authorities! Go now! You must find the killer!\"","Liao Xiwen, who had rushed over upon hearing the news, collapsed to the ground at the sight of the blood-drenched neck under the white cloth.","\"Miss!\" Her maid, Linglong, hurried forward to help her up and lead her out of the courtyard.","She had told her mistress not to come. What was there to see in a corpse? She was bound to have nightmares tonight.","Sitting on her bed and drinking medicine, Kong Wanru looked at her daughter being supported by the maid and confirmed, \"Is Concubine Su really dead?\"","Liao Xiwen sat weakly on a stool, her voice thin and trembling. \"Mother, you didn't see it. Her head was gone. She died so miserably.\"","Kong Wanru leaned against her soft pillows, lost in thought. \"What did your father say?\"","\"Father is furious. He’s already sent people to report it to the officials,\" Liao Xiwen replied. \"Mother, do you think the killer will come back?\"","Kong Wanru looked out the window. Her own illness hadn't even cleared up yet, and she hadn't expected the concubine to die first.","\"To strike so ruthlessly, there must be a deep grudge. Stay inside the manor for the next few days. Don't go out.\"","Liao Xiwen nodded vigorously. Even if someone begged her to go out, she wouldn't. Who knew if the killer was targeting Concubine Su specifically or the entire Liao Manor?"]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Return to Anyang Prefecture","paragraphs":["Inside the government office, before Meng Hechuan could even warm his seat, the butler from the Liao Manor arrived.","\"Your Honor, last night a concubine in our manor was murdered. Her head is missing, and four servants are also dead. My master sent me to report the crime and begs you to send someone to investigate immediately.\"","Meng Hechuan's expression drastically changed. Assassinating a woman in the inner chambers of a court official's home was simply unheard of.","He personally led his men to the Liao Manor to investigate.","The yamen runners turned Concubine Su's courtyard upside down and finally found a black wooden token by the corner of the wall. The three characters for 'Soul-Reaping Sect' were clearly visible on the back.","Meng Hechuan had been an official for many years and had seen countless cases, big and small. He also had some understanding of the martial arts world's gangs.","Among them, the Soul-Reaping Sect had the worst reputation and was the one he least wanted to encounter.","\"Lord Liao, has Concubine Su offended anyone from the martial arts world recently?\"","Liao Wangshu shook his head. \"My cousin is but a weak woman; she absolutely would not have any ties with people from the martial arts world.\"","Meng Hechuan lightly stroked his beard and murmured, \"The Soul-Reaping Sect is an organization that kills for money. If Concubine Su has no ties with the martial arts world, then someone must have paid for her life.\"","He raised his eyes and asked, \"Does she have any enemies? Has she had any disputes with anyone recently?\"","Liao Wangshu pondered, \"My cousin rarely leaves the manor and has never even interacted with male guests. It's impossible for her to have disputes with anyone, let alone have enemies.\"","Meng Hechuan didn't believe it. \"Without enemies, why would they take her head after killing her? You spend all day working at the government office; there might be things you are unaware of.\"","Liao Wangshu's gaze steadied, thinking that what the prefect said was not impossible.","He looked at the butler standing behind him. \"Has Concubine Su had any conflicts with anyone recently?\"","The butler bowed and reported, \"To answer the master, the concubine rarely goes out. If there's anything to be done, she orders the servants in her courtyard to do it, but those four people are all dead now.\"","Meng Hechuan's fingers unconsciously tapped the token. Thinking of something, he looked up and asked Liao Wangshu, \"How many concubines are there in your manor?\"","Liao Wangshu raised his eyebrows, not understanding why Meng Hechuan would ask this.","\"To answer Your Honor, I only have one wife and one concubine in my manor.\"","Meng Hechuan continued asking, \"How do the two get along? Have there ever been any quarrels?\"","As soon as these words came out, Liao Wangshu immediately understood his meaning.","He hurriedly explained, \"Your Honor, my wife is weak and bedridden all year round. My cousin often serves her tea and water by her side. The two have a harmonious relationship, like sisters, and have never had any disputes.\"","Meng Hechuan frowned deeply. With no enemies inside or outside, who would want to kill her?","The sickly Liao Tingjun was helped inside. With red, swollen eyes and a pale face, he looked like a soulless husk.","He knelt before Meng Hechuan, his knees hitting the ground with a heavy thud.","\"Your Honor, since it has been confirmed that the concubine was killed by an assassin from the Soul-Reaping Sect, I beg you to immediately send men to the sect to arrest the killer. Torture them to reveal the identity of the person who hired them, and avenge my concubine.\"","Seeing his son kneeling and begging, Liao Wangshu gritted his teeth, unable to bear it.","He turned and bowed to Meng Hechuan, \"Under the whole heaven, every spot is the sovereign's ground. Even people in the martial arts world should be governed by the imperial court. They absolutely cannot kill the innocent indiscriminately. I beg Your Honor to arrest the murderer to bring peace to her wronged soul.\"","Meng Hechuan clenched his fists, took a deep breath, and let out a heavy sigh.","\"In past cases, although there were suspicions, evidence was lacking. Now, with this token, the evidence is conclusive. We can make a move.\"","Since he decided to act, he couldn't just catch one person. He might as well take this opportunity to completely eradicate the Soul-Reaping Sect.","Relying solely on yamen runners, the combat power was far from enough. He had to write to the governor to dispatch troops for support.","Phantom galloped along the official road with Concubine Su's head, riding day and night without sleeping.","He finally caught up with Song Jinzhao and the others at an inn the night before they arrived in Anyang Prefecture.","\"I've brought the head. Can you cure my poison now?\" He opened the lid, revealing the bloody head.","Song Gaoli, standing to the side, had his pupils shrink and was so frightened that he crashed into Song Qiming's arms, constantly crying for help.","Phantom glanced at him with disdain. How could a man be so worthless?","Song Jinzhao bent down to meet Concubine Su's dilated pupils, which were covered with a thin layer of ice. It seemed she died with a grievance.","\"Sit down and stretch out your hand.\" Song Jinzhao placed her hand on Phantom's wrist.","His blood vessels were contracted, his pulse weak, and his qi and blood were tense and unsmooth. On the surface, he seemed fine, but internally he was hollow, constantly consuming his qi and blood.","Song Jinzhao placed an empty teacup in front of Phantom. \"Drop some blood into it.\"","Thick blood fell from his fingers into the bowl. Seeing the squirming nematodes clustered together, even Song Qiming closed his eyes, not wanting to look anymore.","Only Song Shixue stood behind Song Jinzhao without leaving.","Her tender, pretty eyebrows frowned into an inverted V shape, and she squinted at the nematodes in the bowl without taking a step back.","\"The Gu poison has lived in your body for too long. You look fine on the outside, but your qi and blood have long been depleted. You can't handle strong medicine. We have to go from light to heavy, combining treatment with nourishment.\"","Phantom's face was as calm as water, but his pale fingertips trembled slightly. \"Just tell me how long it will take to completely cure the poison?\"","\"Half a month.\" Song Jinzhao turned her head and told Song Shixue to get a brush, ink, paper, and inkstone.","A moment later, a detailed detoxification process and prescription were pushed in front of Phantom.","\"As long as you strictly follow the treatment course I wrote, the Gu poison will definitely be cured in half a month.\"","After reading it, Phantom folded the paper and tucked it into his clothes. \"I hope what you say is true. If the Gu poison isn't cured in half a month, I will come find you again.\"","With that, he turned to leave. Just as his fingers touched the doorframe, a gust of wind struck from behind.","He quickly turned around and caught the wooden box thrown by Song Jinzhao.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Dispose of it.\"","Thinking that the Gu poison hadn't been cured yet, Phantom took a deep breath and took the wooden box containing the head with him.","The grayish-white sky was gradually replaced by the dark night.","Under the eaves, Fushun craned his neck to look at the intersection, muttering constantly, \"Why aren't they back yet?\"","They had been waiting since the afternoon. Two hours had passed, and there was still no sign of them.","Qingshuang looked at the empty street, her heart also feeling empty.","\"They were probably delayed by something on the road. I'll go set up the stove first so the Eldest Miss and the others can eat as soon as they get back.\"","The clopping sound of horse hooves came from afar. Lanxi excitedly turned her head and called out to stop Qingshuang, who was walking inside, \"I see the carriage! They're back!\"","Qingshuang abruptly turned and ran back. The four of them ran down the steps and stood on the road waiting.","Two carriages, one in front and one behind, stopped. Lanxi and Fushun quickly ran over to lead the horses.","\"Eldest Miss, Eldest Young Master, Second Miss, Young Master.\"","Not long after they sat down, the servants brought all the food up.","The mutton in the iron pot bubbled, and a table full of fresh vegetables stunned Song Gaoli.","He picked up a vibrant green shepherd's purse and put it in his mouth. After chewing twice, a fresh fragrance filled his entire mouth.","\"Shepherd's purse shouldn't have grown out at this time of year. Where did this come from?\"","As a country kid, Song Gaoli knew better than anyone what vegetables grew in what season.","It was freezing cold outside, without a single blade of grass in sight. How could there possibly be fresh vegetables?","Song Qiming answered between bites, \"They were grown at home. My sister built a greenhouse on the estate, so we can grow vegetables even in the dead of winter.\"","Song Gaoli was so overwhelmed with shock that his mind went completely blank.","What on earth was a greenhouse? How come he had never heard of such a thing?"]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: Factional Struggles in the Korean Court: A Request to Confer the Title of Village Mistress","paragraphs":["Inside the study, Fushun and the other three were all present.","Chunxing opened the ledger and handed it to Song Jinzhao.","\"Eldest Miss, this is all the profit from the vegetable shop over the past half month, totaling seventeen thousand two hundred taels of silver.\"","An exquisite wooden box with its lid open sat on the table, filled with a thick stack of banknotes, all in denominations of one hundred taels.","After Song Jinzhao finished reviewing the ledger, Fushun stepped forward, bowed, and said, \"The vegetables in greenhouses one to three will have their final harvest in three days. Greenhouses four to six, which were planted ten days later, are growing more slowly due to the temperature and will need about another half month.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up at the four of them. \"Has Prefect Meng visited the farm?\"","Fushun nodded. \"On the third day of our opening, Prefect Meng came to ask about it on his own initiative. We followed your instructions and took him on a tour of the farm. The next day, he asked me to go to the government office to clearly explain the construction methods of the vegetable greenhouses and the precautions for planting. Someone was even recording it on the side.\"","Qingshuang stepped forward and said, \"After I delivered the Eldest Young Master's letter to the Ye residence, Mr. Ye told you not to worry, but he didn't mention anything else.\"","Song Jinzhao's fingers tapped idly on the table as she ran through everything in her mind.","Anyang Academy starts the day after tomorrow. Tomorrow, I must go to the Ye residence with Qiming.","\"You three step out first. Qingshuang, stay.\"","Chunxing, Fushun, and Lanxi respectfully turned and exited the study, closing the door behind them.","\"How is the situation with the Yan family?\"","Qingshuang looked up and asked, \"I haven't made a move yet, but the Yan family's goods were burned before they could enter the city. Was that your doing, Miss?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"I happened to run into them on the road.\"","Qingshuang pursed her lips. The servants responsible for escorting the Yan family's goods claimed it was heavenly fire. How did the Eldest Miss manage to do that?","\"As soon as Yan Fengnian returned, he immediately went to the Meng residence, presumably to save Yan Baoyi. The Prefect did not seem to agree, and the next day Yan Baoyi was escorted to his place of exile.\"","\"When news of the burned goods reached the city, Yan Fengnian was so overwhelmed by anger that he fell ill. Doctor Gu from the Gu Clinic visited him for several consecutive days to treat him, and he has now recovered. I heard that after the Lantern Festival, he will be heading to Jiangnan to purchase more goods.\"","Song Jinzhao crossed her legs, a faint smile appearing on her face. \"He is quite pragmatic. It seems Yan Baoyi has been completely abandoned.\"","After traveling for days, on their second day back home, everyone except the young Song Anhao slept until the sun was high in the sky.","Chunxing, who stayed home to cook, quickly served breakfast. The rich meal made Song Jinzhao and the other two sigh with emotion that having servants was indeed comfortable.","After breakfast, Song Gaoli packed his bags and returned to the academy.","Song Jinzhao and Song Qiming brought gifts and headed to the Ye residence to visit Ye Liangyu.","After stepping out of the carriage, Song Jinzhao noticed two tall and sturdy young men standing at the entrance of the Ye residence. She slowed her pace and examined them carefully.","These two were completely different from the servants in Ye Liangyu's household; they looked like they had come out of a military camp.","Upon being welcomed into the main hall, the man sitting below Ye Liangyu caught Song Jinzhao's attention.","Qin Yunqian smiled and stood up to greet her. \"Miss Song, long time no see.\"","Song Jinzhao gave a slight nod. \"Young Master Qin.\" It seemed the men in the courtyard had been brought by Qin Yunqian.","After taking their seats, Ye Liangyu began to test Song Qiming to see if his studies had fallen behind during his time back in the village.","Feeling bored, Qin Yunqian signaled to Song Jinzhao with his eyes. \"Want to step outside for a chat?\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the master and disciple who were deep in conversation, then stood up and followed Qin Yunqian out of the main hall.","By the pond in the courtyard, Qin Yunqian looked at Song Jinzhao and spoke meaningfully, \"Miss Song has highly skilled martial arts, but I never expected your medical skills to be this excellent as well. Even the imperial doctors in the palace were helpless regarding Lord Ye's legs, yet you managed to cure him in the end.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. He seemed to have a hidden meaning in his words.","Qin Yunqian's gaze remained fixed on Song Jinzhao's face without shifting away.","\"Currently, the two princes at court stand as equals, and the civil and military officials are divided into two factions supporting the Prince of Qi and the Prince of Ying. Ye Liangyu refuses to pledge allegiance to either prince.\"","\"He holds a high position and has an upright and unyielding character. As the Deputy Censor-in-Chief, he carries the responsibility of advising the emperor on his faults and correcting the officials' mistakes. He has offended many people, which is why someone wanted him dead.\"","\"News of Ye Liangyu's fully healed legs has already reached the capital. It won't be long before the Emperor restores him to his original post. You cured his legs, and your younger brother is his only student. Having offended both princes before even entering the capital, his future situation as a court official is truly worrisome.\"","Song Jinzhao looked down at the school of fish fighting for food in the pond. Though she had her own thoughts, she did not voice them, only saying, \"My brother is currently just a Xiucai. Whether he can pass the exams to become a Juren is yet to be seen. Why should I worry about groundless fears?\"","Qin Yunqian replied, \"This August is the triennial provincial examination. Although your brother began his schooling late, he has made rapid progress and is already among the top students at Anyang Academy. Passing the provincial exam will be no problem for him.\"","\"If he can score high in the metropolitan examination the following February, Ye Liangyu will definitely keep him in the capital as an official. When the city gates catch fire, the fish in the moat suffer. Miss Song, you must absolutely ensure that you and your family do not become those fish.\"","Inside the main hall, after finishing the academic examination, Ye Liangyu asked, \"How did you come up with the idea to request an imperial decree to make your sister a Township Princess?\"","Song Qiming's tone was steady and slow, as if every word had been carefully considered.","\"Previously, because of the matter regarding the construction of the waterwheel and the capture of the northern thieves, the Emperor had already issued a decree to reward my sister. Now that our family is engaged in business, we lack no silver. Rather than having the Emperor bestow gold, silver, and jade ornaments again, it is better to ask for the title of Township Princess.\"","\"My sister is smart and talented, with superb martial arts and excellent medical skills. It is a pity that women cannot participate in either the civil or military examinations. It is better to exchange her merits for a noble title available to women, at least to make her status more distinguished.\"","Ye Liangyu tapped his fingers lightly on the table. \"What did your sister say?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"My sister said that asking for money is not as good as asking for power. Although a Township Princess holds no real power, the rank is a primary seventh grade. Because of that status, others will not be able to bully us at will. Besides, it is not as if history lacks records of women exceptionally being granted titles of marquis or appointed as prime ministers. We just have to take it step by step.\"","Ye Liangyu's gaze hardened, and he could not help but secretly marvel at Song Jinzhao's great ambition.","To be made a marquis or a prime minister—she really dared to dream!","Seeing that he did not speak, Song Qiming said softly, \"If requesting the title of Township Princess is difficult, Teacher doesn't need to put himself in too tough a spot.\"","Ye Liangyu waved his hand. \"Before the new year, I already wrote a letter and had someone deliver it to the capital. Once Meng Hechuan's memorial requesting a reward arrives, someone in the court will naturally propose it. The Emperor will not be stingy over a mere Township Princess title. However, as for what you mentioned about being made a marquis or prime minister, I'm afraid that will be as difficult as ascending to the heavens.\"","Song Qiming smiled without saying a word, immediately changed the subject, and began chatting casually about his time practicing martial arts and hunting at home."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: The Prime Minister Opposes","paragraphs":["In the dead of winter, memorials sent to the capital from various provinces were often delayed on the road. Coupled with the imperial court being sealed for the New Year, many affairs had piled up.","Meng Hechuan's memorial was not expedited, so by the time Emperor Xiao Chengjing saw it, it was already the fourth day after the court reopened.","When he read Meng Hechuan's account of growing vegetables in the north during the bitter winter, he was so astonished that he read the full three pages of detailed explanations over and over again, only stopping when his eyes blurred and his head spun.","Xiao Chengjing leaned back against the dragon throne, his eyes narrowed, his mind full of uncertainty.","Off-season planting—how did a commoner woman come up with such an idea?","Pass my decree: summon Prime Minister Gu Qishan, Minister of Works Ou Shinian, and Hanlin Academy Scholar Fei Yanzhang for an immediate audience.","Ou Shinian gripped the edges of the paper tightly, his eyes narrowed and his brow twitching.","Your Majesty, who came up with this method?","Xiao Chengjing handed the memorial to the three men. It is still that commoner woman, Song Jinzhao. The Anyang Prefecture was already eating greenhouse vegetables before the New Year.","Reading Meng Hechuan's words of praise for Song Jinzhao in the memorial, Prime Minister Gu Qishan looked somewhat dazed.","If this method is popularized, it will greatly alleviate the problem of winter food shortages. If it can be planted in the north, it will definitely work in the south.","Ou Shinian said excitedly, Not only that, but the winter climate in the south is warmer than in the north. The yield will only be higher, and the cost will be lower than in the north.","Xiao Chengjing's heart trembled. He looked toward the Hanlin Academy Scholar Fei Yanzhang and asked, Beloved Subject Fei, the Hanlin Academy has a vast collection of books. Have you ever seen any relevant books on greenhouse planting like this?","Fei Yanzhang cupped his hands. To reply to Your Majesty, this humble subject has read extensively through ancient texts and has never seen this method. The ideas of this woman named Song Jinzhao are truly extraordinary.","Xiao Chengjing rested his arm on the dragon head of his throne. What is even more rare is that she took the initiative to offer this method to the imperial court. Meng Hechuan requested a reward for this woman in his memorial, but I do not know what to bestow upon her.","Ou Shinian let out a very soft sigh.","Even though Song Jinzhao's construction of the waterwheel had caused him to be fined a year's salary, it was truly a great pity that such a talent could not enter the Ministry of Works to serve the court.","It was such a shame that she was a woman.","Prime Minister Gu Qishan suggested, Song Jinzhao comes from a farming family and is of poor background. This humble subject believes that rewarding her with some gold and silver would be best.","The Prime Minister is mistaken. Meng Hechuan mentioned in the memorial that Song Jinzhao could earn tens of thousands of taels of silver in profit by selling greenhouse vegetables. By dedicating this method to the court, she essentially cut off her own path to wealth, which shows she does not care about gold and silver.","Xiao Chengjing felt this made sense. How does Beloved Subject Fei think I should reward her?","Fei Yanzhang replied, To Song Jinzhao, being able to serve Your Majesty is something no amount of gold and silver can buy. This woman has talent but comes from a humble background. This humble subject believes Your Majesty could elevate her status, for example, by conferring upon her the title of Lady of the County.","Gu Qishan immediately stepped forward to object. Your Majesty, this humble subject thinks this is inappropriate. Song Jinzhao is of low commoner status. Conferring the title of Lady of the County would be too heavy an imperial grace. It would be better to reward her with an inscribed plaque to show imperial favor, which would also bring glory to her family's door.","Fei Yanzhang rolled his eyes at him, speechless. It is precisely because of her poor background that she needs to be granted a title. Your Majesty has already bestowed a plaque upon her for the merit of the waterwheel; there is no need to bestow another. Based on the merits Song Jinzhao has established, she is absolutely worthy of a mere title of Lady of the County.","Seeing the two arguing endlessly, Xiao Chengjing looked toward the Minister of Works. Beloved Subject Ou, who of the two do you think makes more sense?","Ou Shinian, who was repeatedly reading the instruction manual, was suddenly caught in a dilemma.","His gaze accidentally fell on the palace maids serving in the hall, and a flash of inspiration hit his mind.","He stepped forward and said, Song Jinzhao is currently at a marriageable age. The most important thing in a woman's life is to marry a good husband. Why doesn't Your Majesty issue an edict to graciously bestow a marriage upon her?","Not only did Gu Qishan and Fei Yanzhang fail to react, but even the Emperor was stunned.","To think he would actually consider playing matchmaker!","Xiao Chengjing asked, Since you have brought it up, do you have a suitable candidate in mind?","Ou Shinian said, his face glowing red, There are many young and talented men in the Ministry of Works who are not yet married. Song Jinzhao is good at ingenious ideas, so she would surely share their interests. Your Majesty can choose from among them. This humble subject thinks it couldn't be better.","...","All was completely silent. The three of them were shocked by Ou Shinian's shamelessness.","He wanted to rake every benefit into his own pockets. He had truly made a good suggestion.","If it weren't for the fact that Ou Shinian was already over fifty, married with children, and even had grandchildren, he probably would have wanted to step up himself.","At this moment, a eunuch walked in from outside the door. Your Majesty, the Duke of Qing requests an audience outside.","Xiao Chengjing waved his hand and sat down. Let him in.","After entering, Chu Liuyun walked to the middle of the imperial study, knelt down, and bowed.","Reporting to Your Majesty, this humble subject has returned to the capital from the garrison rotation at the western suburbs camp, and has come specifically to present the military report.","The head eunuch handed the military report to the Emperor.","Rise, my beloved subject. This winter rotation has been hard on you. The Lantern Festival is in two days, so I grant you three days of leave to rest well at home.","Chu Liuyun kowtowed in gratitude. Thank you for Your Majesty's profound grace.","Xiao Chengjing looked at the rising Chu Liuyun and suddenly remembered that he and Song Jinzhao should know each other.","Thus, he waved his hand, signaling the eunuch to take the memorial over for him to see.","Beloved Subject Chu, this is the memorial sent by the Prefect of Anyang.","Gu Qishan suggested rewarding Song Jinzhao with gold and silver; Fei Yanzhang believes she should be conferred the title of Lady of the County; Ou Shinian wants me to issue a marriage edict to pick a good husband for her. You are acquainted with Song Jinzhao. Which reward do you think is best?","After reading the memorial, Chu Liuyun could not help but secretly admire her.","As a commoner woman, to be able to repeatedly establish merits that made the Emperor consider how to reward her—there were not many women in the world who could achieve this through their own abilities. She could be considered the first.","To reply to Your Majesty, this humble subject once sent people to investigate Song Jinzhao's background. Her father was crushed to death by a falling rock while building the canal. Upon hearing the sudden bad news, her mother gave birth prematurely to a son and then passed away as well. At that time, Song Jinzhao was only fourteen.","Besides this newborn brother, she also had a younger brother and sister who were only ten years old. The Song family was poor and had already divided their household. Her two uncles could not afford to raise four children, so they wanted to adopt out her premature brother to a wealthy family in the village to bring them a son, and send her sister to be a child bride to ward off bad luck for someone else.","Song Jinzhao was unwilling. In front of her grandparents, she swore an oath that she would raise her three younger siblings herself, and that she would not marry until her brother Song Qiming was married and had a family.","Three years have passed, and Song Qiming is now only thirteen. The marriage bestowal mentioned by Minister Ou is truly inappropriate.","The Emperor was stunned, his breathing unconsciously becoming lighter.","I never asked about Song Jinzhao's family background in detail. I did not expect it to be like this.","Chu Liuyun smiled and said, Your Majesty need not dwell on it too much. After her parents passed away, Song Jinzhao started taking risks by going up the mountain to hunt for money. By the time this humble subject left the border, she had already set up a stall in Xining City and started a business. Although her life was not wealthy, she did not lack food or clothing.","Gu Qishan spoke with deep sincerity, a faint smile on his face.","The Duke of Qing is ill-informed. The Song family has not only moved to Anyang Prefecture now, but they have also bought shops and estates, earning gold every day. Even Song Qiming has passed the exams to become a scholar and has taken Ye Liangyu as his teacher. The Song family has long since broken free from their destitute circumstances of the past.","\"Oh?\" Chu Liuyun raised an eyebrow. \"I didn't expect Song Jinzhao's younger brother to be so promising. It's only been a few years, and he has already passed the imperial exams to become a scholar?\"","The Emperor furrowed his brows in surprise. \"Who did you just say Song Qiming took as his master?\""]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: Linghui Township Lady","paragraphs":["Gu Qishan almost bit his own tongue. He had spoken too fast and failed to guard his mouth.","\"Ye Liangyu. It's said that his legs were cured by Song Jinzhao.\"","The emperor leaned back, shooting a sharp gaze at Chancellor Gu Qishan.","\"The capital and Anyang Prefecture are thousands of miles apart, yet you seem to know the Song family's situation like the back of your hand.\"","Gu Qishan hurriedly lowered his head in panic. \"I only heard rumors, Your Majesty.\"","The emperor looked away, his deep and complex gaze sweeping across Fei Yanzhang's face.","After a moment of contemplation, he said, \"Song Jinzhao is outstanding in both talent and virtue, and has repeatedly made extraordinary contributions. I am deeply gratified. Have the Ministry of Rites follow the regulations and confer upon her the title of Lady Linghui. See to it immediately.\"","No matter how reluctant he was, Gu Qishan had no choice but to kneel along with Fei Yanzhang and the others, shouting loudly, \"Your Majesty is wise! Long live the Emperor!\"","A mere title of Lady was naturally something Song Jinzhao could handle, but the problem was her deep relationship with Ye Liangyu.","Fei Yanzhang alone was one thing, but the Duke of Qing had also stepped in, and there was no stopping him.","In the main hall of the Prince of Qi's estate, Gu Qishan recounted everything that had just happened in the imperial study to the Prince of Qi in great detail.","The man sitting in the seat of honor wore a purple brocade jacket with python patterns, and mink-lined brocade trousers with kneepads. His boots were embroidered with four-clawed golden dragons. Anyone with a discerning eye could tell at a glance that he was of imperial descent.","The Prince of Qi slammed his fist heavily onto the table, causing the tea to spill over the rim of the cup.","\"Looking at my royal father's current attitude, once Ye Liangyu's legs are completely healed, he will definitely issue a decree for him to return to the court. Why can't we get rid of this stubborn thorn!\"","None of the assassins sent had returned. Unsure of exactly how many guards were inside the Ye residence, Xiao Rongche didn't dare send any more men.","Gu Qishan said, \"Your Highness, the Censorate is currently filled entirely with our people and the Prince of Ying's people. Even if Ye Liangyu returns, it will be difficult for him to make a single move. You need not worry too much.\"","The Prince of Qi sneered viciously. \"Aren't there still two tough nuts to crack? He may have no one in the Censorate, but the Hanlin Academy favors him. Fei Yanzhang's actions today must have been instructed by Ye Liangyu.\"","Gu Qishan furrowed his brows tightly. \"Ye Liangyu uplifting Song Jinzhao is nothing more than for the sake of his student. Song Qiming is currently just a scholar. Your Highness doesn't need to take them to heart.\"","\"What is worth looking into is the Duke of Qing. Did he speak up for Fei Yanzhang today because of Ye Liangyu or Song Jinzhao?\"","The Prince of Qi stopped tapping his fingers on the table, his voice lowering with a chilling intent. \"If it's because of Song Jinzhao, then so be it. But if it's Ye Liangyu, then we must be on guard.\"","He turned his head and ordered the guard standing nearby, \"Immediately send someone to keep an eye on the Duke of Qing's estate. See which officials Chu Liuyun has been close to recently.\"","\"Yes, sir.\" The guard clasped his hands over his sword and obeyed.","...","Inside the Song family clinic in Anyang Prefecture, Song Jinzhao was reviewing the pulse records from Liu Xuanqing's recent consultations with Kong Wanru.","Over twenty days, there had been a total of seven consultations. The first two times were relatively normal, but the later pulse readings were recorded as having a weak beat and a slight deficiency in qi and blood, with the condition worsening each time.","Liu Xuanqing stood beside her and explained, \"During those few days, Madam Kong happened to catch a cold. Her body is already weak, so it took half a month of medication for her to get better. When I visited to check her pulse yesterday, there were already signs of full recovery.\"","Song Jinzhao closed the medical record. \"It's fine. I will go over and take a look tomorrow.\"","Kong Wanru had caught a cold right after she left. Thinking of Concubine Su's actions, Song Jinzhao felt there was something strange about this.","The entire afternoon, Song Jinzhao was either auditing accounts or on her way to audit accounts, going through the mountain of contracts one by one.","There were even vegetable-ordering business partners who, upon learning that Song Jinzhao had returned, specifically brought gifts to her door, begging to increase their orders.","She was so busy all afternoon that she didn't even have time to take a sip of water.","When she returned home in the evening, Song Qiming was squatting at the door of the woodshed, staring at the little white tiger in the bamboo basket.","Seeing them return, he quickly waved at Song Shixue. \"Xuetuan has opened its eyes a crack.\"","Xuetuan was the name Song Shixue had given the little white tiger.","Covered in white fur and picked up on a snowy day, it shared a character with her name, which made Song Shixue feel a sense of closeness.","While waiting for Xuetuan to open its eyes, the siblings' feelings had been constantly on edge.","Before the deal was sealed, perhaps there would be a miracle?","Song Jinzhao held onto Song Anhao's hand to keep him from lying on the ground.","Children were forgetful and loved playing with small animals. At first, he had been a bit jealous, but after a few days, he became incredibly fond of it.","\"We'll know if it's cross-eyed in a few days when its eyes are fully open. Right now, looking at its cervical spine, it seems normal.\"","Born less than ten days ago, it already weighed three or four catties. Its back formed a straight line, and it crawled around quite nimbly.","The day before the Lantern Festival, the temperature dropped sharply, and Anyang Prefecture welcomed its third heavy snowfall since the new year.","Seeing a carriage stop at the door, the gatekeeper thought it was another distant relative coming to beg for money. He was just about to close the door when he saw Song Jinzhao emerge from the carriage.","His hand paused on the door; it was Dr. Song.","Snowflakes fell on the umbrella. The snow-white fox fur beautifully contrasted with the red plum blossoms embroidered on her cloak, making them vibrant but not gaudy. Coupled with the cold and aloof expression in Song Jinzhao's eyes, anyone would wonder which high-ranking official's noble daughter this was.","The gatekeeper reopened the half-closed gate and stepped over the threshold to welcome her. \"Has Dr. Song come to consult for the Madam?\"","Calculating the time, the once-every-three-days visit should actually be tomorrow.","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"I just returned and heard from Xuanqing that the Madam caught a cold. I wanted to come and see for myself. I wonder if it is convenient today?\"","The gatekeeper said, \"Please wait a moment, Dr. Song. I will go in and ask right away.\"","During the New Year period, everyone knew about the grand spectacle of the Song family's vegetable shop having its threshold trampled by restaurant merchants from all over Anyang Prefecture.","With two extremely lucrative shops, plus the manors and fields outside the city, who didn't know that the Song family was now incredibly wealthy?","Being able to grow vegetables in the dead of winter meant that no one would treat her as just an ordinary doctor anymore. Even the attitude of the Liao residence's gatekeeper was much more respectful than before."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Determining that the Herbal Decoction Has Been Tampered With","paragraphs":["Walking through the corridor, the servants in the manor hurried past with their heads bowed, their mouths shut tight as if sealed with tape.","Yesterday at the medical clinic, Song Jinzhao had already learned that Canying not only killed Concubine Su, but also slaughtered all the servants in her courtyard, including that man, Wang Zhong.","Since the murderer had not been caught, it seemed that everyone in the Liao Manor was now in a state of panic, afraid that they would be the next victim.","Entering Chunshui Courtyard, Song Jinzhao could not help but curl the corners of her mouth into a sarcastic smile.","The atmosphere here was much livelier than outside; there were even people gathering together and whispering to each other.","Inside the room, Liao Xiwen, who was sitting on a stool, saw Song Jinzhao coming and quickly stood up to take two steps forward.","Her eyes curved into crescents as she grinned and said, \"Miss Song, you are finally back.\"","Ever since the incident at home, Liao Xiwen had not stepped out of the house. When she felt scared in the middle of the night, she could not help but think of how Song Jinzhao had saved her during the horse stampede.","If only she were as formidable as her. Not only would she not fear assassins, but she could also catch them.","Her arm was firmly grasped by the other party, as if the fingers were going to dig into her flesh.","Facing Liao Xiwen's shining eyes, Song Jinzhao froze for a moment before pulling her arm away. Their relationship was not quite at that level yet.","\"Miss Liao, you look a bit pale. Did you not sleep well at night?\"","Liao Xiwen lowered her eyes and said in disappointment, \"A few days ago, something happened in the manor, and I have not slept well for several nights.\"","Several times she had dreamed of Concubine Su's ghost coming to her for help, and when the plea failed, the ghost tried to drag her down to hell with her.","After waking up in a cold sweat, she could not fall back asleep and could only catch up on her rest during the day.","Song Jinzhao said, \"Later, I will write a soothing prescription for you, Miss Liao. Drink it before bed, and I guarantee you will sleep soundly until dawn.\"","Liao Xiwen nodded joyfully, \"Thank you, Miss Song.\"","With her fingers resting on Kong Wanru's wrist, the room was extremely quiet. Everyone was waiting for Song Jinzhao's pulse diagnosis.","As expected, the prescription she had given previously had no effect at all.","Although her complexion looked rosy on the surface, her insides were actually hollow and deteriorating day by day.","\"Have everyone leave.\"","Kong Wanru thought Song Jinzhao was going to examine her lower body again, so she immediately ordered all the maids out, not even letting Liao Xiwen stay.","The door was shut tight. Just as she was about to take off her pants, Song Jinzhao suddenly spoke, \"Your body has not recovered; in fact, it is getting worse.\"","Kong Wanru's fingertips trembled, and in an instant, all the color drained from her face. \"Is it because I caught a cold a few days ago, so my body is a bit weak?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"A cold affects the nose, mouth, throat, and lungs. The prescription I gave you treats the uterus and menstruation. Based on the recorded pulse, I suspect the medicine you drank was tampered with. Are the medicine dregs still around?\"","Kong Wanru leaned against the pillow with a wooden expression, a chill running from her head down to her toes.","\"They were thrown out.\"","The ancients believed in sending the illness to the road, thinking that the medicine dregs were tainted with the patient's sickness and bad luck.","They would throw the useless dregs onto the road for pedestrians to trample on, believing this would crush the sickness and bad luck.","\"Are the dregs from the last two days still here?\"","Kong Wanru opened her mouth to call for someone, but swallowed her words right at the tip of her tongue.","Last time, worried that her medicine would be tampered with, she had already replaced some of the servants and arranged for two people to supervise each other when brewing and serving the medicine.","They were all servants and house-born slaves she had brought from her maiden home. If problems still occurred under these circumstances, who else could she trust?","\"Xiwen, come in.\"","Liao Xiwen, who was standing at the door, heard Kong Wanru call her name. She gestured for the others to step away from the door to prevent them from seeing anything they should not.","She pushed the door open and quickly closed it, finding her mother leaning against the couch, fully dressed.","Kong Wanru stared at her only daughter and said, \"Doctor Song says there is a problem with the medicine. The medicine dregs are in the small kitchen next door. Go and bring them here.\"","\"Have Linglong immediately go and tell the gatekeeper that the manor's servants are only allowed to enter and not leave these days. I want to catch the person who tampered with my medicine.\"","Liao Xiwen stood frozen in place, her arms pressed helplessly against her thighs.","\"I will go do it right away.\" Her hand could not stop trembling as she turned to open the door, her heart racing as if it could not wait to jump out of her chest.","Opening the door, Liao Xiwen called Linglong to the side and whispered a few instructions before taking another maid towards the small kitchen.","Seeing them come out carrying the medicine pot, a maid in green standing under the eaves suddenly changed her expression, her eyes darting around like a frightened sparrow.","She took small, panicky steps backward until she was out of the courtyard gate, then turned and quickly ran away."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: Catching People","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao emptied the dregs from the medicine pot to inspect them, but found nothing unusual.","Concubine Su was dead. Without their master, the person tampering with the medicine would definitely stop, but some traces could not be erased.","Song Jinzhao washed the medicine pot clean with water. Sniffing carefully, she could detect a faint scent of musk and aconite.","\"The dregs are correct now, but they must have been tampered with before. There is the scent of musk and aconite. Since the smell remains even after washing, it must have been brewed more than just once or twice.\"","Liao Xiwen was puzzled. \"If they weren't discovered, why would they stop?\"","Kong Wanru's face tightened, her gaze like two ice picks. \"That's because Concubine Su is dead.\"","Liao Xiwen stopped talking, as if she had suddenly gone mute. Thoughts raced wildly in her mind, and the more she thought about it, the more shocked she became, until she could barely stand.","If Concubine Su was behind this incident, could she also be related to all the miscarriages her mother had suffered in the past?","Kong Wanru was so enraged she almost crushed her back teeth. Thinking of the tampered decoctions, she opened her eyes and began to issue orders.","\"Arrest the two maids responsible for brewing the medicine at once. Search their rooms immediately. We must find evidence.\"","Even if the person was dead, the truth had to be uncovered. Her years of suffering could not be in vain; she wouldn't let her off the hook so easily even in death!","Opening the door, Liao Xiwen pointed at a maid standing in the corner and shouted, \"Someone, seize her!\"","The maid, her hands restrained, looked bewildered and asked fearfully, \"Miss, what wrong has this servant committed?\"","Liao Xiwen ignored her. Her gaze swept quickly through the crowd, and she frowned in dissatisfaction as she questioned the others.","\"Where is Hongju?\"","The crowd looked at one another and shook their heads.","\"She was just here. How could she disappear?\"","Liao Xiwen felt a sudden sense of foreboding and yelled, \"Hurry up and find her!\"","The two maids' rooms were turned upside down. Linglong walked in holding a paper parcel commonly used for medicine.","\"Miss, these medicines were found in Hongju's room.\"","Liao Xiwen turned her head and signaled, \"Show them to Miss Song.\"","Musk, sanqi, aconite, morning glory seeds...","They were all there without exception. This time, they wanted to make Kong Wanru completely lose her ability to bear children.","\"These are it. You can make the arrest.\"","Filled with righteous indignation, Liao Xiwen said to Kong Wanru, \"Hongju is missing. I have already sent people to look for her. The mansion gates are closed, so she definitely can't escape.\"","Halfway through searching the Liao mansion, the gatekeeper dragged Hongju into the Spring Water Courtyard.","He threw Hongju onto the ground and opened her bundle, which was full of gold and silver jewelry, as well as silver ingots.","\"Madam, when I went to the latrine, I bumped into this girl trying to crawl out through the dog hole. All these things were found on her person.\"","Kong Wanru forced her sick body off the couch, her eyes like an evil spirit crawling out of the abyss. \"Why did you betray me? Have I ever mistreated you?\"","Hongju trembled. She crawled over, hugged Kong Wanru's legs, and begged incessantly.","\"Madam, I didn't mean to. It was Concubine Su who threatened me. I had no choice but to listen to her. I am innocent.\"","Kong Wanru raised her foot to kick her away, but her right leg lacked the strength.","Liao Xiwen hurriedly rushed forward and supported Kong Wanru's arm.","She kicked Hongju's shoulder and pointed at the jade bracelets and hairpins in the bundle, scolding, \"You keep claiming you're innocent, so where did these things come from?\"","\"I think you are just greedy. You would do anything for money. A despicable person who betrays her master for glory and forgets loyalty for profit. Today, I must hand you over to the authorities.\"","\"What is all this noise!\" An angry roar made everyone's eardrums ring.","Everyone looked up and saw Liao Wangshu standing at the door, his face as dark and livid as the bottom of a scorched pot.","\"I just returned to the mansion and it's in an uproar, closing the gates and searching the premises. Are you trying to turn the world upside down!\"","Liao Xiwen angrily rushed up to explain, \"Father, you don't know. Concubine Su instructed Hongju to poison Mother's medicine, trying to make her permanently infertile.\"","\"Now we have both the culprit and the loot, and we are about to send Hongju to the authorities.\"","Liao Wangshu's expression froze. After reacting, he glanced at Song Jinzhao and Liu Xuanqing, the two outsiders.","He sternly reprimanded Liao Xiwen, \"With outsiders present, what do you look like shouting and making a fuss? Your speech and demeanor lack the quiet gentleness of a lady from a noble family. I'll have your grandmother teach you properly another day.\"","After speaking, he looked at Song Jinzhao. \"Doctor Song, please do not spread word of what happened in the mansion today.\"","After being respectfully escorted out of the Liao mansion, Liu Xuanqing sat in the carriage and said, \"It seems Lord Liao wants to turn a big issue into a small one, and a small one into nothing.\"","A faint smile curled the corners of Song Jinzhao's mouth. \"Family scandals should not be aired in public. It's not surprising he reacted this way.\"","Liu Xuanqing thought of how he had visited multiple times to check her pulse without noticing anything, while Song Jinzhao figured it out after just one visit. He couldn't help but feel discouraged.","\"I started learning medicine at seven, finished my apprenticeship at twenty, and have practiced for nearly fifty years. Yet I couldn't even tell that a patient was taking the wrong medicine. I am truly incompetent; I've learned my medical skills in vain all these years.\"","Seeing him look up with a depressed face, Song Jinzhao comforted him, \"The person prescribing the medicine was very clever, and they used a cold as a smokescreen. It's completely normal that you didn't notice. The insidious methods of the inner courtyard are endless; it's not your fault.\"","Liu Xuanqing leaned against the carriage wall and shook his head. \"I know it's not my fault. It's just that after being a doctor for so many years and reaching this age, my medical skills are still so shallow. I feel like I haven't learned anything and have lived in vain. My heart feels empty.\"","Song Jinzhao's gaze softened, looking just like the mentor who guided her when she first started her hospital internship. Her tone carried a strong sense of guidance and instruction.","\"The path of medicine is vast, and learning it has no end. There is always someone better, and there are always higher mountains. As long as you have given it your all, you haven't lived in vain.\"","\"Besides, as far as I know, before I came, you were the best doctor in Anyang Prefecture. There's no need to belittle yourself.\"","Liu Xuanqing looked at Song Jinzhao helplessly. \"But Grandmaster, you are only seventeen, and I am already sixty. How can I not feel dealt a blow!\"","Song Jinzhao opened her mouth, hesitating to speak.","After a long pause, she explained, \"Although I am only seventeen, my mental age is older. I matured early.\""]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: Exterminating the Life-Taking Sect","paragraphs":["Returning to the clinic, Song Jinzhao called Qingshuang over and instructed, \"Tomorrow morning, spread the news about the Liao Manor's concubine plotting against the legal wife. Make sure Meng Hechuan finds out, but do it covertly.\"","Qingshuang nodded. \"This servant understands.\"","The next morning, right when the bustling market was at its most crowded, the news of the Liao Manor's concubine plotting against the legal wife, causing her to miscarry more than ten times, began to spread rapidly among the crowd.","By the time Liao Wangshu found out, the rumors had already spread through the streets and alleys.","Faced with the prying eyes of his colleagues at the government office, Liao Wangshu burned the official documents on his desk and rushed out with messy steps.","This matter quickly reached Meng Hechuan's ears.","He had previously thought that Liao Wangshu's wife and concubine had a harmonious relationship, but now it turned out they had a grudge. Since Concubine Su was dead, Kong Wanru was highly suspicious.","\"Someone, have Liao Wangshu come see me.\"","Liao Wangshu had barely stepped into his manor when he was summoned back by Meng Hechuan's order.","In the council chamber, faced with Meng Hechuan's inquiry, he had no choice but to explain the entire cause and effect of the matter.","He slapped his knee in frustration.","\"Family scandals should not be aired, and my cousin is already dead. This lowly official originally wanted to let the matter rest. Who knew it would spread out, causing such an uproar and troubling Your Excellency.\"","Meng Hechuan furrowed his brows. \"Have you ever thought that the one who hired the Suoming Sect to assassinate Concubine Su is very likely your wife?\"","Liao Wangshu looked up in horror. \"My wife only discovered the poison in the medicine yesterday. It couldn't possibly be her.\"","Meng Hechuan: \"What if she knew earlier?\"","Liao Wangshu shook his head in doubt: \"If that were true, my cousin is already dead, why would she expose the matter now!\"","Meng Hechuan: \"The truth is not yet known, but as long as there are doubts and clues, we can investigate.\"","With everything mixed together, Liao Wangshu's mind was a mess right now, and he was extremely annoyed.","After pondering for a long time, he stood up, cupped his hands, and pleaded, \"Your Excellency, accidents have been happening one after another in the manor, and everyone is already in a state of panic. If you go to question my wife again, who knows what the neighborhood will say.\"","\"As for the drugging, since my cousin is already dead, let's leave this matter at that.\"","\"As for who hired the assassin, why not wait until the Suoming Sect is wiped out and interrogate the one who did it? My wife's health is weak, she really can't handle the torment.\"","Meng Hechuan pondered for a moment before agreeing to Liao Wangshu's request.","\"In that case, we'll wait until the Suoming Sect is wiped out before questioning.\"","Liao Wangshu knelt and kowtowed. \"Thank you for your understanding, Your Excellency. This lowly official will not hesitate to die ten thousand times.\"","The dense sound of horse hooves rang out outside the door. Song Jinzhao put down the medicinal herbs and walked to the door, finding a cavalry unit galloping past on the street, holding high the banner of the Longbei Province garrison.","Not only that, overnight, many tents had appeared outside the city, and soldiers were drilling in the morning.","Looking at the government office's convoy delivering grain outside the city, Song Jinzhao instructed Lanxi, \"Go find out what's going on.\"","An hour later, Lanxi ran into the clinic covered in snow and wind.","Seeing that his head and body were covered in snow, Song Shixue handed him a long towel from the shelf.","\"Why didn't you use an umbrella? When the snow melts, it'll all be water, and you'll easily catch a cold.\"","Lanxi's arm paused slightly.","He unnaturally took the long towel, lowering his head to avoid Song Shixue's eyes. \"This lowly one is wearing several layers of clothes, I won't catch a cold.\"","Song Jinzhao looked at Lanxi. \"Did you find out clearly?\"","The long towel was tightly clenched in Lanxi's hand. He walked up to Song Jinzhao and said, \"Replying to Eldest Miss, this lowly one found a familiar bailiff to ask. He said the five lives in the Liao Manor were killed by a martial arts organization, and the government mobilized the army to wipe out the Suoming Sect.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow. Concubine Su's matter was only exposed yesterday, and they found out about the Suoming Sect so quickly?","\"Do you know exactly which assassin from the Suoming Sect it is?\"","Lanxi shook his head. \"The murderer dropped a token representing the identity of the Suoming Sect at the crime scene. It's not clear exactly who it is right now.\"","Song Jinzhao rubbed her chin in surprise. The token representing identity was so important, yet he happened to drop it.","This matter seemed bizarre no matter how you looked at it. Could it be intentional?","\"What about the location of the Suoming Sect? Didn't they say they've always been elusive like a divine dragon?\"","\"How many people are there in the assassin organization? The government troops outside the city look to be only over a thousand, can they win?\"","Lanxi leaned close to Song Jinzhao's ear and whispered, \"I heard that an anonymous righteous martial artist sent a letter to the government office. The information about the Suoming Sect in the letter was crystal clear, and even the appearance of the sect master was drawn.\"","Song Jinzhao lowered her eyes and chuckled silently. This matter was definitely done by that assassin.","Borrowing strength to strike, using the government's knife for revenge, he actually had the same idea as her.","On the morning two days later, led by a square-faced deputy general, the thousands of government troops stationed outside the city packed up and left Anyang City.","What surprised Song Jinzhao was that the sickly Eldest Young Master of the Liao Manor was actually among the marching troops.","At the end of the first lunar month, the vegetables in greenhouses four to six of the farm began to be harvested.","At the entrance of the restaurant, Li Tianchong looked at the workers unloading the goods and said to Song Jinzhao, \"Miss Song, I wonder when the third batch of vegetables will be available for sale. How about we sign the contract in advance?\"","Standing to the side, Li Zi'en had long admired Song Jinzhao to the point of prostrating in admiration.","In less than two months, the income was tens of thousands of taels.","Such incredible money-making ability was truly astonishing, yet others couldn't imitate it.","The ideas were all in Song Jinzhao's head, popping up one after another in an endless stream. Others couldn't steal them even if they wanted to.","Song Jinzhao smiled and said, \"The third batch will be twenty days later. If you sign now, you can get a ten percent discount.\"","In mid-February, the weather was still very cold. After a winter, the cabbage and radishes stored by every household were almost consumed, and vegetables would be even scarcer then.","Hearing that Song Jinzhao was offering a ten percent discount, Li Tianchong immediately ordered a hundred thousand catties of goods.","When the shopkeepers of other restaurants found out, they also signed the contracts in advance.","Chunxing, who was in charge of managing the vegetable shop, was very puzzled by this.","\"Eldest Miss, our vegetables obviously have no trouble selling, why offer a ten percent discount? We can sell them at the original price.\"","Song Jinzhao closed the box containing the contracts. \"Because in a few days, the winter vegetable planting technique will no longer be a secret. Everyone in the Dongzhao Kingdom will know. If we don't sign the contracts in advance, the price of vegetables will definitely plummet when the third batch is harvested.\"","Meng Hechuan had been personally brought to the farm by Lanxi to visit, and he immediately reacted. \"Is Eldest Miss referring to Prefect Meng?\"","Song Jinzhao nodded: \"I've already had Prefect Meng present the greenhouse construction method to the imperial court. There should be a result soon.\"","Lanxi thought of the breach of contract clause on the contract and suddenly realized.","\"So that's why you doubled the penalty for breach of contract, because you were worried they would default?\"","Song Jinzhao tapped the lid of the box backhandedly. \"With double the penalty, even if they want to default, we won't lose out.\"","The technique had been handed over, so they had to make a final profit and not let themselves lose money."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: The King of Qi with Malicious Intent","paragraphs":["Song Shixue sat on the threshold of the woodshed, looking dejected as she held Xuetuan, who had already grown to six pounds.","It wasn't obvious when its eyes were fully open, but now its deep blue, flame-like tiger eyes unconsciously drew toward the middle. It was undoubtedly cross-eyed.","She sadly rubbed her chin against the fur on top of the little tiger's head, feeling terrible.","Song Anhao stumbled over and handed a candied hawthorn stick to Song Shixue to comfort her.","\"Second Sister, don't be sad. I think Xuetuan is quite cute like this, looking all silly and adorable.\"","Song Shixue took the candied hawthorn but had no appetite to eat it.","\"I don't think it's ugly; my heart just aches for it.\"","\"Eldest Sister said that a tiger being cross-eyed will affect its vision. It won't be able to judge height or distance properly. It will choose to look at things with just one eye, and over time, the vision in the other eye will worsen, and it can't be cured.\"","Song Anhao rested his chin on his hand, pacing back and forth at the woodshed door like a little adult.","\"Then just cover its eyes and make it switch which eye it uses every day. That way, its eyes won't get worse.\"","Song Shixue blinked. \"That's actually a good idea. Why didn't I think of that?\"","Song Anhao put his hands on his hips and lifted his chin high. \"It means I'm smart. I'm a genius.\"","Song Shixue stood up and flicked his ear. \"Do you even know what a genius means?\"","Song Anhao tilted his head and widened his eyes. \"Of course I know. Someone like Eldest Sister is a genius. The grandpa and grandma living next door all say so.\"","He puffed out his chest and declared loudly, \"When I grow up, I want to be as amazing as Eldest Sister.\"","Song Shixue patted the top of his head, turned around to put Xuetuan back, and said, \"Then you have to work hard. Eldest Sister is good at so many things. You have to start learning from a young age. Start memorizing books and practicing martial arts tomorrow, and maybe you'll catch up to her.\"","Not knowing the hardships of studying and practicing martial arts, Song Anhao immediately raised his hand and promised, \"No problem, I'll start learning tomorrow.\"","So, early the next morning, Song Anhao purposely woke up early to exercise with Song Qiming and Song Shixue.","As a result, he collapsed on the ground in exhaustion after running only five laps around the garden, and he couldn't even hold the horse stance for half a cup of tea's time.","Before he even started reading, Song Shixue had only recited the Three Character Classic twice, and he was already getting sleepy, face-planting onto the small bed in the clinic to meet the Duke of Zhou in his dreams.","The Prince of Qi's Manor in the capital.","The guard in charge of tailing and tracking knelt down and reported, \"Your Highness, these are the movements of the Duke of Qing over the past half month. We haven't found him getting close to any officials in the court. It's all normal official business, and they are all military officers.\"","Xiao Rongche quickly flipped through the records. \"It seems that because Song Jinzhao helped him capture the Shuobei thieves, Chu Liuyun spoke up for her.\"","The guard asked, \"In that case, should we pull our men back?\"","Xiao Rongche threw the record book onto the table. \"Withdraw them.\"","\"Send someone to tell Yongjia the news that Chu Liuyun and Song Jinzhao have a close relationship. I shouldn't need to teach you how to say it!\"","The guard lowered his head. \"This subordinate understands.\"","Inside the Biluo Palace, Xiao Yongjia was sitting on the couch, intently embroidering the long river and bamboo forest in her hands.","Her delicate, fair fingers wove up and down the embroidery hoop. Looking at the gradually forming bamboo leaves, the corners of her mouth curled up like a newly blooming crabapple in spring, full of brightness and joy.","Two palace maids hurried in from outside. When they saw Xiao Yongjia's face full of smiles, they both slowed their steps.","The two exchanged a glance, both hesitating over whether to tell their master the matter.","After a long while, the maid with a coiled bun gritted her teeth, took a deep breath, walked to the couch, and whispered, \"Princess, recently there are rumors in the palace that the Duke of Qing has fallen for a commoner woman and even requested the Emperor to confer her a title.\"","\"Hiss!\" Xiao Yongjia quickly pulled her hand out from under the embroidery hoop, a bright red bead of blood welling up from the tip of her index finger.","\"Princess!\" The maid's face trembled, and she fell to her knees with a thud.","Xiao Yongjia pressed a handkerchief against the bleeding needle prick. \"It's fine. Who is this commoner woman you mentioned?\"","The maid lowered her gaze, not daring to look directly into Xiao Yongjia's eyes.","\"Her name is Song Jinzhao. I heard they met when she assisted the Duke of Qing in capturing the Shuobei thieves.\"","Xiao Yongjia's slender eyebrows furrowed slightly as she asked to confirm, \"Is it the woman who built the hydraulic chain pump?\"","The maid nodded and replied, \"That's her. According to the eunuchs at the Hall of Preserving Harmony, before the new year, Song Jinzhao came up with an idea to grow fresh fruits and vegetables in the dead of winter. The Emperor was extremely pleased and wanted to reward her.\"","The maid's voice grew softer and softer, her face almost sinking to the stone tiles.","\"Lord Fei of the Hanlin Academy proposed granting her a title, but the Prime Minister disagreed. The Duke of Qing hurriedly entered the palace to speak up for her, and in the end, the Emperor conferred Song Jinzhao the title of Lady Linghui.\"","\"People in the palace are saying that the Duke of Qing wants to elevate Song Jinzhao's status so that he can marry her when she arrives in the capital.\"","Xiao Yongjia clenched her fists, her nails digging into her palms until they turned red.","She subconsciously bit her lip, smudging her carefully applied pink lip rouge.","Xiao Yongjia's heart was in turmoil, a dozen different thoughts tangling together in her mind, making her completely unable to do anything else.","After pondering for nearly an hour, she stood up and walked outside. Thinking that court should not have dismissed yet, she took her attendants to wait outside the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","A loud, drawn-out announcement of the court's dismissal rang out, and the crowd poured out from the Hall of Supreme Harmony.","Xiao Yongjia and her personal maid eagerly searched the crowd for Chu Liuyun's figure.","Chu Liuyun, who was descending the steps, looked up and saw a familiar figure.","Their eyes met. He slowed his pace, gradually falling to the very back of the crowd.","After almost everyone had left, Chu Liuyun finally turned right and strode over, stopping in front of Xiao Yongjia.","\"This humble minister greets Your Royal Highness the Princess.\"","Xiao Yongjia raised her hand to signal him to dispense with the formalities, her peripheral vision drifting to the two personal maids standing beside her.","The two lowered their heads and tacitly led the others to wait a few paces away."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: Misunderstanding Resolved, the Imperial Decree Arrives","paragraphs":["She looked at Chu Liuyun with a gaze that was three parts nervous and seven parts afraid, terrified of hearing an unfavorable answer.","\"Brother Liuyun, I heard you met a woman you like in Xining City. Is it true?\"","Chu Liuyun raised his eyebrows in astonishment and asked in confusion, \"Xining City? What woman I like? Who? Who did you hear this from?\"","Seeing his blank expression, Xiao Yongjia felt he wasn't lying, and the heart suspended in her chest settled down just a bit.","\"Rumors in the palace say you've fallen for a woman named Song Jinzhao, and that's why you begged Imperial Father to confer upon her the title of Township Princess Linghui.\"","Chu Liuyun's eyes widened in disbelief. He never expected such rumors to spread, especially within the palace.","Realizing she had waited outside specifically for him today, Chu Liuyun hastily explained, \"I don't like her, and I wasn't the one who requested the Township Princess title.\"","\"Lord Fei from the Hanlin Academy proposed it first. I just happened to pass by, and when the Emperor learned I had met Song Jinzhao, he asked for my opinion. I merely put in a good word for her.\"","\"Song Jinzhao and I have only met two or three times. I don't like her at all.\" He repeated himself, afraid Xiao Yongjia wouldn't believe him.","Looking at his flustered explanation, the young girl turned her head and asked shyly, \"Then what kind of woman does Brother Liuyun like?\"","The cold wind blew Xiao Yongjia's dark hair against her cheeks, her flushed face tainted with a touch of pink.","Chu Liuyun said, \"I like someone who smiles with pure innocence, who has a kind heart. Someone who is usually quiet, gentle, and considerate, but gets a little fussy when things happen. Someone who thinks of me when she's happy, and tells me when she's sad.\"","He paused slightly, his gaze fixed firmly on a small mole near the upper part of the young girl's cheek.","\"It would be best if she had a small mole on both her left and right cheeks. That would look especially cute.\"","Xiao Yongjia froze before the realization hit her. The joy in her eyes grew so intense it nearly overflowed like water. She bit her lip hard, barely managing to suppress the corners of her mouth from rising.","\"Oh—I suddenly remembered that Imperial Mother was looking for me. I'll take my leave first.\"","The young girl's heart pounded like a beating drum. Too shy to even look at Chu Liuyun, she grabbed her skirt and quickly ran off.","The fluttering hem of her skirt transformed into a sky full of flowers, scattering over Chu Liuyun's heart.","He lowered his head and smiled softly. There were only six months left until her sixteenth birthday; it was time to start preparing for certain things in advance.","Upon returning to the palace, Xiao Yongjia picked up the embroidery resting on her couch and happily took up her needle to continue sewing.","She had two small moles on her face. Brother Liuyun was talking about her!","After only a few stitches, she put down the embroidery again and walked over to her dressing table, carefully examining herself in the bronze mirror.","As her smile deepened, the two raised cherry-like moles appeared exceptionally bright, completely revealing the young girl's inner thoughts.","The army responsible for annihilating the Life-Claiming Sect had not yet returned, but the decree-bearing eunuch, having completed a series of complex procedures, arrived at Anyang Prefecture a step ahead of them.","\"Eldest Miss, many officials have arrived outside! They say they are from the palace, here to read an imperial decree!\"","The servants had just opened the estate gates in the morning when they saw soldiers clearing the way not far off, beating gongs and drums, looking incredibly solemn and dignified.","Just as the servant girl stood at the door watching the spectacle, she never expected the group to head straight toward her, stopping right at the entrance of the Song Estate.","The official bearing the decree stunned the maidservant with just a few words. She hastily curtsied in apology, turned, and ran back inside.","Running and shouting along the way, her voice reached the inner courtyard, alerting the entire household.","Song Qiming, who was drinking porridge, suddenly choked. Coughing twice and clutching his throat, he said, \"Sister, could it be~?\"","Factoring in the distance and time, it was a few days later than they had anticipated.","Song Jinzhao used a handkerchief to wipe the steamed egg custard off Song Anhao's face. \"Let's go out and see.\"","The Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites, dressed in his official uniform, saw a young woman leading the way out of the house. Having seen her portrait beforehand, he recognized at a glance that this person was Song Jinzhao.","Sweeping his gaze from top to bottom, the Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites was somewhat startled by the confidence and composure exuding from Song Jinzhao.","Her bright eyes held a sharpness and steadiness unlike ordinary women, and her back, straight as a pine, surpassed countless noble scions in the capital.","With just one glance, one could see her uniqueness. Though young, she possessed the majesty and aura of a head of the household, a trait typically exclusive to men.","Lanxi led people to bring over the incense altar. As curling smoke rose, the Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites took the imperial decree from the yellow silk box and unrolled it.","He raised his voice and shouted, \"Song Jinzhao, receive the decree!\"","Having received an imperial decree once before, Song Qiming and Song Shixue lifted their robes and knelt down with relative calm.","On the contrary, Qingshuang and the others kneeling at the very back felt extremely anxious and uneasy.","Please don't let it be bad news.","\"By the grace of Heaven, the Emperor decrees: The Song family's daughter, Song Jinzhao, is innately intelligent, outstanding in talent and virtue, and has repeatedly achieved extraordinary merits. Our heart is greatly comforted. We hereby confer upon her the title of Township Princess Linghui, grant her a mandate of honor, and she shall enjoy a stipend according to the regulations. Respect this!\"","Chunxing, Qingshuang, and the others widened their eyes in shock. Not daring to look up, they could only stare at the ground, their eyes darting wildly.","Township Princess! The Eldest Miss has been titled a Township Princess!!!","Song Jinzhao looked up and received the decree with both hands. \"Thank you, Your Majesty, for your profound grace. Long live the Emperor, long live, long long live!\"","The eunuch standing to the side, seeing that the decree had been read, stepped forward and respectfully handed the lacquer tray containing the official mandate robes to Song Jinzhao.","\"Congratulations, Township Princess Linghui. This is your auspicious attire. If the Emperor summons you in the future, or if you attend a palace night banquet, you may wear this robe for your audience.\"","\"Many thanks, Eunuch.\" Song Jinzhao took the tray and handed it to Song Qiming, who was kneeling beside her.","A cyan brocade sleeved shirt and long skirt, along with two stoles embroidered with magpie motifs folded in a cross, lay there. The exquisite floral embroidery looked incredibly lifelike; at a glance, it was clearly the work of palace embroiderers.","Watching the officials and eunuchs leave on horseback, Chunxing and the others leaned their right hands against the doorframe, their legs turning to jelly.","Fushun lived at the farmstead. Among the five servants present, the calmest was actually the youngest, Lanxi.","The neighbors only dared to come out and see what had happened after the people had left.","Song Shixue picked up a scroll placed on the right side of the lacquer tray and unrolled it.","The decree paper was a full meter long, stamped with numerous red official seals.","Pointing to the two characters on the far right of the scroll, Song Shixue asked, \"What is a Gaoshen?\"","Song Qiming handed the tray to Qingshuang and leaned close to Song Shixue to see what was written on the scroll.","\"A Gaoshen is Sister's letter of appointment as a Township Princess. It proves her identity. She will need to bring this every year when she goes to the government office to collect her annual stipend.\"","Song Shixue's eyes widened in pleasant surprise.","She buried her head and carefully read the words on it, then looked up in confusion. \"Why doesn't it say how much the annual stipend is?\"","Song Qiming said, \"They usually don't write it. Sister is a primary seventh-rank Township Princess, so her annual stipend should be eighty shi of rice.\"","Song Shixue began to calculate mentally on her fingers.","One mu of medium-grade paddy field can yield one shi of unhusked rice, which is about seven dou of husked rice.","Eighty shi of rice was equivalent to the yield of one hundred and fourteen mu of medium-grade paddy fields, and it was tax-free. This was simply too much!"]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Meng Hechuan: Am I Just a Pawn in Their Scheme","paragraphs":["\"What! Song Jinzhao was bestowed the title of Lady Linghui?\" Li Tianchong stood up from his chair in disbelief, accidentally pulling out two hairs from his beard, making him grimace in pain.","The news came too suddenly. Why would they bestow an official title upon a commoner girl out of nowhere?","Unlike a regular reward, this was an official mandate with a rank.","Li Zien nodded vigorously, \"It's spread all over the city now. The ones who came to read the decree are an official from the Ministry of Rites and a palace eunuch. They are staying at the post house.\"","Li Tianchong paced back and forth in the hall, full of doubts. \"Why the title? What is the reason? It must be for a great merit, otherwise the Emperor would not issue such a decree.\"","Li Zien shook his head, \"I don't know. The Song family's shop didn't open today, and even their medical clinic is closed.\"","Inside the post house, Peng Mu, Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites, was sitting and drinking with the Prefect of Anyang.","Meng Hechuan picked up his wine cup, took a sip, and asked curiously, \"Lord Peng, how did the Emperor come to think of bestowing Song Jinzhao with a title? For a commoner woman, this is a rare favor.\"","He knew that once his memorial was submitted, the Emperor would definitely reward Song Jinzhao.","He had assumed it would be some gold and silver jewelry, silks, decorative items, or perhaps another plaque to bring honor to her family. He never expected an official title.","This meant that Song Jinzhao's status would be completely different from now on.","Peng Mu jokingly raised his cup and flattered him, \"Lord Meng, why must you speak such pleasantries in front of me?\"","\"With the help of Lord Fei and the Duke of Qing, it would be hard for the Emperor not to agree. Once Lord Ye is restored to his former post in the future, you will surely be promoted!\"","\"Ah?\" Meng Hechuan uttered in astonishment.","He was completely baffled. What was all this about? Why couldn't he understand a word of it?","\"Lord Peng, why do you say this? What does this have to do with Lord Fei and the Duke of Qing?\"","Peng Mu's hand paused while holding the cup, \"Wasn't this something you and Lord Ye had already discussed and agreed upon?\"","Meng Hechuan frowned, even more confused. \"Agreed upon what?\"","Seeing that Meng Hechuan seemed genuinely unaware, Peng Mu set down his cup and spoke seriously, \"As soon as you submitted the memorial requesting a reward for Song Jinzhao, Lord Fei of the Hanlin Academy proposed to the Emperor that she be granted a title, and even the Duke of Qing spoke up in her favor.\"","\"Fei Yanzhang and Ye Liangyu are sworn brothers, and Song Jinzhao is the elder sister of Lord Ye's beloved disciple. Was all of this not planned by you all in advance?\"","Meng Hechuan sat frozen on his stool. Thinking back to how Song Jinzhao had specifically had her servant hand the letter to him, he blinked, and the chaotic thoughts in his mind began to sort themselves out one by one.","They were just missing a spark, waiting for him to submit the memorial.","Noticing his strange expression, Peng Mu asked softly, \"Was this really not your intention?\"","Meng Hechuan felt a complex mix of emotions. He had unknowingly become a link in someone else's scheme, and he had jumped in willingly.","His mouth twitched. He awkwardly picked up his chopsticks to grab some food while forcing a fake smile.","\"I am but a mere prefect; how could I have such great ability? Song Jinzhao has repeatedly achieved extraordinary merits. She deserves this title, and I suppose Lord Fei and the Duke of Qing thought the same.\"","Ye Liangyu had a terrible relationship with the two princes in the court, and he didn't know which side this Vice Director of the Ministry of Rites stood on, so it was best to distance himself from the matter.","Peng Mu suddenly realized that this matter actually had nothing to do with Meng Hechuan.","His expression softened. He raised his wine cup and praised, \"Over the years, Lord Meng has achieved remarkable political success in Anyang Prefecture. Even without relying on Lord Ye, I'm sure you are not far from a promotion. Allow me to offer you a toast in advance.\"","Knowing that Song Jinzhao had been granted the title of Lady Linghui, Song Gaoli, who had finally gotten a day off, came over that afternoon carrying pastries bought from the Sweet Snow Pavilion to congratulate her.","Looking at the imperial decree enshrined on the incense altar, Song Gaoli shook his head in admiration, his eyes shining brightly.","\"You haven't even become an official yet, and Sister Jinzhao already has an official rank. It's simply unimaginable!\"","Song Qiming looked up at the bright yellow imperial decree resting in its casket.","\"That's why my sister is amazing. No matter what it is, as long as she wants to do it, she will definitely achieve it.\"","Song Gaoli turned his head and asked in confusion, \"So why did the Emperor grant Sister Jinzhao a title this time? Wasn't she already rewarded for the waterwheel matter last time?\"","After so much time had passed, they surely wouldn't reward her again for the same thing.","Song Qiming withdrew his gaze, the smile in his eyes fading a little. \"My sister presented the method of off-season planting to the imperial court.\"","\"Ah? Then won't you lose a way to make money in the future?\"","Song Gaoli knew how good the business at the Song family's vegetable shop had been these past few days. The expensive vegetable prices definitely brought in a lot of money.","Song Qiming turned around and sat on a stool. \"My sister said that no matter how much money we make, it cannot compare to power. The estate is just outside the city; no matter how strictly we guard it, we wouldn't be able to keep it a secret for long. It's better to just present it to the court to benefit the country and the people.\"","Song Gaoli thought about it and felt it made sense. He plopped down and said, \"If you ask me, Sister Jinzhao is the one with foresight. Otherwise, where would this title of Lady Linghui come from?\"","\"Anyway, your family isn't short of money now. It's good to present it for merit, saving yourselves from being targeted by others. If someone else found out and presented it to the court first, this immense credit would be gone.\"","During dinner that evening, not only did Ye Liangyu come, but even Academy Director Mu Hongyue brought gifts to offer his congratulations.","Brought over by their father to offer congratulations, Liu Renyi and Liu Renzong secretly nudged Liu Xuanqing's arm.","\"Father, acknowledging this grandmaster was definitely the right choice.\""]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: Off-Season Planting Method Revealed, Regretful Subscribers","paragraphs":["Meng Hechuan looked at the tightly closed gates of the Song Manor. Frowning slightly, he ordered his subordinate to knock.","In the kitchen, two maidservants were cooking. Hearing the knock, they looked outside in confusion.","\"Who would come visiting right at noon?\"","One of them set down the vegetables in her hands and wiped them clean with a cloth. \"Watch the fire, I'll go take a look.\"","Opening the manor gates, she saw the visitor dressed in official robes, flanked by yamen runners. The maid was stunned for a moment before immediately kneeling.","\"This servant greets Your Excellency.\"","Meng Hechuan said, \"Rise. Is the Township Lady at home?\"","The maid stood up and hurriedly opened the double doors to their widest.","Bending her knees slightly and keeping her head bowed, she answered, \"Eldest Miss went to the clinic. She won't be back for another half an hour.\"","\"She still went to the clinic?\" She was already a Township Lady, yet she still treated patients?","He stepped over the threshold. \"No matter, I shall simply sit and wait.\"","After inviting the guests into the main hall, the maid quickly ran into the kitchen. \"Qingshui, the Prefect has arrived. Hurry and serve tea, I will go to the clinic to call Eldest Miss back.\"","About half an hour later, Song Jinzhao returned in her carriage.","She walked into the main hall with a smile. \"The clinic was closed yesterday, so there were quite a few patients today. I have kept you waiting, Lord Meng.\"","Meng Hechuan stood up, clasped his hands, and bowed deeply to Song Jinzhao. \"It is I who lacked courtesy by not sending a calling card in advance. I did not expect that the Township Lady would still go to the clinic today.\"","Although Song Jinzhao's rank as a Township Lady was the primary seventh grade, and Meng Hechuan's rank as a Prefect was the primary fifth grade, one was a title bestowed by the Emperor, while the other was an official appointment by the imperial court. In terms of etiquette, nobility outranked officialdom, so he had to bow when seeing Song Jinzhao.","Song Jinzhao curtsied slightly to return the greeting. \"Regardless of my status, I am still a doctor. May I ask what brings Lord Meng here today?\"","Meng Hechuan raised his head and signaled his subordinate to present the gifts. \"I came this time, firstly, to congratulate Miss Song on being granted the title of Township Lady Linghui by the Emperor.\"","\"Secondly, to have your annual stipend for the first half of this year brought over. It is forty piculs of rice in total, all newly harvested grain from the latter half of last year.\"","\"In our dynasty, the annual stipend is collected in two installments. When the second half of the year arrives, the Township Lady can send a servant or steward to the yamen to collect it.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at the wooden box. Inside lay an exquisite white porcelain vase. Judging by the patterns, it was likely from a famous kiln, valued at around twenty or thirty taels of silver.","She signaled Qingshuang with her eyes to accept it. \"There is no need for Your Excellency to go to such expense next time. The thought itself is enough.\"","Seeing Song Jinzhao accept the gift, Meng Hechuan pondered for a moment before saying, \"There is one more thing. The Emperor has already ordered the popularization of out-of-season fruit and vegetable cultivation. Taking advantage of the fact that winter is not yet over, I wish to lead by example and guide the people of Anyang City to grow a batch first. We currently lack an experienced hand. Could the Township Lady lend me the steward named Fushun from your estate for a few days?\"","Song Jinzhao smiled warmly. \"It is his blessing to be highly regarded by Your Excellency. There is still half a month before the final batch of vegetables at the estate is ready for harvest. You must return him by then.\"","Seeing her agree so readily, the slight dissatisfaction Meng Hechuan felt toward Song Jinzhao for scheming against him completely dissipated.","\"Naturally. It won't take half a month; ten days will suffice.\"","Staring at the newly released methods for out-of-season fruit and vegetable cultivation on the notice board, along with the trial planting registration rules posted by the yamen, Li Zien nearly spat out a mouthful of blood on the spot.","The farmers he had hired hadn't even sneaked into Song Jinzhao's farm yet, and this secret was already announced to the whole world. It was simply appalling.","Deflated, he returned home and recounted the news to his father.","Li Tianchong's brows furrowed deeply. He abruptly turned, rushed into the study, and pulled out the signed contracts from the drawer.","Seeing the doubled penalty fee for breach of contract written on them, he pounded the desk in deep remorse.","\"Why didn't I think of this at the time? She had planned this all along.\"","Originally, for vegetables that were impossible to get even if you fought for them, it didn't matter how high the penalty fee was, because they would never breach the contract anyway.","Looking at it now, every step she took had an ulterior motive.","She was worried that once the cultivation methods were popularized and everyone knew how to grow them, no one would be willing to buy her vegetables at a high price anymore. That was why she set the penalty fee so high.","Watching his father's reaction, Li Zien instantly understood as well. \"Father, what do we do now? We've already paid the money!\"","Li Tianchong tossed the contracts onto the desk and sat heavily in his chair.","\"What else can we do? We can only swallow this bitter pill.\"","\"Fortunately, the newly planted vegetables won't grow that fast. Keep an eye on the situation at the various restaurants. If the customers find it too expensive, we will lower the price. We'll just have to settle for earning a little less.\"","\"Also, send someone to the yamen to register immediately. Don't let others beat us to it.\"","It was exactly as Song Jinzhao had expected.","After the notice was posted, more than half of the merchants who had signed contracts in advance regretted it. Had they known, they would have waited until the vegetables were harvested to buy them.","But they did not dare seek out Song Jinzhao.","Two days ago, they would have definitely run to the Song family's shop to pick a fight, forcing Song Jinzhao to lower the price and sign new contracts.","But now she was a Township Lady. They had no choice but to grit their teeth and swallow their grievances."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Wives and Concubines in Conflict: The Most Venomous is a Woman's Heart","paragraphs":["Three days after the notice was posted, Meng Hechuan sat in the government office holding a registration list that barely filled a single page, feeling extremely irritated.","\"Why are they all tenant farmers? Haven't any ordinary peasants signed up?\"","The head runner bowed his body, looking troubled as he said, \"My Lord, the oiled paper needed to build the vegetable greenhouses costs money, and many commoners find it too expensive.\"","Meng Hechuan narrowed his eyes and frowned. \"It's no longer as freezing as the dead of winter. Didn't the notice state that those without money could spread thatch on the ground for insulation, use reed and rice stalks to erect windbreaks, and substitute straw mats for oiled paper? Every household has these things. If they don't have to buy oiled paper, why do they still think it's expensive?\"","The head runner's shoulders slumped as he explained with a bitter expression, \"My Lord, many of the rice stalks left over from last year's autumn harvest were eaten by pigs and sheep over the winter. The rest were composted and buried in the fields. If they really had to scrape some together, they would have to tear down their roofs and rip up their mattresses.\"","\"Furthermore, spring begins in just a month and a half. Many people say they will wait until the beginning of winter next year to plant, avoiding the two coldest months. By planting two crops back-to-back, they will have enough to eat through the winter.\"","Meng Hechuan set down the list in astonishment. Not even having straw—he truly hadn't considered that.","Tapping his fingers continuously on the desk, he pondered for a long while before saying, \"Since that is the case, all the runners in the government office must participate in this trial planting. They must learn every single detail from start to finish.\"","\"Most of the farmers are illiterate, so there will definitely be many problems when planting vegetables in the winter. When the time comes, have these runners go door-to-door to teach them, lest they sow the seeds but fail to grow any vegetables.\"","The head runner bowed his head in compliance. \"Yes, I will give the orders immediately.\"","...","Watching the cavalry galloping past on the street, some of the men still had blood on them.","Qingshuang stood beside Song Jinzhao and whispered, \"Eldest Miss, those should be the troops sent to annihilate the Life-Claiming Sect. It looks like they succeeded.\"","Song Jinzhao tilted her head and instructed in a low voice, \"How did the annihilation go? Did they capture anyone and bring them back? Have Lanxi go and ask around.\"","Qingshuang nodded. \"Understood.\"","An hour after leaving, Lanxi returned to the medical clinic carrying a bag of chestnuts.","\"Originally, they caught seven survivors and even captured the sect leader of the Life-Claiming Sect alive. But on the way back, he killed his seven subordinates and escaped by himself. By the time they found him, he had already fallen off a cliff to his death.\"","Song Jinzhao's eyes, as clear as winter snow, shifted slightly.","The leader of an assassin organization must possess highly advanced martial arts. Having finally managed to escape, how could he fall to his death for no reason?","It must have been the work of that assassin who was poisoned with the Gu toxin. He was seeking revenge.","Inside the government office, Meng Hechuan sat in his chair with a distressed expression. With no survivors, how was he supposed to investigate the Liao family's case?","Who exactly was the true mastermind behind Concubine Su's death?","\"Men, inform Lord Liao to send all the maids and servants from his wife's courtyard over tonight. I will interrogate them one by one. Also, bring over the one who administered the poison previously.\"","The next day, Song Jinzhao went to the Liao residence for her usual medical consultation, but before she could enter, she was stopped by the Liao family's steward.","He knelt on the ground, explaining subserviently, \"To reply to the Township Princess, my lord has ordered the residence to close its doors and decline all guests for these few days. Please trouble yourself to come back in a few days.\"","Just as Song Jinzhao was about to leave, she heard people arguing inside. It sounded like the voices of Liao Xiwen and her father.","On her way back, she passed by a clinic and happened to see government runners escorting someone out, with quite a few commoners watching at the door.","In the gloomy dungeon, Meng Hechuan stared at the bright red fingerprints on the confession, his heart sinking to the bottom of a cliff.","The true mastermind hadn't been interrogated out of them, but everything else had been spilled completely.","Indeed, nothing is more venomous than a woman's heart.","Thinking of the Guo residence previously, and looking at the Liao residence now, it was a good thing he hadn't taken any concubines and his wife was his first spouse; otherwise, his heart would truly be in a panic.","Summoned to the government office, Liao Wangshu flipped through the confessions on the table one by one, his entire complexion changing.","Meng Hechuan said, \"This is how things stand. Concubine Su's three miscarriages were caused by your wife, and your wife's twelve miscarriages were caused by Concubine Su.\"","Looking at the doctor's confession regarding Concubine Su taking medicine to induce premature birth, resulting in the fetus being underdeveloped, physically frail, and plagued by illness, Liao Wangshu was so full of hatred that his teeth nearly shattered from clenching.","He only had this one son, and he never expected his illness came about this way.","In order to be the first to give birth to the eldest son, she truly resorted to any means necessary. It was foolish to the extreme.","After finishing reading the confessions, Liao Wangshu sat in his chair and remained silent for a long time.","Meng Hechuan could understand his feelings at this moment and sat quietly, waiting for him to digest the information.","It was unknown how much time had passed before Liao Wangshu lifted his head, looking as if he had aged more than ten years all at once.","He spoke in a heavy tone, \"My Lord, my cousin is already dead. I do not wish to pursue the matters she committed any further.\"","\"As for my wife, although she is at fault, she is also a victim. Family scandals should not be spread outside. For the matters of the inner residence, I ask Your Lordship to allow me to handle them myself.\"","Meng Hechuan replied, \"The murder of Concubine Su likely has nothing to do with your wife. The Life-Claiming Sect has already been annihilated. Without witnesses, we cannot track down the true mastermind. I am afraid this case will become an unsolved mystery.\"","Liao Wangshu tightly gripped the confession, sighing as he spoke exhaustedly, \"Having committed so many wicked deeds, her death is not to be pitied. Thank you, My Lord, for your hard work these past few days. I do not wish to pursue this case any further.\"","Meng Hechuan nodded in satisfaction. His efforts on this case hadn't been entirely in vain.","At the very least, he had used this opportunity to annihilate a wicked martial arts assassin organization, establishing the majesty of the imperial court.","If any martial artists dared to make a move again, they would have to be more cautious. From now on, murder cases of this nature should decrease significantly."]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: The Heartbroken Daughter and the Heartless Mother","paragraphs":["When Song Jinzhao visited again three days later, she found that all the servants and maids in the Spring Water Courtyard were unfamiliar faces. Two guards stood outside the courtyard gate, and even Liao Xiwen was nowhere to be seen.","Looking at Kong Wanru lying on the bed, she seemed as if her soul had been drained away. Her dark eyes were hollow and lifeless, and her whole body exuded a deathly aura of lost hope.","Just as she set down her medicine chest, Kong Wanru's voice reached her ears.","Doctor Song, you do not need to come here anymore.","Song Jinzhao turned around and looked at her. You do not want to get pregnant anymore?","The corners of the woman's mouth curled into an extremely faint smile, hard to tell if it was self-deprecation or bitterness.","It is the same whether I am treated or not. I will never be able to have my own child again. What is the point of being able to give birth?","Just like this dark and sunless Spring Water Courtyard, she would never be able to leave until she died of old age.","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows, feeling dissatisfied. Is Liao Xiwen not your child?","Kong Wanru weakly closed her eyes. A daughter will eventually be married off. She cannot inherit the family property, so having one is the same as not having one.","Song Jinzhao rolled her eyes to the heavens, decisively picked up her medicine chest, and left. You deserve to never have a son in this lifetime.","Not long after walking out of the Spring Water Courtyard, Song Jinzhao bumped into Liao Xiwen near the rockery.","Miss Song... no, she quickly curtsied and greeted, Greetings, Lady of the County.","Song Jinzhao noticed the dark circles under her eyes and her somewhat sallow complexion, clear signs that she had not slept well.","Did you not take the soothing medicine I prescribed for you?","A wave of bitterness rose in Liao Xiwen's throat as she forced out, I was upset, so I did not take it.","May I ask, Lady, how is my mother's illness? I heard from the new maids that she has not eaten for the past two days.","Song Jinzhao asked, You did not go to see her?","Liao Xiwen shook her head, her eyes growing slightly moist. My father said that my mother made a mistake and will not let me see her. He even replaced all the servants in the Spring Water Courtyard. There are guards at the door, so I cannot get in.","Song Jinzhao blinked, having already guessed most of what happened.","It was likely that Concubine Su's multiple miscarriages were the work of Kong Wanru.","Now that the truth had come to light, not only was her marital relationship shattered, but Kong Wanru was also imprisoned in her courtyard, which was why she no longer wanted treatment.","Your mother harbors a death wish and told me not to come anymore. Without a son, she does not want to live.","Tears welling in her eyes, Liao Xiwen stood blankly on the spot. Even until Song Jinzhao's figure disappeared from her sight, she did not move an inch, as if she had been frozen.","Without a son she did not want to live, so did that mean she, her daughter, was not important to her at all?","After being titled as the Lady of the County, the pace of Song Jinzhao's life did not change much.","The only difference was that commoners would kneel and bow before speaking to her, respectfully addressing her as Lady before daring to rise.","As the weather gradually warmed up, Song Jinzhao had the manor's servants transplant all the flowers in the garden into pots, and then tilled the soil.","When Song Qiming returned from the academy and saw the uneven, dug-up garden, he curiously asked Song Jinzhao what she was doing.","The farm is outside the city, too far away to conveniently check on at any time, so I plan to plant the potatoes in the garden.","Thinking of that pile of sprouted potatoes brought all the way from Xining City, many had already died.","Song Qiming looked worried. I saw that many of the sprouts have withered. Can they still survive?","Song Jinzhao nodded. Some that are greenish on the surface and haven't fully sprouted should be able to survive. About half of the ones that sprouted earlier still look viable. Let's plant them first and see.","It was precisely because there were not many that she did not dare to plant them at the farm and leave them entirely to the servants.","With only this small amount of seeds, if they were all ruined, it would probably be difficult to find more.","She did not yet want to take a sheepskin map and cross the ocean in search of a new continent.","Song Qiming lowered his voice and confirmed with Song Jinzhao, Sister, can these potatoes really yield over a thousand catties per mu?","He had asked several times, always feeling it was too surreal.","The yield of rice per mu was one shi, which was only about one hundred and sixty catties. He dared not even imagine what a concept of over a thousand catties was.","Song Jinzhao gave him a positive answer once again. You will know once they are grown.","After the last batch of greenhouse vegetables was harvested, Song Jinzhao had people dismantle the greenhouses and start tilling the land.","They scattered a layer of plant ash to prevent pests and diseases and supplement potassium fertilizer, waiting until the weather warmed up in April to start planting peanuts."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu Failed the Preliminary Examination","paragraphs":["Zhang Yuanzong, the magistrate of Xining City, held the official document just sent from Anyang Prefecture in both hands, his eyes falling on the two preliminary exam papers placed on the desk.","One was barely passable, while the other was completely unreadable; he felt it dirtied his eyes just to glance at it.","\"They are all cousins. Song Qiming was able to test all the way to the top of the list, so why are these two having such a hard time even passing the preliminary county exam? I want to do them a favor, but I cannot even find a way to do it!\"","The advisor, standing to the side with a bowed posture, spoke tactfully, \"A dragon has nine sons, and each is different, let alone cousins. The brother personally taught by Lady Linghui is naturally going to be different.\"","Zhang Yuanzong put down the official document and leaned back in his chair, his mind exhausted.","\"Never mind this Song Yaozu, but tell me, should I let Song Yongnian pass the preliminary exam?\"","The advisor asked in return, \"Does Your Honor think that if we force him through the preliminary exam, he will be able to pass the second round?\"","Zhang Yuanzong's eyes widened, and he blurted out without the slightest hesitation, \"That is definitely impossible. If I forcibly push him through and it gets discovered, it would be considered cheating.\"","The advisor nodded in agreement, \"In my humble opinion, since he cannot pass the second round, we should not let him slide on the preliminary exam either.\"","He raised his hands to indicate two different heights. \"Failing by this much is different from failing by that much.\"","\"If he fails the preliminary exam, Lady Linghui will not say much, but if he fails the second round, she might actually come to Your Honor for a favor.\"","Zhang Yuanzong suddenly understood. \"What you say makes sense.\"","He closed the exam papers and handed them over. \"In that case, let us forget it. After all, Song Jinzhao did not come looking for me anyway.\"","\"Wait until the second round is over, and then I will take some people to the Song family to offer congratulations, so as to avoid them asking me about the exam results.\"","The list of those who passed the preliminary exam was posted on the wall at the entrance of the county office. Oldest Song, Second Song, and his wife led their children and read it from beginning to end three times, but they could not find the names of Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu on it.","Despite feeling incredibly disappointed, Oldest Song patted Song Yongnian's shoulder comfortingly. \"It is alright. You can take the exam again next year. This time was just testing the waters anyway.\"","Song Yongnian lowered his head in disappointment as he was led out of the crowd. His throat choked up, and his eyes were already red.","\"Father, I will definitely pass next year.\"","Oldest Song replied, \"Father believes in you.\"","Under the posted list, Second Song slapped Song Yaozu heavily on the back and said angrily, \"You have studied for two years and could not even pass the preliminary exam. I paid your tuition for these two years for nothing.\"","Song Yaozu was hit so hard he pitched forward, and Second Aunt Song quickly grabbed his hand tightly.","The people standing nearby turned to look at them, their eyes showing disdain.","Second Aunt Song pushed Second Song's back with her hand. \"Yaozu is still young, and it is his first time. If he did not pass, he can just take it again next time. Why are you hitting him?\"","Having finally squeezed out of the crowd, Second Song turned around with his hands on his hips. \"Qiming passed at the age of eleven after studying for one year. You are ten and have studied for two years, so why could you not pass? You could not even pass the preliminary exam. All that studying went straight into a dog's belly!\"","Second Aunt Song frowned and stopped him. \"Why are you speaking so loudly? Are you afraid others will not hear you? Let us go home. Stop making a fool of yourself in public.\"","Being scolded, Second Song's eyes widened larger than a bull's, and he panted heavily in anger.","Seeing that he was angry and refused to leave, Second Aunt Song leaned in and whispered, \"Yaozu is not the only one who did not pass. Yongnian's name is not up there either.\"","Second Song's eyes lit up. \"Really?\"","\"Of course. I checked it twice. It is definitely not there.\" Second Aunt Song stuffed the slip of paper with the two names into Second Song's hand.","Second Song's anger subsided a little. He held his breath and took a deep breath to comfort himself.","Song Gaoli studied for three years before he passed the exams to become a scholar. It has only been two years, so it is normal not to pass. Maybe he will pass next year.","Waiting for news at home, Old Man Song was so anxious that he had no appetite for breakfast. He kept pacing back and forth at the door of the old house, waiting for them to return.","His pacing even made Old Lady Song, who was sitting on a small stool holding Song Yongshi, feel her heart pounding.","\"You keep walking around. Why did you not go with them this morning?\"","Old Man Song turned around and said, \"Both the husband and wife went, and you have to watch the child at home. An old man like me would just be an eyesore if I tagged along.\"","As the two were talking, familiar footsteps reached their ears.","Old Man Song hurriedly turned his head to look down the road.","He saw the six members of the first and second branches of the family walking down the road with their heads bowed, looking very grim.","His heart skipped a beat, suddenly feeling that something was wrong.","Did they fail the preliminary exam?"]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Zhang Yuanzong Visits to Offer Congratulations, Astonishing the Song Family","paragraphs":["As he approached, he rushed up and asked, \"How did it go? Did they pass the preliminary exam?\"","Oldest Song raised his head and shook it. His face looked suppressed, and his voice was low, accompanied by a heavy sigh that seemed to weigh a thousand pounds.","\"Yongnian and Yaozu's names are not on the list.\"","Old Man Song stumbled backward. Although he had prepared himself for this, he still felt an empty void inside.","He took a deep breath and forced a smile. \"It's fine. Scholar Zheng said this time was just for practice. The main focus is next year.\"","They originally thought that even if the boys didn't pass the main exam, they would at least pass the preliminaries. Failing even the preliminaries meant they were far from becoming child scholars.","For an entire day, the rooms of the two Song family branches were eerily quiet, with hardly anyone speaking.","As soon as Song Yongnian returned, he locked himself in his room to read. Tears rolled down from his eyes onto the paper. He quickly tried to wipe them away with his sleeve, eventually soaking the fabric completely.","In the second branch's courtyard, Song Laidi walked out carrying a wooden bucket full of laundry. She was still wearing the clothes Song Jinzhao had given her for the New Year.","Song Pandi, following beside her with a basin, looked disappointed as she muttered softly, \"I knew he wouldn't pass, but I didn't expect him to actually fail.\"","Song Laidi stopped in her tracks. She turned her head to look through the window. Song Yaozu was sitting at the table, chewing on the end of his brush. Not a trace of sorrow over failing the exam could be seen on his face; instead, he looked completely indifferent.","How could this not make someone angry?","In order to support his studies, the family ate worse than before. After two years of paying for his education, this was the result. At this rate, he probably wouldn't pass next year either.","\"Grandpa only promised to subsidize three years of tuition. If he doesn't pass next year, Dad won't let him continue studying.\"","Cutting back on food and clothing with no return to show for it—the one who absolutely couldn't stand this the most was the usually lazy Second Song.","The heavy atmosphere between the two branches of the Song family lasted for two whole days before it finally eased a bit.","Having bragged so much outside before the exam, Second Song and his wife didn't leave the house for three consecutive days, afraid of being mocked by the villagers.","The weather cleared up and temperatures began to warm. Every household started repairing their farm tools in preparation for the upcoming spring plowing.","A piercing sound of gongs and drums came from the village entrance, shattering the peace of Song Family Village.","As the sound grew louder, people stepped out of their homes one after another, wanting to see what was happening.","As the seventh-grade county magistrate's procession entered the village, with gongs and drums clearing the way and three groups of yamen runners surrounding the official sedan chair, the roadsides fell into a dead silence.","Why was there another high official coming to the village? What were they here to do?","Watching the procession pass by their doors, many villagers followed from a distance, not daring to get too close.","The official sedan chair was set down in front of the old house. Standing at the door, Old Man Song and the others saw Zhang Yuanzong step out of the chair, and they immediately knelt, kowtowed, and shouted, \"Commoners pay their respects to the Lord Magistrate.\"","Seeing this, the villagers watching from behind the sedan chair also knelt and kowtowed.","Why had the county magistrate come? And stopped right in front of Old Man Song's house.","Zhang Yuanzong's gaze fell on the slightly gray-haired Old Man Song. He quickly stepped forward to help him up. \"Old Mr. Song, there is no need for such formalities. I have come today to offer my congratulations.\"","Old Man Song and his family were stunned, completely unaware of what had happened.","Congratulations? Congratulations for what?","Didn't they fail the exam? They didn't even pass the preliminaries.","They welcomed him into the house to sit down. The uneven floor caused Zhang Yuanzong's official hat to tilt slightly as he sat on the chair, and he didn't dare lean all the way back.","He grinned widely and said, \"Miss Song came up with the idea of building greenhouses in the dead of winter to grow vegetables inside, and she freely offered this off-season planting method to the imperial court. His Majesty has specially granted her the title of Township Lady Linghui. This is an honor for our Xining City.\"","\"To be able to raise such a virtuous and talented granddaughter who is loyal to the imperial court, it is all due to your excellent guidance...\"","Faced with Zhang Yuanzong's endless stream of praise, the people sitting or standing in the main hall had turned into a bunch of dimwits, not knowing how to react.","Second Song and Second Aunt Song, who had just walked to the door, stood dumbfounded on the spot, their souls having already flown out of their bodies.","Township Lady? Who was he talking about? Song Jinzhao?","The oldest girl in the Song family was Song Jinzhao; besides her, they couldn't think of anyone else.","When Old Man Song spoke, his lips trembled, causing the loose skin on his face to wobble up and down.","\"Lord Magistrate, are you talking about my eldest granddaughter, Jinzhao?\"","Zhang Yuanzong nodded happily. \"Besides Song Jinzhao, what other commoner woman in the world could achieve this? Blessed by His Majesty's profound grace, this is a great event that brings honor to your ancestors.\"","For Xining City to produce a Township Lady, it not only brought glory to Zhang Yuanzong's face but also counted as his political achievement.","Coupled with being the first to build a waterwheel the year before last, with a little more effort, his position as county magistrate could be moved up next year.","Second Aunt Song's legs went weak, and she flopped to her knees on the ground.","Zhang Yuanzong looked toward the door curiously, and Old Man Song quickly explained, \"This is my Second Song. They live elsewhere and just rushed over.\"","Recovering his senses, Oldest Song quickly gave Second Song a look, signaling him to help her up.","The couple tremblingly stepped over the threshold and stood against the wall. Their chests heaved erratically, as if experiencing a tsunami.","Township Lady... Did Song Jinzhao become an official?","She was just a girl, how could that be possible!","Zhang Yuanzong sat in the Song family's old house for nearly half an hour, chatting about everything from Song Jinzhao's childhood to the passing of her parents. He praised her the entire time, even flattering her deceased parents to the heavens.","It wasn't until he left his congratulatory gifts and his procession departed that the Song family and the others finally began to fully process what had happened.","Oldest Song's voice stuttered as he hesitantly asked, \"How high of an official is a Township Lady?\"","No one answered, and no one knew.","Old Man Song had just sat down to drink a bowl of water to calm his nerves when the village chief, Song Mancang, rushed in with some people.","\"Old Man Song, I heard that Jinzhao was granted the title of Township Lady by His Majesty. Is it true?\"","He had just asked the yamen runners guarding outside, and at first listen, he couldn't quite believe it.","Old Man Song looked at Song Mancang. As he spoke, his head, hands, and body all trembled, almost spilling the water in his bowl.","\"They said she is Township Lady Linghui.\"","Second Song reached out and grabbed Song Mancang's arm. \"Village Chief, what kind of official is a Township Lady?\"","Song Mancang tightly gripped the armrest with his right hand as he sat down, his eyes losing focus.","\"A Township Lady is not an official, it's a noble title. A seventh-grade imperial mandate holds a distinguished status. Usually, only imperial relatives or the wives and daughters of exceptionally high-ranking officials receive such a title.\"","Oldest Song shrieked, \"Seventh grade? Doesn't that mean she's as big as the county magistrate!\"","Old Man Song and the others felt a buzzing in their heads. No wonder the county magistrate's attitude had been so gentle earlier, full of praise in every word. It turned out her rank was the same as his.","Song Mancang shook his head and explained, \"A Township Lady has no actual power, so it's not the same as an official position. But her status is highly respected; even the county magistrate must treat her with courtesy when they meet.\"","He slapped his thigh with great regret. \"The most important thing is that a Township Lady receives an annual stipend, and people registered in the same household can be exempt from corvee labor. Old Man Song, you split up the family way too early.\"","Not only did they fail to reap the benefits of Song Qiming being a scholar, but now even Song Jinzhao was eating imperial grain, yet the imperial grace couldn't benefit the other two branches. It could be said they suffered a massive loss.","The room fell into a dead silence. Seeing that none of them were speaking, Song Mancang pondered for a long while before saying, \"Old Man Song, what do you think about writing a letter to have Jinzhao come back for a visit? For such a joyous occasion, we absolutely must open the village ancestral hall to offer sacrifices to our ancestors and comfort the spirits of our forebears.\"","Old Man Song snapped back to reality and spoke up, Jinzhao has a lot on her plate in Anyang Prefecture and probably will not have the time. How about we wait until they come back to discuss this?","Song Mancang pondered for a long time. Thinking of the vast distance to Anyang Prefecture, he said, Then we will hold the ceremony twice. Tomorrow, we will open the inner ancestral hall and you can pay respects to the ancestors on Jinzhao's behalf. We will hold it again once they return.","Old Man Song had no objections to this. His mind was still a bit muddled, and the title of Lady of the County kept floating before his eyes. He needed some time to process it all."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: The Child from Another Family, Madame Meng Sends an Invitation","paragraphs":["After the village chief left, the villagers came in wave after wave.","With questions coming one after another, Old Man Song and Oldest Song were almost numb from answering.","Having finally managed to deal with everyone, Old Man Song paced around with his hands behind his back a couple of times before looking at Song Yongnian.","\"Yongnian, come with your grandpa. Let's write a letter to your Sister Jinzhao.\"","Song Yongnian returned to the room, writing as Old Man Song dictated.","Once the ink was dry and the letter was sealed in an envelope, Old Man Song handed it to Oldest Song.","\"Tomorrow, after the ancestral sacrifice, go to the city and find a merchant caravan heading to Anyang Prefecture. Have them deliver this letter to Jinzhao.\"","Oldest Song took the letter with both hands and tucked it into his robe. \"Father, shouldn't we have Jinzhao and the others come back? For such a grand occasion, shouldn't we host a banquet?\"","Old Man Song waved his hand in refusal. \"The journey is long and arduous. A round trip takes half a month, and Qiming is studying at the academy without a break. They must be very busy. Just send the letter to let them know the county magistrate visited. Jinzhao will naturally come back when she has the time.\"","In the afternoon, Old Man Song took joss paper and the aged Huadiao wine Song Qiming had bought for him, heading to the foot of the back mountain to visit the graves of Third Song and his wife.","Oldest Song and Second Song also followed along to burn paper offerings.","Old Man Song poured cup after cup of the precious Huadiao wine he usually couldn't bear to drink in front of Third Song's grave, repeating every single word Zhang Yuanzong had said to the deceased couple.","\"Qiming is good at his studies, and Jinzhao is even more promising. My son, you raised a wonderful daughter. It's just a pity you aren't here to see it.\"","Squatting to the side burning joss paper, Old Lady Song kept wiping her tears, her eyes red from crying.","The children were so successful, yet her son had died before he could enjoy a single day of their blessings. Why was his fate so bitter!","Oldest Song and Second Song squatted side by side behind Old Man Song. Looking at the names on the tombstone, they felt a mix of pity and envy.","Their niece and nephew from the third branch were rising to greatness, while their own children couldn't even pass the exams to become child scholars. The massive disparity left them feeling hollow inside, as if a cold wind were blowing through their hearts.","The next day, the village ancestral hall was opened for the sacrifice. Everyone in Song Family Village attended, surrounding Old Man Song and his family to curry favor. Even the usually arrogant Master Zhao took the initiative to come over and greet Old Man Song, acting extremely humble.","Through an acquaintance, Oldest Song paid some silver to have a merchant caravan deliver the letter to Song Jinzhao, along with two of the congratulatory gifts Zhang Yuanzong had brought the day before.","Old Man Song kept the pastries and wine for himself, but the remaining tea set and top-grade writing brushes and inkstone were to be sent to Anyang Prefecture.","The items looked expensive and weren't things they could put to use.","Every household in the village drank tea from simple bowls, and giving such fine writing tools to Song Yongnian and Song Yaozu would be a waste. They definitely had to be sent to Anyang Prefecture for Song Qiming to use.","Upon receiving the letter, Song Jinzhao looked at the tea set and the wolf-hair brushes with the She inkstone in the box, then instructed Chunxing to store the items in the warehouse.","Song Shixue looked up and asked, \"Aside from the county magistrate visiting to offer congratulations, what else did Grandpa say?\"","Song Jinzhao handed the letter to Song Shixue. \"Yongnian and Yaozu failed the preliminary county exam.\"","\"Ah,\" Song Shixue stared at the fairly neat handwriting on the letter, which looked like Yongnian's. \"Grandpa must be very sad. If they couldn't pass the preliminary exam, it will probably be difficult for them to pass next year, too.\"","When Song Qiming returned from the academy in the evening, he read the letter and silently set it down.","During their first visit to Scholar Zheng's home over the New Year, the teacher had mentioned that Yaozu was somewhat clever but lacked the patience to focus on his studies, let alone study hard day and night.","Yongnian was considered rather mediocre. If he spent another year or two, he might be able to pass the exam to become a child scholar, but as for becoming a Xiucai, he hadn't even considered it.","\"Sister, the village is opening the ancestral hall. Are we going back for the New Year this year?\"","The provincial exams were in August. If he could successfully participate in the metropolitan exams next February, they had no plans to return for the New Year.","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"We'll see after your provincial exams are over.\"","The round trip would take too much time, and unless something important happened, she really didn't want to go back.","Chunxing came in holding an invitation. \"Eldest Miss, the Meng family sent someone to deliver this this afternoon. Madam Meng would like to invite you to go for a spring outing in a few days.\"","Ever since she was granted the title of Lady of the County, dozens of banquet invitations had been sent to Song Jinzhao. If it wasn't for admiring plum blossoms, it was for admiring apricot blossoms.","There were also various messy elegant gatherings and tea parties. Song Jinzhao had attended once and never went again.","Song Shixue felt that sitting in a crowd making awkward small talk was incredibly boring. She would rather spend that time reading a few more medical books and treating a few more patients.","As for Song Jinzhao, she absolutely couldn't stand the old madams and ladies trying to play matchmaker for no reason. Every single one of them wanted to introduce her to young talents, and when she refused, they all assumed she was just being shy.","Just dealing with their relentless pestering made Song Jinzhao feel more exhausted than working in the fields.","So later on, she simply rejected them all and didn't attend a single one.","Glancing at the invitation, the neat, elegant small regular script was clearly a woman's handwriting.","After the Lantern Festival, Guo Yiyao had gone to the capital with Meng Xiaozhe. This beautiful handwriting didn't look like something a maid could write.","\"Did Madam Meng write this invitation herself?\"","Chunxing nodded. \"That's what the messenger told Qingshui. The servant who delivered the letter also mentioned that Madam Meng sincerely hopes you will do her the honor this time.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at the meeting location on the invitation.","Ming Garden? It seemed to be outside the city.","Qingshuang glanced at the invitation and quietly reminded her, \"Eldest Miss, Ming Garden is a property of the Li family.\"","Song Jinzhao raised an eyebrow."]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: Lady Meng's Test","paragraphs":["The carriage stopped at the foot of the hill. Bypassing a large, rippling clear lake, a forest of mountain peach trees came into view, already blooming with small pink flowers. A faint, elegant floral scent lingered in the air, captivating the senses.","Passing through the peach grove, bright yellow winter jasmine bloomed profusely among the shrubs on the hillside. Against such beautiful scenery, the woman sitting in the pavilion wearing an indigo padded jacket seemed somewhat out of place.","Madam Meng sat properly on the stone bench. Although her posture appeared dignified and elegant, every detail revealed her tension and anxiety.","Her fingers repeatedly twisted her handkerchief, her body shifted restlessly, and she looked up and down countless times. She had already sighed silently over a dozen times.","It was truly difficult being forced into such an awkward situation without the ability to refuse.","A maid looked up and saw Song Jinzhao approaching, hurriedly whispering a reminder, Madam, Lady Linghui is here.","Madam Meng jerked her head up to look in Song Jinzhao's direction. As the distance closed, she hastily stepped out of the pavilion and curtsied.","Blessings to you, my lady.","Song Jinzhao glanced around. Aside from a few of the Meng residence's maids, there was no one else.","Did Madam Meng only invite me?","Madam Meng's lips twitched in an awkward smile. Knowing that you dislike crowds, my lady, I didn't invite anyone else.","With the spring peach blossoms adding beauty and the winter jasmine bringing warmth, how could we let it go to waste? You busy yourself at the medical clinic all day, my lady; this is the perfect opportunity to come out and relax.","Since Song Jinzhao's status had undergone an earth-shattering transformation, Madam Meng could no longer treat her as the highly skilled commoner physician she once was.","Song Jinzhao gave a gentle smile. Weren't we supposed to meet at Ming Garden? Why is Madam Meng waiting outside?","Madam Meng looked left and right, her eyes unfocused as if searching for something.","I saw that the scenery outside was lovely, and I couldn't bear to miss it, so I stayed a bit longer. It is still early; how about I take you for a stroll first, my lady?","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows, a thoughtful look in her eyes.","It seemed her guess was right. The person who wanted to see her today was not Madam Meng.","Meeting at Ming Garden, the Li family's territory, and having the prefect's wife act as the intermediary—the person coming must have an extraordinary background.","Madam Meng raised a hand to stop her maids from following. Qingshuang glanced at Song Jinzhao and tactfully stepped back.","The winter jasmine growing among the shrubs formed bright and vivid clusters, their cheerful colors naturally refreshing the mind and spirit.","I've heard that whenever Anyang Academy posts its monthly rankings, your brother is always proudly listed in the top three. For this year's provincial examinations, he is sure to pass with flying colors.","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a faint smile. That was before. After entering the Upper House, there are too many outstanding peers. The boy has been so discouraged he can hardly lift his head.","During the academy's first monthly exam in early March, including the new students admitted this year, there were thirteen students in the Upper House. Song Qiming ranked fifth from the bottom, and he was almost depressed over it.","For nearly half a month, he had been studying late into the night every day, and he spent much more time at the Ye residence than before.","Madam Meng didn't think much of it and instead praised, The students of the Upper House are all exceedingly talented. It is already incredibly rare for Young Master Song to have tested into it so quickly. With Lord Ye guiding him, the August provincial exams will definitely not be a problem. The only question is whether Lord Ye will still be around by then.","A dark glint flashed through Song Jinzhao's eyes as she followed the other woman's lead and asked, What do you mean by that?","Madam Meng feigned surprise and raised her brows slightly. Did you not know, my lady? The Emperor intends to restore Lord Ye to his former post. In a little while, he will likely be returning to the capital.","Nowadays, Ye Liangyu could walk without his crutches. Aside from being unable to run or do strenuous exercise, he looked no different from a normal person. Going to the academy to teach every day, many people subconsciously no longer thought about his leg."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: The King's Royal Concubine","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao smiled faintly. \"Qiming hasn't mentioned it to me, so I suppose it hasn't been completely finalized yet.\"","Madam Meng continued to probe. \"I heard from my husband that when Lord Ye left the capital, his relationship with the two princes was not very harmonious. I wonder how things will be when he returns this time? Your brother is Lord Ye's only student, so surely he must know something.\"","Song Jinzhao reached out and brushed her fingers over the stamens of the winter jasmine. \"Qiming is only thirteen. How could Mr. Ye discuss major court affairs with a child? Mr. Ye used to be an imperial censor, a position that easily offends people, so I imagine his relationship with anyone wouldn't be too good.\"","Madam Meng pursed her lips and looked away. Why was she so impenetrable?","If she didn't reveal a single bit of information, what was she supposed to report when she went back?","After strolling for nearly half an hour, seeing that she could no longer stall for time, Madam Meng helplessly frowned.","As they reached the entrance of Ming Garden, she put on a very troubled expression. The words rolled around on her tongue a couple of times before she swallowed them back, as if she were stuck.","Meeting Song Jinzhao's nonchalant gaze, she finally opened her mouth.","\"Actually, the person who wanted to see you today isn't me, but Prince Ying's side consort, Li Qinyun.\"","Song Jinzhao asked in confusion, \"Li Tianchong's daughter? Isn't she in the capital? Why did she suddenly come back?\"","Anyang Prefecture and the capital were thousands of miles apart; even riding a horse would take over a month. Furthermore, Li Qinyun was a side consort, and under normal circumstances, she would rarely be allowed to visit her family.","Madam Meng replied, \"The day after tomorrow is Li Tianchong's birthday. Side Consort Li is favored, and Prince Ying specially granted her the grace to return and celebrate her father's birthday.\"","\"The day before yesterday, she suddenly sent someone to my door, saying she wanted to meet you. Given her status, I couldn't easily refuse, which is why I invited you to go on a spring outing. Side Consort Li is already waiting inside.\"","In reality, to leave some time to speak with Song Jinzhao alone, Madam Meng had deliberately moved their meeting time up by an hour. Unfortunately, she still hadn't managed to find out anything.","Song Jinzhao asked, \"Does Madam Meng know why Side Consort Li wants to see me?\"","Madam Meng shook her head. \"She only said she wanted to see for herself the elegance of the lady personally titled by the Emperor. She didn't say anything else.\"","When Li Qinyun married into Prince Ying's manor, Meng Hechuan had not yet been transferred to serve as the Prefect of Anyang. Madam Meng and Li Qinyun had never met. This sudden request had startled not only Madam Meng but even Meng Hechuan.","Historically, the struggle for the throne was always accompanied by bloodshed and sacrifice, especially for the officials who chose sides.","Successfully backing the winning prince meant a meteoric rise, but failing meant not just demotion or dismissal; in severe cases, it could implicate one's entire family, leading to their deaths.","Meng Hechuan certainly did not want people to think he had defected to Prince Ying.","A few steps into Ming Garden, Song Jinzhao saw four guards standing outside the enclosure with their swords, their expressions very serious.","Seeing women approaching, one of them turned and walked inside, bringing out a maidservant when he returned.","\"This must be Lady Linghui. Her Ladyship has been waiting for you for quite some time.\"","Madam Meng noted the maid's attitude and demeanor, her heart pounding and unable to calm down for a long time.","She carefully stole a glance at Song Jinzhao, feeling as though she had pushed the other woman into a pit of fire.","Hopefully, nothing bad would happen!","The woman sitting on the embroidered stool wore a pale lotus-colored dress embroidered with golden birds. As she looked up toward the door, the pure gold kingfisher feather hairpin in her chignon swayed gently, accentuating her exquisitely beautiful face with a touch of charm.","Song Jinzhao's eyes held a smile as she raised her eyebrows in slight surprise.","It seemed that Prince Ying's decision to marry her wasn't entirely due to the Li family's vast wealth; no man could resist a face like that.","Li Qinyun had seen portraits of Song Jinzhao. Seeing her in person, she realized the woman was not particularly tall or large, making it hard to imagine that such a woman could hunt down fierce tigers and black bears.","Song Jinzhao stopped calmly and gave a slight curtsy. \"This subject greets Her Ladyship.\"","Madam Meng quickly followed with a deep curtsy. \"This subject's wife greets Her Ladyship. Wishing Her Ladyship peace and prosperity.\"","Li Qinyun affectionately stepped forward and held Song Jinzhao's hands, breaking into a bright smile. \"Lady Linghui, there is no need for such formalities. Let us treat today as a meeting between good friends; there is no need to be too strict with the rules.\"","After taking their seats, Li Qinyun's mouth never stopped. The moment the atmosphere cooled down even slightly, she would immediately switch to the next topic and keep chatting.","Even Madam Meng, who frequently attended banquets, could not help but inwardly marvel at Li Qinyun's social grace.","Despite her young age, judging by her conversation, it would not be an exaggeration to say she was a seasoned veteran in social settings."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: Sow Discord","paragraphs":["\"Madam Meng really likes eating plum blossom cakes?\" Li Qinyun suddenly turned her gaze to Madam Meng, who was taking small bites of the pastry.","Madam Meng paused mid-bite. She had only just picked up her first piece; how did it turn into her really liking them?","But since Li Qinyun asked, she could only nod and smile in agreement. \"The plum fragrance is delightful. I like them very much.\"","\"The kitchen has some freshly made ones that are still hot. Hurry and bring Madam Meng another plate.\"","The maid waiting nearby quickly turned and left the room. When she returned, the plum blossom cakes on the plate were still steaming.","Hesitation flickered in Madam Meng's eyes. What was the meaning of this? It seemed a bit overly enthusiastic.","Li Qinyun's gaze landed on Song Jinzhao. \"It is the season for plum blossoms to bloom in Ming Garden, and the beauty of spring should not be wasted. Would Lady Linghui accompany me outside to take a look?\"","She pushed the plate towards Madam Meng. \"Eat more, Madam Meng. They will not taste good once they get cold.\"","Madam Meng could neither chew nor swallow the scalding hot pastry in her mouth. She realized she should not have come inside after dropping the person off earlier.","This was a hint that she was in the way, using food to gag her.","Stepping out of the room, Li Qinyun spoke with a hint of apology in her tone. \"I heard that my older brother and you had some unpleasantness in business. He is simple-minded and clumsy with his words. If he did anything poorly, please forgive him.\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"They were all trivial matters. I did not take them to heart.\"","Li Qinyun stopped walking and looked at Song Jinzhao with eyes full of admiration. \"You are not only intelligent but also very magnanimous. No wonder the Duke of Qing likes you.\"","Her delicate eyebrows furrowed slightly, and the smile on her face dimmed a bit.","\"However, I would like to remind you that Princess Yongjia is enamored with the Duke of Qing. She has already learned from Prince Qi that the Duke of Qing's heart belongs to someone else. Once you enter the capital, I am afraid the princess will cause trouble for you.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows in astonishment and asked in confusion, \"The Duke of Qing likes me? Who said that? Why do I not know about this?\"","She had only met Chu Liuyun twice. They could not even be considered acquaintances, so where did this affection come from?","Li Qinyun's expression froze slightly before she feigned shock, lightly covering her mouth with her handkerchief.","\"When the Emperor conferred the title of Lady Linghui upon you, Prime Minister Gu strongly opposed it. It was the Duke of Qing who stood by and firmly supported you. Did he not tell you?\"","Song Jinzhao stared fixedly at Li Qinyun. This constant talk of affection felt like a trap being set.","\"I have no relationship with the Duke of Qing. He probably spoke up for me because of the matter with the Shuobei thieves. After all, I did help him.\"","Li Qinyun let out a sound of sudden realization, then posed another question.","\"Since there is no relationship, why was Prince Qi so certain, and why did he even bring the matter before Princess Yongjia? The palace was buzzing with rumors during that time, and everyone thought the Duke of Qing liked you. Is this not just causing trouble for you!\"","A flash of understanding crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes.","With the conversation at this point, regardless of whether the matter was true or false, Li Qinyun's purpose in saying these things was to make her detest Prince Qi.","Sowing discord before they had even met, was she, a titled lady living thousands of miles away, really that important?","Was it worth her making a special trip back just to drive a wedge between them?","Song Jinzhao pretended to be angry and condemned in a sharp voice, \"This concerns a young woman's reputation. How could Prince Qi speak such nonsense!\"","Li Qinyun led Song Jinzhao to sit on a stone bench, let out a deep breath, and sighed, \"I suppose it might have something to do with your younger brother.\"","\"Before Lord Ye resigned and returned to his hometown, he repeatedly and bluntly pointed out the faults of Prince Qi's faction in the imperial court. Your brother is Ye Liangyu's student, and you cured his legs. Prince Qi has come to hate you because of this.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded slowly. \"So that is how it is. As a doctor, treating illnesses and saving people is my bounden duty. I did not expect His Highness Prince Qi to be so narrow-minded.\"","Li Qinyun covered her mouth with her handkerchief and whispered quietly, \"To tell you the truth, it was Prince Qi who sent people to cripple Ye Liangyu's legs. If the guards had not arrived in time, let alone his legs, he might have lost his life.\"","Song Jinzhao looked up abruptly and asked in astonishment, \"How did Your Highness learn that those assassins were sent by Prince Qi?\"","Li Qinyun's expression appeared very regretful. \"At the hunting grounds, when my husband chased after them, he caught an assassin. But just as the assassin spat out the words Prince Qi, he was secretly killed.\"","\"Without evidence, it is just empty talk. The Emperor would definitely think that my husband was deliberately targeting Prince Qi, so he did not reveal the truth.\"","\"The court is fraught with danger. Lord Ye has a fiery temper, so we thought it might be for the best if he left the capital. Who would have thought that after such a short time, he would be returning. This time, Prince Qi will definitely not let him off.\"","\"You are familiar with Lord Ye, so you must remind him to be more on guard. He absolutely must not lose his life.\"","Song Jinzhao furrowed her brows, pretending to be deep in thought.","Seeing that she had taken the words to heart, Li Qinyun looked up into the distance and could not help but curl her lips into a smug smile, though she quickly suppressed it.","After finishing the entire plate of plum blossom cakes without seeing the others return, Madam Meng was starting to get restless.","The maid standing by the pillar keeping an eye on her saw this, walked over, and asked, \"Please wait a moment, Madam Meng. I will go bring another plate.\"","\"No need! No need! No need! I am a bit thirsty, bring a pot of hot tea instead.\" If she ate any more, she would surely burst.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao had not spoken for a long time, Li Qinyun continued, \"Although Lord Ye and my husband sometimes have political disagreements, my husband actually admires Lord Ye a lot. Upright and unyielding imperial censors like him with an iron backbone may not be well-liked, but they are what the court needs the most.\"","\"It will not be long before the Emperor restores Lord Ye to his original post. Please tell Lord Ye that if he encounters any difficulties after returning to the capital, or if he is targeted and plotted against by Prince Qi, with just one word from him, my husband will definitely step in to help.\"","Listening to this, Song Jinzhao inexplicably got goosebumps all over her body.","They probably felt that after this ordeal and learning his lesson, Ye Liangyu might be afraid and willing to compromise, so they wanted to win him over in advance.","Unfortunately, that old man's personality had not changed one bit. Showing weakness was completely nonexistent for him.","He was actually planning to return to the capital, wreak havoc, take revenge for his nearly crippled legs, and eliminate Prince Qi and Prince Ying one by one."]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: Is the Emperor Unable to Have Children","paragraphs":["\"I will pass on the message. As for what to do, that is up to Lord Ye himself.\"","The solemn tone coupled with a sorrowful expression made Li Qinyun increasingly believe that Song Jinzhao was currently filled with anxiety.","\"Prince Qi finds you an eyesore. If you submit any more brilliant ideas to the imperial court in the future, Chancellor Gu will definitely jump out to obstruct you when the Emperor grants his rewards. In fact, Lady of the County, you could simply tell my Prince first. He appreciates your talents and will certainly fight for the greatest merit on your behalf.\"","Song Jinzhao curled her lips into a faint smile. \"As a woman, I have no need for such great merit. It is all for the imperial court.\"","Li Qinyun flattered, \"My Prince was indeed right. Your pure and kind heart for the country and the people is the most rare of all.\"","Having sat for nearly half an hour, Madam Meng's bottom was almost numb by the time she waited for them to return.","Seeing that both of their expressions looked very satisfied, Madam Meng started to feel a drumming in her heart.","They had been gone for so long, who knew what they had talked about.","Seeing the empty plates on the table, Li Qinyun smiled and instructed a maid, \"Go pack a plate of plum blossom cakes for Madam Meng to take back, and prepare an extra portion of the other pastries as well. Children love sweet things, so the Lady of the County can also take some back for her younger siblings to taste.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled but said nothing.","Madam Meng's eyes twitched at the corners, cursing Li Qinyun a hundred times in her heart.","Hindered by the other party's status, her thousands of words could only be condensed into one sentence, \"The craftsmanship of Your Highness's chef is simply excellent. I have never tasted such sweet and fragrant plum blossom cakes anywhere else.\"","Li Qinyun lowered her eyes and smiled faintly, a touch of shyness appearing on her face.","\"The chef who made these pastries was originally an imperial chef in the palace. After the Prince established his estate, he has been serving in Prince Ying's residence. This time for my father's birthday, the Prince specially sent him over to be the head chef. You two must definitely come to the birthday banquet the day after tomorrow.\"","Madam Meng said enviously, \"His Highness Prince Ying dotes on Your Highness so much, it truly makes others envious!\"","Song Jinzhao silently watched the two exchange pleasantries.","Envious of what?","Envious that she is a concubine?","Traveling thousands of miles to recruit troops and buy horses for him, he naturally had to show some appreciation. Moreover, it was just a chef; the Prince didn't even show up himself, yet he reaped all the good reputation of honoring his father-in-law.","On the way back, Madam Meng stole several glances at Song Jinzhao. Seeing that she had no intention of speaking, she could only swallow the words on the tip of her tongue.","Song Jinzhao did not go home, but directly had Qingshuang drive the carriage to the Ye residence.","Although Qin Yunqian had already left Anyang Prefecture, he had left many guards for Ye Liangyu.","Song Jinzhao had roughly guessed that the Qin family and Ye Liangyu were mixed up together.","Returning to the capital this time, Ye Liangyu was not unprepared; at the very least, he would not let assassins cripple him again.","After sitting down, Song Jinzhao told Ye Liangyu everything Li Qinyun had said, wanting to know his thoughts.","The more Ye Liangyu listened, the tighter his brows furrowed, and a faint anger emerged on his face.","As soon as Song Jinzhao finished speaking, he slammed his fist onto the table, standing up in a fierce rage with a contorted expression.","\"The national treasury is empty. In the front, the Northern Shuo Kingdom is glaring like a tiger, and in the rear, the southwestern foreign tribes are swarming like bees and ants. As imperial princes, instead of thinking about strengthening the country and enriching the people, they only know how to play political games and form self-serving cliques all day long. If they take the throne, our Dongzhao Kingdom is doomed to perish.\"","Song Jinzhao asked in confusion, \"Does the current Emperor have no other princes?\"","With so many concubines in the imperial harem, how could there be no other princes born?","Could it be that they were all killed off by the mothers of these two princes?","Ye Liangyu shook his head heavily. \"Let alone princes, there is only one princess, Princess Yongjia.\"","\"What about pregnancies?\"","Ye Liangyu shook his head again. \"After Princess Yongjia was born, I haven't heard of any other concubine in the harem getting pregnant. I suppose heaven is not blessing our Dongzhao.\"","Song Jinzhao raised her eyebrows; this was strange.","The imperial concubines didn't use contraception, and with so many encounters every month, how could none of them get pregnant?","\"Could it be that there is a problem with the Emperor's body? Has he been seen by an imperial physician?\"","In order to fight for the throne and eliminate potential competitors, completely cutting off their own father's ability to reproduce was not entirely impossible.","Ye Liangyu was stunned for a good while before saying hesitantly, \"There are countless imperial physicians in the palace, so there shouldn't be any problems.\"","Song Jinzhao stared at him without speaking. Ninety percent of the time, things that defied common sense had a problem.","Whether the Emperor could reproduce or not concerned the foundation of the state.","Even if he couldn't, it wouldn't be spread outside. For such a shameful matter, probably not even the imperial physicians would dare to tell the truth easily. The wrath of an emperor could take a life with a single word.","Seeing Song Jinzhao's demeanor, the more Ye Liangyu thought about it, the more he felt something was wrong. Could there really be a problem with the Emperor's body?","He held his head and paced in circles, feeling extremely panicked inside.","\"Miss Song, this matter absolutely must not be spread outside. Regardless of whether it's true or false, if it reaches the Emperor's ears, it is a capital offense.\"","\"You don't need to worry about Prince Ying's side. I will be returning to the capital in three months. If anything happens, I will block it. Qiming is my only student, and I treat him like my own son. If you encounter any difficulties in the future, Miss Song, you can always come to me.\"","Whether as Song Qiming's sister or the lifesaver who rescued his legs.","With a single word from Song Jinzhao, as long as it didn't violate his principles, he would do his utmost to help.","Song Jinzhao asked Ye Liangyu in return, \"The Emperor only has two princes, and you have offended both of them. In the future, no matter who ascends the throne, your fate will likely not be too good.\" He would probably end up without an intact corpse.","Ye Liangyu clenched his jaw, his unyielding tone carrying a trace of regret.","\"If the princes' virtues do not match their positions, the throne can be passed directly to an imperial grandson. The current Emperor is not yet fifty years old; he can afford to wait.\"","\"At worst, a talented youth from the imperial clan can be chosen to take the throne.\" This possibility was too small, unless the Emperor's lineage completely died out and it truly reached the point of having no successors.","\"Even if none of these work out, by the time the Emperor passes away, I will be old. My parents have already passed, and I have no wife or children in this life. They can take this worthless life as they please.\"","Song Jinzhao gazed at Ye Liangyu with slight surprise, not expecting him to think this way.","From ancient times to the present, it seemed that the famous civil officials in the history books all had particularly stubborn tempers, constantly offering remonstrances at the cost of their lives. The words leave a name in history and be remembered through the ages were truly not just for fun.","\"What kind of person is Princess Yongjia?\" If the princes were unreliable, wasn't there still a princess?","Ye Liangyu thought Song Jinzhao was afraid that Princess Yongjia would target her because of the Duke of Qing matter, so he took a breath and said, \"Rest assured, Anyang Prefecture is thousands of miles away from the capital, and the inner palace cannot interfere in politics. She cannot do anything to you.\"","\"Moreover, as far as I know, Princess Yongjia is not an arrogant or domineering person. I hear she is very gentle and well-behaved, so she shouldn't do anything out of line.\"","Song Jinzhao smiled but didn't speak. She figured that in the minds of these ancients, there was probably no concept of letting a princess ascend the throne to become an empress regnant, so it was better for her not to bring it up."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: Intelligence Questions","paragraphs":["On the day of Li Tianchong's birthday banquet, not a single prominent family or high official in Anyang Prefecture was absent; they all sent representatives to offer their congratulations.","Madam Meng, seated at the ladies' table, let her gaze wander between Ye Liangyu and Song Jinzhao. Had they really aligned themselves with the Prince of Ying?","After the birthday celebrations concluded, on the day before Li Qinyun left Anyang Prefecture, she made a point to greet Song Jinzhao, inviting her to visit the Prince of Ying's manor once she arrived in the capital.","Watching the ornate carriage gradually fade into the distance, Song Qiming felt a sense of unease.","Once the provincial exams in August were over, the spring metropolitan exams would follow in February of the next year. The capital was a place of deception and hidden dangers. If a brick fell from the sky there, it would hit either a royal relative or a third-rank official. Life after entering the capital would likely not be as comfortable as it was now.","He turned his head and said solemnly to Song Jinzhao, Sister, I want to live at my teacher's house for the next few months.","He had to work even harder. Since they were already drawn into the center of power, only by climbing higher could they avoid being bullied.","Remembering that Ye Liangyu would be returning to the capital in three months, Song Jinzhao nodded in agreement.","She reached out and patted Song Qiming's arm. Study hard, but don't overwork yourself. Your health comes first.","Song Qiming nodded vigorously. His original goal had been to successfully pass the provincial exam; he hadn't cared about his ranking in the upcoming spring exam, as long as he passed.","But given the current situation, barely passing the imperial examination was far from enough. To secure a place in the capital, it was best to rank among the very top.","By April, the weather had thoroughly warmed up.","Song Jinzhao directed the servants to plant the cut potato pieces with the sprouts facing upward into the garden soil that had long been tilled.","Out of the corner of her eye, she caught sight of Xuetuan walking over.","Never lacking food or drink, and under Song Shixue's meticulous care, the white tiger cub, now over three months old, already weighed forty catties and looked like a giant, fluffy white cat.","The cross-eyed look in its deep blue tiger eyes had become more pronounced. When its large eyeballs rolled around, it looked incredibly silly and cute, something they had all grown accustomed to.","Sitting in a chair to supervise the work, Song Jinzhao simultaneously sketched and wrote on a piece of paper with her brush.","Expenses in the capital would only be greater. Having plenty of spare funds on hand, she wanted to buy another shop to open a barbecue restaurant.","As the weather got a bit hotter, eating barbecue and drinking ice-cold beer while enjoying the cool evening breeze would absolutely be one of life's greatest pleasures.","Song Jinzhao looked up from time to time to check on the potato planting progress, but her gaze was gradually drawn to Xuetuan, who was walking in circles around a stone not far away.","After watching intently for nearly fifteen minutes, Song Jinzhao frowned.","She walked over and placed her hand in front of Xuetuan. Unable to see the way forward, the white tiger bumped its head right into Song Jinzhao's palm, lifting its head to look around with a somewhat clumsy gaze.","Song Jinzhao tried to play with it and teach it to pounce and bite, but Xuetuan's reactions were extremely apathetic, as if it wasn't interested in anything.","The endless circling, head-shaking, and spinning in place—such stereotypical behaviors made Song Jinzhao doubt Xuetuan's intelligence.","Waking up from his afternoon nap, Song Anhao sluggishly sought out Song Jinzhao, shouting from afar, Eldest Sister! His voice still carried the grogginess of sleep.","Song Jinzhao set Xuetuan down and reached out to catch her youngest brother as he rushed over, gently helping him tidy his hair. Did you sleep well?","Song Anhao rested his head on Song Jinzhao's shoulder, his eyes, like dark grapes, covered in a watery sheen.","I dreamed of eating fish, shrimp and egg custard, and pork and vegetable meatballs. Sister, I really want to eat them right now.","Song Jinzhao gently stroked Song Anhao's soft back, leaning her head back to let him stand properly.","Not right now. I'll have Qingshui make them for dinner.","Song Anhao pouted and began counting on his fingers. Not knowing what time it was, he looked up at the sun.","The sunlight was too glaring, making his eyes uncomfortable. The sun hadn't set yet, so it would definitely be a long while before dinner.","He rubbed his round little belly and acted spoiled, saying, Eldest Sister, I'm a little hungry.","Song Jinzhao curled her lips in a doting smile and pinched his smooth, tender cheek. I think you're just being greedy.","Seeing Xuetuan sitting motionless in place, watching them, a flash of worry crossed Song Jinzhao's eyes.","Shixue already pitied it for its eye problems. If she knew it also had intellectual issues, who knew how heartbroken she would be.","Seeing that Song Jinzhao wasn't falling for his trick, Song Anhao turned and called for Xuetuan to leave with him.","There were pastries left over from the morning on the table. If he couldn't get the delicious food now, he could at least fill his stomach a bit to satisfy his cravings. Otherwise, his mind would keep dwelling on the steamed fish and vegetable meatballs. Eating those dishes in his dream had been so incredibly savory; just thinking about it made his mouth water.","When Song Shixue returned from the medical clinic in the evening, Song Jinzhao didn't immediately share her suspicions with her, but instead observed for a few more days.","Finally, she confirmed that Xuetuan's intelligence truly was impaired. Its sluggish reactions were not entirely due to its vision problems, but rather issues with its brain and neurons.","Ultimately, it was caused by genetic defects."]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: Taking Tuan Tuan to the Veterinarian","paragraphs":["After dinner, as Lanxi was about to head to the front to lock the door, he saw Song Shixue sitting on the steps by the backyard gate, hugging Xuetuan, her shoulders trembling with sobs.","\"Second Miss, what's wrong?\" he asked as he approached.","Song Shixue jerked her head up. The bright firelight illuminated her face. Her eyes were wet with tears, and her sparkling pupils seemed to reflect a sky full of stars, shining brilliantly and evoking a deep sense of pity.","She hastily wiped her tears with her sleeve. Having cried for so long, her cheeks felt a bit raw and tender.","She hugged Xuetuan's neck tightly and turned away so he wouldn't look at her.","\"I'm fine. The wind just made my eyes sting.\"","Lanxi looked around. What wind? Even the leaves were perfectly still.","Knowing that no one in the manor would dare bully Song Shixue—even the Eldest Miss had never spoken a harsh word to her—the only possibility left was the medical clinic.","\"Did a patient have a bad temper and bully you?\"","At the word \"patient,\" Song Shixue's eyes grew red again. She buried her face into Xuetuan's furry neck, shaking her head as she replied in a muffled, heavy voice.","\"No, no patient bullied me. It's Xuetuan.\"","Lanxi looked in confusion at the little white tiger resting obediently in Song Shixue's arms. It looked perfectly normal, and it certainly couldn't have bitten her.","Song Shixue said, \"My sister says there's something wrong with Xuetuan's brain. She says he's a fool.\"","Lanxi froze, his gaze repeatedly circling the tiger's head. No wonder it usually acted so silly and cute, completely lacking the majestic aura of the king of the forest. It turned out it really was just dumb.","Seeing that she was still upset, Lanxi sat down on the steps.","He offered some comfort. \"Actually, being a bit dumb isn't so bad. You won't have to worry about it hurting people when it grows up. As long as it has enough food and drink and can live peacefully, that's already very good.\"","Song Shixue widened her eyes in disbelief, glaring at Lanxi. She picked up Xuetuan and prepared to leave.","\"I would rather it bite me than have something wrong with its brain. Who would want to be a fool if they could be normal?\"","\"To understand nothing, to not know happiness or experience joy, living a dull life forever—how sad it must be.\"","Watching Song Shixue's angry departing figure, Lanxi sat frozen in place for a long time.","He hadn't said anything wrong. It was born an orphan and riddled with illnesses. If Song Shixue hadn't picked it up, it would have died long ago.","Now it had a home, sheltered from the wind and rain, had food without needing to hunt, and had someone who loved it wholeheartedly. Was that not considered lucky?","Song Shixue moved Xuetuan's bed into her own room. Waking up in the middle of the night, she saw it sleeping soundly in its bed, and her aching heart felt slightly better.","After a sleepless night, Song Shixue woke up in the morning with a tight scalp, feeling exhausted all over.","During breakfast, Song Jinzhao noticed the dark circles under her eyes. Recalling her devastated expression from yesterday—like a bolt from the blue—when she learned about Xuetuan's intellectual issues, she spoke up. \"If you didn't sleep well, you can rest at home. I'll go to the clinic today.\"","Song Shixue shook her head. \"Aren't you going to look at shops today, Sister? I'm not tired, and I can't sleep anyway.\"","Just before she headed out the door, Lanxi suddenly stepped in front of her.","It wasn't just Song Shixue who hadn't slept well yesterday; he hadn't either. He had woken up before dawn and couldn't fall back asleep no matter how hard he tried.","\"There's a veterinarian in the northern part of the city with excellent medical skills. Although the Eldest Miss is a great doctor, she treats humans after all. Do you want to take Xuetuan to see the vet? It might help.\"","Song Shixue stopped in her tracks. Her eyes darted around for a moment before she turned and ran back inside. \"Wait for me a moment, I'm going to tell my sister.\"","She ran up to Song Jinzhao and said with a hopeful face, \"Sister, I want to take Xuetuan to see a vet. I won't go to the clinic this morning.\"","Song Jinzhao put down the ledger in her hand. \"Do you want Qingshuang to go with you?\"","Song Shixue shook her head. \"Lanxi will go with me. He said there's a vet in the north of the city with exceptional skills.\"","Song Jinzhao nodded. \"Go ahead. Stay safe.\"","After Song Shixue's figure disappeared around the corner, Qingshuang, who was standing to the side, asked, \"Eldest Miss, can Xuetuan's illness be cured?\"","Song Jinzhao shook her head. \"Illnesses brought from the womb are highly unlikely to be cured.\"","Genetic problems couldn't even be cured in modern times with advanced medicine, let alone in ancient times.","Qingshuang pursed her lips helplessly. \"Then the Second Miss is going to be heartbroken. She's been depressed since yesterday.\"","Song Jinzhao handed over the ledger, stood up, and draped her outer coat over her shoulders. \"Raising a pet is no different from raising a child. As long as there's a sliver of hope, the owner wants to try. It's good to go see a vet; after all, I'm not a professional.\"","Qingshuang picked up the oiled paper umbrella by the door and took two quick steps to catch up. \"Are we still going to look at shops now?\"","With the Second Miss absent, Doctor Liu was the only one at the clinic, and he definitely wouldn't be able to handle it all.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"It's still early. We'll look at the two shops near the clinic first and leave the rest for the afternoon.\"","Lanxi brought Song Shixue to the livestock market in the northern part of the city. At a glance, countless donkeys, cows, sheep, and horses were tied to hitching posts, waiting to be sold.","The cries of the surrounding livestock rose and fell. Hearing this, Xuetuan, held in her arms, lifted its head to look around. Its eyes held no predatory desire towards the living creatures, but rather confusion and curiosity.","The ground was littered with urine and feces. Whenever they encountered a spot that was truly impassable, Lanxi would stretch out his foot for Song Shixue to step on, so her embroidered shoes wouldn't get dirty.","\"The vet Fushun mentioned is just up ahead. I heard there isn't a cow or sheep he can't cure.\"","When the two arrived, they happened to see a middle-aged man wearing an apron using a knife to slice open a cyst on a horse's belly. Yellowish pus and blood burst out with a squelch. It looked disgusting, yet it also offered a weirdly satisfying sense of release.","Only after the vet had cleaned and bandaged the wound did he notice Song Shixue and Lanxi standing nearby.","\"Here for a consultation?\" This girl didn't look like someone who would come to a place like this. From their attire, it was obvious they were a master and a servant.","Song Shixue hastily held Xuetuan out in front of him. \"Yes, to get him treated.\"","Seeing clearly what was being handed to him, the vet raised his eyebrows in surprise.","He used a rag to briefly wipe the splattered blood off his hands, took Xuetuan with both hands, and looked directly into the tiger's eyes to examine it carefully.","\"A white tiger, that's quite rare. It looks to be only three or four months old.\"","Song Shixue nodded. \"It's only been a hundred and two days since he was born.\"","At this, not only the vet but even Lanxi looked at her in astonishment.","A hundred and two days. To think she remembered it so precisely!"]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: Opening a Barbecue Restaurant","paragraphs":["After a hands-on examination, the vet placed Xuetuan on the wooden board to stand. \"There's a problem with its eyes. Has it been like this since it opened them?\"","Song Shixue nodded in agreement. \"Yes, it wasn't very obvious when it first opened its eyes, but later the pupils grew closer and closer together.\"","The vet slowly shook his head and flipped Xuetuan over so its belly faced up. \"Its eyes just grew this way; it can't be cured. You've raised it very well, miss. Why care if its eyes don't look good?\"","It wasn't as if he hadn't seen tiger cubs on the mountain before. To be honest, even those raised by their own mothers weren't this robust.","Its fur was sleek and glossy, which meant it not only ate well but was definitely bathed often.","Lan Xi spoke up to explain, \"My young lady doesn't mind its eyes at all. It's just that it's a bit silly, and there seems to be a problem with its brain. We want to see if it can be cured.\"","The vet frowned and grabbed the tiger's leg to make it stand. Without a mother tiger to teach by example, captive tiger cubs could be a bit clumsy, but they were far from stupid.","Song Shixue told the vet about a series of Xuetuan's abnormal behaviors.","The vet put the little tiger on the ground, observing its eye reactions and posture. Finally, he brought a small chick and placed it on the ground, trying to get the tiger to bite it.","As a result, let alone biting, it didn't even know how to bat at it with its paws. Its reactions were slow, its eyes were dull and unfocused, and it seemed completely uninterested in everything. It was worse than a cat.","...","After nearly an hour, the vet helplessly returned the little tiger to Song Shixue.","White tigers were so rare. How did it end up growing like this? What a pity!","\"There is indeed a problem with its brain. To put it nicely, it's slow and mentally underdeveloped. To put it harshly, it's an idiot, a fool. Plus, without a mother tiger to teach it, these symptoms will only become more obvious.\"","Song Shixue clenched her fists, feeling a bit of a palpitation.","\"Do you mean it would be better for it to live with its own kind?\"","The vet shook his head with a heavy expression.","\"Someone like it absolutely cannot stay with its own kind. With its unusually colored fur and poor brain, it would be ostracized by other tigers. Even if it were bullied, it wouldn't be able to fight back and could only endure it.\"","Song Shixue asked, \"Then what should we do? Is there really no other way?\"","The vet put his hands on his hips. \"You can talk to it more and train it with sounds and actions. It might get a little better, but it won't be too obvious.\"","On the way back, Song Shixue didn't say a word. Lan Xi, walking beside her, didn't know what to do.","Upon arriving home and learning that Song Jinzhao had gone to the clinic in the morning, Song Shixue didn't go to the clinic anymore. Instead, she took Song Anhao to play with Xuetuan in the room.","Watching her younger brother play so well with Xuetuan, she took a deep breath and slowly exhaled. She should look on the bright side; at least it seemed very happy right now.","Song Jinzhao had looked at two shops in the morning and wasn't very satisfied with either. One building was too old, and the other was too small and right next to the main street, without even a place to set up a grill.","When returning home for lunch, Song Shixue told her what the vet had said. \"Sister, I've thought it through. If it can't be cured, then it can't be cured. This is all God's arrangement. Knowing that Xuetuan couldn't survive in the mountains, He purposely arranged for us to find it.\"","Song Jinzhao pursed her lips and smiled. Her words could be understood as self-hypnosis after running out of options. The little girl had accepted her fate.","In the afternoon, Song Shixue went to the clinic as usual. Song Jinzhao spent two hours looking at three more shops and finally decided on the one with the largest area and a five-meter-wide open space out front.","When summer arrived, setting up tables outside, feeling the gentle breeze, and eating barbecue with beer—business would definitely be exceptionally good.","The barbecue shop didn't need much renovation, and it opened less than seven days after buying the storefront.","The smell of charcoal mixed with the aroma of meat, making the whole street mouthwateringly fragrant.","Staring at the sizzling, greasy mutton on the grill, large handfuls of spices were sprinkled on it as if they were free, tempting everyone's appetites and making them constantly swallow their saliva.","Li Tianchong and his son sat inside the shop, their eyes lingering on the barbecue chef's fluid movements. For the first three days of opening, not only were the tables inside full, but even the outdoor seating was packed.","\"Another shop that will bring in a fortune every day. Song Jinzhao really has a lot of fresh ideas in her head.\" Li Tianchong bit the meat on the bamboo skewer with his upper and lower teeth. With one bite, it was numbingly spicy and filled his mouth with the aroma of meat.","Li Zi'en took a big bite of half a lamb kidney. \"It's actually quite similar to roasted lamb; she just changed the way it's sold.\"","Li Tianchong finished a skewer of mutton in two bites. \"It seems inexpensive, but in reality, there's only a little bit of meat on each skewer. It's simply a huge profit.\"","Li Zi'en turned his head and pointed at the vegetarian dishes on the shelf against the wall. \"That's what you call expensive. Two skewers of cabbage combined cost as much as meat. How is this any different from daylight robbery?\"","\"And this beer, it doesn't seem very intoxicating. The cost definitely isn't high.\"","Despite complaining about the prices, neither father nor son felt bad while eating. There was a table full of bamboo skewers. By the time they finished, their stomachs were bulging. When they burped, the taste of barbecue mixed with beer swirled in their mouths; they couldn't get enough and still wanted more.","It was just that their stomachs were too small and couldn't fit any more.","Seeing the good business of the barbecue shop, people started imitating it half a month after it opened. However, the taste always fell short and couldn't compare to the special barbecue seasoning Song Jinzhao had formulated."]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: Ye Liangyu Returns to the Capital: The Intense Competition in the Upper College","paragraphs":["In late June, following an imperial decree from Xiao Chengjing, Ye Liangyu, who had packed his bags long ago, was ready to set off for the capital.","Standing before the carriage loaded with chests, Ye Liangyu could not help but repeat the instructions he had already given several times over the past few days.","\"I have already spoken with Dean Mu. From now on, you will submit your extracurricular assignments to him for review every two days. If there is anything you do not understand, you can ask him. There are less than two months left until the provincial examination. You must not slack off. I will wait for you in the capital.\"","Song Qiming cupped his hands and bowed, promising in a serious tone, \"I will definitely not disappoint you, sir.\"","Watching the carriage gradually move away, Song Qiming slightly clenched his hands by his sides, suppressing the reluctance in his heart.","The night was as dark as ink, like a smudged inkstone. The candle in Song Qiming's room was not extinguished until midnight.","He slept soundly until dawn, without a single dream.","Song Shixue, who was warming up, heard the door open and turned her head. Seeing Song Qiming come out, a wide smile immediately spread across her face.","\"Brother, you haven't been home these past few days, your martial arts practice must have slacked off.\"","Splashing cold well water on his face, Song Qiming stretched his arms and loosened his joints. \"The guards at my teacher's house wake up before dawn every day to drill. I followed them and didn't miss a single day.\"","The siblings stood side by side in a horse stance. Half an hour later, they began to spar with real weapons.","Lan Xi stood to the side, holding a sword and watching. While Song Qiming was away, he had been the one sparring with Song Shixue. Now, watching them, he felt a bit empty inside.","Covered in sweat, Qingshuang downed the water in the teapot in one gulp, grabbed her whip, and walked toward Lan Xi. \"Let's the two of us have a go.\"","Lan Xi looked at the middle-aged woman who was more than twice his age. She looked about the same age as his deceased mother, and fighting her made him feel somewhat disrespectful.","Seeing Lan Xi standing still, Qingshuang, eager to test some new moves, struck a stance and urged, \"Hurry up, attack me with your fastest speed.\"","Lan Xi glanced at the siblings sparring fiercely beside them, then darkened his face, swung his sword, and darted forward.","Half an hour later, after being whipped flying for the fifth time, Lan Xi lay sprawled spread-eagle on the ground.","The first time it locked his waist, the second time it snared his leg, the third time it wrapped around his arm, the fourth time it nearly struck his neck, and the fifth time it drew blood. This was not just a simple spar; it was clearly bullying the young.","Qingshuang put away her whip with satisfaction and walked over to help Lan Xi up. \"Your lower body is unstable, and you are not as strong as the Second Miss. You still need more practice.\"","Lan Xi, who was two years older than Song Shixue, felt a lump in his throat. The Second Miss was personally taught by the Eldest Miss; how could they be compared?","Song Jinzhao leaned against the door with her arms crossed, her gaze sweeping over the four of them. The potatoes planted in the garden were growing very well and would be harvested in August. October was the fiftieth birthday of the Emperor of the Dongzhao Kingdom.","She planned to enter the capital before the birthday, but it seemed like these few people would not be enough.","After finishing his morning exercises, bathing, changing clothes, and eating breakfast, Song Qiming arrived at the academy with nearly half an hour left before the morning recitation.","As soon as he sat down, Ji Youming picked up an essay from the desk, turned around, and leaned closer. \"Qiming, I feel like what I wrote is too superficial, but I cannot think of any other arguments to write about. Could you help me see how to revise it?\"","Under Ye Liangyu's one-on-one guidance, coupled with Song Qiming's desperate efforts to catch up, his ranking had skyrocketed in the several monthly exams since entering the Upper House. He had already left Ji Youming far behind, showing a faint momentum of catching up to He Feixuan, the top student of the Upper House.","At the academy, he was reading books anytime and anywhere. His intense level of competition exerted extremely strong pressure on the other students in the Upper House.","Afraid of falling behind, everyone started to push themselves relentlessly, leaving them all with dark circles under their eyes."]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: Young Potatoes","paragraphs":["During the noon break, Song Gaoli and Song Qiming sat opposite each other in the pavilion. The ink stains on their cuffs had dried, leaving no marks on the white paper they rested upon.","To prepare for the provincial exams in August, and to prove himself without leaving any regrets, Song Gaoli studied constantly. He not only lost the five pounds he had gained during the New Year but also shed an additional fifteen pounds, making him look significantly thinner.","\"In a few days, the academy will have a break. Hu Fengye mentioned there's an elegant gathering at the West Garden. Many students from academies and schools in Anyang Prefecture will be there to exchange essays and discuss poetry. Do you want to go together?\"","After Wang Rui, Song Qiming, and Ji Youming passed into the Upper House, Hu Fengye was left in the Inner House. Song Gaoli often went to consult him, and over time, the two had become good friends.","Song Qiming looked up and asked, \"Morning or afternoon?\"","He had to go to Mu Hongyue's house in the morning and had no time for anything else.","Song Gaoli replied, \"It's a full-day event. Exchanging essays in the morning, discussing and appreciating poetry in the afternoon, and we'll have lunch at the West Garden.\"","Song Qiming thought for a moment and agreed, \"Then I'll head over in the afternoon. It's a good opportunity to interact with people from other academies and schools.\"","Although Anyang Academy was the best in Anyang Prefecture, there were also talented students from other academies and family schools who had renowned reputations. Song Qiming had been in Anyang Prefecture for less than a year in total. All his energy was spent on studying, and the little free time he had was squeezed out for martial arts.","He avoided elegant gatherings, poetry meets, and banquets whenever possible. His social network, aside from his classmates at the academy, consisted only of the elders Ye Liangyu had taken him to visit. With the provincial exams approaching, it was time to meet competitors outside his own academy to know what to expect.","Seeing that the potato plants were flourishing with lush leaves and had reached their maximum height, Song Jinzhao gently scraped away the topsoil with a small hoe. Upon seeing egg-sized potatoes hanging from the roots, she breathed a slight sigh of relief; it seemed the harvest would be good.","Digging them all out, she found that this single potato seedling had produced a total of ten potatoes. The largest was the size of a fist, while the smallest was only slightly bigger than a fingernail.","The tender potatoes had paper-thin skins and were full of moisture. Song Jinzhao directly had Qingshui boil them with their skins on in salted water.","In the evening, the four siblings gathered around the table. Faced with food they had never eaten before, a curious Song Qiming was the first to pick up a potato and pop it into his mouth.","He wondered how this miraculous crop, capable of yielding a thousand catties per acre, would taste.","The moment it entered his mouth, before he even bit down with his teeth, it melted as he pressed it between his tongue and the roof of his mouth. It was like eating an egg, smooth and tender. Besides a fragrant earthy scent, there was a crisp, faint sweetness. It was delicious.","Song Jinzhao ate two, one large and one small. The larger one was slightly starchier, while the smaller one was like a soft-boiled egg.","At this stage, the potatoes had less starch, making them suitable for boiling or stir-frying into shreds. To make mashed potatoes or potato noodles, they would have to wait until August when they matured into old potatoes, which would not only yield a higher harvest but also be more filling.","\"Eldest Sister, it's delicious! I want more.\" Song Anhao reached out but couldn't grab the plate, anxiously tapping the table with her wooden spoon.","\"Sister, can we make this again tomorrow?\" Song Shixue's eyes sparkled, also finding it delicious.","Song Qiming thought of the vastly different-sized potatoes on the plate. \"Digging them up now before they've fully grown, isn't it a bit of a pity?\"","If they all grew to the size of a fist, digging up just one plant would provide enough food for several meals.","Song Jinzhao placed the remaining two small ones into Song Anhao's bowl. \"It is a bit of a pity. We'll have one more meal of them tomorrow and then stop digging until they are fully mature.\"","Aside from the ones being sent to the palace, a large portion of this batch of potatoes would become seeds for next year's planting, so they couldn't eat them freely and could only have a little taste."]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: Harvested in August, with a Yield of a Thousand Jin per Mu","paragraphs":["The provincial exam took place once every three years. The city of Longbei Province gathered scholars and xiucai from all over. With ten days left before the exam, the streets, inns, and teahouses were practically packed with thousands of scholars.","The braised food shop and barbecue restaurant were overflowing with customers every day. Considering that the scholars taking the exam had no time to wait in line, Song Jinzhao even introduced a door-to-door delivery service. The delivery fee was only five copper coins per order. If an order was placed a day in advance, it would be delivered to the door at the agreed time the next day. If multiple people ordered together for the same location and reached a certain amount, the delivery fee could even be waived.","Looking at the delivery boys bustling about on the streets, many shops followed suit and started delivering takeout, with the Li family's inn and restaurant leading the charge.","In the garden of the Song Manor, Chunxing and the others were busy digging up potatoes. Compared to the tender potatoes eaten in late June, most of the mature potatoes now were the size of a fist, and some of the larger ones were the size of two fists.","\"Eldest Miss, it's a letter from Song Family Village.\" Lanxi ran over holding two letters.","Of the two letters, one was addressed to Song Jinzhao, and the other to Song Gaoli. The village chief must have asked the messenger to bring them together.","\"Send someone to deliver this letter to Song Gaoli at Anyang Academy. They should be having lunch at this hour.\"","\"Yes.\" Lanxi took the envelope with both hands, turned around, and asked the other servants to run the errand.","Song Shixue held Song Anhao with her right hand and beckoned Xuetuan to move closer to Song Jinzhao with her left.","\"Sister, what does the letter say?\"","Song Jinzhao replied, \"Grandpa knows Qiming is going to take the provincial exam, so he told him to do his best and not be nervous. Whether he passes or not, he should remember to write a letter to let him know.\"","Song Shixue took the letter and read it a couple of times. \"Yongnian's handwriting is getting better and better.\"","Song Jinzhao glanced at it and nodded in agreement. \"Neither Yongnian nor Yaozu passed the county exam to become a tongsheng this year. Grandpa must be very disappointed. Maybe one of them can pass next year.\"","By next year, the three-year period would be up. If they couldn't pass, she wondered if the first and second branches of the family would give up, or let them continue studying.","After a busy day, and making sure no potatoes were left in the soil, Chunxing had someone bring over a steelyard and began weighing them basket by basket.","After weighing and adding up all the catties, Chunxing's hands were trembling as she wrote down the numbers.","\"Eldest Miss, we harvested a total of two hundred and seventy catties of potatoes.\"","Ten catties of potato seedlings, two and a half fen of land, yielding one thousand and eighty catties per mu. It was simply astonishing, truly a divine crop.","If every household could plant them, they would never have to worry about running out of food again.","Song Jinzhao looked at the potatoes in the bamboo baskets. The potatoes of this era had nowhere near the yield of modern improved seeds.","With such good soil and careful tending, a yield of two or three thousand catties per mu would be absolutely no problem in modern times, but now it was just barely a thousand.","\"Clean off the dirt, put the potatoes in black cloth bags, and store them in the cellar. Place wooden boards on the ground, and lay straw on the boards. Don't put them against the wall, and make sure to keep them away from light and moisture so they don't sprout.\"","Two hundred and seventy catties of potatoes, even if all used as seeds, would only yield over seven thousand catties next year. It would take at least several years for every household to plant them. After presenting the birthday gift, she could suggest planting them in the south now, where there were two harvests a year, cutting the time in half.","When Song Qiming returned in the evening and learned of the yield, he excitedly spun around in circles. \"A thousand catties per mu! It's actually a thousand catties per mu!\"","\"This is wonderful! With such a high yield, if every household plants them, how many people could be fed!\"","As if thinking of something, he stopped and said to Song Jinzhao, \"Sister, do you need me to write to my teacher immediately and ask him to present the potatoes to the Emperor to claim credit for you?\"","After going to the capital, the title of Lady of the Township was a bit low. It was time for his sister to get a promotion."]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: Prediction of the Provincial Examination","paragraphs":["Song Jinzhao stood with his hands behind his back. \"No need, I will deliver it personally this time. The twenty-fifth of the tenth month is the current Emperor's birthday. After the provincial examinations are over, we will head to the capital immediately. These potatoes will be our birthday gift.\"","Song Qiming furrowed his brows in thought. \"The results of the provincial exam won't be released until the end of the eighth month. With the deadline being the twenty-fifth of the tenth month, isn't the schedule a bit too tight?\"","They couldn't travel day and night without rest like the government's posthouse couriers. To rush from Anyang Prefecture to the capital in less than two months was simply cutting it too close.","Song Jinzhao replied, \"We will set off as soon as the results are posted. We'll use a two-horse carriage. As long as we don't delay on the road, we should be able to make it.\"","Next year's second month would mark the spring imperial examination; once they left for the capital, they definitely wouldn't be returning this year.","The tension brought about by the provincial exam lingered over Anyang Prefecture for weeks. It wasn't until all three sessions of the exam were completely finished that the thousands of students were finally liberated.","Aside from those with weaker constitutions who had been physically broken by the grueling nine-day exam and were now bedridden in their inns, most people only rested for a single day before heading out into the city to attend literary gatherings and banquets to build their social networks.","Some went to teahouses, taverns, or even brothels to relieve the pent-up stress of their exam preparations.","A very small fraction even went to temples to pray to Buddha and cast fortunes, hoping to predict whether they would pass with flying colors.","It was commonly known as the last hurrah before the results were announced.","Meanwhile, on the morning of the second day after the exams ended, Song Qiming visited Mu Hongyue to discuss the questions and his answers for the three sessions, aiming to estimate his performance and whether he would pass.","Song Qiming wrote down all the exam questions and his corresponding answers on a piece of paper. \"This is roughly it. The accuracy is above ninety percent.\"","Even though he had written it himself, the word count was massive. No matter how good Song Qiming's memory was, he couldn't replicate it flawlessly; there were bound to be a few words or sentences out of order.","Stroking his beard, Mu Hongyue read through the pages and revealed a gratified smile. After two months of interaction, he was extremely confident in Song Qiming's academic prowess.","But this was the provincial exam. To perform so flawlessly under such immense pressure truly proved that the younger generation was a force to be reckoned with.","\"This is the first answer sheet I've seen, but I am certain it is absolutely the most perfect one. You haven't let Brother Ye down. He truly took in a brilliant disciple.\"","Joy blossomed in Song Qiming's heart. He bowed deeply and said, \"Thank you for your guidance over these past two months, Headmaster. Your student will never forget this kindness.\"","Mu Hongyue smiled, waving his hand and shaking his head. \"I was entrusted with a task, and I merely fulfilled it faithfully. Whether you had these two months with me or not, you would have passed and become a Juren. The spring examination is next February. If you aren't in a hurry to go to the capital, you can continue to study here with me.\"","\"Thank you, Headmaster. However, before my teacher left, he instructed me to find him in the capital. Therefore, your student plans to depart as soon as possible. I will set off right after the results are released.\"","Mu Hongyue raised his eyebrows in surprise. \"In such a rush? Aren't you going to return to your hometown to visit first?\"","Song Qiming replied, \"The journey to the capital is long, and there is less than half a year until the spring exam. I want to push myself a bit further, so it's better to head to the capital early.\"","Mu Hongyue sighed and nodded. \"That's true. Brother Ye is surely waiting for you.\"","Even with Ye Liangyu's mentorship, if Song Qiming couldn't achieve a high ranking, or worse, failed the exam, everything would be in vain.","It was just that this child was still so young and his path had been too smooth. It was hard to guarantee he wouldn't stumble in the future, and he wondered if Brother Ye would be able to protect him.","As he was leaving the Mu residence, a servant led a few people walking towards him.","He Feixuan, Wang Xu, Wang Rui, Ji Youming, Hu Fengye... more than half of the Upper House students had arrived, and even two of the top students from the Inner House were there.","\"I thought we had arrived early enough, but I didn't expect Qiming to be leaving already.\" A polite smile touched the corners of He Feixuan's lips. He was deeply intrigued by this fellow student who had nearly caught up to him in the academy's final assessment.","If given another two months, Song Qiming might have genuinely surpassed him.","What made it even more pressuring was that the boy was only thirteen years old, while he himself was already past twenty. The age gap was significant.","When it came to genius, anyone would feel a sense of inadequacy in front of Song Qiming!"]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: An Alternative Approach by Song Gaoli","paragraphs":["Wang Xu wore a smile on his face. No matter how jealous he felt inside, he had to say pleasant things and flatter Song Qiming a little.","\"Qiming is Lord Ye's only disciple. Out of respect for Lord Ye, the dean naturally has to take extra care of him.\"","Song Qiming calmly cupped his hands in greeting to the group and said with a hint of shyness, \"To be honest with you all, I was a bit nervous taking the provincial exam for the first time. I stayed up all night after finishing the exam yesterday, so I had no choice but to seek out the dean. There is still about half a month before the results are announced, and I can't just be anxious every day.\"","Wang Xu and the others raised their eyebrows. \"Oh? Looking at Brother Song's rosy complexion, I imagine you must have performed quite well.\"","Everyone visiting Mu Hongyue today shared the same purpose. As the most outstanding group of students in the academy, it was perfectly normal for them to be questioned by the academy's teachers after the exam.","The students' examination results were crucial to the academy. They not only represented the teachers' instructional level but also served as the academy's future network in official circles.","Song Qiming did not tell the truth. Before the dust settled, one could not speak too absolutely, as it was hard to guarantee no one would bear a grudge.","\"The dean said my answers were passable, and I should be able to pass the provincial exam.\"","The crowd exchanged glances. It was already a sure thing for Song Qiming to pass and become a Juren. Based on his past performance at the academy, merely passing was not enough; his goal should be the top five or even the first place. Could it be that he underperformed?","Song Qiming cupped his hands to take his leave. \"My family is still waiting for me to return, so I will take my leave first. I wish all my fellow students great success and top honors in the examinations.\"","Watching Song Qiming's retreating back as he left in silence, their hearts sank halfway.","Wang Rui sighed with emotion, \"It is inevitable to be nervous in the examination room at a young age. Regardless of the rank, just passing to become a Juren is good enough.\"","Ji Youming and Hu Fengye exchanged a glance.","Even when facing vicious, blade-wielding thugs, Song Qiming could rise up to resist without losing ground. Would he really be nervous in the examination room? It seemed impossible no matter how they thought about it. Most likely, he was just being modest and didn't want to tell them.","After He Feixuan and the others entered the inner hall, they held the exam papers they had written from memory, waiting for Mu Hongyue to critique them one by one.","\"The writing is excellent. You may go back and await good news.\"","\"The opening breaks into the theme perfectly, and the diction is magnificent. Top tier!\"","At the same time, the homes of inner-courtyard teachers like Yang Yanfeng were also crowded with students. The homes of the teachers for the outer-courtyard students who participated were not spared either.","However, their critiques were much worse than Mu Hongyue's.","\"The writing is mediocre, the artistic conception is acceptable; there is a slight glimmer of hope.\"","\"You lack maturity. Study for another three years.\"","Facing the outer-courtyard students, the teachers' evaluations were mostly, \"Your courage is commendable; take the exam again in three years.\"","The inner-courtyard teacher held Song Gaoli's memorized paper, his brows furrowing tightly, then relaxing, his eyes filled with equal parts surprise and confusion.","\"How did you think of writing it like this?\" The argument of the policy essay was tricky and obscure. He had read over a dozen reconstructed papers, and not a single one was like his.","Furthermore, the tone of flattery in the examination poem was far too strong. It would easily make the inner-curtain examiners feel that this person was obsequious and lacked the backbone of a scholar.","Song Gaoli scratched the back of his head and replied, \"For this provincial exam, given my academic foundation, the hope of passing to become a Juren was already slim. That is why I wanted to find a different path. Song Qiming and I happened to discuss this argument by chance. It was just a passing remark at the time, but when I saw the topic, I figured I could use it, so I expanded on it considerably.\"","The inner-courtyard teacher held up the paper and turned it over. \"And what about this poem?\"","Song Gaoli's earlobes tensed, and he lowered his head in embarrassment.","\"As you know, sir, my poetry is generally below average. Before the exam, I inquired about the past experiences of the chief examiner for this provincial exam, which is why I wrote it this way. It couldn't be worse than what I usually write. If I am lucky enough to have the chief examiner see it, I might even get a high score.\"","\"Even if not, when others see that I am praising the chief examiner, they probably won't give it too low a score.\"","The inner-courtyard teacher's brows furrowed into little peaks. \"Your intentions are too obvious. If word gets out, it will be bad for your reputation.\"","Song Gaoli looked up uncomfortably and quickly lowered his eyes again. \"As long as I can pass, a bad reputation doesn't matter.\"","At most, people would mock him for having impure motives, lacking real talent, and relying on flattery to rise. But so what? It was still better than failing without even trying.","Seeing him say this, the inner-courtyard teacher picked up the paper and carefully read it again. Finally, he said, \"It depends on your luck. If by chance it aligns with the preferences of the inner-curtain examiner grading this paper, there might still be a glimmer of hope.\"","He sighed and seemed ready to let the matter rest, but suddenly asked, \"You are not usually like this. Who came up with this idea for you?\"","Song Gaoli looked away, glancing left and right, and stammered in reply, \"I thought hard for a long time in the examination room and really couldn't come up with a good poem. I resorted to this as a bad plan, truly out of helplessness.\"","The inner-courtyard teacher stared at Song Gaoli meaningfully. Seeing that he wasn't usually this clever, and recalling that Song Gaoli was closest to Song Qiming, the teacher formed a guess in his heart.","If he really managed to pass, this move wouldn't have been in vain. Either way, there was nothing to lose."]}]);
